thub.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/e11e2a2d6bd64c2e35d53199b5831193f4edf6e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:45:53Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:45:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(agent)!: adopt Pi''s native Code Mode (#618)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose the move from run_code to Pi''s native Code Mode\n\nRefs #611\n\n* docs(openspec): make the Code Mode change forward only and drop the shell status fix\n\n* docs(openspec): follow Pi for inner-call results in Code Mode\n\n* feat(agent)!: adopt Pi''s native Code Mode\n\nReplace Sero''s `run_code` tool with Pi''s `codemode` in chat and subagent\nsessions, so one code path serves both. Pi''s inner tool calls are real tool\nevents, so the chat shows them while a script runs.\n\n- `features/codemode` builds the extension for both session types and\n  switches the tool on after the session exists, making `codemode` a base\n  tool the context editor can disable.\n- The output optimizer detects an inner call by the Code Mode id shape,\n  `<parent call id>/<n>`. `@sero-ai/common` documents the shape and moves\n  to 0.23.1.\n- The main process forwards nested-call updates and rebuilds the rows on\n  reopen; the renderer lists them inside the script''s card.\n- Prompt text, the MCP remote-skill gate, and the user docs name `codemode`.\n- `features/code-mode/`, its unit test, and the `run` dependency are gone.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `run_code` is removed. Scripts are JavaScript only and\nreceive an image result as text. A script sets its own time limit with\n`timeout_ms`; Sero adds none, and cancelling the turn stops the script.\n\nCloses #611\n\n* docs(openspec): mark every Code Mode task done\n\nThe delivery tasks are complete: PR #618 is the draft pull request that\ncloses #611, and #609 is closed with a comment naming it.\n\n* fix(agent): handle calls a codemode script makes at the same time and for longer\n\n- share one pre-turn snapshot between writes that start together\n- check remote skill code approval one call at a time per session\n- restart a script''s stall timer when its inner calls start and end\n- keep the subagent activity feed busy while a script still runs\n- send only top-level tool calls to gateway clients\n- leave codemode out of the member tool catalogue\n- show inner rows as cancelled when a turn ends while they are open\n- correct the script API in the Code Mode guide\n\n* fix(agent): report a failed bash call a codemode script made\n\n- bash returns isError and a structured result with exit_code, as Pi''s\n  own bash does, so an inner call is marked failed and the script can\n  read the exit code\n- settle inner calls in the subagent activity feed again\n- show the error text on a failed inner row","tree":{"sha":"d33c6c279b0df29ca7dcfcf395c2236985be410d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/d33c6c279b0df29ca7dcfcf395c2236985be410d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/e11e2a2d6bd64c2e35d53199b5831193f4edf6e5","verification":{"payload":"tree d33c6c279b0df29ca7dcfcf395c2236985be410d\nparent 0417dd27df0c61931313774ad50a54b30d4316f3\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1791236753 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791236753 +0100\n\nfeat(agent)!: adopt Pi''s native Code Mode (#618)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose the move from run_code to Pi''s native Code Mode\n\nRefs #611\n\n* docs(openspec): make the Code Mode change forward only and drop the shell status fix\n\n* docs(openspec): follow Pi for inner-call results in Code Mode\n\n* feat(agent)!: adopt Pi''s native Code Mode\n\nReplace Sero''s `run_code` tool with Pi''s `codemode` in chat and subagent\nsessions, so one code path serves both. Pi''s inner tool calls are real tool\nevents, so the chat shows them while a script runs.\n\n- `features/codemode` builds the extension for both session types and\n  switches the tool on after the session exists, making `codemode` a base\n  tool the context editor can disable.\n- The output optimizer detects an inner call by the Code Mode id shape,\n  `<parent call id>/<n>`. `@sero-ai/common` documents the shape and moves\n  to 0.23.1.\n- The main process forwards nested-call updates and rebuilds the rows on\n  reopen; the renderer lists them inside the script''s card.\n- Prompt text, the MCP remote-skill gate, and the user docs name `codemode`.\n- `features/code-mode/`, its unit test, and the `run` dependency are gone.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `run_code` is removed. Scripts are JavaScript only and\nreceive an image result as text. A script sets its own time limit with\n`timeout_ms`; Sero adds none, and cancelling the turn stops the script.\n\nCloses #611\n\n* docs(openspec): mark every Code Mode task done\n\nThe delivery tasks are complete: PR #618 is the draft pull request that\ncloses #611, and #609 is closed with a comment naming it.\n\n* fix(agent): handle calls a codemode script makes at the same time and for longer\n\n- share one pre-turn snapshot between writes that start together\n- check remote skill code approval one call at a time per session\n- restart a script''s stall timer when its inner calls start and end\n- keep the subagent activity feed busy while a script still runs\n- send only top-level tool calls to gateway clients\n- leave codemode out of the member tool catalogue\n- show inner rows as cancelled when a turn ends while they are open\n- correct the script API in the Code Mode guide\n\n* fix(agent): report a failed bash call a codemode script made\n\n- bash returns isError and a structured result with exit_code, as Pi''s\n  own bash does, so an inner call is marked failed and the script can\n  read the exit code\n- settle inner calls in the subagent activity feed again\n- show the error text on a failed inner row","reason":"valid","signatu