","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/0417dd27df0c61931313774ad50a54b30d4316f3","sha":"0417dd27df0c61931313774ad50a54b30d4316f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/0417dd27df0c61931313774ad50a54b30d4316f3"}],"sha":"e11e2a2d6bd64c2e35d53199b5831193f4edf6e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/e11e2a2d6bd64c2e35d53199b5831193f4edf6e5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/0417dd27df0c61931313774ad50a54b30d4316f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T05:39:03Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T05:39:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): Pi SDK 1.0.2 upgrade POC with Sero''s own code kept (#608)2\n\n* docs(openspec): propose the Pi 1.0 upgrade POC\n\nPlan candidates 1 to 5 of issue #594: the upgrade from Pi 0.84.2 to\n1.0.2 with all custom Sero code kept, then native Code Mode, prompt and\ntool history, MCP and cache warming assessments on a stacked branch.\n\nRefs #594\n\n* chore(deps): move Pi SDK to 1.0.2 and fix what the upgrade breaks\n\nPin the four Pi packages to 1.0.2 and drop the Dependabot ignore entry.\n\n- Move the context editor''s prompt override to the host extension''s\n  before_agent_start handler. It replaces the base part of the prompt and\n  keeps the blocks plugins appended.\n- Write context through SessionManager and refreshContext().\n- Give bridged tools an ExtensionToolContext.\n- Guard tool arguments and details as JSON.\n- Match Pi''s tagged <docs> prompt section when Sero strips it.\n- Keep prompt-cache warming off.\n- Leave the system message out of the session list count.\n- Remove two of the three private SDK reaches and the file rewrite call.\n\nThe POC baseline spec is evidence tooling. Remove it before a merge.\n\nRefs #594\n\n* build(deps): keep one undici 8.x so the app packages on Pi 1.0.2\n\nPi 1.0.2 pins undici 8.10.2 and the desktop app uses 8.11.2. openai takes\nundici as a peer, so each Pi package resolved to two variants and\npnpm deploy stopped with ERR_PNPM_DEPLOY_AMBIGUOUS_PEER.\n\nAlso extend the POC script: session actions, cancel and mid-turn\ncompaction, an override reopen check, and a packaged-app turn.\n\nRefs #594\n\n* docs(openspec): mark the upgrade branch tasks complete\n\nRefs #594\n\n* test(memory): read the snapshot prompt through the Pi 1.0 prompt options\n\n* chore: update based on agent instructions\n\n* fix(agent): keep the context editor''s tool list when the session moves to another entry","tree":{"sha":"923c876a1dd63d6ccbcc3b1c426a6c109175088e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/923c876a1dd63d6ccbcc3b1c426a6c109175088e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/0417dd27df0c61931313774ad50a54b30d4316f3","verification":{"payload":"tree 923c876a1dd63d6ccbcc3b1c426a6c109175088e\nparent 7f79fc8bc00e1a303b2c83703a0e90a41a701b5f\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1791178743 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791178743 +0100\n\nchore(deps): Pi SDK 1.0.2 upgrade POC with Sero''s own code kept (#608)2\n\n* docs(openspec): propose the Pi 1.0 upgrade POC\n\nPlan candidates 1 to 5 of issue #594: the upgrade from Pi 0.84.2 to\n1.0.2 with all custom Sero code kept, then native Code Mode, prompt and\ntool history, MCP and cache warming assessments on a stacked branch.\n\nRefs #594\n\n* chore(deps): move Pi SDK to 1.0.2 and fix what the upgrade breaks\n\nPin the four Pi packages to 1.0.2 and drop the Dependabot ignore entry.\n\n- Move the context editor''s prompt override to the host extension''s\n  before_agent_start handler. It replaces the base part of the prompt and\n  keeps the blocks plugins appended.\n- Write context through SessionManager and refreshContext().\n- Give bridged tools an ExtensionToolContext.\n- Guard tool arguments and details as JSON.\n- Match Pi''s tagged <docs> prompt section when Sero strips it.\n- Keep prompt-cache warming off.\n- Leave the system message out of the session list count.\n- Remove two of the three private SDK reaches and the file rewrite call.\n\nThe POC baseline spec is evidence tooling. Remove it before a merge.\n\nRefs #594\n\n* build(deps): keep one undici 8.x so the app packages on Pi 1.0.2\n\nPi 1.0.2 pins undici 8.10.2 and the desktop app uses 8.11.2. openai takes\nundici as a peer, so each Pi package resolved to two variants and\npnpm deploy stopped with ERR_PNPM_DEPLOY_AMBIGUOUS_PEER.\n\nAlso extend the POC script: session actions, cancel and mid-turn\ncompaction, an override reopen check, and a packaged-app turn.\n\nRefs #594\n\n* docs(openspec): mark the upgrade branch tasks complete\n\nRefs #594\n\n* test(memory): read the snapshot prompt through the Pi 1.0 prompt options\n\n* chore: update based on agent instructions\n\n* fix(agent): keep the context editor''s tool list when the session moves to another entry","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n