b-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/7f79fc8bc00e1a303b2c83703a0e90a41a701b5f","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDdmNzlmYzhiYzAwZTFhMzAzYjJjODM3MDNhMGU5MGE0MWE3MDFiNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/d78e4423ae1a2d7a9fd78fba4eb70fd9a5640aae","sha":"d78e4423ae1a2d7a9fd78fba4eb70fd9a5640aae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/d78e4423ae1a2d7a9fd78fba4eb70fd9a5640aae"}],"sha":"7f79fc8bc00e1a303b2c83703a0e90a41a701b5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/7f79fc8bc00e1a303b2c83703a0e90a41a701b5f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/d78e4423ae1a2d7a9fd78fba4eb70fd9a5640aae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:24:11Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:24:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(agent): keep undo, fork, cancel and model state correct across a session reopen (#614)\n\n* fix(agent): keep undo, fork, cancel and model state correct across a session reopen\n\nA session opens on the last entry in its file, and an undo, a legacy restore\nor a clear wrote nothing. A reopened session then showed the removed turns.\nEach of them now appends a leaf marker.\n\nPi''s createBranchedSession moves the manager it is called on to the new file,\nso after a fork the open parent wrote its next turns to the fork''s file. The\nfork now runs on a second manager.\n\nA cancel during a tool call ended the turn as an error, because the request\nthat starts after the abort fails with stop reason error. The outcome now\nreads the run''s abort signal.\n\nPi restores a model only for a session that has messages. A session with none\nnow opens with the model saved in its file.\n\nagent-node emitted a task event after its file write, with whatever state the\ntask had by then. A second transition could show twice, and a controller that\nanswered an approval at once got approval_not_found. The event now carries the\nstate the transition wrote.\n\n* fix(agent): keep the model and thinking level when a cleared session is reopened\n\n* fix(agent): fork a session that has no file yet from its own manager\n\n* fix(agent): fork from the saved file only when it holds the current entry","tree":{"sha":"59fd65e661caaf523bd21083c4835ff7befaa15d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/59fd65e661caaf523bd21083c4835ff7befaa15d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/d78e4423ae1a2d7a9fd78fba4eb70fd9a5640aae","verification":{"payload":"tree 59fd65e661caaf523bd21083c4835ff7befaa15d\nparent 481e6c9608c464aa4c449476504225764524d0e9\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1791152651 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791152651 +0100\n\nfix(agent): keep undo, fork, cancel and model state correct across a session reopen (#614)\n\n* fix(agent): keep undo, fork, cancel and model state correct across a session reopen\n\nA session opens on the last entry in its file, and an undo, a legacy restore\nor a clear wrote nothing. A reopened session then showed the removed turns.\nEach of them now appends a leaf marker.\n\nPi''s createBranchedSession moves the manager it is called on to the new file,\nso after a fork the open parent wrote its next turns to the fork''s file. The\nfork now runs on a second manager.\n\nA cancel during a tool call ended the turn as an error, because the request\nthat starts after the abort fails with stop reason error. The outcome now\nreads the run''s abort signal.\n\nPi restores a model only for a session that has messages. A session with none\nnow opens with the model saved in its file.\n\nagent-node emitted a task event after its file write, with whatever state the\ntask had by then. A second transition could show twice, and a controller that\nanswered an approval at once got approval_not_found. The event now carries the\nstate the transition wrote.\n\n* fix(agent): keep the model and thinking level when a cleared session is reopened\n\n* fix(agent): fork a session that has no file yet from its own manager\n\n* fix(agent): fork from the saved file only when it holds the current entry","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwtILCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHSMQADz3Wc2QD/Wdr+onEuXqeo9l\nTFKL/U32YJUYQaXQdv5/5lF7k+3ZGseJX1K2zpW8vfnzRXRUSaV9LILD1FAHkp6l\nMuwjDqXVeOxFv+JpUjcy1DZNwysD5G/O6QXNkU4z8Kw1HBRBWQxjVcJo67apZuCI\nt12wFj9qzxNno2uoFJlDQn7W9DRfy0bftTu2nW1XCOaaNxaULKLb3KWrX7c+F5uu\nmIC27Q9KTbB5+Lzy4+81+r6WQ+h8VTukV4eN+3WKLfpYMNhAtOqkjqUK+hwzgpc8\nT4XCW3AAJ+QBXrnKX1nPMa8E/NiLsbRhQnj/Y7WHKa87Y8HvHbwTc3ECOMcBXVeC\nZYLZZous0NxrEmX0r8tlHcfseqkNpZvFUSJ8Te3SeHa3fPV6g351wN51IWuXgQkF\ne3cMkYhJc6cQLyikBmFskxs/Xvyq