s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/72ad6fdd9dcd660f49f19dd2303d38d96126fc22","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDcyYWQ2ZmRkOWRjZDY2MGY0OWYxOWRkMjMwM2QzOGQ5NjEyNmZjMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/f26f18ab3baa20a58140e632f00037dc966a9ccf","sha":"f26f18ab3baa20a58140e632f00037dc966a9ccf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/f26f18ab3baa20a58140e632f00037dc966a9ccf"}],"sha":"72ad6fdd9dcd660f49f19dd2303d38d96126fc22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/72ad6fdd9dcd660f49f19dd2303d38d96126fc22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/f26f18ab3baa20a58140e632f00037dc966a9ccf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:25:32Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:25:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(cli): gate plugin prompt hints on the session''s CLI surface (#590)\n\n* fix(cli): gate plugin prompt hints on the session''s CLI surface\n\nThe MCP and Graphify plugins add their prompt hint when `sero-cli` is active\nand their tool is not a direct tool. A subagent allowlist that names `sero-cli`\nbut not the plugin tools hits that shape while its registry hides the command,\nso the model sees a hint for a command that answers \"unknown command\". The\nplugins cannot tell the two cases apart from `getActiveTools`/`getAllTools`.\n\nThe host knows the session''s CLI registry, so it now announces the command list\nthe session can run on `session_start`, and the plugins gate their hint on it.\nA session kind that does not announce keeps the previous optimistic behaviour.\n\n- Add `SESSION_CLI_SURFACE_EVENT` and `trackSessionCliSurface` to\n  `@sero-ai/common` (0.20.2).\n- Add `announceSessionCliSurface` and emit it from the chat/member and subagent\n  extension factories.\n- Check the announced surface in the MCP and Graphify plugins.\n\nCloses #582\n\n* fix(cli): check every command a plugin hint names\n\nA plugin prompt block names more than one command, and a member allowlist bridges\nplugin tools one at a time, so a session can have part of a plugin''s commands.\nThe MCP block names `mcp` and `mcp_manager`; the Graphify orientation names\n`graphify_query`, `graphify_path`, `graphify_explain` and `graphify_search`.\nChecking only the first name still pointed at a command the session cannot run.\n\nReplace the per-plugin check with `canRunSeroCommand(pi, surface, ...names)`,\nwhich requires `sero-cli`, no named command as a direct tool, and every named\ncommand on the announced surface. The orientation now checks all four names.\nThe tool-result hint names only `graphify_query`, so it keeps checking that one.\n\nCloses #582","tree":{"sha":"decfc0cae38773833631f975a84757e5c7b6dfe2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/decfc0cae38773833631f975a84757e5c7b6dfe2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/f26f18ab3baa20a58140e632f00037dc966a9ccf","verification":{"payload":"tree decfc0cae38773833631f975a84757e5c7b6dfe2\nparent de189ff4155b13354cb3d7de17abdf8a63418448\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790706332 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790706332 +0100\n\nfix(cli): gate plugin prompt hints on the session''s CLI surface (#590)\n\n* fix(cli): gate plugin prompt hints on the session''s CLI surface\n\nThe MCP and Graphify plugins add their prompt hint when `sero-cli` is active\nand their tool is not a direct tool. A subagent allowlist that names `sero-cli`\nbut not the plugin tools hits that shape while its registry hides the command,\nso the model sees a hint for a command that answers \"unknown command\". The\nplugins cannot tell the two cases apart from `getActiveTools`/`getAllTools`.\n\nThe host knows the session''s CLI registry, so it now announces the command list\nthe session can run on `session_start`, and the plugins gate their hint on it.\nA session kind that does not announce keeps the previous optimistic behaviour.\n\n- Add `SESSION_CLI_SURFACE_EVENT` and `trackSessionCliSurface` to\n  `@sero-ai/common` (0.20.2).\n- Add `announceSessionCliSurface` and emit it from the chat/member and subagent\n  extension factories.\n- Check the announced surface in the MCP and Graphify plugins.\n\nCloses #582\n\n* fix(cli): check every command a plugin hint names\n\nA plugin prompt block names more than one command, and a member allowlist bridges\nplugin tools one at a time, so a session can have part of a plugin''s commands.\nThe MCP block names `mcp` and `mcp_manager`; the Graphify orientation names\n`graphify_query`, `graphify_path`, `graphify_explain` and `graphify_search`.\nChecking only the first name still pointed at a command the session cannot run.\n\nReplace the per-plugin check with `canRunSeroCommand(pi, surface, ...names)`,\nwhich requires `sero-cli`, no named command as a direct tool, and every named\ncommand on the announced surface. The orientation now checks all four names.\nThe tool-result hint names only `graphify_query`, so it keeps checking that one.\n\nCloses #582","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvAKcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAL30QAEig3eefftMhT49Y87A2C3U+\nWHZTg0bPxbq0O+RDBJr+0xHvzyuTH93sklJpHnYoxT3EzfgaPNYv95a/AWnS+7Cj\noawazXSsEMo7ND1zk49EkjBRL5f2jV+BGuJepW+LRyhu2tnsqIwdXQ6WumiSR+Ad\nx+sw5dtQBGqLjI1THn6DcS553PdgWvHRlY8g5Ytboj04vK+TyjQFE2JYndA6KJps\nzlGD1v1fu4bF9p71GpO2vqez7jAgHDWDyqMW8IDH5pIjRvBXZoHDlRTa6wxL1Kuu\nR7bm861jg0MVnjUcajaJDY44VgWtNIPd3wC05TcVX+ADE0xMJN+lK2SAuNNV4lIw\nP0AeQ3nVwIoDsR/w2hAA1+fJLDp614O/I20TlIEulGwSQtshzERm4eKvfj9zdlAb\n6waLVaxgPHxj8TZVEuwuGziLBTBcA5wWqWLRW9SPszPtIrtpGq8HyeOoHe8z9sqH\n19sfmLLLw/tmbmH6X9YP/ad961MMKcKujS2xskoatj+Wih17Aez08Zqz6cX6uoQ8\niWwgIYqVkZ/83L5RVh4PBVz+BFa0KSUb/2DGEI70Cg2iZPNbLS5AnnNhG16XBdt2\nqZUQu78SXAwvjHvKmMwE977glf2+FAZRBfg9WtZiEYWI8D+aVmuqiy7lzORly0TY\nORCpeeqfF6G4hoxmqDuY\n=bOSo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T18:25:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/f26f18ab3baa20a58140e632f00037dc966a9ccf","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGYyNmYxOGFiM2JhYTIwYTU4MTQwZTYzMmYwMDAzN2RjOTY2YTljY2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/de189ff4155b13354cb3d7de17abdf8a63418448","sha":"de189ff4155b13354cb3d7de17abdf8a63418448","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/de189ff4155b13354cb3d7de17abdf8a63418448"}],"sha":"f26f18ab3baa20a58140e632f00037dc966a9ccf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/f26f18ab3baa20a58140e632f00037dc966a9ccf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/de189ff4155b13354cb3d7de17abdf8a63418448/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T17:42:10Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T17:42:10Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"test(orchestrator): de-flake the fs adapter debounce test\n\nThe batching test gave the fs adapter a 50ms window for two writes. On\nmacOS the filesystem events can arrive ~51ms apart under CPU load, so the\nsecond path landed in the next window and the assertion read only a.txt.\n\nWait for the real OS events the watcher receives, then close the debounce\nwindow on a fake clock, matching the state-watcher test pattern. This also\nremoves two 250ms real sleeps from the suite.","tree":{"sha":"e1728d2b94978a32e86e25150d2b7a5afac3acb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/e1728d2b94978a32e86e25150d2b7a5afac3acb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/de189ff4155b13354cb3d7de17abdf8a63418448","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/de189ff4155b13354cb3d7de17abdf8a63418448","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGRlMTg5ZmY0MTU1YjEzMzU0Y2IzZDdkZTE3YWJkZjhhNjM0MTg0NDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/68078ec3eb40ab62f8ecfd4b47fd847c39bd796f","sha":"68078ec3eb40ab62f8ecfd4b47fd847c39bd796f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/68078ec3eb40ab62f8ecfd4b47fd847c39bd796f"}],"sha":"de189ff4155b13354cb3d7de17abdf8a63418448","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/de189ff4155b13354cb3d7de17abdf8a63418448"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/68078ec3eb40ab62f8ecfd4b47fd847c39bd796f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T17:08:27Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T17:08:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: share questionnaire status and validate bridged CLI args (#589)\n\n* refactor: share questionnaire status and validate bridged CLI args\n\nFollow-ups from the PR 588 review that the re-review did not cover:\n\n- schema-bridge: check bridged tool params against the tool''s TypeBox\n  schema before execute, so every bridged tool rejects malformed CLI\n  JSON instead of each tool hand-rolling its own Value.Check.\n- Move the tool result extraction into core/tool-result.ts to keep\n  schema-bridge.ts under the 500 LOC limit.\n- questionnaire-flow: add getQuestionStatus/getQuestionStatuses and use\n  one status derivation in QuestionnaireForm, QuestionnaireReviewStep\n  and the extension''s skipped-question report.\n- Memoise the per-question status map in QuestionnaireForm.\n- Add NonDismissibleDialog and use it for the four onboarding dialogs.\n\n* fix(cli): validate bridged arguments the way Pi does\n\nReview follow-ups on PR 589:\n\n- bridgeTool now runs the tool''s prepareArguments shim and then Pi''s\n  validateToolArguments, so CLI calls reach execute with the same\n  prepared, converted arguments as agent calls. A bare Value.Check\n  rejected values Pi accepts, such as a stringified boolean inside an\n  array argument, and gave no field path on failure.\n- getSkippedQuestions keeps the shallow \"has any answer\" rule. The Pi\n  TUI never renders sub-questions, so the deep rule reported answered\n  TUI questions as \"skipped by user\". The TUI and the report now agree.\n- Drop the unused groupAnswersByQuestionId / NO_SKIPPED_QUESTIONS.\n- QuestionnaireStepTabs takes allAnswered as a prop instead of\n  recomputing it.\n- Tests: prove nested JSON coercion matches agent calls, and drop the\n  pinned error copy.","tree":{"sha":"2093976a8d13f0900ef787cb463741536ca74a7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/2093976a8d13f0900ef787cb463741536ca74a7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/68078ec3eb40ab62f8ecfd4b47fd847c39bd796f","verification":{"payload":"tree 2093976a8d13f0900ef787cb463741536ca74a7b\nparent 437090163bfb66f6aef18ddd9dfff8ca16e4fd49\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790701707 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790701707 +0100\n\nrefactor: share questionnaire status and validate bridged CLI args (#589)\n\n* refactor: share questionnaire status and validate bridged CLI args\n\nFollow-ups from the PR 588 review that the re-review did not cover:\n\n- schema-bridge: check bridged tool params against the tool''s TypeBox\n  schema before execute, so every bridged tool rejects malformed CLI\n  JSON instead of each tool hand-rolling its own Value.Check.\n- Move the tool result extraction into core/tool-result.ts to keep\n  schema-bridge.ts under the 500 LOC limit.\n- questionnaire-flow: add getQuestionStatus/getQuestionStatuses and use\n  one status derivation in QuestionnaireForm, QuestionnaireReviewStep\n  and the extension''s skipped-question report.\n- Memoise the per-question status map in QuestionnaireForm.\n- Add NonDismissibleDialog and use it for the four onboarding dialogs.\n\n* fix(cli): validate bridged arguments the way Pi does\n\nReview follow-ups on PR 589:\n\n- bridgeTool now runs the tool''s prepareArguments shim and then Pi''s\n  validateToolArguments, so CLI calls reach execute with the same\n  prepared, converted arguments as agent calls. A bare Value.Check\n  rejected values Pi accepts, such as a stringified boolean inside an\n  array argument, and gave no field path on failure.\n- getSkippedQuestions keeps the shallow \"has any answer\" rule. The Pi\n  TUI never renders sub-questions, so the deep rule reported answered\n  TUI questions as \"skipped by user\". The TUI and the report now agree.\n- Drop the unused groupAnswersByQuestionId / NO_SKIPPED_QUESTIONS.\n- QuestionnaireStepTabs takes allAnswered as a prop instead of\n  recomputing it.\n- Tests: prove nested JSON coercion matches agent calls, and drop the\n  pinned error copy.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu/CLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyzEQAIt