c8d2dd381e29a18d93379d2c5270d07acf68c678"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/42401970d4e853f8be6973a5574cd9397dccb4f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:09:25Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:09:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(session-tools): rationalise the tools and prompt each session kind starts with (#584)\n\n* docs(openspec): add rationalise-session-tools change\n\nPlan to cut chat start-up context and make every tool a session is\nshown callable in that session, across all agent session kinds.\nFollows the tool inventory for #574.\n\n* docs(openspec): scope tools by session kind in rationalise-session-tools\n\nGoals and Rooms control become chat-only and room becomes member-only,\ndeclared per tool in the plugin manifest and enforced by the host.\nMembers now get the plugin tools their approval grants.\n\n* feat(session-tools): rationalise the tools and prompt each session kind starts with\n\nEvery session was shown tools and prompt text it did not use, and some it\ncould not call. Chat start-up was 53,834 chars on host, and a default subagent\nwas 92,616.\n\n- Move design_library_assets, design_library_settings and mcp_manager behind\n  sero-cli, and automation_browser in chat. Give each a summary that says what\n  the service is, and cut summaries at a word boundary.\n- Add sero.plugin.toolSessionKinds so a plugin says which session kinds may\n  have a tool. Goals and Rooms control are chat only, room is member only, and\n  the goal terminal tools switch on only while a goal runs.\n- Bridge plugin tools through sero-cli in a subagent that has no allowlist.\n- Add the CLI, memory, MCP and graphify prompt blocks only where sero-cli is\n  reachable. Cron sessions get none of them.\n- Pass the real container state to every prompt, fix the container block''s\n  image facts, trim the host block, and name the Pi docs once.\n- Build member read, write and edit through the workspace runtime, load the\n  package behind every approved plugin tool, and log approved tools that\n  cannot be provided.\n- Remove the taste skill pack, stop loading ~/.agents/skills, add a pi-docs\n  skill, and fix the profile AGENTS.md.\n- Add a stub-model contract spec that calls every tool and command each\n  session kind is shown, on host and container, and a small paid check that a\n  real model picks the moved commands.\n\nChat start-up is now 31,505 chars on host (was 53,834) and a default\nsubagent 26,137 (was 92,616).\n\n* fix(session-tools): fix review round 1 findings\n\n- subagent plugin tools bridge without slash commands\n- goal terminal tools follow goal state\n- runtime and MCP/Graphify hints name only commands the session can run\n- Room member file tools use the container path, matched by real path\n- stale plugin tools drop out of the member tool catalogue\n- user-global skills are filtered through symlinks\n- pi-docs skill reads either docs pointer\n- probe fails errors on valid calls, unread writes and missing results\n\n* fix(orchestrator): keep a goal terminal tool the user disables disabled\n\n* fix(session-tools): keep set-title out of the subagent CLI block and probe it\n\n* fix(session-tools): fix review round 2 findings\n\n- chat-only commands are hidden from sessions that are not chats\n- container block drops shell guidance for a subagent with no bash\n- host subagents get the one shared Pi docs pointer\n- user-global skill filter keeps a folder that ~/.agents/skills links to\n- goal pauses when a terminal tool is turned off mid-goal\n- context overrides no longer bring back tools an extension switched off\n- a member catalogue offers only plugin tools reported in this process\n- probe: per-session write file, valid scripted calls, session info check\n\n* fix(session-tools): fix review round 3 findings\n\n- a member catalogue forgets seen tools when a plugin is replaced\n- the user-global skill filter handles a link anywhere in the folder path\n\n* docs(openspec): tick the size table tasks for rationalise-session-tools\n\n* test(session-tools): cover the log line for an approved member tool that is not provided\n\n* fix(session-tools): let every session read the Pi docs its prompt points at\n\n- host read tool may read (not write) the shared Pi docs\n- an Architect owner and a host Room member get the shared docs pointer\n- the contract probe reads the Pi docs README in every session kind\n\n* test(session-tools): agent spec checks that a real model reads the Pi docs\n\n* docs(openspec): tick task 1.1 and correct the Pi docs check in 10.4\n\n* docs(openspec): tick task 10.4 after the manual pass\n\n* test(workspace): use pids no machine can hand out in the dev server tests","tree":{"sha":"c43d42720960265fa7cf72dda9de0ef298b167cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/c43d42720960265fa7cf72dda9de0ef298b167cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/42401970d4e853f8be6973a5574cd9397dccb4f8","verification":{"payload":"tree c43d42720960265fa7cf72dda9de0ef298b167cc\nparent 3453b7de08c0a8e14ca4ec7304f9b8ec4f3ded19\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790683765 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790683765 +0100\n\nfeat(session-tools): rationalise the tools and prompt each session kind starts with (#584)\n\n* docs(openspec): add rationalise-session-tools change\n\nPlan to cut chat start-up context and make every tool a session is\nshown callable in that session, across all agent session kinds.\nFollows the tool inventory for #574.\n\n* docs(openspec): scope tools by session kind in rationalise-session-tools\n\nGoals and Rooms control become chat-only and room becomes member-only,\ndeclared per tool in the plugin manifest and enforced by the host.\nMembers now get the plugin tools their approval grants.\n\n* feat(session-tools): rationalise the tools and prompt each session kind starts with\n\nEvery session was shown tools and prompt text it did not use, and some it\ncould not call. Chat start-up was 53,834 chars on host, and a default subagent\nwas 92,616.\n\n- Move design_library_assets, design_library_settings and mcp_manager behind\n  sero-cli, and automation_browser in chat. Give each a summary that says what\n  the service is, and cut summaries at a word boundary.\n- Add sero.plugin.toolSessionKinds so a plugin says which session kinds may\n  have a tool. Goals and Rooms control are chat only, room is member only, and\n  the goal terminal tools switch on only while a goal runs.\n- Bridge plugin tools through sero-cli in a subagent that has no allowlist.\n- Add the CLI, memory, MCP and graphify prompt blocks only where sero-cli is\n  reachable. Cron sessions get none of them.\n- Pass the real container state to every prompt, fix the container block''s\n  image facts, trim the host block, and name the Pi docs once.\n- Build member read, write and edit through the workspace runtime, load the\n  package behind every approved plugin tool, and log approved tools that\n  cannot be provided.\n- Remove the taste skill pack, stop loading ~/.agents/skills, add a pi-docs\n  skill, and fix the profile AGENTS.md.\n- Add a stub-model contract spec that calls every tool and command each\n  session kind is shown, on host and container, and a small paid check that a\n  real model picks the moved commands.\n\nChat start-up is now 31,505 chars on host (was 53,834) and a default\nsubagent 26,137 (was 92,616).\n\n* fix(session-tools): fix review round 1 findings\n\n- subagent plugin tools bridge without slash commands\n- goal terminal tools follow goal state\n- runtime and MCP/Graphify hints name only commands the session can run\n- Room member file tools use the container path, matched by real path\n- stale plugin tools drop out of the member tool catalogue\n- user-global skills are filtered through symlinks\n- pi-docs skill reads either docs pointer\n- probe fails errors on valid calls, unread writes and missing results\n\n* fix(orchestrator): keep a goal terminal tool the user disables disabled\n\n* fix(session-tools): keep set-title out of the subagent CLI block and probe it\n\n* fix(session-tools): fix review round 2 findings\n\n- chat-only commands are hidden from sessions that are not chats\n- container block drops shell guidance for a subagent with no bash\n- host subagents get the one shared Pi docs pointer\n- user-global skill filter keeps a folder that ~/.agents/skills links to\n- goal pauses when a terminal tool is turned off mid-goal\n- context overrides no longer bring back tools an extension switched off\n- a member catalogue offers only plugin tools reported in this process\n- probe: per-session write file, valid scripted calls, session info check\n\n* fix(session-tools): fix review round 3 findings\n\n- a member catalogue forgets seen tools when a plugin is replaced\n- the user-global skill filter handles a link anywhere in the folder path\n\n* docs(openspec): tick the size table tasks for rationalise-session-tools\n\n* test(session-tools): cover the log line for an approved member tool that is not provided\n\n* fix(session-tools): let every session read the Pi docs its prompt points at\n\n- host read tool may read (not write) the shared Pi docs\n- an Architect owner and a host Room member get the shared docs pointer\n- the contract probe reads the Pi docs README in every session kind\n\n* test(session-tools): agent spec checks that a real model reads the Pi docs\n\n* docs(openspec): tick task 1.1 and correct the Pi docs check in 10.4\n\n* docs(openspec): tick task 10.4 after the manual pass\n\n* test(workspace): use pids no machine can hand out in the dev server tests","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu6p1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqzkQAAYWkVRY/m0El7+yR+QK3xvJ\nzZBQOmRDfFdS5CoZ/E0dqWWLpYRfyUAfCxXoLpFrTtiptnZV3dgL1WoDdCC1Vzey\ne5/nhbQUE1bHFzg9KKdjte14MRpfad1hqvnDAKeM97vw4/jy5FD0sSwifat4XigP\nMQScMcp8pVdRPreiUZp6Gujwx5u8z4rHbCg9gOqIvBuO4BOI9JW8GP/UEP5a9NN8\n0F/W0IqkYDY29D8Zwvou6tefgpFZcaIi2jI09JKTkwfYfVn3QYNrhzCpbFVNxmor\nOzvrSfGFqnnV8LWUgygwsNPSJ8DBFjpMVSISGpXuRFKaFBah7PFibjW5pgY6jbBa\nmaYta/TJkPGNRaLYaaV4vlTf6non8PRwOTSQRwZDgPc2unQN1GTL4IrjSKDAoz3X\nwW3hEJAR+XyE3mCt1sC41OVhWh2P/dZMIDqxT2qfQ9AgzyUt15bhoDnBuZ2Rukj8\noDMWuEuQtgAiR4c0RewemMDLBVGcsmqb8LLICbSSt8EB3Pe/NKG5ZoyxtlX7dYAb\njm+s24iOhAMxk6czFSsvgamDn0n1Xyxy+8aGK9j4BACYhbow7+r6JjF2Ktj04rDX\ncwR+kI4ZQO05eheL0Vn0oxDDDRxcBlm7qmarSZo6HqdwAoCyuh/l0IN83zo+kttJ\nIo2famloV8ENweizIVD2\n=c1UJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T12:09:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravata