l":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/a6b3a17e9af3b0427cbef814cb67d2dc90360f87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:20:06Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:20:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(memory): rework memory plugin around curated chat memory (#575)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose memory plugin rework\n\nAdd the rework-memory-plugin OpenSpec change: proposal, design,\nmemory and extension-session-events specs, and tasks.\n\nMemory becomes chat-only, curated and measured: strict save rules,\nglobal and workspace scopes, pinned and on-match delivery through a\nshared QMD instance, a per-workspace scratchpad, an evidence-based\nautomatic tidy-up, and a crash-safe conversion of MEMORY.md. Daily\nlogs, transcript copies, consolidation and memory_search are removed.\n\nThe change also fixes session_start and session_shutdown delivery\nto extensions in every desktop session, replacing #570, and audits\nthe handlers that start to run.\n\n* feat(memory): rework memory plugin around curated chat memory\n\nRebuild the memory plugin as chat-only curated memory, per the\nOpenSpec change rework-memory-plugin.\n\n- Save important facts only: corrections, preferences, decisions\n  with a reason, and traps. Each entry has a scope (global or\n  workspace) and a delivery mode (pinned or on-match).\n- Recall on-match entries through a shared QMD index, once per\n  session, as one message after the user message.\n- Add a per-workspace scratchpad and an automatic tidy-up that\n  removes an entry only with checkable evidence.\n- Show one \"Recalled N memories\" line and one \"Saved:\" line in chat.\n- Deliver session_start and session_shutdown to extensions in every\n  desktop session (replaces #570).\n- Keep the cron and MCP runtimes on globalThis, because Pi evaluates\n  extension modules again after a resource reload.\n- Add a save-recall eval, an offline search eval and live metrics.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: daily logs, session transcripts, consolidation, the\nmemory_search tool, the memory blocks toggle and onboarding step 3 are\nremoved. Subagents, Architect, Rooms and app agents get no memory.\n\n* docs(openspec): mark session-open timing task done\n\n* fix(memory): address review round 1 on the memory rework\n\n- Profile reads fail on any error other than a missing file, so an\n  unreadable USER.md is never reported as empty.\n- The tidy-up removes an entry only when its named file is really gone\n  (ENOENT) and its folder resolves inside the workspace.\n- Unpin refuses an older entry that has no search terms; restore\n  refuses a pinned entry when the pinned set is full.\n- The close-entry check runs inside the write queue, so two sessions\n  cannot save the same fact at once.\n- The shared index: release waits for an open in progress, a failed\n  open is tried again, and search stays on keywords while entries are\n  embedded or when embedding reports errors.\n- Closing a chat twice sends one session_shutdown; a reopen waits for\n  the close. Quit closes sessions before the runtimes they use.\n- Web plugin: clearing history in one workspace no longer removes\n  another workspace''s stored results.\n- Eval: stop a timed-out turn before cleanup, count a duplicate save\n  as noise; the metrics report shows read errors.\n\n* fix(memory): show a refused memory save as a failed row; state the quit time limit in the spec\n\n* fix(memory): address review round 2 on the memory rework\n\n- Tidy-up: walk the evidence path from the workspace root with lstat,\n  so a broken link is never evidence that a file is gone.\n- Search stays on keywords while a memory write runs and for a\n  collection whose last index update failed, so a new entry without a\n  vector is not missed.\n- A refused memory save is its own failed row, never hidden in a\n  collapsed tool group.\n- Web plugin: stored results belong to their workspace; a history\n  clear removes only that workspace''s results, and no workspace reads\n  another''s.\n- Test two sessions saving the same fact at the same time.\n\n* docs(evals): document the memory evals and the memory metrics report\n\n* build(deps): use one better-sqlite3 copy for QMD and the web plugin\n\nQMD pins better-sqlite3 12.10.0 and the web plugin needs ^12.11.1, so\nthe install held two copies, and each needs its own Electron build. An\noverride puts the whole repo on 12.11.1, so the rebuild script goes\nback to checking one copy. The lockfile change beyond removing 12.10.0\nis pnpm relabelling peer suffixes after the override change; no other\npackage version changes.\n\n* fix(memory): keep sorted entries searchable\n\n* fix: stabilize memory startup and onboarding\n\nRemove stale bundled extension paths and correct memory help guidance. Keep profile onboarding aligned with converted memory files, surface model errors, and fix the model picker inside dialogs.\n\n* fix(memory): address the fresh review of the memory rework\n\n- subagent: send session_shutdown only after session_start was sent\n- tidy-up: an unsorted entry the model has seen waits for the 7-day run\n- tidy-up: check Git before the model call; invalid output counts as a run\n- tidy-up: scan merged text; a merge frees its own pinned slots\n- git guard: with no git binary, a folder without .git is safe\n- bash guard: allow `git rm --cached`; match the memory folder as a path\n- preflight: accept the recorded MEMORY.md backup, like the plugin\n- sero-cli batch: pass on memoryRefused so a refusal is never hidden\n- recall: never wait for the index before a turn\n- close check: two shared terms on keywords, not one\n- resource reload: apply the saved context overrides again\n\n* refactor(chat): split ChatMessageItem into one component per message type\n\n* test(agent-node): release a test runner when its run starts, not after a fixed timer\n\n* test(web): keep background state writes out of the session lifecycle test","tree":{"sha":"f31770ca2d2e69a2d3aa8932b7c0bdee026a3ea5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/f31770ca2d2e69a2d3aa8932b7c0bdee026a3ea5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/a6b3a17e9af3b0427cbef814cb67d2dc90360f87","verification":{"payload":"tree f31770ca2d2e69a2d3aa8932b7c0bdee026a3ea5\nparent 8e05d5ec32ada3d58732c10b7052118a85a6101d\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790626806 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790626806 +0100\n\nfeat(memory): rework memory plugin around curated chat memory (#575)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose memory plugin rework\n\nAdd the rework-memory-plugin OpenSpec change: proposal, design,\nmemory and extension-session-events specs, and tasks.\n\nMemory becomes chat-only, curated and measured: strict save rules,\nglobal and workspace scopes, pinned and on-match delivery through a\nshared QMD instance, a per-workspace scratchpad, an evidence-based\nautomatic tidy-up, and a crash-safe conversion of MEMORY.md. Daily\nlogs, transcript copies, consolidation and memory_search are removed.\n\nThe change also fixes session_start and session_shutdown delivery\nto extensions in every desktop session, replacing #570, and audits\nthe handlers that start to run.\n\n* feat(memory): rework memory plugin around curated chat memory\n\nRebuild the memory plugin as chat-only curated memory, per the\nOpenSpec change rework-memory-plugin.\n\n- Save important facts only: corrections, preferences, decisions\n  with a reason, and traps. Each entry has a scope (global or\n  workspace) and a delivery mode (pinned or on-match).\n- Recall on-match entries through a shared QMD index, once per\n  session, as one message after the user message.\n- Add a per-workspace scratchpad and an automatic tidy-up that\n  removes an entry only with checkable evidence.\n- Show one \"Recalled N memories\" line and one \"Saved:\" line in chat.\n- Deliver session_start and session_shutdown to extensions in every\n  desktop session (replaces #570).\n- Keep the cron and MCP runtimes on globalThis, because Pi evaluates\n  extension modules again after a resource reload.\n- Add a save-recall eval, an offline search eval and live metrics.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: daily logs, session transcripts, consolidation, the\nmemory_search tool, the memory blocks toggle and onboarding step 3 are\nremoved. Subagents, Architect, Rooms and app agents get no memory.\n\n* docs(openspec): mark session-open timing task done\n\n* fix(memory): address review round 1 on the memory rework\n\n- Profile reads fail on any error other than a missing file, so an\n  unreadable USER.md is never reported as empty.\n- The tidy-up removes an entry only when its named file is really gone\n  (ENOENT) and its folder resolves inside the workspace.\n- Unpin refuses an older entry that has no search terms; restore\n  refuses a pinned entry when the pinned set is full.\n- The close-entry check runs inside the write queue, so two sessions\n  cannot save the same fact at once.\n- The shared index: release waits for an open in progress, a failed\n  open is tried again, and search stays on keywords while entries are\n  embedded or when embedding reports errors.\n- Closing a chat twice sends one session_shutdown; a reopen waits for\n  the close. Quit closes sessions before the runtimes they use.\n- Web plugin: clearing history in one workspace no longer removes\n  another workspace''s stored results.\n- Eval: stop a timed-out turn before cleanup, count a duplicate save\n  as noise; the metrics report shows read errors.\n\n* fix(memory): show a refused memory save as a failed row; state the quit time limit in the spec\n\n* fix(memory): address review round 2 on the memory rework\n\n- Tidy-up: walk the evidence path from the workspace root with lstat,\n  so a broken link is never evidence that a file is gone.\n- Search stays on keywords while a memory write runs and for a\n  collection whose last index update failed, so a new entry without a\n  vector is not missed.\n- A refused memory save is its own failed row, never hidden in a\n  collapsed tool group.\n- Web plugin: stored results belong to their workspace; a history\n  clear removes only that workspace''s results, and no workspace reads\n  another''s.\n- Test two sessions saving the same fact at the same time.\n\n* docs(evals): document the memory evals and the memory metrics report\n\n* build(deps): use one better-sqlite3 copy for QMD and the web plugin\n\nQMD pins better-sqlite3 12.10.0 and the web plugin needs ^12.11.1, so\nthe install held two copies, and each needs its own Electron build. An\noverride puts the whole repo on 12.11.1, so the rebuild script goes\nback to checking one copy. The lockfile change beyond removing 12.10.0\nis pnpm relabelling peer suffixes after the override change; no other\npackage version changes.\n\n* fix(memory): keep sorted entries searchable\n\n* fix: stabilize memory startup and onboarding\n\nRemove stale bundled extension paths and correct memory help guidance. Keep profile onboarding aligned with converted memory files, surface model errors, and fix the model picker inside dialogs.\n\n* fix(memory): address the fresh review of the memory rework\n\n- subagent: send session_shutdown only after session_start was sent\n- tidy-up: an unsorted entry the model has seen waits for the 7-day run\n- tidy-up: check Git before the model call; invalid output counts as a run\n- tidy-up: scan merged text; a merge frees its own pinned slots\n- git guard: with no git binary, a folder without .git is safe\n- bash guard: allow `git rm --cached`; match the memory folder as a path\n- preflight: accept the recorded MEMORY.md backup, like the plugin\n- sero-cli batch: pass on memoryRefused so a refusal is never hidden\n- recall: never wait for the index before a turn\n- close check: two shared terms on keywords, not one\n- resource reload: apply the saved context overrides again\n\n* refactor(chat): split ChatMessageItem into one component per message type\n\n* test(agent-node): release a test runner when its run starts, not after a fixed timer\n\n* test(web): keep background state writes out of the session lifecycle test","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqusv2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7IAQADItkS27UwueaAssWt/7zmN+\nWNf8E3Yhxo4OmIK7Lx9wBpXYfgk8TdnYl46GgbwikYdmhCGimFGXzRKRCtcD9puQ\nOuE0BenUYYzSX4EQCvbGbm6jVomUgkcM4SiqizO2Md5uMn9BM9I3fINsUo9MOkJz\nzdFFQ7f4K+Z6CwMzHWJ7lEKFR+GG0Kve+ID2nnTl2sdR2828eHtNtn47Z9BKm3Vh\nr9b7Zu3SMfPZPawKS0mBKE+SiJjeTublCFVJKkoXAT6j6UQEzb5Hor08Yg3BGg9D\nQmUQka5/DaRxjSwQfxSEC2IoehF0K1nhDMkYHbQkhZd1bSJOEw+/qYNwudI5XlB9\nJmBROxU+tFX6tt9lcYgagnMVBMqdc3oAtc7L47dKzAt5TGPoiCcnoViL09doiiK/\nu+kW+yIXRDqK8BVukxahe0gjbv6lWfdNCtllwTSwOHV2EbZERVI1n5SAmT2JE2i3\nyzJXd1ZfbhbyXYdHSxXzOyv1GzVs9O6UBa+/LVNrSSVIEQpYC5PQPMe7K7avDexX\ncygfLSYVx5cRy3y309JGAvwBsQ4NqP9sRUASQ9ovIUGn41SjTGs5EZHgL40wf4TC\nasdBS+nq6K55+B/7qgUgyzg5U7XS348S7SCOuaI8a6kzuIadL+F3yqpPh5oe+Gy1\nsWKH39/eP8dMwZJDnDzf\n=EPlW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T20:20