"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/2be2c494e88660578bdb94d5039fe7b0e163bf22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:55:07Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:55:07Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"fix(desktop): stop logging gh reads for workspaces without GitHub\n\nThe Agent Board lists issues and PRs for every workspace. A workspace\nthat is not a git repo, or has no GitHub remote, has none, but each\nread logged a warning plus a blank line. Those two normal states now\nlog nothing; a missing gh, missing auth and other failures still log.","tree":{"sha":"8e00ae58b9aa7a5dcd61ced0a99ddd3cdc653421","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/8e00ae58b9aa7a5dcd61ced0a99ddd3cdc653421"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/2be2c494e88660578bdb94d5039fe7b0e163bf22","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/2be2c494e88660578bdb94d5039fe7b0e163bf22","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDJiZTJjNDk0ZTg4NjYwNTc4YmRiOTRkNTAzOWZlN2IwZTE2M2JmMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/af92f63c0c8a77fa3822245d345a8943475daa13","sha":"af92f63c0c8a77fa3822245d345a8943475daa13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/af92f63c0c8a77fa3822245d345a8943475daa13"}],"sha":"2be2c494e88660578bdb94d5039fe7b0e163bf22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/2be2c494e88660578bdb94d5039fe7b0e163bf22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/af92f63c0c8a77fa3822245d345a8943475daa13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:41:21Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:41:21Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"fix(desktop): log container cleanup failures once per cause\n\nWhen the container service is down, every pending deletion failed and\nlogged a warning with a full stack trace, and startup reconciliation\nran a second pass that repeated every failure. With 72 pending\ndeletions this was about 90% of sero-electron.log.\n\nFailed deletions now log one line per provider and cause, without a\nstack. Reconciliation skips the second pass when it found no new\norphans. Every pending deletion is still tried and kept for retry.","tree":{"sha":"681c82ee40db455ff570d9770aa43c1b3e1df394","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/681c82ee40db455ff570d9770aa43c1b3e1df394"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/af92f63c0c8a77fa3822245d345a8943475daa13","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/af92f63c0c8a77fa3822245d345a8943475daa13","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGFmOTJmNjNjMGM4YTc3ZmEzODIyMjQ1ZDM0NWE4OTQzNDc1ZGFhMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/47df47ef1d1efda024bba40c2f978837147518fd","sha":"47df47ef1d1efda024bba40c2f978837147518fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/47df47ef1d1efda024bba40c2f978837147518fd"}],"sha":"af92f63c0c8a77fa3822245d345a8943475daa13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/af92f63c0c8a77fa3822245d345a8943475daa13"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/47df47ef1d1efda024bba40c2f978837147518fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:32:18Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:32:18Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"fix(desktop): stop nesting the attention button inside the workspace row\n\nThe workspace row is a <button>, and the Architect attention icon inside\nit was also a <button>. HTML forbids that, and React reported it. The\nicon is now a span with role=button, like the row''s other controls, and\nstill opens the project on click, Enter or Space.","tree":{"sha":"7be21e04013d63f703e6fc0811ffaa4fe4d320bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/7be21e04013d63f703e6fc0811ffaa4fe4d320bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/47df47ef1d1efda024bba40c2f978837147518fd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/47df47ef1d1efda024bba40c2f978837147518fd","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDQ3ZGY0N2VmMWQxZWZkYTAyNGJiYTQwYzJmOTc4ODM3MTQ3NTE4ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/33f58680c33b503d186625b574246a9a2708ab16","sha":"33f58680c33b503d186625b574246a9a2708ab16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/33f58680c33b503d186625b574246a9a2708ab16"}],"sha":"47df47ef1d1efda024bba40c2f978837147518fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/47df47ef1d1efda024bba40c2f978837147518fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/33f58680c33b503d186625b574246a9a2708ab16/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:53:40Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:53:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): repair failing E2E and release checks (#569)\n\n- Give the contract E2E launcher a host artifacts root. Since #562 the main\n  process refuses the real ~/.sero-ui under NODE_ENV=test, so Electron exited\n  before its first window.\n- Update two session contract checks to the windowed agent.open result\n  ({ messages, olderCursor }) introduced by #501.\n- Retry temp home removal so Windows can release Chromium file locks.\n- Set the Node heap limit in the E2E Workflow, as the contract and release\n  workflows already do.\n- Run test:packaging with `--mode packaging` instead of an inline variable\n  assignment, which cmd.exe cannot run.\n\nRefs #568","tree":{"sha":"846a9e58619b0957feaad3aaa0ffcc702a15de39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/846a9e58619b0957feaad3aaa0ffcc702a15de39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/33f58680c33b503d186625b574246a9a2708ab16","verification":{"payload":"tree 846a9e58619b0957feaad3aaa0ffcc702a15de39\nparent 8721edc9646840389ca9e51460f1cb58e1cd2ded\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790452420 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790452420 +0100\n\nfix(ci): repair failing E2E and release checks (#569)\n\n- Give the contract E2E launcher a host artifacts root. Since #562 the main\n  process refuses the real ~/.sero-ui under NODE_ENV=test, so Electron exited\n  before its first window.\n- Update two session contract checks to the windowed agent.open result\n  ({ messages, olderCursor }) introduced by #501.\n- Retry temp home removal so Windows can release Chromium file locks.\n- Set the Node heap limit in the E2E Workflow, as the contract and release\n  workflows already do.\n- Run test:packaging with `--mode packaging` instead of an inline variable\n  assignment, which cmd.exe cannot run.\n\nRefs #568","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquCLECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+n4QAKyVwwgxICAJr2GYcF09t7K1\n3dFe7KpnXR/8/52MsYz3WL5AjhxlRwY+2D7bzZg3PWeiTFjR27SrJq1k9giNf3lR\ntYWG14up841wOpXJwT//Wh2+zHvVcL7ol/OGjso7GTUzb/4PL6YRlVLu68PaqT3n\nzbSma0g3t2rDtC1Fv9yW7DJ2n+zblXp7c1VqhqUUtc59jIrMmN9svF05fk49u8I+\nQ/yBhGkfBDcXCAfGu+XDngGoCgaKylCn057UPnDL9GjpPwNZbSzLbjtRXlsqomWM\n3AcdnX+IwJ9UdxhZlc0B2As7rUEeY0JTawzBqfix5RfZGLI8yhau/JD1QqM0JkH7\nUnIBu+Y5E8++gxdstpqFwB6EYhp1ijhhZ4WpMSL2Fb15sQx+wWRPJ5aA3ketZlo3\nEME5v+wDTfVsRVKDyPhQ3oWXOPlfqKaCJNgXa5Ozu2xwC0UaCsFOs6UNG/Gd3uIk\nGIvh9on8NZeF+zAbb2Mqe2NMwAV9VFnEgVgIwu8uiL/NwSpC+lA0X5QNqMEUGlfS\nWnOPNmL+zBHrvfs7BFtiugYQYKIDxI4nE9Uw46dRkbqDujmQlVO5jItA8m2mY9FE\n8P9O88S5mKd7LHZp36CltpzlojPqlvpkYqHsRcD2Bv2D9WBFPw6dprehzPLp0OKN\nzMGkX6tQkxWEeNZAxe98\n=5J9A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T19:53:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://a