te/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/9a73d6f03a6796497861eca5a4aa024915decc87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:21:23Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:21:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mcp): support MCP 2026-07-28 with Apps, Tasks and Skills (#563)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose support-mcp-2026-07-28 change for issue #359\n\nAdd the OpenSpec change for MCP 2026-07-28, MCP Apps, Tasks and\nSkills over MCP: proposal, seven capability specs, design and a\ntask list that lands in four slices.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(openspec): add prototype step and plugin rules to MCP change\n\nAdd a first task group that builds a styleguide prototype for the new\nUI and gates production UI tasks on its approval. Link the sero-plugin\nand sero-prototype skills. Move inline MCP Apps to a neutral\nui.chat.tool-result extension point and the CLI timeout exemption to a\ncli.interactive flag, so the host has no MCP-specific code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(styleguide): add MCP 2026-07-28 review prototype\n\nAdd an interactive prototype for issue 359 in the styleguide. It shows\nMCP apps in a tool result, server input requests over two rounds,\ntasks, remote skill approval, and the new MCP app protocol, Tasks and\nRemote skills views. Link it from the prototype archive.\n\nUpdate the OpenSpec change: fix the tool-call helper path, and add task\n4.7 so that the User Feedback questionnaire shows who asks, as the\nelicitation spec requires.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* refactor(mcp): split server edits and proxy formatting out of runtime files\n\nMove the upsert, remove and enable handlers from mcp-runtime.ts into\nruntime-servers.ts, and move the proxy result formatting and argument\nparsing from runtime-proxy.ts into runtime-proxy-format.ts. Behavior\ndoes not change. Both files now have room for the MCP 2026-07-28 work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* refactor(styleguide): flatten the MCP 2026-07-28 prototype\n\nRemove nested cards, badges for default states, repeated labels and\nlong descriptions. The MCP app now shows Servers, Tasks and Remote\nskills as plain sections with divided rows. Review notes move from the\nproduct view into the review panel.\n\nRecord the UI rules in design D10 so that production UI follows them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* build(mcp): move the MCP plugin to the v2 SDK packages\n\nRun the v1-to-v2 codemod. Replace @modelcontextprotocol/sdk with\n@modelcontextprotocol/client, upgrade @modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps\nto 2.0.1, and add the v2 server and node packages as dev dependencies\nfor the e2e fixture.\n\nThe fixture now serves both protocol eras over stdio through\nserveStdio, and only the 2025 handshake with --legacy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* style(styleguide): use one level of cards in the MCP prototype\n\nPut each MCP app panel (Tasks, Remote skills, Servers) in one card with\na header and count. Rows inside the card use dividers, status dots,\ncolored status badges and icon tiles, but no nested cards.\n\nCorrect the D10 UI rule: cards are allowed one level deep.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* style(styleguide): allow one nested card level in the MCP prototype\n\nShow the protocol details of an opened server in an inner card inside\nthe Servers card. Update the D10 UI rule: a card may hold cards, but\nthose inner cards hold no more cards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* refactor(mcp): use v2 list aggregation and drop v1 type casts\n\nCall listTools() and listResources() without a cursor so that the v2\nclient walks every page and fills its response cache. Remove the casts\non callTool() and on resource contents that the v2 types make\nunnecessary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): negotiate the protocol era through one client factory\n\nAdd createMcpClient() and use it for server connections and the OAuth\ncoordinator. Every client now probes with server/discover and falls\nback to the 2025 initialize handshake. Extension capabilities for MCP\nApps, Tasks and Skills are declared only when their host feature flag\nis on; all flags stay off until their host paths are ready. Sero never\ndeclares sampling or roots.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(openspec): record MCP prototype approval and defaults\n\nRecord that the user approved the MCP 2026-07-28 prototype and its\ndefaults: remote skills start off, headless sessions decline server\ninput, and task results arrive without a new agent turn. Mark task 1.5\ndone and remove the task delivery question from the open questions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): record the negotiated protocol and remember legacy servers\n\nRecord the era, protocol version, server extensions, server version and\ndeprecated-transport flag on each connection. Save a legacy verdict for\neach server and config hash in era-verdicts.json, and connect with a\nlegacy prior next time so that stdio servers are not probed on every\nconnect. A manual reconnect or a config change drops the verdict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(mcp): fall back to SSE only when Streamable HTTP is missing\n\nUse the deprecated SSE transport only when the Streamable HTTP endpoint\nanswers 404 or 405, or when an Agent Plugin asks for SSE. A server\nerror no longer hides behind an SSE retry. The SSE transport now gets\nthe OAuth provider, and the connection is marked as deprecated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): report the failed step, protocol and cache per server\n\nMap connect errors to a failure phase (discovery, legacy fallback,\nauthorization or extension). A 401 or 403 is an authorization failure\nand never selects the legacy era. Add the negotiated protocol, the\nfailure phase and the metadata cache state to each server snapshot.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): show protocol, extensions and failed step in the MCP app\n\nAdd a Protocol card to the server details with the negotiated revision,\nextensions, transport and metadata cache state, and notices for a\ndeprecated SSE transport and for the failed step. The server row shows\nthe revision and problem badges, and no longer shows badges for the\ndefault enabled and no-auth states.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): serve the e2e fixture over stdio and HTTP in both eras\n\nSplit the fixture into one server factory, a stdio entry (both eras, or\nonly the 2025 handshake with --legacy) and a Streamable HTTP entry\nbuilt with createMcpHandler. New server manager tests connect to each\nmode and check the negotiated era.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): cancel one MCP tool call without stopping the others\n\nPass the abort signal from the mcp tool and from the desktop CLI bridge\nthrough the runtime to client.callTool(), so that stopping a call\ncancels only that request. Add tests on a modern HTTP server for the\nrouting headers, the per-request _meta envelope, no session header, and\nper-request cancellation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document protocol negotiation and SSE deprecation\n\nDescribe how Sero picks the 2026-07-28 or 2025 protocol, the saved\nlegacy verdict, the request envelope and headers, the Protocol card on\nthe server view, and the SSE fallback rules. Add a Protocol versions\nsection to the MCP guide. Label the HTTP transport option as Streamable\nHTTP in the server form.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(openspec): record the MCP contract e2e result\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): map MCP input forms to the Sero questionnaire\n\nConvert an MCP form request to questionnaire questions (enum, titled\nenum, multi-select, boolean, string, number and integer), with a\nDecline option on the first question and server text kept as plain\ntext. Convert the answers back with type and constraint checks. A bad\nvalue is asked again once; a form with an unsupported field is declined\nwithout being shown.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): answer server input requests through the question UI\n\nRegister one elicitation/create handler on every server client. It\nanswers legacy elicitation/create requests and the input rounds of\nmodern input_required results (up to 10 rounds) with the Sero\nquestionnaire, labelled with the server and tool. The call context\ncomes from AsyncLocalStorage, with the newest call in flight as the\nfallback for legacy requests. With no question UI (headless or the\nplain Pi CLI) Sero declines at once. An aborted call cancels the open\nquestion. Declined requests post a short notice in the calling chat.\n\nURL-mode requests are declined for now, and only form elicitation is\ndeclared, until the open-page flow is decided.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): let a server ask the user to open a web page\n\nAdd an optional openUrl field to user-feedback question options in\n@sero-ai/common (0.18.1 -> 0.19.0). When the user picks such an option,\nthe host question card opens the URL through its checked external-link\npath and then sends the answer.\n\nThe MCP plugin uses it for URL-mode input requests: one chat question\nwith the full URL, Decline as the safe default, and Open page. Only\nhttp and https URLs are offered; other requests are declined with a\nnotice. Sero now declares URL elicitation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(mcp): keep MCP work moving while a call waits for the user\n\nRun tool calls and resource reads outside the runtime queue. Only\ntheir connection and state work (sync, checks, connect, and the\ncleanup after an authorization failure) stays in the queue, so a\nserver question during a call no longer blocks other MCP actions.\nResource reads also pass the stop signal and the chat notice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(cli): let a bridged tool declare that it waits for the user\n\nAdd an optional interactive flag to a tool''s cli metadata. bridgeTool()\ntreats such a tool like the built-in interactive tools and applies no\nper-command timeout. The MCP tool sets it, because a call can wait for\nthe user to answer a server question. The host does not name any\nplugin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): cover a two-round server input request end to end\n\nAdd a create_contact tool to the e2e MCP fixture that asks for input\nover two input_required rounds, and a contract case that answers both\nrounds through the host question channel and checks the source label\nand the Decline option.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(user-feedback): show who asks a questionnaire\n\nShow the question''s context source under the Questionnaire title, so\nthat a user sees which server and tool asked. Questions without a\nsource look as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document server input requests\n\nDescribe what the user sees when a server asks for input, how Decline\nand Cancel differ, the re-ask after a bad value, page requests, and\nthe headless decline. Add the implementation rules to the plugin\nREADME.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): allow more tools in the e2e fixture\n\nThe fixture now also serves create_contact, so the era tests check that\necho is listed instead of an exact tool list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): partition cached server data by account\n\nResolve a principal ID for each connection: anon without auth, a\nSHA-256 hash for a bearer token (the token is never stored), and a\nrandom ID for an OAuth authorization, stored with its tokens. A new\nsign-in creates a new ID, a token refresh keeps it, and sign-out\nremoves it. Pass the ID to the client as its cache partition and record\nit on the connection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): honor server cache hints in the metadata cache\n\nMove metadata-cache.json to version 2. Each entry records the account\nthat listed it, the server''s cacheScope and an expiry from its ttlMs.\nA private entry from another account is not shown, an expired entry is\nshown as stale, and a version 1 file is read as stale. Servers are\nwritten in sorted order. The Protocol card shows until when the cache\nis fresh.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* refactor(mcp): move connection helpers out of the server manager\n\nMove the environment, request, listing and protocol helpers into\nconnection-helpers.ts so that server-manager.ts keeps room for the\nlist-changed work. Behavior does not change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): refresh cached inventory when a server reports a change\n\nRegister tool and resource list-changed handlers on every client. The\nclient lists again, the connection takes the new items, and the runtime\nwrites the metadata cache entry and the snapshot in its queue. Sign-out\nnow removes the server''s private cache entry. The e2e fixture gets a\nreveal_tool that makes the server report a changed tool list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): list a server again when its cached inventory expires\n\nAdd refreshInventory() to the server manager. While the server''s TTL\nholds, the client serves the lists from its response cache and sends no\nrequest. The proxy calls it before it returns the tools or resources of\na connected server whose cache entry has expired.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document the metadata cache and its isolation\n\nDescribe the version 2 metadata cache: the partition keys (server,\nconfig hash, principal, scope), TTL handling, refresh, removal rules\nand bearer token hashing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): keep OAuth tokens and client data as the SDK gives them\n\nStore tokens and client information field for field, so that the\nissuer stamp of the v2 SDK is kept and returned unchanged. Only\nexpires_in becomes an absolute expiry. Add discovery state storage in\ndiscovery.json, and handle the verifier and discovery invalidation\nscopes. Files saved before the upgrade still load.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(mcp): check the OAuth callback issuer before the code exchange\n\nCheck the callback state first, then pass the full callback query to\nfinishAuth() so that the SDK compares iss with the expected issuer\nbefore it exchanges the code. On an issuer mismatch Sero shows a fixed\nmessage and never the callback text; for an error callback it shows\nonly a known RFC 6749 error code.\n\nAlso fix the provider state(): the SDK asks it for the state of each\nsign-in, but it only read a saved state that nothing wrote, so every\nsign-in failed with \"No OAuth state saved\". It now creates the state\nand saves it for the callback check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): prepare client metadata documents and check registration\n\nAdd the CLIENT_METADATA_URL constant, unset until Sero publishes a\nClient ID Metadata Document, and give it to the SDK. Until then Sero\nuses Dynamic Client Registration. Tests check that the registration is\nsent as a native app with the loopback redirect, and that a configured\nclient ID skips registration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): keep credentials away from a changed authorization server\n\nAfter a full sign-in, the resource metadata names another authorization\nserver. The test checks that the saved tokens carry the issuer stamp,\nthat no token or registration request reaches the new server, and that\nthe server status becomes needs-auth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document OAuth issuer checks and client registration\n\nDescribe the callback state and iss checks, issuer-stamped storage,\ndiscovery state, the behavior after an authorization server change,\ntoken endpoint TLS, scope step-up and the client registration order.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(openspec): record the MCP protocol slice check\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): write the e2e MCP fixture in TypeScript\n\nMerge the three .mjs fixture files into one server.mts that Node runs\nwith type stripping. Flags select the mode: stdio by default, --legacy\nfor the 2025 handshake only, and --http for Streamable HTTP.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): serve MCP app viewers from one server with a session map\n\nThe viewer now runs one loopback server for all app sessions. Each\nsession has a random token. Above eight sessions, the oldest closes.\nclose_viewer takes the viewer ID, so one pane or chat result can close\nits own session without closing others.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): host MCP apps through the official AppBridge\n\nReplace the hand-written postMessage bridge with a bundled shell that\nuses AppBridge and PostMessageTransport from ext-apps. The plugin''s\nVite build writes it to dist/ui/viewer-shell.js, and the viewer server\nserves it. The viewer page now needs no inline script. The shell sends\nthe tool input and result, and declares only the capabilities that\nthe viewer server implements.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): let an app call only the app tools of its own server\n\nThe viewer proxy lists and calls only tools of the owning server that\nare visible to apps and not in excludeTools. A blocked call returns an\nerror result and sends no request to the server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): isolate MCP apps with a default-deny CSP and link checks\n\nAn app without declared domains gets no network access. Declared\ndomains follow the MCP Apps CSP fields and must be web origins. The\napp gets no frame permissions for now. A link opens only after the\nuser picks Open page in the same question as URL-mode requests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): deliver app messages to the chat that shows the app\n\nEach session registers its sendMessage with the MCP runtime. An app\nopened for a chat session sends ui/message as a labeled follow-up that\nstarts a turn, and ui/update-model-context as hidden context for the\nnext turn. A viewer outside a chat does not declare these capabilities.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(desktop): add the ui.chat.tool-result extension point\n\nA tool result can name a plugin component with a seroToolResultView\nmarker in its details. The contribution type, the marker and the\ncomponent props live in @sero-ai/common. Electron validates the point,\nand FederatedContributionMount can pass props to a component.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(desktop): show plugin tool-result views in tool-call details\n\nThe tool-call details mount the ui.chat.tool-result component that a\nfinished result names, between the input and the output. A single call\nor a row with such a view starts open. When nothing matches or the\ncomponent fails, only the normal result shows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): show MCP apps inline in chat tool results\n\ncall_tool adds the seroToolResultView marker and details.mcpApp for a\ntool with an MCP app. The result is kept up to 256 KB. The plugin\ncontributes McpToolResultApp to ui.chat.tool-result. It opens a new\nviewer for the stored call on mount, fits the frame to the page, and\ncloses the viewer on unmount. When the app cannot load, it shows one\nline with the reason.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(desktop): keep the own CSP of loopback frames\n\nThe renderer CSP header replaced the policy of every response, also in\nframes from loopback servers. In a production build this blocked the\ninline script of an MCP app and dropped its no-network policy. A frame\nfrom a loopback server now keeps the policy that its server sends. It\nruns on its own origin, so the renderer policy does not protect the\nrenderer there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): hide app-only tools from the model\n\nA tool with visibility [\"app\"] is only for its server''s MCP app. The\nmodel inventory and cache leave it out, and a model call to it fails\nwithout a request to the server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): cover inline MCP apps end to end\n\nThe fixture server gets a dashboard app with an app-only tool, an app\nthat asks for a domain and a permission, and an app in a format that\nSero cannot show. The new workflow spec stores a real call_tool as a\nmodel sero-cli call and checks the inline app, its own tool call, and\nthe fallback line.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document MCP apps in the chat\n\nThe guide explains inline apps, their isolation, messages, links and\nthe fallback line. The plugin README describes the viewer server, the\nbundled shell, the proxy limits and the stored result details.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* refactor(common): re-export the contribution types in one line\n\nThe index file was at the 500-line limit. app-contributions.ts has only\ntypes, so one export type line replaces the explicit list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): ask before an MCP app gets a permission\n\nAn app that requests the camera, the microphone or the clipboard gets\nit only after the user selects Allow in a question that Sero shows\nwhen the app opens. Deny is the default, and Sero keeps the choice per\napp until the runtime stops. Geolocation is never granted. The chat\nand pane frames pass the granted allow value on to the app frame.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(mcp): ask for the wider scope after insufficient_scope\n\nAfter a 403 insufficient_scope, the SDK asked the runtime provider to\nredirect, but nobody followed it and the scope was lost. The next\nsign-in then connected with the old token and ended at once, so the\ncall kept failing. The runtime provider now saves the requested scope,\nand the next sign-in forces a new authorization for it. A plugin test\ncovers the full step-up path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(openspec): record the scope step-up fix in the design\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): declare MCP Apps support to servers\n\nThe host path for MCP apps is complete, so the client now declares the\nio.modelcontextprotocol/ui extension. Tasks and Skills stay off until\ntheir host paths are ready.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): add MCP task sessions through ext-tasks\n\nA connection whose server declares the Tasks extension gets an\next-tasks session when the Tasks feature is on. Its endpoint ID comes\nfrom the server name, config hash and principal. Task requests use a\nraw dispatch on the connected transport, because the SDK Client codecs\nreject 2026-07-28 task results, and task replies get a one-second poll\nfloor. The fixture''s HTTP mode now serves MCP Tasks for run_report.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): store MCP task records in tasks.json\n\nSero keeps its own record for each task that it follows: the task\nreference, server, principal, origin session, status, retention and\noutcome. Writes are queued and atomic, and records past their\nretention are pruned.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): follow MCP tasks and deliver their outcome to the chat\n\nWhen a server runs a tool call as a task, call_tool stores the task,\nhands it off, and returns the task ID with the sero mcp task commands.\nA tracker in the runtime settles each task, keeps its record current,\nasks the user for task input through the question channel, retries\nafter a lost connection, and delivers the outcome to the chat that made\nthe call without a new turn. Stored tasks resume when the runtime\nstarts; records of another principal are blocked and expired ones are\nremoved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): resume an MCP task after a runtime restart\n\nThe Tasks feature is now on. A new runtime test starts a task, shuts\nthe runtime down, starts a new runtime from the same state directory,\nand sees the outcome reach the chat session. The raw task dispatch no\nlonger leaves an unhandled rejection when a wait is stopped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): add task commands to the mcp tool and the MCP app actions\n\nThe mcp tool takes task_status, task_wait and task_cancel, and the CLI\ntakes sero mcp task status|wait|cancel <id>. A call passes its chat\nsession and tool call, so a task outcome returns to that chat. The MCP\napp gets list_tasks, cancel_task, dismiss_task and task_result.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): add the Tasks panel to the MCP app\n\nA Tasks button in the MCP app shows the number of active tasks and\nopens one card with a row per task: server and tool, status and age,\nthe reason when a task is disconnected or blocked, and Cancel, Result\nor Dismiss. The list refreshes while the app is open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): finish an MCP task across a Sero restart end to end\n\nThe new workflow spec starts a task on the fixture''s HTTP server,\nrestarts Sero, and sees the completed task and its result in the\nTasks panel. The run showed that tasks resumed only after a chat\nsession started, so the runtime now also resumes them on the first\nMCP action.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document MCP tasks\n\nThe guide explains task results in chat, the task commands, the Tasks\npanel, restart, connection loss, another account and retention. The\nplugin README describes the task session, the raw dispatch, the store,\nthe tracker and the actions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): add a skills client for the MCP Skills extension\n\nThe client sends skills/list, skills/get and resources/directory/read\nonly to a server that declares io.modelcontextprotocol/skills. Small\nlocal schemas describe the results, because no SDK package exists for\nthe extension. The fixture now serves a skill with a supporting file\nand a dynamic skill.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): keep remote skills in a registry with manifest-bound approvals\n\nskills.json holds each remote skill by server label and URI, its full\nentry, a digest of its file list, enablement (off by default), a\nchanged flag and the last refresh time. An approval holds only for the\nmanifest that the user approved. A skill missing from a listing stays\nonly while skills/get finds it. The task store and the registry now\nshare one queued, atomic JSON file helper.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): load remote MCP skills with checks and a code gate\n\nThe loader reads a skill''s SKILL.md only when the model loads it, and\nchecks the limits, size, digest, frontmatter and name first. It tags\nthe content with the server and holds the entry for the session, so\nlater reads accept only files in that entry. sero mcp skill\nload|read|ls reach it, and enabled skills appear in a prompt block\nwith their server label. While a session acts on a remote skill, bash\nand run_code need the user''s approval for that skill''s current\nmanifest, and reads of other servers are refused.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): add the Remote skills panel to the MCP app\n\nA Remote skills button opens one card with the number of skills that\nare on, the last refresh and a refresh action. Each row shows the\nserver and name, the description, the URI, a Changed badge with the\nreason, and a switch. A dynamic skill cannot be turned on. The Tasks\nand Remote skills panels now share one open slot, as in the prototype.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): load a remote skill end to end\n\nThe Skills feature is now on. A new contract case refreshes the\nfixture''s skills, checks that they start off, turns one on, loads it,\nreads its supporting file and lists its folder.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document skills over MCP\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* chore(openspec): complete the integration check for MCP 2026-07-28\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(mcp): name Streamable HTTP in the add-server form\n\nNew SSE servers cannot be added, so the form no longer offers HTTP/SSE.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(e2e): capture the MCP guide screenshots from the test server\n\nThe opt-in spec (SERO_E2E_DOCS_MCP=1) records the MCP guide images with\nthe MCP test server, so it needs no model or network. The test server\ngets --no-skills and a styled dashboard app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): update the MCP guide and its screenshots\n\nReplace the three stale MCP images, add images for the protocol card,\nMCP apps, tasks, remote skills and server questions, and correct the\nadd-server steps. Link MCP from User Feedback, Security / Privacy and\nKnown Limitations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(mcp): say that Sero shows the MCP app with the tool call\n\nThe tool result told the user to open the app from the MCP app. Sero now\nshows it in the chat.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): give the task restart test time to finish\n\nThe test takes about 5 s, which is the default timeout, so it failed\nunder full-suite load.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* refactor(desktop): move readToolResultView out of the component file\n\nReact Doctor''s only-export-components rule fires when a component file\nalso exports a plain function, because Fast Refresh cannot preserve\ncomponent state across such a module.\n\n* chore(doctor): waive iframe-missing-sandbox for the MCP viewer frames\n\nThe outer frame embeds Sero''s own loopback viewer shell, whose CSP needs\nallow-same-origin, and the nested MCP app frame stays sandboxed without\nit. The detector also cannot see the sandbox that viewer-shell.ts sets on\nthe frame it creates. The rule stays on for every other file.\n\n* fix(mcp): scope tasks and cancellation to their endpoint\n\nTwo endpoints can return the same remote task id. Sero stored each task\nunder that id alone, so one record replaced the other and an outcome\nreached the wrong chat. Records now use an endpoint-scoped local id, and\nthe remote id stays in the reference for requests to its server.\n\nCancel now applies the same ownership check as resumption: it compares\nthe live principal and endpoint before it sends anything, so a stored\ntask can no longer be cancelled through another account or connection.\n\n* fix(mcp): guard remote-skill reads at the shared read boundary\n\nThe cross-server guard ran only on the proxy route, so the model-visible\nmcp_manager read_resource reached any server while the session acted on a\nremote skill. The guard now lives in the shared resource read, with the\nguard injected by the runtime.\n\nThe manager tool also passed the model-supplied sessionId. Security\nchecks now use callerSessionId from the extension context instead, so a\nspoofed sessionId cannot pick a session that acts on no skill.\n\n* fix(mcp): give each MCP app frame its own origin\n\nThe app frame kept an opaque origin, so the camera and microphone the\nuser approved could not work: getUserMedia rejects an opaque origin with\nSecurityError. Each app now loads from its own <label>.localhost host on\nthe viewer port, so the frame keeps a real origin and stays cross-origin\nfrom the shell and from every other app. The app URL carries no shell\ntoken, so an app cannot load the shell origin. The shell CSP allows the\napp origin in frame-src.\n\nVerified in Chromium against the built shell: the frame origin is the\nper-app host, it is a secure context, and getUserMedia resolves after the\nuser approves the permission.\n\n* fix(desktop): keep the app CSP for .localhost frames\n\nThe Electron CSP hook kept a framed page''s own policy only for exact\n127.0.0.1 or localhost. The MCP viewer now serves each app frame from\n<label>.localhost, so the hook replaced the app''s default-deny policy\nwith the renderer policy and the app''s inline scripts could not run. The\nloopback check now counts .localhost names.\n\n* fix(mcp): guard the UI resource routes too\n\nThe cross-server skill guard covered only the non-ui read path. The\nui:// reader in open_resource and open_tool_ui ran with no check, so a\nremote skill could read another server''s UI resource. Both routes now run\nthe same guard before the read, and they use callerSessionId from the\nextension context, kept apart from the session that app messages go to.\n\n* test(usage): give the refresh fixture sessions distinct timestamps\n\nThe cross-file dedup fingerprint is timestamp plus token count. The two\nfixture sessions used Date.now() separately, so on a fast machine they\ncould share a millisecond and the same token count, and the second was\ndropped as copied history. Give each session its own timestamp.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ab265c4ade8a566d5ed49c708ee06a9130d3b1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/9ab265c4ade8a566d5ed49c708ee06a9130d3b1c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/9a73d6f03a6796497861eca5a4aa024915decc87","verification":{"payload":"tree 9ab265c4ade8a566d5ed49c708ee06a9130d3b1c\nparent 9895532660f319eb1826c74079ed04629e506254\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790367683 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790367683 +0100\n\nfeat(mcp): support MCP 2026-07-28 with Apps, Tasks and Skills (#563)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose support-mcp-2026-07-28 change for issue #359\n\nAdd the OpenSpec change for MCP 2026-07-28, MCP Apps, Tasks and\nSkills over MCP: proposal, seven capability specs, design and a\ntask list that lands in four slices.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(openspec): add prototype step and plugin rules to MCP change\n\nAdd a first task group that builds a styleguide prototype for the new\nUI and gates production UI tasks on its approval. Link the sero-plugin\nand sero-prototype skills. Move inline MCP Apps to a neutral\nui.chat.tool-result extension point and the CLI timeout exemption to a\ncli.interactive flag, so the host has no MCP-specific code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(styleguide): add MCP 2026-07-28 review prototype\n\nAdd an interactive prototype for issue 359 in the styleguide. It shows\nMCP apps in a tool result, server input requests over two rounds,\ntasks, remote skill approval, and the new MCP app protocol, Tasks and\nRemote skills views. Link it from the prototype archive.\n\nUpdate the OpenSpec change: fix the tool-call helper path, and add task\n4.7 so that the User Feedback questionnaire shows who asks, as the\nelicitation spec requires.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* refactor(mcp): split server edits and proxy formatting out of runtime files\n\nMove the upsert, remove and enable handlers from mcp-runtime.ts into\nruntime-servers.ts, and move the proxy result formatting and argument\nparsing from runtime-proxy.ts into runtime-proxy-format.ts. Behavior\ndoes not change. Both files now have room for the MCP 2026-07-28 work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* refactor(styleguide): flatten the MCP 2026-07-28 prototype\n\nRemove nested cards, badges for default states, repeated labels and\nlong descriptions. The MCP app now shows Servers, Tasks and Remote\nskills as plain sections with divided rows. Review notes move from the\nproduct view into the review panel.\n\nRecord the UI rules in design D10 so that production UI follows them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* build(mcp): move the MCP plugin to the v2 SDK packages\n\nRun the v1-to-v2 codemod. Replace @modelcontextprotocol/sdk with\n@modelcontextprotocol/client, upgrade @modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps\nto 2.0.1, and add the v2 server and node packages as dev dependencies\nfor the e2e fixture.\n\nThe fixture now serves both protocol eras over stdio through\nserveStdio, and only the 2025 handshake with --legacy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* style(styleguide): use one level of cards in the MCP prototype\n\nPut each MCP app panel (Tasks, Remote skills, Servers) in one card with\na header and count. Rows inside the card use dividers, status dots,\ncolored status badges and icon tiles, but no nested cards.\n\nCorrect the D10 UI rule: cards are allowed one level deep.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* style(styleguide): allow one nested card level in the MCP prototype\n\nShow the protocol details of an opened server in an inner card inside\nthe Servers card. Update the D10 UI rule: a card may hold cards, but\nthose inner cards hold no more cards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* refactor(mcp): use v2 list aggregation and drop v1 type casts\n\nCall listTools() and listResources() without a cursor so that the v2\nclient walks every page and fills its response cache. Remove the casts\non callTool() and on resource contents that the v2 types make\nunnecessary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): negotiate the protocol era through one client factory\n\nAdd createMcpClient() and use it for server connections and the OAuth\ncoordinator. Every client now probes with server/discover and falls\nback to the 2025 initialize handshake. Extension capabilities for MCP\nApps, Tasks and Skills are declared only when their host feature flag\nis on; all flags stay off until their host paths are ready. Sero never\ndeclares sampling or roots.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(openspec): record MCP prototype approval and defaults\n\nRecord that the user approved the MCP 2026-07-28 prototype and its\ndefaults: remote skills start off, headless sessions decline server\ninput, and task results arrive without a new agent turn. Mark task 1.5\ndone and remove the task delivery question from the open questions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): record the negotiated protocol and remember legacy servers\n\nRecord the era, protocol version, server extensions, server version and\ndeprecated-transport flag on each connection. Save a legacy verdict for\neach server and config hash in era-verdicts.json, and connect with a\nlegacy prior next time so that stdio servers are not probed on every\nconnect. A manual reconnect or a config change drops the verdict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(mcp): fall back to SSE only when Streamable HTTP is missing\n\nUse the deprecated SSE transport only when the Streamable HTTP endpoint\nanswers 404 or 405, or when an Agent Plugin asks for SSE. A server\nerror no longer hides behind an SSE retry. The SSE transport now gets\nthe OAuth provider, and the connection is marked as deprecated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): report the failed step, protocol and cache per server\n\nMap connect errors to a failure phase (discovery, legacy fallback,\nauthorization or extension). A 401 or 403 is an authorization failure\nand never selects the legacy era. Add the negotiated protocol, the\nfailure phase and the metadata cache state to each server snapshot.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): show protocol, extensions and failed step in the MCP app\n\nAdd a Protocol card to the server details with the negotiated revision,\nextensions, transport and metadata cache state, and notices for a\ndeprecated SSE transport and for the failed step. The server row shows\nthe revision and problem badges, and no longer shows badges for the\ndefault enabled and no-auth states.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): serve the e2e fixture over stdio and HTTP in both eras\n\nSplit the fixture into one server factory, a stdio entry (both eras, or\nonly the 2025 handshake with --legacy) and a Streamable HTTP entry\nbuilt with createMcpHandler. New server manager tests connect to each\nmode and check the negotiated era.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): cancel one MCP tool call without stopping the others\n\nPass the abort signal from the mcp tool and from the desktop CLI bridge\nthrough the runtime to client.callTool(), so that stopping a call\ncancels only that request. Add tests on a modern HTTP server for the\nrouting headers, the per-request _meta envelope, no session header, and\nper-request cancellation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document protocol negotiation and SSE deprecation\n\nDescribe how Sero picks the 2026-07-28 or 2025 protocol, the saved\nlegacy verdict, the request envelope and headers, the Protocol card on\nthe server view, and the SSE fallback rules. Add a Protocol versions\nsection to the MCP guide. Label the HTTP transport option as Streamable\nHTTP in the server form.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(openspec): record the MCP contract e2e result\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): map MCP input forms to the Sero questionnaire\n\nConvert an MCP form request to questionnaire questions (enum, titled\nenum, multi-select, boolean, string, number and integer), with a\nDecline option on the first question and server text kept as plain\ntext. Convert the answers back with type and constraint checks. A bad\nvalue is asked again once; a form with an unsupported field is declined\nwithout being shown.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): answer server input requests through the question UI\n\nRegister one elicitation/create handler on every server client. It\nanswers legacy elicitation/create requests and the input rounds of\nmodern input_required results (up to 10 rounds) with the Sero\nquestionnaire, labelled with the server and tool. The call context\ncomes from AsyncLocalStorage, with the newest call in flight as the\nfallback for legacy requests. With no question UI (headless or the\nplain Pi CLI) Sero declines at once. An aborted call cancels the open\nquestion. Declined requests post a short notice in the calling chat.\n\nURL-mode requests are declined for now, and only form elicitation is\ndeclared, until the open-page flow is decided.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): let a server ask the user to open a web page\n\nAdd an optional openUrl field to user-feedback question options in\n@sero-ai/common (0.18.1 -> 0.19.0). When the user picks such an option,\nthe host question card opens the URL through its checked external-link\npath and then sends the answer.\n\nThe MCP plugin uses it for URL-mode input requests: one chat question\nwith the full URL, Decline as the safe default, and Open page. Only\nhttp and https URLs are offered; other requests are declined with a\nnotice. Sero now declares URL elicitation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(mcp): keep MCP work moving while a call waits for the user\n\nRun tool calls and resource reads outside the runtime queue. Only\ntheir connection and state work (sync, checks, connect, and the\ncleanup after an authorization failure) stays in the queue, so a\nserver question during a call no longer blocks other MCP actions.\nResource reads also pass the stop signal and the chat notice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(cli): let a bridged tool declare that it waits for the user\n\nAdd an optional interactive flag to a tool''s cli metadata. bridgeTool()\ntreats such a tool like the built-in interactive tools and applies no\nper-command timeout. The MCP tool sets it, because a call can wait for\nthe user to answer a server question. The host does not name any\nplugin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): cover a two-round server input request end to end\n\nAdd a create_contact tool to the e2e MCP fixture that asks for input\nover two input_required rounds, and a contract case that answers both\nrounds through the host question channel and checks the source label\nand the Decline option.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(user-feedback): show who asks a questionnaire\n\nShow the question''s context source under the Questionnaire title, so\nthat a user sees which server and tool asked. Questions without a\nsource look as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document server input requests\n\nDescribe what the user sees when a server asks for input, how Decline\nand Cancel differ, the re-ask after a bad value, page requests, and\nthe headless decline. Add the implementation rules to the plugin\nREADME.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): allow more tools in the e2e fixture\n\nThe fixture now also serves create_contact, so the era tests check that\necho is listed instead of an exact tool list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): partition cached server data by account\n\nResolve a principal ID for each connection: anon without auth, a\nSHA-256 hash for a bearer token (the token is never stored), and a\nrandom ID for an OAuth authorization, stored with its tokens. A new\nsign-in creates a new ID, a token refresh keeps it, and sign-out\nremoves it. Pass the ID to the client as its cache partition and record\nit on the connection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): honor server cache hints in the metadata cache\n\nMove metadata-cache.json to version 2. Each entry records the account\nthat listed it, the server''s cacheScope and an expiry from its ttlMs.\nA private entry from another account is not shown, an expired entry is\nshown as stale, and a version 1 file is read as stale. Servers are\nwritten in sorted order. The Protocol card shows until when the cache\nis fresh.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* refactor(mcp): move connection helpers out of the server manager\n\nMove the environment, request, listing and protocol helpers into\nconnection-helpers.ts so that server-manager.ts keeps room for the\nlist-changed work. Behavior does not change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): refresh cached inventory when a server reports a change\n\nRegister tool and resource list-changed handlers on every client. The\nclient lists again, the connection takes the new items, and the runtime\nwrites the metadata cache entry and the snapshot in its queue. Sign-out\nnow removes the server''s private cache entry. The e2e fixture gets a\nreveal_tool that makes the server report a changed tool list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): list a server again when its cached inventory expires\n\nAdd refreshInventory() to the server manager. While the server''s TTL\nholds, the client serves the lists from its response cache and sends no\nrequest. The proxy calls it before it returns the tools or resources of\na connected server whose cache entry has expired.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document the metadata cache and its isolation\n\nDescribe the version 2 metadata cache: the partition keys (server,\nconfig hash, principal, scope), TTL handling, refresh, removal rules\nand bearer token hashing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): keep OAuth tokens and client data as the SDK gives them\n\nStore tokens and client information field for field, so that the\nissuer stamp of the v2 SDK is kept and returned unchanged. Only\nexpires_in becomes an absolute expiry. Add discovery state storage in\ndiscovery.json, and handle the verifier and discovery invalidation\nscopes. Files saved before the upgrade still load.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(mcp): check the OAuth callback issuer before the code exchange\n\nCheck the callback state first, then pass the full callback query to\nfinishAuth() so that the SDK compares iss with the expected issuer\nbefore it exchanges the code. On an issuer mismatch Sero shows a fixed\nmessage and never the callback text; for an error callback it shows\nonly a known RFC 6749 error code.\n\nAlso fix the provider state(): the SDK asks it for the state of each\nsign-in, but it only read a saved state that nothing wrote, so every\nsign-in failed with \"No OAuth state saved\". It now creates the state\nand saves it for the callback check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): prepare client metadata documents and check registration\n\nAdd the CLIENT_METADATA_URL constant, unset until Sero publishes a\nClient ID Metadata Document, and give it to the SDK. Until then Sero\nuses Dynamic Client Registration. Tests check that the registration is\nsent as a native app with the loopback redirect, and that a configured\nclient ID skips registration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): keep credentials away from a changed authorization server\n\nAfter a full sign-in, the resource metadata names another authorization\nserver. The test checks that the saved tokens carry the issuer stamp,\nthat no token or registration request reaches the new server, and that\nthe server status becomes needs-auth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document OAuth issuer checks and client registration\n\nDescribe the callback state and iss checks, issuer-stamped storage,\ndiscovery state, the behavior after an authorization server change,\ntoken endpoint TLS, scope step-up and the client registration order.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(openspec): record the MCP protocol slice check\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): write the e2e MCP fixture in TypeScript\n\nMerge the three .mjs fixture files into one server.mts that Node runs\nwith type stripping. Flags select the mode: stdio by default, --legacy\nfor the 2025 handshake only, and --http for Streamable HTTP.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): serve MCP app viewers from one server with a session map\n\nThe viewer now runs one loopback server for all app sessions. Each\nsession has a random token. Above eight sessions, the oldest closes.\nclose_viewer takes the viewer ID, so one pane or chat result can close\nits own session without closing others.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): host MCP apps through the official AppBridge\n\nReplace the hand-written postMessage bridge with a bundled shell that\nuses AppBridge and PostMessageTransport from ext-apps. The plugin''s\nVite build writes it to dist/ui/viewer-shell.js, and the viewer server\nserves it. The viewer page now needs no inline script. The shell sends\nthe tool input and result, and declares only the capabilities that\nthe viewer server implements.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): let an app call only the app tools of its own server\n\nThe viewer proxy lists and calls only tools of the owning server that\nare visible to apps and not in excludeTools. A blocked call returns an\nerror result and sends no request to the server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): isolate MCP apps with a default-deny CSP and link checks\n\nAn app without declared domains gets no network access. Declared\ndomains follow the MCP Apps CSP fields and must be web origins. The\napp gets no frame permissions for now. A link opens only after the\nuser picks Open page in the same question as URL-mode requests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): deliver app messages to the chat that shows the app\n\nEach session registers its sendMessage with the MCP runtime. An app\nopened for a chat session sends ui/message as a labeled follow-up that\nstarts a turn, and ui/update-model-context as hidden context for the\nnext turn. A viewer outside a chat does not declare these capabilities.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(desktop): add the ui.chat.tool-result extension point\n\nA tool result can name a plugin component with a seroToolResultView\nmarker in its details. The contribution type, the marker and the\ncomponent props live in @sero-ai/common. Electron validates the point,\nand FederatedContributionMount can pass props to a component.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(desktop): show plugin tool-result views in tool-call details\n\nThe tool-call details mount the ui.chat.tool-result component that a\nfinished result names, between the input and the output. A single call\nor a row with such a view starts open. When nothing matches or the\ncomponent fails, only the normal result shows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): show MCP apps inline in chat tool results\n\ncall_tool adds the seroToolResultView marker and details.mcpApp for a\ntool with an MCP app. The result is kept up to 256 KB. The plugin\ncontributes McpToolResultApp to ui.chat.tool-result. It opens a new\nviewer for the stored call on mount, fits the frame to the page, and\ncloses the viewer on unmount. When the app cannot load, it shows one\nline with the reason.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(desktop): keep the own CSP of loopback frames\n\nThe renderer CSP header replaced the policy of every response, also in\nframes from loopback servers. In a production build this blocked the\ninline script of an MCP app and dropped its no-network policy. A frame\nfrom a loopback server now keeps the policy that its server sends. It\nruns on its own origin, so the renderer policy does not protect the\nrenderer there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): hide app-only tools from the model\n\nA tool with visibility [\"app\"] is only for its server''s MCP app. The\nmodel inventory and cache leave it out, and a model call to it fails\nwithout a request to the server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): cover inline MCP apps end to end\n\nThe fixture server gets a dashboard app with an app-only tool, an app\nthat asks for a domain and a permission, and an app in a format that\nSero cannot show. The new workflow spec stores a real call_tool as a\nmodel sero-cli call and checks the inline app, its own tool call, and\nthe fallback line.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document MCP apps in the chat\n\nThe guide explains inline apps, their isolation, messages, links and\nthe fallback line. The plugin README describes the viewer server, the\nbundled shell, the proxy limits and the stored result details.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* refactor(common): re-export the contribution types in one line\n\nThe index file was at the 500-line limit. app-contributions.ts has only\ntypes, so one export type line replaces the explicit list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): ask before an MCP app gets a permission\n\nAn app that requests the camera, the microphone or the clipboard gets\nit only after the user selects Allow in a question that Sero shows\nwhen the app opens. Deny is the default, and Sero keeps the choice per\napp until the runtime stops. Geolocation is never granted. The chat\nand pane frames pass the granted allow value on to the app frame.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(mcp): ask for the wider scope after insufficient_scope\n\nAfter a 403 insufficient_scope, the SDK asked the runtime provider to\nredirect, but nobody followed it and the scope was lost. The next\nsign-in then connected with the old token and ended at once, so the\ncall kept failing. The runtime provider now saves the requested scope,\nand the next sign-in forces a new authorization for it. A plugin test\ncovers the full step-up path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(openspec): record the scope step-up fix in the design\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): declare MCP Apps support to servers\n\nThe host path for MCP apps is complete, so the client now declares the\nio.modelcontextprotocol/ui extension. Tasks and Skills stay off until\ntheir host paths are ready.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): add MCP task sessions through ext-tasks\n\nA connection whose server declares the Tasks extension gets an\next-tasks session when the Tasks feature is on. Its endpoint ID comes\nfrom the server name, config hash and principal. Task requests use a\nraw dispatch on the connected transport, because the SDK Client codecs\nreject 2026-07-28 task results, and task replies get a one-second poll\nfloor. The fixture''s HTTP mode now serves MCP Tasks for run_report.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): store MCP task records in tasks.json\n\nSero keeps its own record for each task that it follows: the task\nreference, server, principal, origin session, status, retention and\noutcome. Writes are queued and atomic, and records past their\nretention are pruned.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): follow MCP tasks and deliver their outcome to the chat\n\nWhen a server runs a tool call as a task, call_tool stores the task,\nhands it off, and returns the task ID with the sero mcp task commands.\nA tracker in the runtime settles each task, keeps its record current,\nasks the user for task input through the question channel, retries\nafter a lost connection, and delivers the outcome to the chat that made\nthe call without a new turn. Stored tasks resume when the runtime\nstarts; records of another principal are blocked and expired ones are\nremoved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): resume an MCP task after a runtime restart\n\nThe Tasks feature is now on. A new runtime test starts a task, shuts\nthe runtime down, starts a new runtime from the same state directory,\nand sees the outcome reach the chat session. The raw task dispatch no\nlonger leaves an unhandled rejection when a wait is stopped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): add task commands to the mcp tool and the MCP app actions\n\nThe mcp tool takes task_status, task_wait and task_cancel, and the CLI\ntakes sero mcp task status|wait|cancel <id>. A call passes its chat\nsession and tool call, so a task outcome returns to that chat. The MCP\napp gets list_tasks, cancel_task, dismiss_task and task_result.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): add the Tasks panel to the MCP app\n\nA Tasks button in the MCP app shows the number of active tasks and\nopens one card with a row per task: server and tool, status and age,\nthe reason when a task is disconnected or blocked, and Cancel, Result\nor Dismiss. The list refreshes while the app is open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): finish an MCP task across a Sero restart end to end\n\nThe new workflow spec starts a task on the fixture''s HTTP server,\nrestarts Sero, and sees the completed task and its result in the\nTasks panel. The run showed that tasks resumed only after a chat\nsession started, so the runtime now also resumes them on the first\nMCP action.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document MCP tasks\n\nThe guide explains task results in chat, the task commands, the Tasks\npanel, restart, connection loss, another account and retention. The\nplugin README describes the task session, the raw dispatch, the store,\nthe tracker and the actions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): add a skills client for the MCP Skills extension\n\nThe client sends skills/list, skills/get and resources/directory/read\nonly to a server that declares io.modelcontextprotocol/skills. Small\nlocal schemas describe the results, because no SDK package exists for\nthe extension. The fixture now serves a skill with a supporting file\nand a dynamic skill.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): keep remote skills in a registry with manifest-bound approvals\n\nskills.json holds each remote skill by server label and URI, its full\nentry, a digest of its file list, enablement (off by default), a\nchanged flag and the last refresh time. An approval holds only for the\nmanifest that the user approved. A skill missing from a listing stays\nonly while skills/get finds it. The task store and the registry now\nshare one queued, atomic JSON file helper.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): load remote MCP skills with checks and a code gate\n\nThe loader reads a skill''s SKILL.md only when the model loads it, and\nchecks the limits, size, digest, frontmatter and name first. It tags\nthe content with the server and holds the entry for the session, so\nlater reads accept only files in that entry. sero mcp skill\nload|read|ls reach it, and enabled skills appear in a prompt block\nwith their server label. While a session acts on a remote skill, bash\nand run_code need the user''s approval for that skill''s current\nmanifest, and reads of other servers are refused.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* feat(mcp): add the Remote skills panel to the MCP app\n\nA Remote skills button opens one card with the number of skills that\nare on, the last refresh and a refresh action. Each row shows the\nserver and name, the description, the URI, a Changed badge with the\nreason, and a switch. A dynamic skill cannot be turned on. The Tasks\nand Remote skills panels now share one open slot, as in the prototype.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): load a remote skill end to end\n\nThe Skills feature is now on. A new contract case refreshes the\nfixture''s skills, checks that they start off, turns one on, loads it,\nreads its supporting file and lists its folder.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): document skills over MCP\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* chore(openspec): complete the integration check for MCP 2026-07-28\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(mcp): name Streamable HTTP in the add-server form\n\nNew SSE servers cannot be added, so the form no longer offers HTTP/SSE.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(e2e): capture the MCP guide screenshots from the test server\n\nThe opt-in spec (SERO_E2E_DOCS_MCP=1) records the MCP guide images with\nthe MCP test server, so it needs no model or network. The test server\ngets --no-skills and a styled dashboard app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* docs(mcp): update the MCP guide and its screenshots\n\nReplace the three stale MCP images, add images for the protocol card,\nMCP apps, tasks, remote skills and server questions, and correct the\nadd-server steps. Link MCP from User Feedback, Security / Privacy and\nKnown Limitations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* fix(mcp): say that Sero shows the MCP app with the tool call\n\nThe tool result told the user to open the app from the MCP app. Sero now\nshows it in the chat.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* test(mcp): give the task restart test time to finish\n\nThe test takes about 5 s, which is the default timeout, so it failed\nunder full-suite load.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FEp6piXiMFuQdq6Hr3LHoW\n\n* refactor(desktop): move readToolResultView out of the component file\n\nReact Doctor''s only-export-components rule fires when a component file\nalso exports a plain function, because Fast Refresh cannot preserve\ncomponent state across such a module.\n\n* chore(doctor): waive iframe-missing-sandbox for the MCP viewer frames\n\nThe outer frame embeds Sero''s own loopback viewer shell, whose CSP needs\nallow-same-origin, and the nested MCP app frame stays sandboxed without\nit. The detector also cannot see the sandbox that viewer-shell.ts sets on\nthe frame it creates. The rule stays on for every other file.\n\n* fix(mcp): scope tasks and cancellation to their endpoint\n\nTwo endpoints can return the same remote task id. Sero stored each task\nunder that id alone, so one record replaced the other and an outcome\nreached the wrong chat. Records now use an endpoint-scoped local id, and\nthe remote id stays in the reference for requests to its server.\n\nCancel now applies the same ownership check as resumption: it compares\nthe live principal and endpoint before it sends anything, so a stored\ntask can no longer be cancelled through another account or connection.\n\n* fix(mcp): guard remote-skill reads at the shared read boundary\n\nThe cross-server guard ran only on the proxy route, so the model-visible\nmcp_manager read_resource reached any server while the session acted on a\nremote skill. The guard now lives in the shared resource read, with the\nguard injected by the runtime.\n\nThe manager tool also passed the model-supplied sessionId. Security\nchecks now use callerSessionId from the extension context instead, so a\nspoofed sessionId cannot pick a session that acts on no skill.\n\n* fix(mcp): give each MCP app frame its own origin\n\nThe app frame kept an opaque origin, so the camera and microphone the\nuser approved could not work: getUserMedia rejects an opaque origin with\nSecurityError. Each app now loads from its own <label>.localhost host on\nthe viewer port, so the frame keeps a real origin and stays cross-origin\nfrom the shell and from every other app. The app URL carries no shell\ntoken, so an app cannot load the shell origin. The shell CSP allows the\napp origin in frame-src.\n\nVerified in Chromium against the built shell: the frame origin is the\nper-app host, it is a secure context, and getUserMedia resolves after the\nuser approves the permission.\n\n* fix(desktop): keep the app CSP for .localhost frames\n\nThe Electron CSP hook kept a framed page''s own policy only for exact\n127.0.0.1 or localhost. The MCP viewer now serves each app frame from\n<label>.localhost, so the hook replaced the app''s default-deny policy\nwith the renderer policy and the app''s inline scripts could not run. The\nloopback check now counts .localhost names.\n\n* fix(mcp): guard the UI resource routes too\n\nThe cross-server skill guard covered only the non-ui read path. The\nui:// reader in open_resource and open_tool_ui ran with no check, so a\nremote skill could read another server''s UI resource. Both routes now run\nthe same guard before the read, and they use callerSessionId from the\nextension context, kept apart from the session that app messages go to.\n\n* test(usage): give the refresh fixture sessions distinct timestamps\n\nThe cross-file dedup fingerprint is timestamp plus token count. The two\nfixture sessions used Date.now() separately, so on a fast machine they\ncould share a millisecond and the same token count, and the second was\ndropped as copied history. Give each session its own timestamp.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqttfDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+CUQAGdl9tGSRjYlI4NxUkrWIZo7\nPO9aPTgZUJTxpn6vZwYnWIzdAIpE2vROQ/mD3SUvS4ILt5ZWx+jnA+huPO6KXaOI\ntITvvZZWGMYkSgKpzqoXHcaxWuza2u8aLaJWIskUUZdgIa+QB7BUMitbBabQ2iMd\n4AmPuN9lXaUwPyMs709FTSc3vCEd1YiUDYG+z6h/DHfzEffg6chpiSONIWmxrXgD\n+TRQNO1qkj1YeOmhOYZF25aQZ729eqQ1yPG/0tc17i2pJZ3iiqySA8aP93xjbV7N\nAbq0ccpF7UKmQVu0sycD017r1YXQGL2XVQoKxsAcQOjotlh5h15HKRRIpym3rOel\nVfAogvTKq+FCJc5mukK9VA/Br9Mx+viVOGO3fH90hVLuN8O6ZjLmBgpQg7AGEyHc\n/L1Bc2FTQDulGCUXfGDknBHe/3vN1QxbcZril5om8tRFvW6IzxpmiHZWNiacWMU+\nOCX5QLrIHlfDb5a/nHDxSiD87FX8EuBXVgTx8rLwMDT3oH/Ke20GGz6z5CmSv0y3\n9DxO8hzNIk4G8+1sM9ZFcibnQltRY2ERJ3BoBaAnHTuHfm+rEoXMre9AOFkH1eo6\nhzWJXRDWfwjA/pp+fpgN26SSpqPt3gY1nmI7OzIuxxr9IBfvqGu64j5U5vvDheil\nHtJru6z5qEg7YbJa5//i\n=+QS2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T20:21:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/9a73d6f03a6796497861eca5a4aa024915decc87","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDlhNzNkNmYwM2E2Nzk2NDk3ODYxZWNhNWE0YWEwMjQ5MTVkZWNjODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/9895532660f319eb1826c74079ed04629e506254","sha":"9895532660f319eb1826c74079ed04629e506254","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/9895532660f319eb1826c74079ed04629e506254"}],"sha":"9a73d6f03a6796497861eca5a4aa024915decc87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/9a73d6f03a6796497861eca5a4aa024915decc87"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/9895532660f319eb1826c74079ed04629e506254/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T05:26:44Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T05:26:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(profile): recover profiles that exist on disk and guard the real root (#562)\n\n* feat(profile): recover profiles that exist on disk and guard the real root\n\nAn empty profiles.json left every profile unreachable, and a test process\ncould resolve and write the real ~/.sero-ui. Add discovery and adoption for\nprofile directories the registry no longer lists, salvage before reset, and a\ntest-runner guard on Sero root resolution.\n\n- Resolve the Sero root in one place and throw under a test runner with no\n  override, naming the override to set\n- Isolate the test root per worker and stop hiding [sero:profile] logs\n- Discover profiles under profiles/ and in profiles.broken-*.json, preferring\n  the recorded id and name\n- Adopt a discovered profile at the path it already occupies\n- Offer \"keep existing profiles\" before Reset in the recovery dialog\n- Show discovered profiles in first-run setup and the profile switcher\n- Route profile migration through the shared root resolver\n\nCloses #547\nRefs #548\n\n* docs(openspec): archive recover-orphaned-profiles and sync profile specs\n\nCreate the profile-recovery and profile-registry-test-isolation main specs\nfrom their deltas, then archive the change.\n\n* fix(profile): keep recovered profiles reachable and stop inferring ownership\n\nAddress the review findings on the recovery flow.\n\n- List unregistered profiles in the switcher even when the registry already\n  has profiles, so adopting one does not hide the rest\n- Take identity and folder ownership from discovery instead of inferring\n  ownership from the path; a folder no record describes stays ineligible for\n  permanent deletion\n- Offer the default-root profile when it holds profile data, so a reset with\n  no usable backup still finds it\n- Move the adoption tests into their own file\n- Add recovery instructions to the profiles guide and update the\n  profile-recovery spec\n\n* fix(profile): let adoption recover the default root in either order\n\nCreation-only validation still applied to adoption, so with an empty registry\nand data at both the Sero root and profiles/work, opening Work then Default\nthrew ''reserved for the first default profile''. The containment exception was\nalso directional. Adoption now uses its own overlap rules: the default root and\nits managed children are one profile family in either direction, while\nduplicate paths and unrelated custom overlaps stay rejected.","tree":{"sha":"477f4655da0aecd8c02e96d641da7a8bfbc144f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/477f4655da0aecd8c02e96d641da7a8bfbc144f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/9895532660f319eb1826c74079ed04629e506254","verification":{"payload":"tree 477f4655da0aecd8c02e96d641da7a8bfbc144f1\nparent 4baf2e1ca477f4b5ea434ce20903035e6e6185b9\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790314004 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790314004 +0100\n\nfeat(profile): recover profiles that exist on disk and guard the real root (#562)\n\n* feat(profile): recover profiles that exist on disk and guard the real root\n\nAn empty profiles.json left every profile unreachable, and a test process\ncould resolve and write the real ~/.sero-ui. Add discovery and adoption for\nprofile directories the registry no longer lists, salvage before reset, and a\ntest-runner guard on Sero root resolution.\n\n- Resolve the Sero root in one place and throw under a test runner with no\n  override, naming the override to set\n- Isolate the test root per worker and stop hiding [sero:profile] logs\n- Discover profiles under profiles/ and in profiles.broken-*.json, preferring\n  the recorded id and name\n- Adopt a discovered profile at the path it already occupies\n- Offer \"keep existing profiles\" before Reset in the recovery dialog\n- Show discovered profiles in first-run setup and the profile switcher\n- Route profile migration through the shared root resolver\n\nCloses #547\nRefs #548\n\n* docs(openspec): archive recover-orphaned-profiles and sync profile specs\n\nCreate the profile-recovery and profile-registry-test-isolation main specs\nfrom their deltas, then archive the change.\n\n* fix(profile): keep recovered profiles reachable and stop inferring ownership\n\nAddress the review findings on the recovery flow.\n\n- List unregistered profiles in the switcher even when the registry already\n  has profiles, so adopting one does not hide the rest\n- Take identity and folder ownership from discovery instead of inferring\n  ownership from the path; a folder no record describes stays ineligible for\n  permanent deletion\n- Offer the default-root profile when it holds profile data, so a reset with\n  no usable backup still finds it\n- Move the adoption tests into their own file\n- Add recovery instructions to the profiles guide and update the\n  profile-recovery spec\n\n* fix(profile): let adoption recover the default root in either order\n\nCreation-only validation still applied to adoption, so with an empty registry\nand data at both the Sero root and profiles/work, opening Work then Default\nthrew ''reserved for the first default profile''. The containment exception was\nalso directional. Adoption now uses its own overlap rules: the default root and\nits managed children are one profile family in either direction, while\nduplicate paths and unrelated custom overlaps stay rejected.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtgYUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAP6MQAFRwtMCN7+fJ4SN01FLcQXCw\nDa2+uE/aLiTNJlTyTdchWbWHcbfrp+987RRtmVvEzBEvBJWrn4M6i+54GZ81dL/0\nw1fBIr/ENmO2yWULpFhB3GBC7H1JD3KCOvT6jR1f9MQesH95SXd/19u2xrxqlCrT\nLCJsKHPsK57AFFd2MZ+XhG1f4Wxa86iN7wwCUey3AfR9PqNJuzWn/ITnZvK9sTxi\nqBiBvImiOKXBwYPTJFZc1LjEp1zekIsklRNbJWxZ94q62IKjwN2QGVzqWIkiLKlB\n0YqYpf41SN83mTQkePZzTxZD7sgSsvYN9sTZrKJfdEqIksrL11GBA7TFGKOGAzfT\nxz240JsN06Vt+SIx4BUJ8plhwHk43V1KuBQ/2QZBews5X2zIHMe1qqyMnG3GONAV\nEkSNkTtzl31pcI3w5T0R8YXwFjq1/E3Rs0Y6ns6O6tNhXJJuHJ3etNNs4c0k5+r8\nLq+AGXOZ2FfcnAacm7QREm5/tExNZlaqb4iKRlklFJcMeBsgZ0+qAd7TNKtmhfXW\n0N8sXBlhT9sq3XQDkINnrgmfnKwNsSikyGH61p7LoJICbubYq6CcoCBq+i8GnFen\nZDkyW7uMtTP3VLVovWm58qFgtf8W//xnRLktyTCUXxkOQ5Avg1pjkzh9hYeWPwAo\n5U6T1FSH9s0t+WV32/l7\n=a226\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T05:26:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","fol