view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/4baf2e1ca477f4b5ea434ce20903035e6e6185b9","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDRiYWYyZTFjYTQ3N2Y0YjVlYTQzNGNlMjA5MDMwMzVlNmU2MTg1Yjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/426fdbc38e5137aac982c573ba73e9da85962058","sha":"426fdbc38e5137aac982c573ba73e9da85962058","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/426fdbc38e5137aac982c573ba73e9da85962058"}],"sha":"4baf2e1ca477f4b5ea434ce20903035e6e6185b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/4baf2e1ca477f4b5ea434ce20903035e6e6185b9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/426fdbc38e5137aac982c573ba73e9da85962058/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T20:51:56Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T20:51:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(architect): redesign the Run inspector to the approved prototype (#561)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose the Architect Run inspector redesign\n\nPlan issue #535 from the approved prototype: load activity on open,\nrecord owner wakes with model and tokens, name rows from the project\nrecord, show unmeasured values as unavailable, one headline cost,\nclear empty-filter states, and a layout with no empty space.\n\nRefs #535\n\n* feat(common): publish a Room''s working time on its board view\n\nOrchestratorBoardRoomView gains the optional activeMs and activeSince, filled\nfrom the Room record, so a reader can tell how long a Room has worked. Bumps\n@sero-ai/common to 0.18.1.\n\n* feat(architect): redesign the Run inspector to the approved prototype\n\nThe inspector opens on the newest run and shows its totals, a named activity\ntree on a zoomable timeline, the selected activity''s facts, and three charts,\nlaid out as the prototype with no explanatory copy.\n\n- Activity is named from the project record: research questions, milestone\n  titles, and owner wakes by kind. Owner turns are recorded as operations with\n  model, thinking and token deltas.\n- Running-total charges from one kind of source are one row per activity.\n- A fact that was not recorded is left out of the detail panel; research rows\n  list their Room members'' models.\n- Active time counts the working time Rooms and Workflows report, and time\n  ranges show dates when they cross a day.\n- Project lifetime lists every run with its cost and time.\n\nRefs #535\n\n* fix(orchestrator): lay out the running Workflow like the Architect header\n\nThe live strip inherited the Card''s column layout, so every item stacked and\ncentred. It is now a header: what is running and step progress on the left,\ncost, tokens and elapsed in a side panel on the right. A preview entry shows it.\n\n* docs(openspec): archive the Run inspector redesign and sync its specs\n\n* refactor(architect): split the inspector''s decisions out of its components\n\nReact Doctor flagged four inspector components as too complex and three files\nfor exporting non-components. The label tables, row words, tile values and\ndetail facts move into ui/lib/inspector-view.ts as plain functions; one run''s\nview moves into InspectorRun, keyed by scope so its zoom and selection reset\nwith it; the detail panel is one small component per row type. No behaviour\nchanges.","tree":{"sha":"977153147888ea42dbc274892ac182fca65fdf40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/977153147888ea42dbc274892ac182fca65fdf40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/426fdbc38e5137aac982c573ba73e9da85962058","verification":{"payload":"tree 977153147888ea42dbc274892ac182fca65fdf40\nparent de86a1affcebf6c1180459ddb9753d43c7f35ee5\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790283116 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790283116 +0100\n\nfeat(architect): redesign the Run inspector to the approved prototype (#561)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose the Architect Run inspector redesign\n\nPlan issue #535 from the approved prototype: load activity on open,\nrecord owner wakes with model and tokens, name rows from the project\nrecord, show unmeasured values as unavailable, one headline cost,\nclear empty-filter states, and a layout with no empty space.\n\nRefs #535\n\n* feat(common): publish a Room''s working time on its board view\n\nOrchestratorBoardRoomView gains the optional activeMs and activeSince, filled\nfrom the Room record, so a reader can tell how long a Room has worked. Bumps\n@sero-ai/common to 0.18.1.\n\n* feat(architect): redesign the Run inspector to the approved prototype\n\nThe inspector opens on the newest run and shows its totals, a named activity\ntree on a zoomable timeline, the selected activity''s facts, and three charts,\nlaid out as the prototype with no explanatory copy.\n\n- Activity is named from the project record: research questions, milestone\n  titles, and owner wakes by kind. Owner turns are recorded as operations with\n  model, thinking and token deltas.\n- Running-total charges from one kind of source are one row per activity.\n- A fact that was not recorded is left out of the detail panel; research rows\n  list their Room members'' models.\n- Active time counts the working time Rooms and Workflows report, and time\n  ranges show dates when they cross a day.\n- Project lifetime lists every run with its cost and time.\n\nRefs #535\n\n* fix(orchestrator): lay out the running Workflow like the Architect header\n\nThe live strip inherited the Card''s column layout, so every item stacked and\ncentred. It is now a header: what is running and step progress on the left,\ncost, tokens and elapsed in a side panel on the right. A preview entry shows it.\n\n* docs(openspec): archive the Run inspector redesign and sync its specs\n\n* refactor(architect): split the inspector''s decisions out of its components\n\nReact Doctor flagged four inspector components as too complex and three files\nfor exporting non-components. The label tables, row words, tile values and\ndetail facts move into ui/lib/inspector-view.ts as plain functions; one run''s\nview moves into InspectorRun, keyed by scope so its zoom and selection reset\nwith it; the detail panel is one small component per row type. No behaviour\nchanges.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtY1sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5C8QAEsv6KPQGrjCE5+Au3UR9WBT\n1qvzU5QZz45b6McUHCajUcMB3Upg6lhgKh86M8e6xSqBth/oJiP9mP9vrM4hSFq5\ncWT7isH4S7I1vfVPu3PV8uaug8DytvvnCWpZShR+62TMU7bRnaAVs/sDp4jU/9hV\nnCmmIn1miSlB8QyU5NLxmctIxGev+x9/4v0OHFHIJlaSZnY+ARFpXNsuMvAlamNK\ni0MZFE/VP8cTpaSVitQVmdXYxzUj2mv/0GRLocnyPGko3bGDm7hrcLR2NjYGksTi\n/Tc2bQArfYd+EGpxil8x+7RkqdQLh8nel7cUkEfXyxRV6AH2nwkIlKgd1GKkgd+c\npjLOV+YJQLuGYKcnyf/w3OWCtzGB/h6Qulfc3JH3+vOWPu7S2pVlPGXFJqIVdk83\nVskXkDqw3TI4neEHcsfNrenTQyaLKdIPjD5V89Ih9bXggq5OOVRPthkeMu2C4viY\n4tbrz0XawviniMnp3hMw6ytpeI2S5f2G27YOuFl+mnCdfeloUKeN5zles2GKm0cE\nthu9MnVBdNEG+PwpZiSA5dpa2FjUBl4K9bDrcNYQ8g+pP/WWH3zW1rEKnG1HgPp4\nAlNrRy2NasD1g8/N7g4i