e90e4b372138feb1e1fccc1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/f3838b2407045350e90e4b372138feb1e1fccc1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/75947797b1b177386eea4b8995dc4e8680afe3e5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/75947797b1b177386eea4b8995dc4e8680afe3e5","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDc1OTQ3Nzk3YjFiMTc3Mzg2ZWVhNGI4OTk1ZGM0ZTg2ODBhZmUzZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/8fbed50f793e8bb61c5bfe614b53f53668ca1533","sha":"8fbed50f793e8bb61c5bfe614b53f53668ca1533","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/8fbed50f793e8bb61c5bfe614b53f53668ca1533"}],"sha":"75947797b1b177386eea4b8995dc4e8680afe3e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/75947797b1b177386eea4b8995dc4e8680afe3e5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/8fbed50f793e8bb61c5bfe614b53f53668ca1533/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T22:25:54Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T22:25:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ux): one searchable model picker everywhere (#543) (#558)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose searchable model pickers (#543)\n\nAdd the ux-model-pickers change: one type-to-filter combobox for every\nmodel picker in Architect and the Orchestrator.\n\n- proposal, specs (model-selection-ui, architect-model-overrides,\n  orchestrator-ui), design, tasks and comparison.\n- Rebuild the shared AvailableModelPicker on the Combobox with the\n  provider on every row.\n- One field for a step''s model, tiers first.\n- Tier fields use the picker; the Effective column names the model id\n  and thinking level.\n\nRefs #543\n\n* feat(ui): one searchable model picker everywhere (#543)\n\nEvery model picker in Architect and the Orchestrator is one combobox.\nType to filter by provider, model name and model id; each row and the\nclosed field name the provider.\n\n- Rebuild AvailableModelPicker on Combobox with a flat list and an\n  optional leadingOptions prop for fixed choices.\n- StepModelControl: one field, Auto and the tiers first, clear only a\n  pinned model.\n- ModelSettings and IntakeModelOverrides: the shared field per tier, the\n  inherited choice first; the Project models Effective column reads\n  `<model id> · <thinking level>`.\n- Preview fixtures and captures; comparison.md records each difference.\n- Bump @sero-ai/ui to 0.7.0.\n\nRefs #543\n\n* chore(openspec): mark ux-model-pickers tasks complete (#543)\n\nAll 21 tasks are done; the draft pull request is #558.\n\nRefs #543\n\n* fix(ui): match the model picker filter to filterModelGroups\n\nThe picker searched the full provider/modelId key as well as the\nprovider display name and label, so a provider''s internal key matched\nrows. Match only the provider display name, the model name and the bare\nmodel id, the string filterModelGroups already matches.\n\nRefs #543\n\n* fix(ui): size the model field to the drawing''s 20rem\n\nA side-by-side capture showed the step''s Model field filling the whole\nrow (748px) and pushing Agent and Tools to the right. The drawing draws\na 20rem field in both frames. Use w-80 for the step and both tier\nfields, in place of flex-1.\n\nThe drawing page renders at a 16px root and the app at 13px, so the\nsame token measures 320px in the drawing and 260px in the app.\n\nRefs #543\n\n* fix(ui): anchor the model list to the field and match the drawn size\n\nTwo faults a capture from the real app showed:\n- The popup sized to the input, and the provider beside the input\n  narrowed it, so with a model selected the list clipped every name.\n  Anchor the popup to the whole field. Field, popup and list now share\n  one width.\n- The field was 260px (w-80 at the app''s 13px root) against the\n  drawing''s 320px. Use a fixed 320px for the step and both tier fields.\n\nAlso widen the step Tools popover from w-72 to w-96 so tool\ndescriptions read, and import PluginStyleScope from its subpath in the\nOrchestrator preview: the repository layout check forbids a bare\n@sero-ai/ui import there.\n\nRefs #543\n\n* chore(openspec): archive ux-model-pickers and sync its specs (#543)\n\nSync the three deltas into the main specs:\n- new capability model-selection-ui\n- architect-model-overrides: the shared picker for tier models, and the\n  Effective column as <model id> · <thinking level>\n- orchestrator-ui: a step''s model is one filterable field\n\nThen move the change to openspec/changes/archive/2026-09-23-ux-model-pickers.\n\nRefs #543","tree":{"sha":"413dda9a43bf58393d592aca9c7a327381b65083","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/413dda9a43bf58393d592aca9c7a327381b65083"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/8fbed50f793e8bb61c5bfe614b53f53668ca1533","verification":{"payload":"tree 413dda9a43bf58393d592aca9c7a327381b65083\nparent 42ec0a898011969fd575f3b23745ddbb382e3d53\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790202354 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790202354 +0100\n\nfeat(ux): one searchable model picker everywhere (#543) (#558)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose searchable model pickers (#543)\n\nAdd the ux-model-pickers change: one type-to-filter combobox for every\nmodel picker in Architect and the Orchestrator.\n\n- proposal, specs (model-selection-ui, architect-model-overrides,\n  orchestrator-ui), design, tasks and comparison.\n- Rebuild the shared AvailableModelPicker on the Combobox with the\n  provider on every row.\n- One field for a step''s model, tiers first.\n- Tier fields use the picker; the Effective column names the model id\n  and thinking level.\n\nRefs #543\n\n* feat(ui): one searchable model picker everywhere (#543)\n\nEvery model picker in Architect and the Orchestrator is one combobox.\nType to filter by provider, model name and model id; each row and the\nclosed field name the provider.\n\n- Rebuild AvailableModelPicker on Combobox with a flat list and an\n  optional leadingOptions prop for fixed choices.\n- StepModelControl: one field, Auto and the tiers first, clear only a\n  pinned model.\n- ModelSettings and IntakeModelOverrides: the shared field per tier, the\n  inherited choice first; the Project models Effective column reads\n  `<model id> · <thinking level>`.\n- Preview fixtures and captures; comparison.md records each difference.\n- Bump @sero-ai/ui to 0.7.0.\n\nRefs #543\n\n* chore(openspec): mark ux-model-pickers tasks complete (#543)\n\nAll 21 tasks are done; the draft pull request is #558.\n\nRefs #543\n\n* fix(ui): match the model picker filter to filterModelGroups\n\nThe picker searched the full provider/modelId key as well as the\nprovider display name and label, so a provider''s internal key matched\nrows. Match only the provider display name, the model name and the bare\nmodel id, the string filterModelGroups already matches.\n\nRefs #543\n\n* fix(ui): size the model field to the drawing''s 20rem\n\nA side-by-side capture showed the step''s Model field filling the whole\nrow (748px) and pushing Agent and Tools to the right. The drawing draws\na 20rem field in both frames. Use w-80 for the step and both tier\nfields, in place of flex-1.\n\nThe drawing page renders at a 16px root and the app at 13px, so the\nsame token measures 320px in the drawing and 260px in the app.\n\nRefs #543\n\n* fix(ui): anchor the model list to the field and match the drawn size\n\nTwo faults a capture from the real app showed:\n- The popup sized to the input, and the provider beside the input\n  narrowed it, so with a model selected the list clipped every name.\n  Anchor the popup to the whole field. Field, popup and list now share\n  one width.\n- The field was 260px (w-80 at the app''s 13px root) against the\n  drawing''s 320px. Use a fixed 320px for the step and both tier fields.\n\nAlso widen the step Tools popover from w-72 to w-96 so tool\ndescriptions read, and import PluginStyleScope from its subpath in the\nOrchestrator preview: the repository layout check forbids a bare\n@sero-ai/ui import there.\n\nRefs #543\n\n* chore(openspec): archive ux-model-pickers and sync its specs (#543)\n\nSync the three deltas into the main specs:\n- new capability model-selection-ui\n- architect-model-overrides: the shared picker for tier models, and the\n  Effective column as <model id> · <thinking level>\n- orchestrator-ui: a step''s model is one filterable field\n\nThen move the change to openspec/changes/archive/2026-09-23-ux-model-pickers.\n\nRefs #543","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtFHyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnE0QAHkke+fS64F0GUvZkqm8vVOv\n3GLbS0Y0yFR9kPqXZSkIjRy5D0jYo5SCNFLvdb0IR1aJyMg5ygak4BEYIv90Wkz+\nXgkvg/Wx9l5IFyhxljCuGMLxQnoyUJorMqSjuE2V7/YXxPZWF5WH1hNd4NZg/+91\nKVBCDvk9IT5EDhkYEXyl15sHvjvCaxzeYsY3b8FIlVMWHOgBd50JHHumF5gUEExJ\nmEuQuv3b01JFXaLEJicLw53g1Q496w2nh9m2F0KMZo1Ity88E9P57lk4WvMfc0n5\nqMR9ur8JznTyhO+Xm/CDeUZhUSf+9ev6sCEQw/hjzJiboDXp7OMPkZ0u4ZHNWqVS\nW9+nsQJ2FP30pcYy2vUFLuOxZa9HErfCooBYdn1luCYH4X2OWS7CLMaLjm8hPnB0\n5Ov1+tl24ygKBWNhcOK8bv0WCrNbsUn3Kx0BZKD0ZfPfUTP3y+1Tk8ewaEpNGeaU\nB73HrrRvmSYa0rQR5aa9+zV8odDZ2YAjXJPulfEg+JvuCSKLf+ddsGP0/KzquHNZ\nFkppfTFmtLlzsNCxZPkXSHU37fyN2uNwYPIsFRG1pqOCwephIiqQj//Jl37pGE+3\nSu4OI4ke+Wg1ZDApzL8Ub6Q2VVH+Mgmhzc0lKnchlt8CxztgVqVJ6CXQo74UzMGg\n83g2XZC36lrWObC8+ftu\n=nTiX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T22:25:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/8fbed50f793e8bb61c5bfe614b53f53668ca1533","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDhmYmVkNTBmNzkzZThiYjYxYzViZmU2MTRiNTNmNTM2NjhjYTE1MzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/42ec0a898011969fd575f3b23745ddbb382e3d53","sha":"42ec0a898011969fd575f3b23745ddbb382e3d53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/42ec0a898011969fd575f3b23745ddbb382e3d53"}],"sha":"8fbed50f793e8bb61c5bfe614b53f53668ca1533","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/8fbed50f793e8bb61c5bfe614b53f53668ca1533"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/42ec0a898011969fd575f3b23745ddbb382e3d53/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T20:44:28Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T20:44:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(architect): start a project in an existing workspace (#557)\n\n* feat(architect): start a project in an existing workspace\n\nNew project gains a New folder / Existing workspace choice. Existing\nworkspace replaces Name and Location with a picker of registered\nworkspaces, and the project takes the workspace''s name. A workspace\nthat already holds an Architect project is shown as such and cannot be\nchosen, and the Global workspace is left out.\n\nNew folder now refuses a folder that exists instead of registering it\nin place or making an empty sibling. A project created on an existing\nworkspace records that workspace''s id and path and creates and\nregisters no workspace.\n\nCloses #542\n\n* docs(openspec): mark the apply tasks complete for issue #542\n\n* fix(architect): refuse an existing folder at the real workspace destination\n\nReview round 1 of PR #557 found the new-folder guard unsound.\n\n- Replace the `fileInfo` existence check with `host.pathExists` (`fs.stat`),\n  because `fileInfo` reads the first bytes and returns null when that read\n  fails on a directory, so an existing directory could pass the guard.\n- Check the destination the host would create, `dirname(folder)` joined with\n  `workspaceSlug(basename(folder))`, as well as the folder the user named.\n  `TestRepo` can no longer land on an existing `testrepo`.\n- Move intake resolution into `runtime/intake-placement.ts` and\n  `CreateProjectInput` into `shared/create-project.ts`; `projects-actions.ts`\n  and `record.ts` are back under the 500 LOC limit.\n- Share the workspace slug as `workspaceSlug` in `@sero-ai/common` so the host\n  and the plugin cannot drift apart.\n- Pass both `folder` and `workspaceId` through the tool so the runtime returns\n  its both-fields refusal instead of silently dropping one.\n\n* fix(architect): make intake refuse the real destination and reuse on retry\n\nReview round 2 of PR #557 found two more correctness defects.\n\n- Predict the exact destination the host picks, including the `ensureUniqueId`\n  suffix when the base id is registered elsewhere, and refuse when it exists.\n  Move the id rule (workspaceSlug, ensureUniqueId, isSafe/assertSafeWorkspaceId)\n  into `@sero-ai/common` so the host and the plugin share one spelling.\n- Record the resolved destination as the project''s folder, and have\n  `advanceIntake` adopt an existing workspace by that path. A resume after a\n  lost record update now reuses the workspace instead of making a suffixed\n  sibling.\n- Keep `packages/common/src/index.ts` at 500 LOC and the plugin runtime files\n  under the limit.\n\n* fix(architect): never adopt a workspace another project owns\n\nReview round 3 found that the retry path could adopt a workspace that a\nconcurrent new-folder intake had already created and linked, so two projects\ncould share one workspace. `advanceIntake` now adopts a workspace at the\nrecord''s folder only when no other project already owns it; otherwise it makes\nits own. One project per workspace holds on this path too.\n\n* fix(architect): serialize the workspace claim across intakes\n\nThe ownership guard still raced: ownership was read, the workspace listed or\ncreated, and the id saved in separate awaited steps, so a second new-folder\nintake could read ownership before the first saved its id and adopt the first''s\nworkspace. Move the whole step into `runtime/workspace-claim.ts`, one promise\nqueue per runtime (the `RecordStore` write-queue precedent), and re-read the\nproject after acquiring the queue so a second call for the same project sees the\nsaved id. A focused test drives the interleave and fails without the queue.\n\n* chore(common): bump @sero-ai/common to 0.18.0\n\nThe package gains the shared workspace id rule (workspaceSlug,\nensureUniqueId, isSafeWorkspaceId, assertSafeWorkspaceId), so a new\nversion is needed before it can be republished.\n\n* docs(agents): bump the version of an npm-published package in the same PR","tree":{"sha":"77651f6f8b3bb5647692636be2efe5c19b64c83a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/77651f6f8b3bb5647692636be2efe5c19b64c83a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/42ec0a898011969fd575f3b23745ddbb382e3d53","verification":{"payload":"tree 77651f6f8b3bb5647692636be2efe5c19b64c83a\nparent 49a304fd73bcec4f5e193f28b4f1872396c89292\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790196268 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790196268 +0100\n\nfeat(architect): start a project in an existing workspace (#557)\n\n* feat(architect): start a project in an existing workspace\n\nNew project gains a New folder / Existing workspace choice. Existing\nworkspace replaces Name and Location with a picker of registered\nworkspaces, and the project takes the workspace''s name. A workspace\nthat already holds an Architect project is shown as such and cannot be\nchosen, and the Global workspace is left out.\n\nNew folder now refuses a folder that exists instead of registering it\nin place or making an empty sibling. A project created on an existing\nworkspace records that workspace''s id and path and creates and\nregisters no workspace.\n\nCloses #542\n\n* docs(openspec): mark the apply tasks complete for issue #542\n\n* fix(architect): refuse an existing folder at the real workspace destination\n\nReview round 1 of PR #557 found the new-folder guard unsound.\n\n- Replace the `fileInfo` existence check with `host.pathExists` (`fs.stat`),\n  because `fileInfo` reads the first bytes and returns null when that read\n  fails on a directory, so an existing directory could pass the guard.\n- Check the destination the host would create, `dirname(folder)` joined with\n  `workspaceSlug(basename(folder))`, as well as the folder the user named.\n  `TestRepo` can no longer land on an existing `testrepo`.\n- Move intake resolution into `runtime/intake-placement.ts` and\n  `CreateProjectInput` into `shared/create-project.ts`; `projects-actions.ts`\n  and `record.ts` are back under the 500 LOC limit.\n- Share the workspace slug as `workspaceSlug` in `@sero-ai/common` so the host\n  and the plugin cannot drift apart.\n- Pass both `folder` and `workspaceId` through the tool so the runtime returns\n  its both-fields refusal instead of silently dropping one.\n\n* fix(architect): make intake refuse the real destination and reuse on retry\n\nReview round 2 of PR #557 found two more correctness defects.\n\n- Predict the exact destination the host picks, including the `ensureUniqueId`\n  suffix when the base id is registered elsewhere, and refuse when it exists.\n  Move the id rule (workspaceSlug, ensureUniqueId, isSafe/assertSafeWorkspaceId)\n  into `@sero-ai/common` so the host and the plugin share one spelling.\n- Record the resolved destination as the project''s folder, and have\n  `advanceIntake` adopt an existing workspace by that path. A resume after a\n  lost record update now reuses the workspace instead of making a suffixed\n  sibling.\n- Keep `packages/common/src/index.ts` at 500 LOC and the plugin runtime files\n  under the limit.\n\n* fix(architect): never adopt a workspace another project owns\n\nReview round 3 found that the retry path could adopt a workspace that a\nconcurrent new-folder intake had already created and linked, so two projects\ncould share one workspace. `advanceIntake` now adopts a workspace at the\nrecord''s folder only when no other project already owns it; otherwise it makes\nits own. One project per workspace holds on this path too.\n\n* fix(architect): serialize the workspace claim across intakes\n\nThe ownership guard still raced: ownership was read, the workspace listed or\ncreated, and the id saved in separate awaited steps, so a second new-folder\nintake could read ownership before the first saved its id and adopt the first''s\nworkspace. Move the whole step into `runtime/workspace-claim.ts`, one promise\nqueue per runtime (the `RecordStore` write-queue precedent), and re-read the\nproject after acquiring the queue so a second call for the same project sees the\nsaved id. A focused test drives the interleave and fails without the queue.\n\n* chore(common): bump @sero-ai/common to 0.18.0\n\nThe package gains the shared workspace id rule (workspaceSlug,\nensureUniqueId, isSafeWorkspaceId, assertSafeWorkspaceId), so a new\nversion is needed before it can be republished.\n\n* docs(agents): bump the version of an npm-published package in the same PR","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtDosCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPVQQAJvfBFsRyjKnt9aMbpK8Y2WC\nm/hSuNzjE51ECnOKDBzDnNrmNerMc4+yfgbP9g8LhJjyMCc/Ah2rmTSi22yf0cKZ\nsrtDQnNXPr7U1txA/KcHNq8v02H73dKpRZQSPI569MkOIXpnmGscGfGhgYtTw7Dj\np+w1mC3OtNuM0v2P51EzeyNp+LL5KROtxOpbFyWqSNMoseb+2yk134Ou3tpVfIzx\nutPDuQ1cnbrukaApwqPPiCtu55S8RdmMpU3HHG+Tn9JtOxpRXl6rmYhT7lw+useD\n/ir4tle7hjpPSUfyfUlI8CpQs15qBOZG6YlyFzBumtnno1vX5khYyBvdVpSZjDBk\nQnX/sbQrG6QsUV26CfhfNtjGLsQRvn2wvSv8X+r3Yo7HDuZ8Mvi3fuemuScftDal\nBRm3XC2QP6hZZkaU4I0o0nsbyUsInSi79iMJNnewuaa9d3d3V0wsF6BPaGTRgdee\nPzotuHVnnIsQFLr105alEUuLCBnBt6aajXfHjbsg5KqpFXgzdC+f55LEFFn0+Yx/\ng92Cqq0TAnboAkJKHbQhtNDo62gika2CwskeT771u7ynswMpoQkkW0023XDQybht\njqsLgzMBowyOgFkr5yZxXdieOACROV1NjGWZTsisUu6q3+/l4QgqISdoaIAFbNXQ\n1qE+FT/3RSili50TZqvR\n=VUi/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T20:44:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/42ec0a898011969fd575f3b23745ddbb382e3d53","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDQyZWMwYTg5ODAxMTk2OWZkNTc1ZjNiMjM3NDVkZGJiMzgyZTNkNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/49a304fd73bcec4f5e193f28b4f1872396c89292","sha":"49a304fd73bcec4f5e193f28b4f1872396c89292","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/49a304fd73bcec4f5e193f28b4f1872396c89292"}],"sha":"42ec0a898011969fd575f3b23745ddbb382e3d53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/42ec0a898011969fd575f3b23745ddbb382e3d53"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/49a304fd73bcec4f5e193f28b4f1872396c89292/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T19:05:09Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T19:05:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(navigation): return one Back to where the user came from (#554)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose following the thread between apps (#541)\n\nPlanning artifacts for issue #541, from the binding drawing\n6-follow-the-thread.html:\n\n- app-navigation-history: a launch replaces the entry the app opened on, a\n  workspace switch records a step, and Back/Forward name the landing workspace.\n- orchestrator-ui: a Workflow''s settings line names the Architect project it\n  came from, and a Room''s header names the project that opened it.\n- orchestrator-dispatch-handle: creation retains the project''s display name.\n\nThe proposal corrects the issue''s data claim: Loop.project.projectId and\nRoom.definition.projectContext already exist and are already populated by\nArchitect dispatch. The change adds the name and the two surfaces.\n\ncomparison.md records the capture method and the departures decided up front;\nno frame has been captured yet.\n\nNo source change.\n\n* feat(navigation): return one Back to where the user came from\n\nOpening a Workflow or a Room from Architect pushed a second history entry, so one Back did not reach the project. Switching workspace overwrote the current entry, so Back skipped the page the user left. Neither surface named the Architect project that sent the work.\n\n- A launch replaces the entry the shell pushed for the app.\n- A workspace switch records the app''s page in the new workspace as a step.\n- Back and Forward name the workspace they land in.\n- A Workflow''s settings line names the project it came from; a Room''s header names the project beside its state. Both link by project id.\n- Creation keeps the project''s display name as a display-only snapshot.\n\n* fix(navigation): record a same-app workspace change on every path\n\nsetActiveApp records a new app and workspace, but it returns early when the app is already active. Callers that set the workspace and then open the same app recorded nothing, so the app mount replaced the current entry and Back skipped the page the user left.\n\nRoute those callers through selectWorkspaceForApp: it records the step when the app stays, and leaves the step to the app open when the app changes. Affects app control, the editor bridge, the dev-server panel, pending-question cards, Agent Board cards, and workspace create, clone and add-folder.\n\n* docs(navigation): note the workspace-aware Back and the Explorer non-goal\n\nUpdate the Back and forward guide for in-app history and the named landing workspace, and record Explorer''s built-in history model as an explicit non-goal of this change.\n\n* chore(common): bump @sero-ai/common to 0.17.0\n\nThe project context gains an optional display name, so the published package needs a new version before it can be republished.","tree":{"sha":"2cb1298eeb633429bf6005d3afc70e77cb378f50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/2cb1298eeb633429bf6005d3afc70e77cb378f50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/49a304fd73bcec4f5e193f28b4f1872396c89292","verification":{"payload":"tree 2cb1298eeb633429bf6005d3afc70e77cb378f50\nparent ff66f6aed53b2bf079f9853c72b338cd8c759a6a\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790190309 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790190309 +0100\n\nfeat(navigation): return one Back to where the user came from (#554)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose following the thread between apps (#541)\n\nPlanning artifacts for issue #541, from the binding drawing\n6-follow-the-thread.html:\n\n- app-navigation-history: a launch replaces the entry the app opened on, a\n  workspace switch records a step, and Back/Forward name the landing workspace.\n- orchestrator-ui: a Workflow''s settings line names the Architect project it\n  came from, and a Room''s header names the project that opened it.\n- orchestrator-dispatch-handle: creation retains the project''s display name.\n\nThe proposal corrects the issue''s data claim: Loop.project.projectId and\nRoom.definition.projectContext already exist and are already populated by\nArchitect dispatch. The change adds the name and the two surfaces.\n\ncomparison.md records the capture method and the departures decided up front;\nno frame has been captured yet.\n\nNo source change.\n\n* feat(navigation): return one Back to where the user came from\n\nOpening a Workflow or a Room from Architect pushed a second history entry, so one Back did not reach the project. Switching workspace overwrote the current entry, so Back skipped the page the user left. Neither surface named the Architect project that sent the work.\n\n- A launch replaces the entry the shell pushed for the app.\n- A workspace switch records the app''s page in the new workspace as a step.\n- Back and Forward name the workspace they land in.\n- A Workflow''s settings line names the project it came from; a Room''s header names the project beside its state. Both link by project id.\n- Creation keeps the project''s display name as a display-only snapshot.\n\n* fix(navigation): record a same-app workspace change on every path\n\nsetActiveApp records a new app and workspace, but it returns early when the app is already active. Callers that set the workspace and then open the same app recorded nothing, so the app mount replaced the current entry and Back skipped the page the user left.\n\nRoute those callers through selectWorkspaceForApp: it records the step when the app stays, and leaves the step to the app open when the app changes. Affects app control, the editor bridge, the dev-server panel, pending-question cards, Agent Board cards, and workspace create, clone and add-folder.\n\n* docs(navigation): note the workspace-aware Back and the Explorer non-goal\n\nUpdate the Back and forward guide for in-app history and the named landing workspace, and record Explorer''s built-in history model as an explicit non-goal of this change.\n\n* chore(common): bump @sero-ai/common to 0.17.0\n\nThe project context gains an optional display name, so the published package needs a new version before it can be republished.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtCLlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWUQQAFRsBBj8oZh74JkjpcMDa84n\nFlh8cOX8bdrX6AQyBaqWl0rBgdnshwS2mLtijw3jseZj6ot/cIcvEZFzKnL9ALXD\njDDCoZzTXxCDfAMsgOt87s5IvJqD+/Nea43zwQwga8erB5jYnHr3E0LH+VxJCH4Q\n0tSe5iXyQ9PbqK37NpMtF0dK5sjFLOf5Kz6qy0BJDSJs4Edd1zoNMtNNNktMeD05\nM4q1CKsvJbJERFd89D9iVwBaZHD9778zQ53+YRaBwXmnIfeXU3/lZfsE13vYPLO6\n1sRJnRfjK2yQhsBOM5AvAXhsU0C2++SYpnyFupzPnT5jI2JTgPnoLgQ4cWlCxJXn\nDq2k8DeCjPg0AHwEceTRFE9h5LaeCxc47PCdBlwkM6I5B+6QWw0yEfMg0CfVs8Hv\n2paMgNig+YDiotpB3rUE/vw7Hlm2MAAIFHjNf3guj/I03TZwfrZtlgy+d2PUHxBv\nA1Ho9DX6buS2BQ5LpvINR/J0J0nQy9bovBKz8Nk6X+WH2OeyVG6kDZNFIRFB3SQd\nArCCeqhho9gd4FF+LVhiAiNknALprT1swTDo4y5z38GFsAKoqv6RqDX5xNtzNWYj\n2Zkvosf0qKH2YkELW0TXMg28VLwxtP9hGVUGzF/UBaPpcO9IG7Q7B2iEdi5A+Kq+\ndBuwaotvNLX8MGwgvZ19\n=GUt1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T19:05:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/49a304fd73bcec4f5e193f28b4f1872396c89292","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDQ5YTMwNGZkNzNiY2VjNGY1ZTE5M2YyOGI0ZjE4NzIzOTZjODkyOTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/ff66f6aed53b2bf079f9853c72b338cd8c759a6a","sha":"ff66f6aed53b2bf079f9853c72b338cd8c759a6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/ff66f6aed53b2bf079f9853c72b338cd8c759a6a"}],"sha":"49a304fd73bcec4f5e193f28b4f1872396c89292","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/49a304fd73bcec4f5e193f28b4f1872396c89292"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/ff66f6aed53b2bf079f9853c72b338cd8c759a6a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:20:13Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:20:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ux): start something (issue #540) (#553)\n\n* feat(ux): start something (issue #540)\n\nBring the four screens that start work to the approved drawing\n`5-start-something.html`, and show what planning cost.\n\n- The Room brief stops claiming nothing is spent; it reads \"The team starts\n  only when you press Start room.\"\n- The Room wait and the Workflow planning screen drop their invented steps,\n  bar and countdown for one spinner and the real elapsed time.\n- The Room proposal shows the Room''s saved `planningUsage` beside Start room,\n  drops the approval subtitles and hint, reads `Read this workspace`, and no\n  longer truncates member names.\n- A Workflow''s Review step shows `Planning this cost $0.012` from the loop''s\n  saved `planningUsage`.\n- The Catalog repo controls sit on one row, the model-tier chip names its\n  tier, and an entry''s Details lists the steps it runs.\n- Sizes, spacing and radii come from the theme''s existing ladder, so a theme\n  change carries through. No new token is introduced.\n\nPreviews render each real surface for the captures in `comparison.md`.\n\n* fix(ux): keep names capitalised in the access sentence\n\n`accessSentence()` lower-cased the composed access value, so a Room\nreaching GitHub read `Read github` and `Push github`. It now builds the\nsentence from the access facets with a verb per mode and a phrase per\ntarget, so names keep their capitals. A value with no mode is returned\nwith the sentence''s leading capital.\n\nCovered by `ui/__tests__/access-tile.test.ts`, which the drawing''s\nread-only case alone did not exercise.\n\n* fix(ux): address the round-1 review findings\n\nBlocking:\n\n- `accessSentence()` joined every mode into one verb list beside one target\n  list, so `edit-workspace` + `read-github` read \"Edit and read this\n  workspace and GitHub\" and `run-commands` alone read \"Run commands in\".\n  Each entry now becomes its own phrase, keeping the action with its target:\n  \"Edit this workspace and read GitHub\".\n- `PlannerWait` counted setInterval callbacks, so a delayed timer left the\n  clock behind the request (3.6s elapsed read as 0:02). It now measures from\n  the mount time and uses the interval only to refresh the display.\n\nNon-blocking, fixed:\n\n- The Workflow wait never appeared: `create` awaits the planner before the\n  draft id exists, so the wizard stayed on Describe through the whole call.\n  `CreateLoopWizard` now shows the wait while creating, which is what the new\n  requirement claims.\n- `apps/docs-site/docs/guide/rooms.md` described the removed five-step screen\n  and still claimed the time remaining. The prose now describes the spinner\n  and the real elapsed time, and the proposal''s planning cost.\n\n* fix(ux): address the round-2 review findings\n\n- `accessSentence()` left `reach-internet` and `other-tools` as bare\n  targets, so `read-workspace` + `other-tools` read \"Read this workspace and\n  other tools\" — unmapped tool access presented as read access. Each\n  target-only label now carries its own action: \"reach the internet\", \"use\n  other tools\".\n- `CreateLoopWizard` unmounted the Describe form while creating, so a failed\n  create returned an empty form. The form stays mounted and hidden while the\n  wait shows, keeping the prompt and settings the user entered.\n\n* chore(openspec): archive ux-start-something and sync its specs\n\nMove the completed change to `openspec/changes/archive/2026-09-22-ux-start-something/`\nand apply its delta to `openspec/specs/orchestrator-ui/spec.md`: one modified\nrequirement (the member list now covers the proposed team) and nine added\nrequirements for the Room brief, planner wait, planning cost, proposed team,\nCatalog repo row, model tier, Details steps, and the drawing rule.\n\n`openspec validate --specs --strict`: 25 specs, 0 failed.\n\n* fix(ux): clear the React Doctor warnings on this branch\n\nReact Doctor flagged three issues on changed lines. All are resolved; a local\n`react-doctor --scope changed` now reports 92/100, no issues.\n\n- `PlannerWait` initialized its timestamp with `useRef(Date.now())`, which\n  rebuilds the value on every render. It uses a lazy `useState` initializer.\n- `RoomProposal` had cyclomatic complexity 26. The adjust panel, recompute\n  diff, proposed team, action row and reasoning panel are now separate\n  components; the parent is a six-branch assembly.\n- `accessSentence` scanned the phrase array with `includes()` inside its loop.\n  It dedupes through a `Set`.\n\nNo behaviour change.","tree":{"sha":"aaed5ec3efff5b42f1e3c824048ff58cc3f63891","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/aaed5ec3efff5b42f1e3c824048ff58cc3f63891"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/ff66f6aed53b2bf079f9853c72b338cd8c759a6a","verification":{"payload":"tree aaed5ec3efff5b42f1e3c824048ff58cc3f63891\nparent 0e0863eb89212a022becaa68f3d822de0209a9d6\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790108413 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790108413 +0100\n\nfeat(ux): start something (issue #540) (#553)\n\n* feat(ux): start something (issue #540)\n\nBring the four screens that start work to the approved drawing\n`5-start-something.html`, and show what planning cost.\n\n- The Room brief stops claiming nothing is spent; it reads \"The team starts\n  only when you press Start room.\"\n- The Room wait and the Workflow planning screen drop their invented steps,\n  bar and countdown for one spinner and the real elapsed time.\n- The Room proposal shows the Room''s saved `planningUsage` beside Start room,\n  drops the approval subtitles and hint, reads `Read this workspace`, and no\n  l