o/commit/0e0863eb89212a022becaa68f3d822de0209a9d6","sha":"0e0863eb89212a022becaa68f3d822de0209a9d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/0e0863eb89212a022becaa68f3d822de0209a9d6"}],"sha":"ff66f6aed53b2bf079f9853c72b338cd8c759a6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/ff66f6aed53b2bf079f9853c72b338cd8c759a6a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/0e0863eb89212a022becaa68f3d822de0209a9d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T17:12:53Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T17:12:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ux): history and comparison (#552)\n\n* docs(openspec): plan the history and comparison UX change (#539)\n\nAdd the ux-history-and-comparison change for issue #539: History as its own\nview with saved subjects, the Room''s publish row and tab counts, and a run''s\nstep titles and stop reason.\n\nSpecs touch architect-project-record, architect-ui, orchestrator-run-record\nand orchestrator-ui, and add orchestrator-reflection.\n\n* feat(architect): record what a history entry is about\n\nAdd an optional subject and detail to HistoryEntry, and rewrite every\nhistory writer to save a name-first cause with the milestone, Workflow,\nRoom or decision it names. Entries written earlier keep their text and\ninvent no link.\n\n* feat(architect): open History as its own view\n\nAdd a history navigation mode and a milestone focus, a History view with a\ncentred timeline, day headings, per-entry dots, subject links, folded notes\nand Show earlier, and persist the folds through the host layout service.\nRemove the History disclosure from the project page''s right rail.\n\n* feat(orchestrator): name a run''s steps and its reason\n\nSave each visited step''s title on the run summary, print the run''s own stop\nreason in the chip, show the start as day, short month and time, and name the\nsteps by title with a fallback to the step id. Rows separate by a hairline and\nthe column labels are uppercase mono.\n\n* feat(orchestrator): show a Room''s counts and name its published artifact\n\nThe publish row names what was published and offers one Open control, the\nactivity filters and the Work, Claims and Artifacts tabs carry their counts,\nthe pills and tabs take the drawing''s treatment, and the brief ends at its\nlast field.\n\n* test(ux): capture the history-and-comparison surfaces\n\nAdd previews for the History view, a Room''s activity with its side panel, and\na Workflow''s attempt history, plus a fresh-record History read through the\nreal view. Record the captures, the fixed defects and the stated departures in\ncomparison.md.\n\n* docs(openspec): mark the history-and-comparison tasks complete\n\n* fix(ux): address the first review round\n\nPreserve each run''s step title by saving it on the visit, so a plan revision\ncannot rewrite the name a finished run ran under. Give the History view its\nown scroll region. Split the history recording into one shared appendHistory\nhelper and move evidenceIsStale beside worktreeFingerprint to keep the files\nwithin the 500-line limit. Fold a manual resume''s block reason, name a resumed\nresearch Workflow by its title, and update the Architect guide.\n\n* chore(openspec): archive the history-and-comparison change and sync its specs\n\nApply the five delta specs to the main specs (add orchestrator-reflection) and\nmove the completed change to openspec/changes/archive/2026-09-22-ux-history-and-comparison.\n\n* refactor(ui): clear the React Doctor findings\n\n- Split the preview harness Preview into a disclosure hook and one\n  component per render branch, so no React function carries the whole\n  multi-state tree.\n- Decompose ActivityRow into derived parts plus avatar, promoted-card and\n  sentence pieces.\n- Stop exporting the preview Room maps; they are only read in their own\n  module.","tree":{"sha":"4f6892d8c71009671d0c6927ca6c6b3375baa0d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/4f6892d8c71009671d0c6927ca6c6b3375baa0d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/0e0863eb89212a022becaa68f3d822de0209a9d6","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f6892d8c71009671d0c6927ca6c6b3375baa0d0\nparent 17e47590de53b9f686a6f978056849df50431430\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790097173 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790097173 +0100\n\nfeat(ux): history and comparison (#552)\n\n* docs(openspec): plan the history and comparison UX change (#539)\n\nAdd the ux-history-and-comparison change for issue #539: History as its own\nview with saved subjects, the Room''s publish row and tab counts, and a run''s\nstep titles and stop reason.\n\nSpecs touch architect-project-record, architect-ui, orchestrator-run-record\nand orchestrator-ui, and add orchestrator-reflection.\n\n* feat(architect): record what a history entry is about\n\nAdd an optional subject and detail to HistoryEntry, and rewrite every\nhistory writer to save a name-first cause with the milestone, Workflow,\nRoom or decision it names. Entries written earlier keep their text and\ninvent no link.\n\n* feat(architect): open History as its own view\n\nAdd a history navigation mode and a milestone focus, a History view with a\ncentred timeline, day headings, per-entry dots, subject links, folded notes\nand Show earlier, and persist the folds through the host layout service.\nRemove the History disclosure from the project page''s right rail.\n\n* feat(orchestrator): name a run''s steps and its reason\n\nSave each visited step''s title on the run summary, print the run''s own stop\nreason in the chip, show the start as day, short month and time, and name the\nsteps by title with a fallback to the step id. Rows separate by a hairline and\nthe column labels are uppercase mono.\n\n* feat(orchestrator): show a Room''s counts and name its published artifact\n\nThe publish row names what was published and offers one Open control, the\nactivity filters and the Work, Claims and Artifacts tabs carry their counts,\nthe pills and tabs take the drawing''s treatment, and the brief ends at its\nlast field.\n\n* test(ux): capture the history-and-comparison surfaces\n\nAdd previews for the History view, a Room''s activity with its side panel, and\na Workflow''s attempt history, plus a fresh-record History read through the\nreal view. Record the captures, the fixed defects and the stated departures in\ncomparison.md.\n\n* docs(openspec): mark the history-and-comparison tasks complete\n\n* fix(ux): address the first review round\n\nPreserve each run''s step title by saving it on the visit, so a plan revision\ncannot rewrite the name a finished run ran under. Give the History view its\nown scroll region. Split the history recording into one shared appendHistory\nhelper and move evidenceIsStale beside worktreeFingerprint to keep the files\nwithin the 500-line limit. Fold a manual resume''s block reason, name a resumed\nresearch Workflow by its title, and update the Architect guide.\n\n* chore(openspec): archive the history-and-comparison change and sync its specs\n\nApply the five delta specs to the main specs (add orchestrator-reflection) and\nmove the completed change to openspec/changes/archive/2026-09-22-ux-history-and-comparison.\n\n* refactor(ui): clear the React Doctor findings\n\n- Split the preview harness Preview into a disclosure hook and one\n  component per render branch, so no React function carries the whole\n  multi-state tree.\n- Decompose ActivityRow into derived parts plus avatar, promoted-card and\n  sentence pieces.\n- Stop exporting the preview Room maps; they are only read in their own\n  module.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsrcVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHjoQAD7RdIt97O7nWYxWD+jyqn5L\ngUqBszL62cZnujCJQeapHm1Jwb4sGD8eWQZwT18p8YbhinW3vr4h8P0j4t1tjlRb\n4DocF+TwIS7uDyYriCI2wWRur6D76qdwkSV/jqjBoJiarjxlKRo9zR9rMt23Acyy\nHVAOdgmJtJa3idedzNDITHbq0PxhPs6xpoFFUoQ0As0d8tq0bFvBHXp0LGzgAAKF\nICOTbnwC9/scu5EhlJrwJd2Wbk8XLoD2OWZMvAAStvTddkm+oSWPr7H+2IRP/muj\nS53VAN/sPgLGFmzxb1Ye4OezMt+5RZ2/dsOBos17ASdW1389dUiqoRoqlcw9BkK+\nCUxgZPrcZ1ztnb85+t4rCEq0/e7q5F3KMxY+JCuwYabJ3YdxDXRjFakAw+iOOSQR\nIzGe/dM5Y8bmuBM0PQfz3DYuYNa7CdpRIBu9A212+MtnyO/QVrBP+SvKaRYvW/W4\nPk1hdq9rp3wMd/eKkpn3IvUXqrWy85/texnWxaLf8OTu5jtXmA3wBrJHuQq1EwOj\nVw6MdVvbUm6e6bClo23pUUAroelI1jHGizU2ZbJYcf3AB+PdWJu0JAfns+x1u3l1\nYXDyFI9SCfrU3GXyvXLMjs+riTZNz2dHOFY7Z6hO0MXuH+fAaMBii6/b7u8Dj7CI\nE6B8q1km8Qxhfj8Pu3Uk\n=vg0s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T17:12:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/0e0863eb89212a022becaa68f3d822de0209a9d6","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDBlMDg2M2ViODkyMTJhMDIyYmVjYWE2OGYzZDgyMmRlMDIwOWE5ZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/17e47590de53b9f686a6f978056849df50431430","sha":"17e47590de53b9f686a6f978056849df50431430","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/17e47590de53b9f686a6f978056849df50431430"}],"sha":"0e0863eb89212a022becaa68f3d822de0209a9d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/0e0863eb89212a022becaa68f3d822de0209a9d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/17e47590de53b9f686a6f978056849df50431430/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:37:26Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:37:26Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"chore(openspec): archive the three UX changes and sync their specs\n\nArchives, in the order the changes themselves require:\n\n  2026-09-22-ux-activity-at-a-glance\n  2026-09-22-ux-act-on-it\n  2026-09-22-ux-read-the-outcome\n\nThe order is not cosmetic. All three modify `architect-ui` and\n`architect-project-record`, and `ux-read-the-outcome` REVERSES a rule the other\ntwo write: both of those say \"Retry step SHALL also be offered in the header with\nthe same effect as the control on the milestone\", and the last one says \"the\nheader SHALL offer the whole recovery control the milestone rail used to carry\n— and the milestone rail MUST NOT repeat it\". Archived in any other order, the\nearlier text wins and the spec no longer describes what shipped.\n\nVerified before each archive that the delta is a faithful base for the merge:\n`ux-read-the-outcome`''s \"Project page shows four parts\" is byte-identical to the\narchived `ux-act-on-it` version for its first 937 characters, differing only in\nthat final sentence and the \"Stopped step\" scenario. The merge keeps everything\nthe earlier change added — the cap scenario, the two-things-to-do scenario, the\n\"MAY carry a field\" sentence — and applies only that reversal.\n\nSpecs synced rather than skipped, so `openspec/specs/` describes what shipped:\n\n  new capabilities\n    activity-state               5 requirements\n    orchestrator-ui             20 (5 + 6 + 9 from the three changes, stacked)\n    workspace-attention          3\n    orchestrator-run-accounting  4\n    orchestrator-run-record      3\n    room-artifacts               4\n\n  existing capabilities\n    architect-ui                10 -> 14, including the reversal above\n    architect-project-record     5 -> 10\n    architect-model-overrides    5 -> 7\n    orchestrator-dispatch-handle 5 -> 6\n\n`orchestrator-ui` had no main spec before this, only deltas from three unarchived\nchanges; those deltas are now merged in order, which is why the archive had to\nhappen now rather than later.\n\nopenspec doctor: root ok. No active changes remain.","tree":{"sha":"f46dde7f02e2d5bb74bf0d9c98e836eca7b35e38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/f46dde7f02e2d5bb74bf0d9c98e836eca7b35e38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/17e47590de53b9f686a6f978056849df50431430","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/17e47590de53b9f686a6f978056849df50431430","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDE3ZTQ3NTkwZGU1M2I5ZjY4NmE2Zjk3ODA1Njg0OWRmNTA0MzE0MzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/7a52f9ef0d760d2997e2d15eac26eab92f12f407","sha":"7a52f9ef0d760d2997e2d15eac26eab92f12f407","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/7a52f9ef0d760d2997e2d15eac26eab92f12f407"}],"sha":"17e47590de53b9f686a6f978056849df50431430","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/17e47590de53b9f686a6f978056849df50431430"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/7a52f9ef0d760d2997e2d15eac26eab92f12f407/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:30:09Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:30:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ux): read the outcome (issue #538) (#550)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose read the outcome (issue #538)\n\nPlan the third change in the agent and workspace UX audit: when work finishes\nor stops, the result and the reason come first, said once.\n\nFour surfaces across the Orchestrator and Architect plugins:\n\n- A Workflow''s ending becomes one Result row above the settings for every\n  ending, with the request that started it opening from the objective.\n- A stopped milestone states the run''s own saved reason once, with the whole\n  recovery control in the header and no copy on the milestone row.\n- Milestone evidence reads as a list of checks, each command''s output behind\n  its own row.\n- A Room''s result leads with the result and the inline final plan; cost by\n  member is folded with full names; Delete Room moves into the more menu.\n- A member''s Info tab leads with model, tools, access and spend; an over-limit\n  member reads as a fault.\n\nThree behaviour fixes:\n\n- The run record keeps why a run ended and which steps a restart left in\n  flight, and an interrupted step stops reading as completed. The field\n  applies from now on; a run that already ended keeps its summary.\n- Line breaks the command surface escaped are decoded there, so only that path\n  is affected. Stored artifacts render their structure without being rewritten.\n- A member at or over its per-member limit uses the same fault rule the project\n  and the Room already use.\n\nNew capabilities: orchestrator-run-record, room-artifacts. Modified:\norchestrator-ui, architect-ui, architect-project-record. This change modifies\narchitect-ui''s \"Project page shows four parts\", which ux-act-on-it also\nmodifies, so those two changes must be archived before this one.\n\nThe binding drawing is\napps/styleguide/public/prototypes/agent-workspace-ux-audit/3-read-the-outcome.html.\n\nAn independent review of the first draft found a factual error in the frame-1\nrecord, a merged #537 requirement that forbade moving Retry step, a decode rule\nthat rewrote legitimate text, and that changing the run summary alone could not\nhave fixed the issue''s own example. The plan records the decisions those raised.\n\n* feat(ux): read the outcome (issue #538)\n\nMake the result and the reason the first thing on the page when work finishes\nor stops, said once, from the record.\n\nArchitect, the project header:\n\n- The reason now comes from the run''s own record instead of a sentence written\n  without one: the limit''s own text, a restart sentence composed from the\n  interrupted steps, or a plain statement that no cause was recorded.\n- The reason rides the activity line beside the state glyph, as the drawing has\n  it, and `stateLine` is left alone — that field is what the Architect reported\n  in its own words, and a stop reason is not something it said.\n- The whole recovery control moved from the milestone row into the header,\n  including a Workflow cap''s field and \"Approve cap and resume\". The row keeps\n  its title, its state and its Orchestrator link.\n- Evidence reads as one row per check, each owning its complete output, with a\n  duration only where the record holds one. The capture row runs the same\n  preview action the preview card does.\n\nOrchestrator, the Workflow page:\n\n- One Result row above the settings for every ending, replacing the card that\n  led with a status word the state line already carried.\n- The request that started the Workflow opens from a disclosure on the\n  objective, for every Workflow, so a Workflow with both no longer says the\n  objective twice and one with neither says nothing.\n- A file named in a result opens from its row; a reference the host cannot open\n  stays plain text.\n\nOrchestrator, a Room''s result:\n\n- The result is the Room''s own closing line, then the Conductor''s plan open at\n  its first section with the author''s others folded. Duration, spend, team and\n  artifact counts left the body; the team is the roster and the artifacts are\n  listed.\n- Cost by member folds with full names, no bars, and the total in its summary.\n- Delete Room moved into the Room''s ⋯ menu.\n\nOrchestrator, a member''s Info tab:\n\n- Model, tools, access and spend lead. Turns, tokens, retries, compactions and\n  skills fold behind Usage, and \"no worktree\" is an access fact rather than a\n  card of its own.\n\nThree behaviour fixes:\n\n- The per-run summary retains why a run ended and which steps a restart left in\n  flight, and an interrupted step no longer reads as completed. Applies from now\n  on; a run that already ended keeps the summary it was written with.\n- Line breaks the Room command surface escaped are decoded there, so only that\n  path is affected. Stored artifacts render their structure without being\n  rewritten.\n- A member at or over its per-member limit uses the same fault rule as a project\n  and a Room. `spendTone` and `spendRatio` moved to `@sero-ai/common` so the\n  three surfaces share one rule; the Architect re-exports them.\n\nReview of the captures found six defects no test in this change caught: the\nmember Info tab right-aligned and truncated every value, the spend ring had no\ncolumn of its own, ACCESS read lower-case, `Delivered` printed a raw locale\nstamp and the raw destination id, the plan card rendered no sections at all\nbecause the preview harness lost its bridge, and one capture was clipped. All\nsix are fixed. Frame 2 of the drawing has no preview and was not compared side\nby side; that gap is recorded in `comparison.md`.\n\nNew capabilities: orchestrator-run-record, room-artifacts. Modified:\norchestrator-ui, architect-ui, architect-project-record.\n\n* fix(ux): resolve the three blocking review findings\n\nRound 1 of 3. Codex returned red on three correctness defects; all three are\nconfirmed in source and fixed here.\n\n1. The retry move lost a supported recovery path. The header retry required\n   `retryStepId`, which the time-limit writer clears, so a time-limit stop had\n   neither the header control nor the one removed from the milestone row. The\n   same pass also discarded the returned error and had no pending state, so a\n   refusal was invisible.\n\n   The recovery is now one control the header owns: `RetryWorkflowControl` runs\n   `actions.retry` with no cap — which retries the step when the record names\n   one and restarts the Workflow when it does not — and carries its own pending\n   state and its own refusal output. `useHeaderActions` returns nothing for a\n   stopped dispatch so it appears exactly once, beside the reason it answers.\n\n2. The new ⋯ menu was clipped. It was an absolutely-positioned div inside the\n   50px `overflow-hidden` Room top bar, so Delete Room fell outside the visible\n   area. It now uses the shared `DropdownMenu` — a portal, so no clipping, with\n   the keyboard and focus behaviour every other menu in the product has.\n   `DeleteConfirmationButton` gained an optional controlled mode so the menu can\n   own the trigger while the same AlertDialog still asks first, with the same\n   copy about preserved worktrees.\n\n3. The restart sentence could name the wrong step. It used the step''s position\n   in the run''s activation list, but that is the order steps happened to run:\n   a run that executed plan steps 1 and 3 and was interrupted on the third\n   reported \"step 2\". The number now comes from the PLAN. `toRunSummary` takes\n   the plan''s step ids and records each step''s `planIndex`; `loop-store` passes\n   them at every write. When no plan position was recorded, the sentence states\n   no number rather than guessing one.\n\nTwo type errors the fixes introduced were caught by `pnpm typecheck` and fixed:\n`runs.map(toRunSummary)` in `spend-agreement.test.ts` was passing the array\nindex as `planStepIds` in three places, and the new control asked for a `busy`\nprop `ProjectPage` does not have — it owns its own pending state instead.\n\nChecks: root typecheck 29/29, orchestrator 1616 passed, architect 555 passed.\n\n* docs(agents): how to capture a UI surface for review\n\nThe preview harness exists to give a browser a URL to screenshot, but nothing\nrecorded how to use it for a review or the traps that cost time doing it.\n\nCovers the loop (add a preview that renders the real component, start the\nharness, screenshot by id, read the PNG, capture the drawing, open every fold on\nboth sides) and the traps:\n\n- screenshot at a viewport wider than the panel, or the right edge is clipped;\n- a fixture that sets the host bridge with `??=` loses to one that got there\n  first, and the surface renders with its data silently missing — this is what\n  made the Room''s plan card show no sections while every test passed;\n- Playwright''s CLI and its module are separate installs with separate browser\n  builds;\n- ImageMagick is not installed, so compose sheets in the browser;\n- Radix menus and dialogs portal, so query `document.body`.\n\nEnds with what captures caught on ux-read-the-outcome that no test did.\n\n* fix(ui): clear the react-doctor warnings from this PR\n\nReact Doctor went 85/100 with 10 warnings to 93/100 with none. All ten were in\ncode this PR introduced or touched.\n\nKeys no longer come from a list position:\n\n- `ArtifactProse` keyed every span and every line by its index, which re-keys\n  the whole list when one line is inserted. Both now use a name derived from the\n  part''s own text plus how many identical ones came before, via a new\n  `partKeys` in `ui/lib/artifact-document.ts` — a document can repeat a rule or\n  a heading, so the text alone is not unique.\n- `RoomCompletion` keyed each plan section the same way, and now names them the\n  same way.\n- `Evidence` keyed each check by `name:index`; `EvidenceCheck` now carries a\n  `key` built the same way, computed at the end of `evidenceLines`.\n- `StepCard`''s file references were keyed by index; they are now keyed by where\n  each part starts in the text, which is the identity `WithCode` beside it\n  already used.\n\nOne performance rule: the run-index test cloned with\n`JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(…))`. Cloning is now `structuredClone`, and the\n\"written before this change\" case parses an actual on-disk JSON document, so it\npins the old shape rather than restating a literal.\n\nOne complexity rule on `RoomRoster`''s `MemberRow`. The function is identical on\n`main`, so the warning was pre-existing and merely reported because this PR\ntouches the file. Reduced anyway, with no behaviour change: the four facts a row\nreads about a member moved into `memberFacts`, and the three-way row tone into\n`rowTone`.\n\nChecks: react-doctor 93/100 no issues, root typecheck 29/29, orchestrator 1616\npassed, architect 555 passed.","tree":{"sha":"18a56b20847ba9d925bf65681532c7e61e952656","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/18a56b20847ba9d925bf65681532c7e61e952656"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/7a52f9ef0d760d2997e2d15eac26eab92f12f407","verification":{"payload":"tree 18a56b20847ba9d925bf65681532c7e61e952656\nparent 90ee3c3e765f9a1c6ed7a7ba6570f0ac26dbcc4f\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790058609 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790058609 +0100\n\nfeat(ux): read the outcome (issue #538) (#550)\n\n* docs(openspec): propose read the outcome (issue #538)\n\nPlan the third change in the agent and workspace UX audit: when work finishes\nor stops, the result and the reason come first, said once.\n\nFour surfaces across the Orchestrator and Architect plugins:\n\n- A Workflow''s ending becomes one Result row above the settings for every\n  ending, with the request that started it opening from the objective.\n- A stopped milestone states the run''s own saved reason once, with the whole\n  recovery control in the header and no copy on the milestone row.\n- Milestone evidence reads as a list of checks, each command''s output behind\n  its own row.\n- A Room''s result leads with the result and the inline final plan; cost by\n  member is folded with full names; Delete Room moves into the more menu.\n- A member''s Info tab leads with model, tools, access and spend; an over-limit\n  member reads as a fault.\n\nThree behaviour fixes:\n\n- The run record keeps why a run ended and which steps a restart left in\n  flight, and an interrupted step stops reading as completed. The field\n  applies from now on; a run that already ended keeps its summary.\n- Line breaks the command surface escaped are decoded there, so only that path\n  is affected. Stored artifacts render their structure without being rewritten.\n- A member at or over its per-member limit uses the same fault rule the project\n  and the Room already use.\n\nNew capabilities: orchestrator-run-record, room-artifacts. Modified:\norchestrator-ui, architect-ui, architect-project-record. This change modifies\narchitect-ui''s \"Project page shows four parts\", which ux-act-on-it also\nmodifies, so those two changes must be archived before this one.\n\nThe binding drawing is\napps/styleguide/public/prototypes/agent-workspace-ux-audit/3-read-the-outcome.html.\n\nAn independent review of the first draft found a factual error in the frame-1\nrecord, a merged #537 requirement that forbade moving Retry step, a decode rule\nthat rewrote legitimate text, and that changing the run summary alone could not\nhave fixed the issue''s own example. The plan records the decisions those raised.\n\n* feat(ux): read the outcome (issue #538)\n\nMake the result and the reason the first thing on the page when work finishes\nor stops, said once, from the record.\n\nArchitect, the project header:\n\n- The reason now comes from the run''s own record instead of a sentence written\n  without one: the limit''s own text, a restart sentence composed from the\n  interrupted steps, or a plain statement that no cause was recorded.\n- The reason rides the activity line beside the state glyph, as the drawing has\n  it, and `stateLine` is left alone — that field is what the Architect reported\n  in its own words, and a stop reason is not something it said.\n- The whole recovery control moved from the milestone row into the header,\n  including a Workflow cap''s field and \"Approve cap and resume\". The row keeps\n  its title, its state and its Orchestrator link.\n- Evidence reads as one row per check, each owning its complete output, with a\n  duration only where the record holds one. The capture row runs the same\n  preview action the preview card does.\n\nOrchestrator, the Workflow page:\n\n- One Result row above the settings for every ending, replacing the card that\n  led with a status word the state line already carried.\n- The request that started the Workflow opens from a disclosure on the\n  objective, for every Workflow, so a Workflow with both no longer says the\n  objective twice and one with neither says nothing.\n- A file named in a result opens from its row; a reference the host cannot open\n  stays plain text.\n\nOrchestrator, a Room''s result:\n\n- The result is the Room''s own closing line, then the Conductor''s plan open at\n  its first section with the author''s others folded. Duration, spend, team and\n  artifact counts left the body; the team is the roster and the artifacts are\n  listed.\n- Cost by member folds with full names, no bars, and the total in its summary.\n- Delete Room moved into the Room''s ⋯ menu.\n\nOrchestrator, a member''s Info tab:\n\n- Model, tools, access and spend lead. Turns, tokens, retries, compactions and\n  skills fold behind Usage, and \"no worktree\" is an access fact rather than a\n  card of its own.\n\nThree behaviour fixes:\n\n- The per-run summary retains why a run ended and which steps a restart left in\n  flight, and an interrupted step no longer reads as completed. Applies from now\n  on; a run that already ended keeps the summary it was written with.\n- Line breaks the Room command surface escaped are decoded there, so only that\n  path is affected. Stored artifacts render their structure without being\n  rewritten.\n- A member at or over its per-member limit uses the same fault rule as a project\n  and a Room. `spendTone` and `spendRatio` moved to `@sero-ai/common` so the\n  three surfaces share one rule; the Architect re-exports them.\n\nReview of the captures found six defects no test in this change caught: the\nmember Info tab right-aligned and truncated every value, the spend ring had no\ncolumn of its own, ACCESS read lower-case, `Delivered` printed a raw locale\nstamp and the raw destination id, the plan card rendered no sections at all\nbecause the preview harness lost its bridge, and one capture was clipped. All\nsix are fixed. Frame 2 of the drawing has no preview and was not compared side\nby side; that gap is recorded in `comparison.md`.\n\nNew capabilities: orchestrator-run-record, room-artifacts. Modified:\norchestrator-ui, architect-ui, architect-project-record.\n\n* fix(ux): resolve the three blocking review findings\n\nRound 1 of 3. Codex returned red on three correctness defects; all three are\nconfirmed in source and fixed here.\n\n1. The retry move lost a supported recovery path. The header retry required\n   `retryStepId`, which the time-limit writer clears, so a time-limit stop had\n   neither the header control nor the one removed from the milestone row. The\n   same pass also discarded the returned error and had no pending state, so a\n   refusal was invisible.\n\n   The recovery is now one control the header owns: `RetryWorkflowControl` runs\n   `actions.retry` with no cap — which retries the step when the record names\n   one and restarts the Workflow when it does not — and carries its own pending\n   state and its own refusal output. `useHeaderActions` returns nothing for a\n   stopped dispatch so it appears exactly once, beside the reason it answers.\n\n2. The new ⋯ menu was clipped. It was an absolutely-positioned div inside the\n   50px `overflow-hidden` Room top bar, so Delete Room fell outside the visible\n   area. It now uses the shared `DropdownMenu` — a portal, so no clipping, with\n   the keyboard and focus behaviour every other menu in the product has.\n   `DeleteConfirmationButton` gained an optional controlled mode so the menu can\n   own the trigger while the same AlertDialog still asks first, with the same\n   copy about preserved worktrees.\n\n3. The restart sentence could name the wrong step. It used the step''s position\n   in the run''s activation list, but that is the order steps happened to run:\n   a run that executed plan steps 1 and 3 and was interrupted on the third\n   reported \"step 2\". The number now comes from the PLAN. `toRunSummary` takes\n   the plan''s step ids and records each step''s `planIndex`; `loop-store` passes\n   them at every write. When no plan position was recorded, the sentence states\n   no number rather than guessing one.\n\nTwo type errors the fixes introduced were caught by `pnpm typecheck` and fixed:\n`runs.map(toRunSummary)` in `spend-agreement.test.ts` was passing the array\nindex as `planStepIds` in three places, and the new control asked for a `busy`\nprop `ProjectPage` does not have — it owns its own pending state instead.\n\nChecks: root typecheck 29/29, orchestrator 1616 passed, architect 555 passed.\n\n* docs(agents): how to capture a UI surface for review\n\nThe preview harness exists to give a browser a URL to screenshot, but nothing\nrecorded how to use it for a review or the traps that cost time doing it.\n\nCovers the loop (add a preview that renders the real component, start the\nharness, screenshot by id, read the PNG, capture the drawing, open every fold on\nboth sides) and the traps:\n\n- screenshot at a viewport wider than the panel, or the right edge is clipped;\n- a fixture that sets the host bridge with `??=` loses to one that got there\n  first, and the surface renders with its data silently missing — this is what\n  made the Room''s plan card show no sections while every test passed;\n- Playwright''s CLI and its module are separate installs with separate browser\n  builds;\n- ImageMagick is not installed, so compose sheets in the browser;\n- Radix menus and dialogs portal, so query `document.body`.\n\nEnds with what captures caught on ux-read-the-outcome that no test did.\n\n* fix(ui): clear the react-doctor warnings from this PR\n\nReact Doctor went 85/100 with 10 warnings to 93/100 with none. All ten were in\ncode this PR introduced or touched.\n\nKeys no longer come from a list position:\n\n- `ArtifactProse` keyed every span and every line by its index, which re-keys\n  the whole list when one line is inserted. Both now use a name derived from the\n  part''s own text plus how many identical ones came before, via a new\n  `partKeys` in `ui/lib/artifact-document.ts` — a document can repeat a rule or\n  a heading, so the text alone is not unique.\n- `RoomCompletion` keyed each plan section the same way, and now names them the\n  same way.\n- `Evidence` keyed each check by `name:index`; `EvidenceCheck` now carries a\n  `key` built the same way, computed at the end of `evidenceLines`.\n- `StepCard`''s file references were keyed by index; they are now keyed by where\n  each part starts in the text, which is the identity `WithCode` beside it\n  already used.\n\nOne performance rule: the run-index test cloned with\n`JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(…))`. Cloning is now `structuredClone`, and the\n\"written before this change\" case parses an actual on-disk JSON document, so it\npins the old shape rather than restating a literal.\n\nOne complexity rule on `RoomRoster`''s `MemberRow`. The function is identical on\n`main`, so the warning was pre-existing and merely reported because this PR\ntouches the file. Reduced anyway, with no behaviour change: the four facts a row\nreads about a member moved into `memberFacts`, and the three-way row tone into\n`rowTone`.\n\nChecks: react-doctor 93/100 no issues, root typecheck 29/29, orchestrator 1616\npassed, architect 555 passed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsiBxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfz0QAEvPOEy1yZxRqgF4R2Mt/var\n2HUbXCK6F6JGutnQ7R786sF6E0ia3tR9QT+3wU8Tbp1XgsnRlP6XhqHoRBXb11CX\nIFZoEbq39HMgQTDhP30RIQWAciWEpnQ1C3HICtTvlDrjXEmt64Cphe4+20BxYPEM\n4w5OQ7/tunnYOyEzf/92VLyVsgAAa1kI3z000OpZw7b+RoBQSzc/qedtuLssJ3yp\n2fZdXuOEqXqBaBNPrTsALOpWPxybBLlketZKT2CMlejAgQNg7RfZQV7TXU7WxxLJ\nzUD+BIOSL1hG9fGE12Bj6kmK2KYT6wiOVrWdb4VX5mQsaNWsNieHFdEcsABSAmEQ\n5WVTrmRLj9lI8QMdCmqvTdMEvXEFZByKNQzJolwJpnJYJ/3XaOpw0HYqBQZ+XYNL\nGJ9jVTDd4Ya1IGH/e2oRp461FzuJrZb4MHNUIS9C33ZMsTbdxSc+akgBTtJaL3kt\njMiKDS9keCoRz0Uv8g6XPpvsEDoVbswlcBTb+XyA+1yNtiEA52mmA7QxdeVPVwMH\nWLsrr1E0c47YPCtu/Qrv2vn1zby4LkT54tDKqBDx/+LAFgcACPPES13MJreQn3xH\nVFry0sutbuK5cBBZUt/8f8Cy+Npc8EwR1Kan33rdM9um71pgrI9XqSXcFMmzS5wq\nDK1NgEVUFGH9oL0H6dUw\n=5x7E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T06:30:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/7a52f9ef0d760d2997e2d15eac26eab92f12f407","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDdhNTJmOWVmMGQ3NjBkMjk5N2UyZDE1ZWFjMjZlYWI5MmYxMmY0MDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/90ee3c3e765f9a1c6ed7a7ba6570f0ac26dbcc4f","sha":"90ee3c3e765f9a1c6ed7a7ba6570f0ac26dbcc4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/90ee3c3e765f9a1c6ed7a7ba6570f0ac26dbcc4f"}],"sha":"7a52f9ef0d760d2997e2d15eac26eab92f12f407","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/7a52f9ef0d760d2997e2d15eac26eab92f12f407"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/90ee3c3e765f9a1c6ed7a7ba6570f0ac26dbcc4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:41:45Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:41:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: act on it (issue #537) (#549)\n\n* docs(openspec): add the ux-act-on-it change for issue 537\n\nPlans proposal 2 of the agent and workspace UX audit: a stopped project\nleads with what stopped and carries the control that fixes it, a\ncancelled research Room is named and explained, a Room states its hold\nonce, and the Workflow page gains a labelled settings line.\n\nTwo figures are corrected to match the limits that enforce them. A\nWorkflow''s spend reads the total maxCostUsd is tested against, which is\nthe larger figure Home already shows, not the run-only sum the Workflow\npage derives. This reverses decision 4 on the issue. A Room''s elapsed\ntime counts accumulated active time in the engine as well as on screen,\nfollowing the pattern Goals already use.\n\nAdds the two drawn layout options the proposal could not answer, and\nrecords which was chosen.\n\n* fix(orchestrator): show the spend and the elapsed time the limits enforce\n\nA Workflow''s spend read lower on its own page than on Home, because the\npage summed only the runs while maxCostUsd counts planning, reflection\nand every run. lifetimeUsage() in shared/usage.ts is now the single\nderivation the limit check, the index and the page all call.\n\nA Room''s elapsed time and its maxWallClockMs both measured the wall\nclock since startedAt, so a Room paused nine days against a one-hour\nlimit read \"229h 28m of 1h\" and could not be resumed without an\nextension. Rooms now accumulate active time the way Goals already do:\nwithRoomStatus banks or reopens the period on every status change, and\nthe limit check, resume and the header read that figure. A record with\nno accumulator is seeded from its wall clock, so an existing Room keeps\nthe time it has used rather than being handed a fresh budget.\n\nTasks 1.1-1.6 of openspec/changes/ux-act-on-it.\n\n* feat(architect): save why a research Room stopped, and name it\n\nA block on delegated work was one sentence in blockedReason carrying the\nRoom''s id, its status and an instruction. The project page could only\nshow the id, and why the Room could not run commands was one line among\nsixty-four History entries.\n\nThe record now holds a BlockedWork: what the work is called, the state it\nended in, when, and the cause when a research-access decision recorded\none. observeResearchRooms saves the title it already had in hand, and\nunblock clears it. A record written before these fields still renders\nfrom the sentence.\n\nThe planning-attempt count is not used as a cause: it counts attempts to\nplan the Room, not times the Room stopped.\n\nTasks 2.1-2.4 of openspec/changes/ux-act-on-it.\n\n* feat(architect): put the control that fixes the stop beside the sentence\n\nThe cap strip was the second card down, under a heading that said\nnothing needed the user. The project header now carries the controls for\nthe state it names: the new-cap field and Raise and resume at the cap,\nand Open Room plus \"Tell Architect what to do next\" when delegated work\nstopped without reporting.\n\nStateLine takes a set of actions and an optional field, because raising\na cap needs a number rather than a confirmation. Every control here also\nexists where it did before, so nothing is only reachable from the\nheader, and LimitBanner is gone rather than duplicated.\n\n\"Tell Architect what to do next\" focuses the existing directive box. It\nis a way into that box, not a second way to send one.\n\nTasks 3.1-3.4 of openspec/changes/ux-act-on-it.\n\n* feat(architect,orchestrator): say which kind of nothing, once\n\n\"Needs you · none\" was a heading, a count label and a card reading \"You\nhave nothing to review.\" The section is now absent while it is empty and\nreturns with its controls as soon as it holds something; whether the\nproject is paused is already on the header and the projects list.\n\nMilestones that do not exist yet say what produces them once, in the\nsection header, instead of repeating it in a dashed card.\n\nA Room whose saved events did not arrive said \"Nothing has happened\nyet.\" It now says the activity is not available and how many events are\nsaved, which is the difference between unreadable and empty.\n\nTasks 4.1-4.4 of openspec/changes/ux-act-on-it.\n\n* feat(orchestrator,architect): say what a thing is set to, under a label\n\nThe Workflow page carried its settings as seven icon chips, and the two\nsettings the user can change sat in a separate row of buttons below them.\nEach value now sits under a label that names it, and Context and Delivery\nopen from the value itself. Queued events and source health move to the\nWorkflow''s state line, because they say why nothing has happened, not what\nthe user chose.\n\nSteps lead with their Result. The instruction, the expected result and the\nmarks that place the step in the plan open from a chevron; a step whose\nroute was not taken reads \"Not taken\" from the same rule that dims it on the\nMap; the loop-back is drawn on the plan rail instead of a banner naming two\nstep ids. Delete moves into More actions, away from Run again.\n\nA Room on hold asks once. One card holds the question, the members'' own\nwords and the three controls, replacing a stop banner, a Read it strip and\nthree duplicate buttons in the header. The header drops its status dot and\nits turns-active count, which the Team roster already says in words.\n\nProject models states the owner as a row of the tier table, carrying the\nsource and the tier it outranks out of the resolver and onto the record. A\ntier that inherits a global it cannot read says so, instead of asking the\nuser to choose something that is neither missing nor theirs. The saving\nrules go behind one disclosure.\n\n* feat(orchestrator): draw the Workflow page as the approved drawing sets it\n\nThe Workflow page now follows frame 4 of 2-act-on-it.html in its plain,\nTune, loop-back and branches states.\n\nOne top row holds the back link, the title and every control once. The\ntitle''s status badge, the \"Plan\" fold and the completion card for a\ncomplete Workflow are gone, because the page already said each of them.\nA complete Workflow also drops the state line: every step reads Done and\nthe Attempt history fold counts the runs.\n\nplanStages() classifies each dependency level as a single step, steps that\nrun together, a branch or a mix, and Map and Details both draw from it.\nGroups are a dashed box with the group''s icon on the rail, and the\nloop-back bracket gets the width its hooks need.\n\nA step is the drawing''s compact card: the Result under the title, the\nlabelled facts behind the chevron, and Model, Agent and Tools behind Tune,\nwhich now use the styled Select. The card no longer shows the model or the\nexecution target.\n\nThe settings values that open something have a dotted underline and a\npointer, and so does the back link. Reflect all leaves the Workflows tab;\neach Workflow has its own Reflect, and agents keep reflect_workspace.\n\ncomparison.md records every departure from the drawing and why.\n\n* refactor(ui): use the styled Select instead of native selects\n\nA native select draws the operating system''s control and looks out of\nplace beside the rest of a Sero surface. The local model editor, the admin\nagent editor, the git pull request pane and the styleguide theme picker now\nuse the Select from @sero-ai/ui. An unset choice uses a sentinel value or a\nplaceholder, because Radix refuses an empty item value.\n\nNativeSelect stays in @sero-ai/ui because the published package exports it.\n\n* feat(architect,desktop): open the project and its folder from where they are named\n\nThe workspace tree''s attention icon opens the Architect project page when\nthe attention comes from a project, as one history entry. An icon raised by\na Workflow or a Room opens nothing, as before. The project header''s\nworkspace path opens the folder through the host''s showItemInFolder.\n\nProject models, the inspector''s View picker and the intake model overrides\nuse the styled Select. The Effective column and the owner row name the\nmodel only; the thinking picker beside them already says the level. The\nArchitect tests drive a small Select stand-in, because jsdom cannot open\nthe Radix popover.\n\n* fix(orchestrator,architect,desktop): address PR 549 review\n\n- Room hold: one roomControls rule feeds the card and the header. Resume\n  shows only on a paused Room with no open approval, and Stop stays on a\n  delivery a restart interrupted.\n- Active time: starting no longer spends the budget, and restart recovery\n  seeds a legacy record once so a paused Room''s clock stops growing.\n- openGlobalAppView cancels a pending switch to another app.\n- A research stop no longer names an access decision whose answer\n  granted the access.\n- block() without `on` clears blockedOn; drop an unused import; the docs\n  no longer point at Reflect all.\n\n* refactor(orchestrator): split the Workflow and Room hold components React Doctor flagged\n\nMove the hold card''s wording and namesSentence to lib/room-hold.ts and\nthe state line''s working to lib/loop-state-line.ts. Split the step\nheader, Tune panel, Workflow top row and notices into their own\ncomponents. Key code spans by their offset in the text, not the index.\n\n* test(desktop): remove two races that failed CI on unrelated changes\n\n- The Qwen reasoning test shared a fixed /tmp folder and removed it while\n  the runtime could still write into it. It now uses a folder per run and\n  retries the removal.\n- The removed-capture test deleted the folder once combined.log existed,\n  while the stdout write could still be in flight, which reported a write\n  failure instead of the missing file. It now waits for both files to\n  hold every byte.","tree":{"sha":"2cc118e88f6458e30fb187f33f65edf009a6c815","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/2cc118e88f6458e30fb187f33f65edf009a6c815"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/90ee3c3e765f9a1c6ed7a7ba6570f0ac26dbcc4f","verification":{"payload":"tree 2cc118e88f6458e30fb187f33f65edf009a6c815\nparent fd826e92c2ec21982b98cc74b1e4551c40e03167\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1790019705 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790019705 +0100\n\nfeat: act on it (issue #537) (#549)\n\n* docs(openspec): add the ux-act-on-it change for issue 537\n\nPlans proposal 2 of the agent and workspace UX audit: a stopped project\nleads with what stopped and carries the control that fixes it, a\ncancelled research Room is named and explained, a Room states its hold\nonce, and the Workflow page gains a labelled settings line.\n\nTwo figures are corrected to match the limits that enforce them. A\nWorkflow''s spend reads the total maxCostUsd is tested against, which is\nthe larger figure Home already shows, not the run-only sum the Workflow\npage derives. This reverses decision 4 on the issue. A Room''s elapsed\ntime counts accumulated active time in the engine as well as on screen,\nfollowing the pattern Goals already use.\n\nAdds the two drawn layout options the proposal could not answer, and\nrecords which was chosen.\n\n* fix(orchestrator): show the spend and the elapsed time the limits enforce\n\nA Workflow''s spend read lower on its own page than on Home, because the\npage summed only the runs while maxCostUsd counts planning, reflection\nand every run. lifetimeUsage() in shared/usage.ts is now the single\nderivation the limit check, the index and the page all call.\n\nA Room''s elapsed time and its maxWallClockMs both measured the wall\nclock since startedAt, so a Room paused nine days against a one-hour\nlimit read \"229h 28m of 1h\" and could not be resumed without an\nextension. Rooms now accumulate active time the way Goals already do:\nwithRoomStatus banks or reopens the period on every status change, and\nthe limit check, resume and the header read that figure. A record with\nno accumulator is seeded from its wall clock, so an existing Room keeps\nthe time it has used rather than being handed a fresh budget.\n\nTasks 1.1-1.6 of openspec/changes/ux-act-on-it.\n\n* feat(architect): save why a research Room stopped, and name it\n\nA block on delegated work was one sentence in blockedReason carrying the\nRoom''s id, its status and an instruction. The project page could only\nshow the id, and why the Room could not run commands was one line among\nsixty-four History entries.\n\nThe record now holds a BlockedWork: what the work is called, the state it\nended in, when, and the cause when a research-access decision recorded\none. observeResearchRooms saves the title it already had in hand, and\nunblock clears it. A record written before these fields still renders\nfrom the sentence.\n\nThe planning-attempt count is not used as a cause: it counts attempts to\nplan the Room, not times the Room stopped.\n\nTasks 2.1-2.4 of openspec/changes/ux-act-on-it.\n\n* feat(architect): put the control that fixes the stop beside the sentence\n\nThe cap strip was the second card down, under a heading that said\nnothing needed the user. The project header now carries the controls for\nthe state it names: the new-cap field and Raise and resume at the cap,\nand Open Room plus \"Tell Architect what to do next\" when delegated work\nstopped without reporting.\n\nStateLine takes a set of actions and an optional field, because raising\na cap needs a number rather than a confirmation. Every control here also\nexists where it did before, so nothing is only reachable from the\nheader, and LimitBanner is gone rather than duplicated.\n\n\"Tell Architect what to do next\" focuses the existing directive box. It\nis a way into that box, not a second way to send one.\n\nTasks 3.1-3.4 of openspec/changes/ux-act-on-it.\n\n* feat(architect,orchestrator): say which kind of nothing, once\n\n\"Needs you · none\" was a heading, a count label and a card reading \"You\nhave nothing to review.\" The section is now absent while it is empty and\nreturns with its controls as soon as it holds something; whether the\nproject is paused is already on the header and the projects list.\n\nMilestones that do not exist yet say what produces them once, in the\nsection header, instead of repeating it in a dashed card.\n\nA Room whose saved events did not arrive said \"Nothing has happened\nyet.\" It now says the activity is not available and how many events are\nsaved, which is the difference between unreadable and empty.\n\nTasks 4.1-4.4 of openspec/changes/ux-act-on-it.\n\n* feat(orchestrator,architect): say what a thing is set to, under a label\n\nThe Workflow page carried its settings as seven icon chips, and the two\nsettings the user can change sat in a separate row of buttons below them.\nEach value now sits under a label that names it, and Context and Delivery\nopen from the value itself. Queued events and source health move to the\nWorkflow''s state line, because they say why nothing has happened, not what\nthe user chose.\n\nSteps lead with their Result. The instruction, the expected result and the\nmarks that place the step in the plan open from a chevron; a step whose\nroute was not taken reads \"Not taken\" from the same rule that dims it on the\nMap; the loop-back is drawn on the plan rail instead of a banner naming two\nstep ids. Delete moves into More actions, away from Run again.\n\nA Room on hold asks once. One card holds the question, the members'' own\nwords and the three controls, replacing a stop banner, a Read it strip and\nthree duplicate buttons in the header. The header drops its status dot and\nits turns-active count, which the Team roster already says in words.\n\nProject models states the owner as a row of the tier table, carrying the\nsource and the tier it outranks out of the resolver and onto the record. A\ntier that inherits a global it cannot read says so, instead of asking the\nuser to choose something that is neither missing nor theirs. The saving\nrules go behind one disclosure.\n\n* feat(orchestrator): draw the Workflow page as the approved drawing sets it\n\nThe Workflow page now follows frame 4 of 2-act-on-it.html in its plain,\nTune, loop-back and branches states.\n\nOne top row holds the back link, the title and every control once. The\ntitle''s status badge, the \"Plan\" fold and the completion card for a\ncomplete Workflow are gone, because the page already said each of them.\nA complete Workflow also drops the state line: every step reads Done and\nthe Attempt history fold counts the runs.\n\nplanStages() classifies each dependency level as a single step, steps that\nrun together, a branch or a mix, and Map and Details both draw from it.\nGroups are a dashed box with the group''s icon on the rail, and the\nloop-back bracket gets the width its hooks need.\n\nA step is the drawing''s compact card: the Result under the title, the\nlabelled facts behind the chevron, and Model, Agent and Tools behind Tune,\nwhich now use the styled Select. The card no longer shows the model or the\nexecution target.\n\nThe settings values that open something have a dotted underline and a\npointer, and so does the back link. Reflect all leaves the Workflows tab;\neach Workflow has its own Reflect, and agents keep reflect_workspace.\n\ncomparison.md records every departure from the drawing and why.\n\n* refactor(ui): use the styled Select instead of native selects\n\nA native select draws the operating system''s control and looks out of\nplace beside the rest of a Sero surface. The local model editor, the admin\nagent editor, the git pull request pane and the styleguide theme picker now\nuse the Select from @sero-ai/ui. An unset choice uses a sentinel value or a\nplaceholder, because Radix refuses an empty item value.\n\nNativeSelect stays in @sero-ai/ui because the published package exports it.\n\n* feat(architect,desktop): open the project and its folder from where they are named\n\nThe workspace tree''s attention icon opens the Architect project page when\nthe attention comes from a project, as one history entry. An icon raised by\na Workflow or a Room opens nothing, as before. The project header''s\nworkspace path opens the folder through the host''s showItemInFolder.\n\nProject models, the inspector''s View picker and the intake model overrides\nuse the styled Select. The Effective column and the owner row name the\nmodel only; the thinking picker beside them already says the level. The\nArchitect tests drive a small Select stand-in, because jsdom cannot open\nthe Radix popover.\n\n* fix(orchestrator,architect,desktop): address PR 549 review\n\n- Room hold: one roomControls rule feeds the card and the header. Resume\n  shows only on a paused Room with no open approval, and Stop stays on a\n  delivery a restart interrupted.\n- Active time: starting no longer spends the budget, and restart recovery\n  seeds a legacy record once so a paused Room''s clock stops growing.\n- openGlobalAppView cancels a pending switch to another app.\n- A research stop no longer names an access decision whose answer\n  granted the access.\n- block() without `on` clears blockedOn; drop an unused import; the docs\n  no longer point at Reflect all.\n\n* refactor(orchestrator): split the Workflow and Room hold components React Doctor flagged\n\nMove the hold card''s wording and namesSentence to lib/room-hold.ts and\nthe state line''s working to lib/loop-state-line.ts. Split the step\nheader, Tune panel, Workflow top row and notices into their own\ncomponents. Key code spans by their offset in the text, not the index.\n\n* test(desktop): remove two races that failed CI on unrelated changes\n\n- The Qwen reasoning test shared a fixed /tmp folder and removed it while\n  the runtime could still write into it. It now uses a folder per run and\n  retries the removal.\n- The removed-capture test deleted the folder once combined.log existed,\n  while the stdout write could still be in flight, which reported a write\n  failure instead of the missing file. It now waits for both files to\n  hold every byte.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsYh5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApRIQADL7IJYCmNbnwOg98UFx+KyD\nrAYC5bCWrZwlgKTfgdivWPcsN6UQjc6lcygojWLgmPUdp8xQviGrhmdFEFsEu70h\nnHnvyDGLIvEv2VfoF8jeRGuEDiLk4rBuyELKc1VOXvBWhSs9FBU+JJoz30Nodl4M\n/CPzJFCb+4iq+A3bWHj56h2zyI1duqMuGKilVyYY721tr1TNlIHbQumUWK1dHYnD\nr/mHLUkTH3HT5CdFSEjxhQcgaaXFBN+NaKohrpCDNw3UGFuasI8kmVhtDmFPnt8C\nMGuoaS5ggYT0y55zoOWmP7m1fYxb9pxipRZWzrOtEWWNv4uRwP6glVZD4fY6ZANx\nqXWEfxHmyl8NJrqSxcI3Mm63pDxL6AEItj3YzJp3TUChkEMXGej++P4Fdv+YEbgR\nrxmGuoBkPEbVKiPubyiAX83GpWtRiKRr30WUKCmB6s/5hmsv5pxbi0UykIhy6wLY\naZ7U0OGjHp/ulBmJTn/+luOjRrpdI7/LC06Z7sqb8FFiMfGzY0PdIclM/wa32BPJ\nCg4jOrqSyXJM1M4BqFAUKUqcN566XHiefLTKCqAo+jCIieFZDo+Zncpf/r7QzVf9\nTnVAcTiMUmGf/eYSdRFS4uCf8P5dthi3cq9d+wLrRcQ2apirNq3t835wusESE/T8\nxGnOwfdg0iU9mvZkp+xG\n=tIiT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T19:41:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/90ee3c3e765f9a1c6ed7a7ba6570f0ac26dbcc4f","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDkwZWUzYzNlNzY1ZjlhMWM2ZWQ3YTdiYTY1NzBmMGFjMjZkYmNjNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/fd826e92c2ec21982b98cc74b1e4551c40e03167","sha":"fd826e92c2ec21982b98cc74b1e4551c40e03167","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/fd826e92c2ec21982b98cc74b1e4551c40e03167"}],"sha":"90ee3c3e765f9a1c6ed7a7ba6570f0ac26dbcc4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/90ee3c3e765f9a1c6ed7a7ba6570f0ac26dbcc4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/fd826e92c2ec21982b98cc74b1e4551c40e03167/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T13:56:23Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T13:56:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(ci): drop the dead Turbo cache wiring and cut the desktop suite cost (#545) (#546)\n\n* ci(test): drop the dead Turbo remote cache wiring\n\nThe workflow passed secrets.TURBO_TEAM and secrets.TURBO_TOKEN to Turbo in\nfive task steps and reported whether they arrived in four more steps. Neither\nsecret exists on the repository, so every run reported:\n\n  Turbo remote cache credentials: absent (local cache only)\n\nTurbo therefore used a local cache on an ephemeral runner. The cache was\nthrown away after each run, and the workflow claimed a cache it did not have.\n\nRemove the four report steps and the eight credential lines. Turbo keeps a\nlocal cache. To restore a remote cache, provision TURBO_TEAM and TURBO_TOKEN\nand add the wiring back.\n\nPart of #545.\n\n* perf(desktop): cut test import and environment cost and use CI CPUs\n\nThe desktop suite is the slowest task in the Tests job. It spends more wall\nclock loading modules and building fake browsers than running tests. Two\nchanges reduce that cost.\n\nRunner use. CI runs one package at a time (turbo --concurrency=1), so the\n33% worker cap left three of the four runner CPUs idle: 33% of 4 CPUs rounds\nto one worker. Use 75% when CI is set, which rounds to three workers, and\nkeep the 33% cap for local runs that put three packages on one machine.\n\nEnvironment. Twenty-four renderer test files never touch the DOM. Mark them\nwith the node environment so Vitest does not build a jsdom environment for\nthem. The three remaining files without a pragma need jsdom.\n\nImport. ToolCaptureReport imported the @sero-ai/ui root barrel. That barrel\nre-exports calendar.tsx, which pulls react-day-picker and date-fns into four\ntest files that never use a date picker. Import the dialog subpath instead,\nwhich the file''s other imports already do.\n\nMeasured on 489 test files, 3022 tests, warm cache, median of two runs:\n\n  workers  before   after\n  1        146.1s   138.1s     (import 56.6s -> 51.6s, env 19.1s -> 15.6s)\n  3         54.3s    52.4s\n\nWorker count dominates: 146.1s at one worker, 54.3s at three. The CI runner\nis about twice as slow per unit of work as the development machine, and the\n1-worker figure reproduces the ~272s the issue records, so the suite should\nfall from roughly 272s to roughly 105s.\n\nPart of #545.","tree":{"sha":"07134d8ec1f645ec387dbf53ec757d1a70549fec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/07134d8ec1f645ec387dbf53ec757d1a70549fec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/fd826e92c2ec21982b98cc74b1e4551c40e03167","verification":{"payload":"tree 07134d8ec1f645ec387dbf53ec757d1a70549fec\nparent 19e69adff842b0ea6f1efc2a1732266f12f6e888\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1789912583 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789912583 +0100\n\nperf(ci): drop the dead Turbo cache wiring and cut the desktop suite cost (#545) (#546)\n\n* ci(test): drop the dead Turbo remote cache wiring\n\nThe workflow passed secrets.TURBO_TEAM and secrets.TURBO_TOKEN to Turbo in\nfive task steps and reported whether they arrived in four more steps. Neither\nsecret exists on the repository, so every run reported:\n\n  Turbo remote cache credentials: absent (local cache only)\n\nTurbo therefore used a local cache on an ephemeral runner. The cache was\nthrown away after each run, and the workflow claimed a cache it did not have.\n\nRemove the four report steps and the eight credential lines. Turbo keeps a\nlocal cache. To restore a remote cache, provision TURBO_TEAM and TURBO_TOKEN\nand add the wiring back.\n\nPart of #545.\n\n* perf(desktop): cut test import and environment cost and use CI CPUs\n\nThe desktop suite is the slowest task in the Tests job. It spends more wall\nclock loading modules and building fake browsers than running tests. Two\nchanges reduce that cost.\n\nRunner use. CI runs one package at a time (turbo --concurrency=1), so the\n33% worker cap left three of the four runner CPUs idle: 33% of 4 CPUs rounds\nto one worker. Use 75% when CI is set, which rounds to three workers, and\nkeep the 33% cap for local runs that put three packages on one machine.\n\nEnvironment. Twenty-four renderer test files never touch the DOM. Mark them\nwith the node environment so Vitest does not build a jsdom environment for\nthem. The three remaining files without a pragma need jsdom.\n\nImport. ToolCaptureReport imported the @sero-ai/ui root barrel. That barrel\nre-exports calendar.tsx, which pulls react-day-picker and date-fns into four\ntest files that never use a date picker. Import the dialog subpath instead,\nwhich the file''s other imports already do.\n\nMeasured on 489 test files, 3022 tests, warm cache, median of two runs:\n\n  workers  before   after\n  1        146.1s   138.1s     (import 56.6s -> 51.6s, env 19.1s -> 15.6s)\n  3         54.3s    52.4s\n\nWorker count dominates: 146.1s at one worker, 54.3s at three. The CI runner\nis about twice as slow per unit of work as the development machine, and the\n1-worker figure reproduces the ~272s the issue records, so the suite should\nfall from roughly 272s to roughly 105s.\n\nPart of #545.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr+YHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATQMQAE+3YsbWSVzvM85PpWAPlysv\nej1JldqAFDyH2KSGUami4D/hN+pIzYxLdZtVsPDqlkL/NiiVKajK6I996dg7VdjP\nA3vGDlYuMDld8UhyQoq1Kn+vrslXyNIkHt2iqBN6sx9hP00f7wmrAqD+K0N7Bw1U\n+YC1Q6QlsALazzj7zD/XZJf2tUEiKpSM4OWvBrracKGev6sOqWkuFjc0vWutLtNE\ndHtSj6KzltlP8CYW4mm4Sx3S+2SQ4H9I2ivA8nxC48J6a5kAWgiubmV2moD40eRi\nF1SWxDVgKSU9BcCCxUi9eXwG9voWusaGg7gCyq+sBrYt1EsCH6Y+Hg65qmlhWMUy\nbZ6823NwuuprnOfXBg2OQjRteNHxAwvow+5H5NytTQQ67cWSpugS7wdyx1D0MVLU\nm625Gy0VAfrRntoRREyBid5qaylw/CfWNlmst9wDGnJS0PHEmPMET/U2Qo2WneDd\n7kH0W7/lbbWGzZUPeR4YiB0MDF4gS1kYN7JjY36w35L66fo9nrri5Be8lkqdylLm\nGKKhrFphUKFreyUwSQTQeIKWv4UN9V3VlJUlQg1e/XG3FExiydo1WspWjkY1eDtw\nAoQYI/dbLX2+KlEZIhAx5qFNrzdkq+PJ7YDPrCTM1FN+THbQ3A/BJlh8bP4MRUlK\nAc6QPEzriMyETEoXiqP/\n=B1I4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T13:56:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/fd826e92c2ec21982b98cc74b1e4551c40e03167","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGZkODI2ZTkyYzJlYzIxOTgyYjk4Y2M3NGIxZTQ1NTFjNDBlMDMxNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/19e69adff842b0ea6f1efc2a1732266f12f6e888","sha":"19e69adff842b0ea6f1efc2a1732266f12f6e888","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/19e69adff842b0ea6f1efc2a1732266f12f6e888"}],"sha":"fd826e92c2ec21982b98cc74b1e4551c40e03167","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/fd826e92c2ec21982b98cc74b1e4551c40e03167"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/19e69adff842b0ea6f1efc2a1732266f12f6e888/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T12:50:10Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"Dan Carter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T12:50:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(activity): one activity vocabulary across Architect, Orchestrator and the tree (#544)\n\n* docs: added openspec proposal for ux-activity-at-a-glance\n\n* feat(activity): one activity vocabulary across Architect, Orchestrator and the tree\n\nCloses #536.\n\nNine states, each with a word, its own glyph shape and a sentence saying what\nhappens next, shared from @sero-ai/common so one situation reads the same on\nevery surface. \"Working\" is reachable only through a liveness mark a runtime\nwrote while it watched a run report, which is the fault this change exists to\nfix: a saved status of running outlived its Workflow by three days.\n\nWhether work needs the user is decided once, in activity-attention.ts, so the\nworkspace tree flags exactly what the Orchestrator lists word as asking.\n\nSurfaces, drawn to the approved proposal at\napps/styleguide/public/prototypes/agent-workspace-ux-audit/1-activity-at-a-glance.html:\n\n- Architect projects list: four-column grid, mono column header, the ask as an\n  amber pill, attention and stopped rows washed, spend as \"$5.52 of $10\".\n- Architect project header: a bordered band with spend divided into its own\n  shaded column, the phase rail naming the current phase, the owner''s paragraph\n  folded under \"What Architect reported\". No glow and no pulse; nothing on these\n  surfaces animates.\n- Orchestrator Home: a quiet status line instead of a headline, a plain \"Needs\n  you\" card grouped by the work it belongs to, and the three starts moved into\n  the shell top bar.\n- Workflows and Rooms lists: title, then the state as a glyph chip and a\n  sentence, what it waits for, and money alone in mono.\n- Workspace tree: one chip beside a workspace that needs the user or has\n  stopped, carrying the owning app''s own sentence.\n\nAlso fixed while comparing the build against the drawing frame by frame:\n\n- Architect claimed \"Working\" from a mark written earlier in the session after\n  its runtime stopped. Nobody refreshes the mark once it stops, so liveness is\n  now gated on the runtime running.\n- The Orchestrator preview harness had no @container/panel root, so every\n  container query collapsed to its narrow layout and hid the real columns.\n- A Room row claimed wall-clock elapsed as time spent working. Nothing records\n  work time, so it no longer says so.\n\nDeletes ui/components/LoopList.tsx, which the new Workflows list replaced.\n\nThe earlier Architect rule that amber may never be a wash is superseded by this\nproposal, which washes the glyph chip, the ask pill and the attention row. The\nsupersession is recorded in styles.css.\n\n* docs(ux-audit): carry the eight approved proposals with the code that follows them\n\nThe code comments, the OpenSpec proposal and issues #537-#543 all name these\nfiles as the binding visual spec. Without them the paths dangle on main.\n\nThese nine are self-contained: no images, no external assets. evidence.html,\nflows.html and the screenshot library stay on the audit branch, so 39 in-page\nlinks to evidence.html and 8 to flows.html do not resolve here. The drawings\nare left exactly as approved rather than edited to hide that.\n\nAlso ticks task 8.4, the screenshot comparison against these drawings. It was\ndone; the deliberate departures it asks for are recorded on the pull request.\n\n* fix(activity): guard the two upgrade paths and clear the React Doctor warnings\n\nA review of #544 found two crashes that only happen on upgrade, which is why\nevery suite stayed green: no test loads a record written by the previous\nversion.\n\nclearLiveRun read `loop.runtime.liveRun` unguarded, and reconcileLoop calls it\nbefore reconcileRecovered, whose first line already tolerates a loop persisted\nwithout a runtime field. Startup recovery threw on exactly the shape the\ncomment there says to expect.\n\nprojectAttention destructured `project.activity`. The field is required on\nArchitectProjectView, but normalizeArchitectIndex only checks that `projects`\nis an array and then casts, so an index written before the contract existed\nreaches it whole. The cast means no typecheck can catch this.\n\nBoth now return early, and both regression tests were confirmed to fail without\nthe guard.\n\nReact Doctor, all five warnings:\n  - ownerSentence moves from ActivityWord.tsx to ui/lib/format.ts, so the\n    component file exports components only.\n  - The preview fixtures are read only inside their own file, so they stop\n    being exported.\n  - WorkspaceNode''s trailing row controls become WorkspaceRowActions, a local\n    component beside the two already in that file. Keeping it in the same file\n    is deliberate: moving it out relocates three findings that main already\n    carries into a new path CI would read as new.\n  - OrchestratorApp''s nine route branches move to OrchestratorRoutes.tsx,\n    leaving the app with the shell, the banners and the wiring.\n\nCyclomatic complexity drops from 14 and 21 respectively. The three remaining\nfindings in WorkspaceNode are all pre-existing on main; one swapped rule\n(html-no-nested-interactive to prefer-tag-over-role) is an artifact of the\nextraction, and the underlying markup is unchanged.\n\npnpm typecheck 29/29, pnpm test 24/24 packages.","tree":{"sha":"dd6569253ef6381d132933b0027c3283a533fb66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/dd6569253ef6381d132933b0027c3283a533fb66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/19e69adff842b0ea6f1efc2a1732266f12f6e888","verification":{"payload":"tree dd6569253ef6381d132933b0027c3283a533fb66\nparent 87a3814463f90e072e0b4e9b3c869ad0d98c137f\nauthor Dan Carter <danielrosscarter@gmail.com> 1789908610 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789908610 +0100\n\nfeat(activity): one activity vocabulary across Architect, Orchestrator and the tree (#544)\n\n* docs: added openspec proposal for ux-activity-at-a-glance\n\n* feat(activity): one activity vocabulary across Architect, Orchestrator and the tree\n\nCloses #536.\n\nNine states, each with a word, its own glyph shape and a sentence saying what\nhappens next, shared from @sero-ai/common so one situation reads the same on\nevery surface. \"Working\" is reachable only through a liveness mark a runtime\nwrote while it watched a run report, which is the fault this change exists to\nfix: a saved status of running outlived its Workflow by three days.\n\nWhether work needs the user is decided once, in activity-attention.ts, so the\nworkspace tree flags exactly what the Orchestrator lists word as asking.\n\nSurfaces, drawn to the approved proposal at\napps/styleguide/public/prototypes/agent-workspace-ux-audit/1-activity-at-a-glance.html:\n\n- Architect projects list: four-column grid, mono column header, the ask as an\n  amber pill, attention and stopped rows washed, spend as \"$5.52 of $10\".\n- Architect project header: a bordered band with spend divided into its own\n  shaded column, the phase rail naming the current phase, the owner''s paragraph\n  folded under \"What Architect reported\". No glow and no pulse; nothing on these\n  surfaces animates.\n- Orchestrator Home: a quiet status line instead of a headline, a plain \"Needs\n  you\" card grouped by the work it belongs to, and the three starts moved into\n  the shell top bar.\n- Workflows and Rooms lists: title, then the state as a glyph chip and a\n  sentence, what it waits for, and money alone in mono.\n- Workspace tree: one chip beside a workspace that needs the user or has\n  stopped, carrying the owning app''s own sentence.\n\nAlso fixed while comparing the build against the drawing frame by frame:\n\n- Architect claimed \"Working\" from a mark written earlier in the session after\n  its runtime stopped. Nobody refreshes the mark once it stops, so liveness is\n  now gated on the runtime running.\n- The Orchestrator preview harness had no @container/panel root, so every\n  container query collapsed to its narrow layout and hid the real columns.\n- A Room row claimed wall-clock elapsed as time spent working. Nothing records\n  work time, so it no longer says so.\n\nDeletes ui/components/LoopList.tsx, which the new Workflows list replaced.\n\nThe earlier Architect rule that amber may never be a wash is superseded by this\nproposal, which washes the glyph chip, the ask pill and the attention row. The\nsupersession is recorded in styles.css.\n\n* docs(ux-audit): carry the eight approved proposals with the code that follows them\n\nThe code comments, the OpenSpec proposal and issues #537-#543 all name these\nfiles as the binding visual spec. Without them the paths dangle on main.\n\nThese nine are self-contained: no images, no external assets. evidence.html,\nflows.html and the screenshot library stay on the audit branch, so 39 in-page\nlinks to evidence.html and 8 to flows.html do not resolve here. The drawings\nare left exactly as approved rather than edited to hide that.\n\nAlso ticks task 8.4, the screenshot comparison against these drawings. It was\ndone; the deliberate departures it asks for are recorded on the pull request.\n\n* fix(activity): guard the two upgrade paths and clear the React Doctor warnings\n\nA review of #544 found two crashes that only happen on upgrade, which is why\nevery suite stayed green: no test loads a record written by the previous\nversion.\n\nclearLiveRun read `loop.runtime.liveRun` unguarded, and reconcileLoop calls it\nbefore reconcileRecovered, whose first line already tolerates a loop persisted\nwithout a runtime field. Startup recovery threw on exactly the shape the\ncomment there says to expect.\n\nprojectAttention destructured `project.activity`. The field is required on\nArchitectProjectView, but normalizeArchitectIndex only checks that `projects`\nis an array and then casts, so an index written before the contract existed\nreaches it whole. The cast means no typecheck can catch this.\n\nBoth now return early, and both regression tests were confirmed to fail without\nthe guard.\n\nReact Doctor, all five warnings:\n  - ownerSentence moves from ActivityWord.tsx to ui/lib/format.ts, so the\n    component file exports components only.\n  - The preview fixtures are read only inside their own file, so they stop\n    being exported.\n  - WorkspaceNode''s trailing row controls become WorkspaceRowActions, a local\n    component beside the two already in that file. Keeping it in the same file\n    is deliberate: moving it out relocates three findings that main already\n    carries into a new path CI would read as new.\n  - OrchestratorApp''s nine route branches move to OrchestratorRoutes.tsx,\n    leaving the app with the shell, the banners and the wiring.\n\nCyclomatic complexity drops from 14 and 21 respectively. The three remaining\nfindings in WorkspaceNode are all pre-existing on main; one swapped rule\n(html-no-nested-interactive to prefer-tag-over-role) is an artifact of the\nextraction, and the underlying markup is unchanged.\n\npnpm typecheck 29/29, pnpm test 24/24 packages.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr9aCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAllgQAAR57sZIeypW9HDNAF1/BgoY\ndd540Y8VscEtsVcwrjPrnuUxFFEEKYVC8R9oGcystcUyiP7Stuit51h+j62GZOVS\n8MYCwgWjfkpPNZxcdPePD1Q3jKtt39+QuVlGLmNf/c/LsbF5ar0ta8wf4Wpo/ndg\n4Eetu4do8o8heurKrIRxd5z5GD4ENddO9qaszmdi5Se6fIUpAkwjdBq2xUZOvEUa\nojOdHU8yFrCNHFKss9Mc4CXVyWgp0Slx3ZHUC/0sKNUcDAg6wkTEndRXmcN9mfGO\ncAcZ4XdMRCOidF8kG4/XEt8ILKLycY//XMhepl6yNKtWqVoBGk6cmdpRbhWrvzYD\n8Q2vmFFG5lWa5H8qNMiVMZVrgR8O/gGs9HJh4E1jDc3o7xlbMx7i3cxwXzAIxdWL\n2BP9SmGwjKEpAIr3E2uguOznSHlSRXdGTczXhlhq/zXQpiK4OrvQ1/+DHlz7HUQz\nLziXjM7CN98GoPLPAddeQM1ulvrYTx1gW5uMl42RZb32C7AS1ANq95WXKJGQlYmV\nxP4MvIjLg8x00ppv4aCfkLZTl3h2yHxHbAsrgM6gzGhDCJwiwh1dFjHYCkSls09E\n6Ep5pcx3qPRgOE6xK41eJR5Zwc5DDnFXSzkhCx2gl3T1VgE7dxhRGWDmWVFviXJO\nbTsNe+E9y/R