I5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/2c278e8a5a5ac5e1c9a57b459594acef38adb87b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T22:15:18Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T22:15:18Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"fix(architect): show the maintenance subscription as watching, not running\n\nThe maintenance milestone is a standing Workflow subscription that never\nleaves the running status, so the rail said \"Workflow is running\" while the\nOrchestrator showed both steps done and nothing executing.\n\nThe watcher now stamps the dispatch with the loop''s last run and its\nearliest scheduled fire. The rail labels the subscription \"watching\" and\nshows one short line: the next run when known, else the last run. A failure\nstill shows as interrupted with its reason.","tree":{"sha":"f838f504c58234928dd3b0019472e52a369228a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/f838f504c58234928dd3b0019472e52a369228a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/2c278e8a5a5ac5e1c9a57b459594acef38adb87b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.git