ttps://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/999a0cd13b69ff589501f5cd71fc876b050b086b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T21:49:29Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T21:49:29Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"fix(architect): say when a run has no trace instead of showing zeros\n\nA project whose work ran before run journals existed, or one that has not\nrun yet, has no journal on disk. The inspector folded nothing, showed a row\nof zero tiles and reconciled that zero against the project spend, so a run\nread as if it cost nothing and under-reported the whole budget.\n\nThe trace answer now carries a `recorded` flag, false when a journal has\nneither a checkpoint nor a record. Spend is only reconciled against a trace\nthat exists. The inspector shows \"Nothing recorded\" with the reason in place\nof the tiles, and the run state says the same even while the run is open.\n\nThe flag is copied through the projects tool result by name, and a tool\ntest pins that pass-through, because the runtime and UI tests each passed\non their own side of the seam while the flag never crossed it.","tree":{"sha":"f8aa72d801157a4eedb0e6b5f39b63e5a7af41c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/f8aa72d801157a4eedb0e6b5f39b63e5a7af41c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/999a0cd13b69ff589501f5cd71fc876b050b086b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"