ro-labs/sero/git/trees/d152756deddef092ab365fd3c156cd6ed5e95710"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/ca987eb9d28ab0c61627a14734b9bf11f872f7e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/ca987eb9d28ab0c61627a14734b9bf11f872f7e9","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGNhOTg3ZWI5ZDI4YWIwYzYxNjI3YTE0NzM0YjliZjExZjg3MmY3ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/4bdd4229f604c8eac80d933367903fec38bff971","sha":"4bdd4229f604c8eac80d933367903fec38bff971","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/4bdd4229f604c8eac80d933367903fec38bff971"}],"sha":"ca987eb9d28ab0c61627a14734b9bf11f872f7e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/ca987eb9d28ab0c61627a14734b9bf11f872f7e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/4bdd4229f604c8eac80d933367903fec38bff971/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:43:33Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:43:33Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"docs: hand off the architect efficiency change\n\nThe implementation is at 32/34 and green. Two tasks remain: one measurement\ncommand, and two verification passes that need no code.\n\nWritten mainly as a stop list. The remaining work is small, and the risks around\nit are all of the same kind: treating a deliberate, recorded compromise as a\ndefect. The five React Doctor warnings, the zero session counters, the aggregate\ncoverage, the empty model provenance for delegated work and the read-only Room\ngap are each either recorded as an unknown or deferred to a task that owns them.\n\nIt also says what to do when the live measurement fails, because it has failed\ntwice: record it and move on. A recorded unknown is a valid outcome for 8.2. A\nfourth attempt is not.","tree":{"sha":"54f40d78e8789a0a7a7f9a6eed777055b9e75579","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/54f40d78e8789a0a7a7f9a6eed777055b9e75579"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/4bdd4229f604c8eac80d933367903fec38bff971","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/4bdd4229f604c8eac80d933367903fec38bff971","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDRiZGQ0MjI5ZjYwNGM4ZWFjODBkOTMzMzY3OTAzZmVjMzhiZmY5NzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/a084687eadb9d1ccdc9c714e0c6d506dbaee10b8","sha":"a084687eadb9d1ccdc9c714e0c6d506dbaee10b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/a084687eadb9d1ccdc9c714e0c6d506dbaee10b8"}],"sha":"4bdd4229f604c8eac80d933367903fec38bff971","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/4bdd4229f604c8eac80d933367903fec38bff971"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/a084687eadb9d1ccdc9c714e0c6d506dbaee10b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:40:09Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:40:09Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"fix(architect): answer the inspector''s accessibility and identity findings\n\nReact Doctor flagged the new inspector. The accessibility ones were real: a row\nwas a clickable div with no keyboard handler and no focus, so a keyboard reader\ncould move the selection but not act on a row. The row is now an option with a\nselected state, a focus target, and Enter or Space doing what a click does.\n\nTwo smaller ones: the selected view is computed once rather than on every render,\nand the records list is memoised so the range and filter memos below it are not\nrecomputed against a fresh array each time.\n\nThe filter loop also built its membership test per record per filter. It now uses\nsets, so filtering a long trace is one pass rather than a scan inside a scan.\n\nReact Doctor 77 -> 78 on the changed scope, with the accessibility warnings\ncleared. Architect 423 tests still pass.","tree":{"sha":"5a2389c3cf054db8f9277add1841af5f5e930c24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/5a2389c3cf054db8f9277add1841af5f5e930c24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/a084687eadb9d1ccdc9c714e0c6d506dbaee10b8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/a084687eadb9d1ccdc9c714e0c6d506dbaee10b8","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGEwODQ2ODdlYWRiOWQxY2NkYzljNzE0ZTBjNmQ1MDZkYmFlZTEwYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/1da2f5223a77143a9d513995eccc17580cd84e3e","sha":"1da2f5223a77143a9d513995eccc17580cd84e3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/1da2f5223a77143a9d513995eccc17580cd84e3e"}],"sha":"a084687eadb9d1ccdc9c714e0c6d506dbaee10b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/a084687eadb9d1ccdc9c714e0c6d506dbaee10b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/1da2f5223a77143a9d513995eccc17580cd84e3e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:38:22Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:38:22Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"refactor: split the six files this change pushed over 500 LOC\n\nThe repository keeps every source file at or below 500 lines, and a change that\ntakes a file over it has to split it before completion. Six files crossed that\nline. Each split follows a seam the code already had, so nothing moved between\nconcerns and no behaviour changed.\n\n    packages/common/src/orchestrator-contract.ts   464 -> 480\n    packages/common/src/index.ts                   491 -> 464\n    architect/runtime/projects-actions.ts          468 -> 482\n    architect/runtime/services.ts                  475 -> 497\n    desktop/subagent/runtime/runner.ts             489 -> 479\n    orchestrator/shared/types.ts                   495 -> 498\n\nSeven new modules, each named for the subject it now owns:\n\n- `orchestrator-project-context.ts` — project and run attribution, which is a\n  closed contract of its own. `resolveOrchestratorTriggerIntent` stayed behind\n  because it reads the creation options, and moving it would have made the two\n  files import each other.\n- `orchestrator.ts` — the Orchestrator''s re-exports as one group, so the package\n  barrel is a list of groups rather than forty blocks.\n- `work-recovery-actions.ts` — preview, repair and retry: work with a workspace\n  that may need starting again.\n- `model-default-actions.ts` — tier defaults, which are checked against the real\n  catalogue and reported with the revision they produce.\n- `service-helpers.ts` — the git and evidence helpers.\n- `session-observation.ts` — the mapping from a session event to an observation.\n  This is the piece worth reading on its own: an identity comes from the event\n  when the SDK reports one and is absent when it does not, and no timing is\n  derived from text deltas.\n- `session-output.ts` — reading a session''s own answer and tool summary.\n\nTwo imports moved with their code: `commitOf`/`worktreeFingerprint` in the\nservices test, and `ModelDefaultInput` in the projects tool.\n\nVerification: root `pnpm typecheck` 29/29, Architect 423 tests, Orchestrator\n1449, desktop subagent 99. No file in the change is over 500 lines except the\nbaseline e2e spec, which is a test.","tree":{"sha":"0709e9a973894d458580dc3c71dd9a85167b53eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/0709e9a973894d458580dc3c71dd9a85167b53eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/1da2f5223a77143a9d513995eccc17580cd84e3e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/1da2f5223a77143a9d513995eccc17580cd84e3e","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDFkYTJmNTIyM2E3NzE0M2E5ZDUxMzk5NWVjY2MxNzU4MGNkODRlM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/70817dfa0f04b58c6766e95154cb80420ff44ca8","sha":"70817dfa0f04b58c6766e95154cb80420ff44ca8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/70817dfa0f04b58c6766e95154cb80420ff44ca8"}],"sha":"1da2f5223a77143a9d513995eccc17580cd84e3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/1da2f5223a77143a9d513995eccc17580cd84e3e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/70817dfa0f04b58c6766e95154cb80420ff44ca8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:23:57Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:23:57Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"test(architect): keep the after measurement beside the baseline\n\nOverwriting baseline.json with the 8.2 run would have destroyed the task 5.4\nevidence it is compared against. The after figure goes in its own file, so both\nmeasurements stay readable.","tree":{"sha":"e98c8818be88dc81e5698cf0e7c4413e080cf5cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/e98c8818be88dc81e5698cf0e7c4413e080cf5cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/70817dfa0f04b58c6766e95154cb80420ff44ca8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/70817dfa0f04b58c6766e95154cb80420ff44ca8","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDcwODE3ZGZhMGYwNGI1OGM2NzY2ZTk1MTU0Y2I4MDQyMGZmNDRjYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/ca6811ee5267a61ee676f3028a1db1615569aa91","sha":"ca6811ee5267a61ee676f3028a1db1615569aa91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/ca6811ee5267a61ee676f3028a1db1615569aa91"}],"sha":"70817dfa0f04b58c6766e95154cb80420ff44ca8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/70817dfa0f04b58c6766e95154cb80420ff44ca8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/ca6811ee5267a61ee676f3028a1db1615569aa91/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:23:40Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:23:40Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"test(architect): give discovery room to finish before the measurement\n\nThe planning objective timed out in discovery while a Room worked on the project\nquestion, before any milestone existed. The harness waited seven minutes for a\nmilestone; discovery research can take longer. Both discovery waits are now\nfifteen minutes.\n\nThe outcome comparison for task 8.2 is recorded in the design doc. It covers the\nimplementation objective before and after, and records the missing planning\nfigure as an unknown rather than leaving it implied.\n\nThe numbers do not show an efficiency gain and the doc says why: the two runs did\ndifferent amounts of work. The earlier one stopped at its first accepted\nmilestone; the later one ran further research and reached release, so more cost\nand more wall-clock is what more work costs. The record cannot separate that from\na genuine regression, so it is an unknown. What did change measurably is the\ninstrumentation: coverage moved from a bare aggregate total to partial with\ncall-level detail, and the record now names the model and effort level that ran.","tree":{"sha":"d35806df56264d9d27ce339e4372ca6878ee5405","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/d35806df56264d9d27ce339e4372ca6878ee5405"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/ca6811ee5267a61ee676f3028a1db1615569aa91","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/ca6811ee5267a61ee676f3028a1db1615569aa91","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGNhNjgxMWVlNTI2N2E2MWVlNjc2ZjMwMjhhMWRiMTYxNTU2OWFhOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/f588294ccab80da9acc8b2a4afd0299877bdb654","sha":"f588294ccab80da9acc8b2a4afd0299877bdb654","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/f588294ccab80da9acc8b2a4afd0299877bdb654"}],"sha":"ca6811ee5267a61ee676f3028a1db1615569aa91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/ca6811ee5267a61ee676f3028a1db1615569aa91"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/f588294ccab80da9acc8b2a4afd0299877bdb654/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:33:51Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:33:51Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"docs(architect): document what the change made true\n\nThree claims in the docs were no longer accurate, and the rest is new material\nfor the surfaces this change added.\n\nModel selection was described as \"the first available model that supports\nreasoning, or the first available model if none supports reasoning\". That is not\nhow the owner resolves any more. It uses the MED tier, which is the project\ndefault when one is set and otherwise the global Admin selection, and a tier never\nfalls back to another provider: an unavailable model or unsupported thinking level\nis refused with the reason. Both the guide and the reference said the old thing.\n\nThe cost section said the cap limits spending. It limits the work Architect\nstarts, not what a run already in flight can spend, and the spend line is a lower\nbound when a source reported a total without detail or reported nothing at all.\nThe guide now says that, and adds the run inspector: it opens on totals, reading\noperations is a separate action, the activity chart drives the timeline filter,\nthe selected panel shows own and inclusive cost separately, shared activity is\nreported beside a run''s figure rather than inside it, and a filtered total says\nwhich scope it covers.\n\nThe reference gains a runs-and-telemetry section: run grouping by objective, the\njournal and research-report paths, and the terms the inspector uses. It records\nthat a total nobody reported stays absent rather than zero, and that an older\nrecord keeps the amount it recorded without inventing the calls behind it.\n\nARCHITECTURE.md gains the boundaries this change actually crossed. The session\ntelemetry contract is closed and explicit: identities and host timestamps, null\nrather than an inferred value, and no first-token timing because the SDK exposes\nno such event. Architect delegates through Orchestrator and sends closed project\ncontext with the creation request, which Orchestrator keeps across recovery. And\n`@sero-ai/common` is published, so a type change there needs a release before a\nplugin depending on the new field can ship.\n\nDocs build succeeds (`pnpm --filter @sero-ai/docs-site build`).","tree":{"sha":"9a3aba2957b272536511bec7f924ca3a01bbc9c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/9a3aba2957b272536511bec7f924ca3a01bbc9c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/f588294ccab80da9acc8b2a4afd0299877bdb654","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/f588294ccab80da9acc8b2a4afd0299877bdb654","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGY1ODgyOTRjY2FiODBkYTlhY2M4YjJhNGFmZDAyOTk4NzdiZGI2NTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/eb3ae98e49af5b0a3569c0176b8d660c96424b30","sha":"eb3ae98e49af5b0a3569c0176b8d660c96424b30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/eb3ae98e49af5b0a3569c0176b8d660c96424b30"}],"sha":"f588294ccab80da9acc8b2a4afd0299877bdb654","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/f588294ccab80da9acc8b2a4afd0299877bdb654"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/eb3ae98e49af5b0a3569c0176b8d660c96424b30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:31:40Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:31:40Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"test(architect): check the boundaries that cross the seam\n\nTask 8.1 names five scenarios. Three are already covered by their own suites and\nare cited rather than duplicated: the Room-to-Workflow handoff by\n`dispatch-recovery.test.ts`, independent review and focused repair by\n`owner-contract.test.ts`, and restart telemetry by `run-journal.test.ts`.\n\nThe two that no single suite could see are the ones where the Architect and the\nOrchestrator have to agree:\n\n- A prepared dispatch keeps the model snapshot it was resolved with. Changing the\n  project''s selection mid-run would leave one run''s work half on each selection,\n  so the snapshot is asserted unchanged while the next dispatch is asserted to\n  pick up the new model and a new revision.\n- A restart with partial telemetry reports what it has and marks the rest\n  incomplete rather than zero. One source reports a total; the counters nobody\n  reported stay absent, and the trace still reconciles with the budget for its\n  own scope.\n\nThe budget and permission boundaries are checked from the other direction: the\nreserved dispatch carries the approved cap, and preparing work adds no authority\nto the session that owns the project.\n\nVerification: 5 cases. Architect 423 tests, both typechecks clean.","tree":{"sha":"be68c7f88908a4daaf8ee46dcc9a124a11fd3be8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/be68c7f88908a4daaf8ee46dcc9a124a11fd3be8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/eb3ae98e49af5b0a3569c0176b8d660c96424b30","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/eb3ae98e49af5b0a3569c0176b8d660c96424b30","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGViM2FlOThlNDlhZjViMGEzNTY5YzAxNzZiOGQ2NjBjOTY0MjRiMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/6c215345e093ea502e03396975451ebc12183657","sha":"6c215345e093ea502e03396975451ebc12183657","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/6c215345e093ea502e03396975451ebc12183657"}],"sha":"eb3ae98e49af5b0a3569c0176b8d660c96424b30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/eb3ae98e49af5b0a3569c0176b8d660c96424b30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/6c215345e093ea502e03396975451ebc12183657/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:29:49Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:29:49Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"feat(architect): name what the inspector is looking at\n\nThe view showed numbers without saying what state produced them, so an open run\nand an interrupted one looked alike, and a bounded total read as a complete one.\n\nOne derivation in `ui/lib/run-state.ts` decides the state for every surface, and\neach state carries a word: the tone is decoration on top of it, so nothing\ndepends on seeing a colour.\n\nThe pairs that had to stay apart:\n\n- An interrupted run is not an active one. A run that never recorded an end while\n  the project is stopped says so, and its detail says that late activity from work\n  already running still appears here rather than being hidden.\n- A partial history is not an empty one. A view with nothing reported at all says\n  the two causes look alike, which is the honest thing to say when telemetry\n  failure and a view that never started are indistinguishable from here.\n- A zoomed range with no rows is not an empty view. It says nothing is in the\n  range.\n- Waiting comes from an observed wait cause only. Elapsed time alone never infers\n  it, and the detail says so.\n\nVerification: 14 new cases. 13 cover loading before an answer, nothing recorded,\nactive with no activity yet, waiting from an observed cause and not from elapsed\ntime, a failure carrying its count, interrupted versus active, a partial history\nfrom either the page or the summary, a zoomed range reading as its own state, and\nevery state having a label. 1 covers a stopped project still showing the late\nworker''s usage and calling the run interrupted. Architect 418 tests, both\ntypechecks clean.\n\nPhase 7 is complete.","tree":{"sha":"5701ee3e738b10ceb0587d3d05581060120ad887","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/5701ee3e738b10ceb0587d3d05581060120ad887"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/6c215345e093ea502e03396975451ebc12183657","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/6c215345e093ea502e03396975451ebc12183657","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDZjMjE1MzQ1ZTA5M2VhNTAyZTAzMzk2OTc1NDUxZWJjMTIxODM2NTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/e1bceea034f58ca1f6c6ff06b5f88b00086dadc1","sha":"e1bceea034f58ca1f6c6ff06b5f88b00086dadc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/e1bceea034f58ca1f6c6ff06b5f88b00086dadc1"}],"sha":"6c215345e093ea502e03396975451ebc12183657","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/6c215345e093ea502e03396975451ebc12183657"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/e1bceea034f58ca1f6c6ff06b5f88b00086dadc1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:27:56Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:27:56Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"feat(architect): chart what the runtime actually reported\n\nThe inspector showed totals and rows but nothing that made the shape of a run\nvisible. It now draws cumulative spend, spend by activity and spend by model, all\ncomputed from the same records the totals above them read, so a chart and a total\ncannot disagree.\n\nThree ways a chart would have lied, each closed:\n\n- A parent''s inclusive cost already contains its children''s. The breakdown sums\n  the exclusive figures, and the inclusive figure is shown for the selected\n  operation only, labelled inclusive. Adding both would count a grandchild three\n  times.\n- Shared activity is charged once to the project, not to a run. It is reported\n  beside the run''s own figure instead of inside it.\n- A filtered view is part of a run. It now says which scope its total covers\n  rather than presenting a slice as the whole. An activity bar in the chart sets\n  that filter, so the chart and the timeline move together.\n\nAn unmeasured value is still never invented: a chart with nothing priced says\nthere is nothing to chart instead of drawing a line at zero, and the model\nbreakdown keeps the model and its effort level as one row, because two effort\nlevels are two decisions and merging them hides one.\n\nVerification: 17 new cases. 12 cover exact cumulative values, a re-read not\ndrawing the line backwards, an unpriced set charting nothing, activity totals and\nordering, the same model at two effort levels staying two rows, an unrecorded\nmodel keeping its cost, a breakdown stating whether it is the whole run,\nexclusive versus inclusive cost and their termination on a cycle, and shared\nversus attributable cost not leaking into each other. 5 cover the view: the\ncharts rendering exact values, an activity bar driving the timeline filter, the\nselected panel showing own and inclusive cost separately, and an unpriced view\nsaying so rather than drawing zero. Architect 404 tests, both typechecks clean.","tree":{"sha":"411da3be92fa482cfb302e72ba8915e5a5146a46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/411da3be92fa482cfb302e72ba8915e5a5146a46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/e1bceea034f58ca1f6c6ff06b5f88b00086dadc1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/e1bceea034f58ca1f6c6ff06b5f88b00086dadc1","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGUxYmNlZWEwMzRmNThjYTFmNmM2ZmYwNmI1Zjg4YjAwMDg2ZGFkYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/6f9c756ef905c30d4965ae1f7400ea66a2b8267c","sha":"6f9c756ef905c30d4965ae1f7400ea66a2b8267c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/6f9c756ef905c30d4965ae1f7400ea66a2b8267c"}],"sha":"e1bceea034f58ca1f6c6ff06b5f88b00086dadc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/e1bceea034f58ca1f6c6ff06b5f88b00086dadc1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/6f9c756ef905c30d4965ae1f7400ea66a2b8267c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:24:51Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:24:51Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"feat(architect): build the run inspector\n\nThe trace read added for 7.1 had no reader. This is the full-width inspector the\nprototype settled: it opens from the project controls menu at\n`projects/<id>/inspector`, the host keeps it in history, and the header returns to\nthe project. Escape does the same, so a keyboard reader is never stranded.\n\nA summary is what opens, and it carries no records. Loading the activity is an\nexplicit act, so opening the page reads a total rather than a trace, and the\nrecords then arrive a bounded page at a time.\n\nThe timeline renders the rows in view and nothing else. A trace with fifty\nthousand spans costs the same to scroll as a short one, and a test asserts the\nwindow stays inside the viewport plus its overscan at every scroll position,\nincluding past the end.\n\nThe logic lives in `ui/lib/timeline.ts` as pure functions, so filtering,\nwindowing, ranging and zooming are tested without rendering. Preferences go to\nthe host layout service, never browser storage, so leaving the inspector and\nreturning shows the filters that were on.\n\nAn unmeasured value is never filled in. A missing timing says so instead of\nreading as a fast zero, an unavailable token counter is named rather than shown\nas zero coverage, and a failure carries the word as well as the colour.\n\nVerification: 24 cases. 14 cover bounded windowing on a high-span fixture,\nfilter combination, an absent model contributing no filter option, a record with\nno time staying visible, and zoom clamping at both edges. 10 cover the view:\nsummary without detail, detail only on request, return to the project, an\nincomplete total saying it is a lower bound, arrow-key selection, Escape, the\nselected row surviving a re-render, filters persisting across a return, a failure\nkeeping its word, and an unobserved timing not reading as zero. Architect 388\ntests, both typechecks clean.","tree":{"sha":"be4bbb08000669bd1fbe2a3dda283fe0a250ac9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/be4bbb08000669bd1fbe2a3dda283fe0a250ac9c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/6f9c756ef905c30d4965ae1f7400ea66a2b8267c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/6f9c756ef905c30d4965ae1f7400ea66a2b8267c","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDZmOWM3NTZlZjkwNWMzMGQ0OTY1YWUxZjc0MDBlYTY2YTJiODI2N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/d5aed0c8cc456a65d345e0c1da624c33ec60effd","sha":"d5aed0c8cc456a65d345e0c1da624c33ec60effd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/d5aed0c8cc456a65d345e0c1da624c33ec60effd"}],"sha":"6f9c756ef905c30d4965ae1f7400ea66a2b8267c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/6f9c756ef905c30d4965ae1f7400ea66a2b8267c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/d5aed0c8cc456a65d345e0c1da624c33ec60effd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:17:42Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:17:42Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"feat(architect): read a trace without letting it out of the runtime\n\nThe inspector needs a project''s trace and nothing else did. The journal already\npages, but reading it directly would hand the renderer whatever a producer wrote,\nand a journal record is stored with an open shape so a future producer can add a\nfield without changing a type.\n\n`queryTrace` is that boundary. It authorizes by looking the project record up, so\na foreign id, a deleted project and a typo are all the same answer: nothing.\nReading is a projection over a named key list, and a value that is not a\nprimitive or a list of strings is dropped rather than stringified, because\nturning a payload into text to send it is still sending it. Token counters are\ncopied as numbers from usage and nothing else is.\n\nDetail is opt-in. `detail` defaults to off, so a summary request returns no\nrecords at all, and a caller cannot lift the page bound by asking for more. A\nsummary that could not fold everything reports `incomplete` instead of\npresenting a prefix total as the run total.\n\nReached through the existing `architect_projects` tool as a `trace` action: the\nrenderer already calls that channel, so no preload or IPC type changed.\n\nVerification: 9 cases cover a foreign project reading nothing and reading nothing\nafter a refusal, a prompt and a payload and a reasoning block and an API key all\nbeing dropped from a record, a name list surviving while a nested object does not,\ntoken counters surviving without a non-numeric usage field, a summary carrying no\nrecords, a detail page respecting its bound, and the tool action defaulting\n`detail` to false. Architect 364 tests, both typechecks clean.","tree":{"sha":"a9a0f0115b9d58b7eda297113274490b5a00f382","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/a9a0f0115b9d58b7eda297113274490b5a00f382"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/d5aed0c8cc456a65d345e0c1da624c33ec60effd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/d5aed0c8cc456a65d345e0c1da624c33ec60effd","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGQ1YWVkMGM4Y2M0NTZhNjVkMzQ1ZTBjMWRhNjI0YzMzZWM2MGVmZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/8bc6d2f654fcec39f9b41fee1e452736c8683fbc","sha":"8bc6d2f654fcec39f9b41fee1e452736c8683fbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/8bc6d2f654fcec39f9b41fee1e452736c8683fbc"}],"sha":"d5aed0c8cc456a65d345e0c1da624c33ec60effd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/d5aed0c8cc456a65d345e0c1da624c33ec60effd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/8bc6d2f654fcec39f9b41fee1e452736c8683fbc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:11:24Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:11:24Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"feat(architect): do not ask a model what the caller already said\n\nEvery successful plan was followed by a second model call to decide how the work\nshould be triggered, even when the caller had already said the work happens once\nor handed over validated triggers. The contract carried a trigger intent for this\nexact case and nothing read it, so the call was always made.\n\nThe Orchestrator now resolves the intent first. A caller that declared the work\none-off, or supplied triggers, has already answered the question the extractor\nexists to ask, so the extractor is not called. An unspecified caller keeps the\nnatural-language path unchanged.\n\nOne-off also means one-off: the Architect sends an empty trigger list, so the\nplanner''s own suggestion cannot schedule a milestone that the project asked for\nonce. Supplied triggers win over any second opinion, and an older caller that\nsets triggers without an intent keeps its existing meaning.\n\nVerification: 4 cases count the model calls on a creation. A one-off milestone\nplans without the extractor and ends with no triggers; supplied triggers survive\nwithout rediscovery; an unspecified caller still makes the second call and\nderives the schedule; triggers without an explicit intent are treated as\nsupplied. Orchestrator 1449 tests, Architect 355, both typechecks clean.\n\nPhase 6 is complete.","tree":{"sha":"7dfbafc4936e8b780d3c115be54e42a6ae567033","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/7dfbafc4936e8b780d3c115be54e42a6ae567033"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/8bc6d2f654fcec39f9b41fee1e452736c8683fbc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/8bc6d2f654fcec39f9b41fee1e452736c8683fbc","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDhiYzZkMmY2NTRmY2VjMzlmOWI0MWZlZTFlNDUyNzM2Yzg2ODNmYmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/c27462fafd4db9af7b43260b2e2a3e1ff931815b","sha":"c27462fafd4db9af7b43260b2e2a3e1ff931815b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/c27462fafd4db9af7b43260b2e2a3e1ff931815b"}],"sha":"8bc6d2f654fcec39f9b41fee1e452736c8683fbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/8bc6d2f654fcec39f9b41fee1e452736c8683fbc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/c27462fafd4db9af7b43260b2e2a3e1ff931815b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:08:14Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:08:14Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"feat(architect): say who is allowed to be an independent check\n\nThe guidance said a completion report is a claim, not evidence, and that\nacceptance needs evidence to pass. It never said that the agent which ran the\ncheck has to be someone other than the agent that did the work, so an\nimplementer''s own suite could read as the independent verification — the exact\nsubstitution the resilience spec forbids.\n\nThe owner contract, the Workflow planner and the Room planner now say the same\nthree things: a self-check is never acceptance; a reviewer that edits the product\nis the author of that edit and needs judgment from elsewhere; and a re-review\ncovers the named findings and what the repair touched instead of a fresh\nwhole-project audit, so unrelated evidence that is still current is not thrown\naway by a new worker or milestone.\n\nThe contract also records the finding from the measured baseline: a review that\nmust execute something needs a workspace it can run in, so a read-only Room is\nthe wrong place for it and the check belongs in a Workflow.\n\nVerification: this is guidance, so it is assessed as behaviour in 8.1 and 8.2\nrather than asserted as text. Architect 355 tests, Orchestrator 1445, both\ntypechecks clean. One Orchestrator case, the debounced fs:changed batching test,\nfailed once in a full run and passed on a re-run and three isolated runs; it\ntouches no code this change modifies.\n\nThe contract snapshots moved with the text.","tree":{"sha":"909dcec0f2516c577007105b1fa70553b39470c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/909dcec0f2516c577007105b1fa70553b39470c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/c27462fafd4db9af7b43260b2e2a3e1ff931815b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/c27462fafd4db9af7b43260b2e2a3e1ff931815b","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGMyNzQ2MmZhZmQ0ZGI5YWY3YjQzMjYwYjJlMmEzZTFmZjkzMTgxNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/ce7f87d392bd6f39f1057c3a9bd0a53ac18cc8d9","sha":"ce7f87d392bd6f39f1057c3a9bd0a53ac18cc8d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/ce7f87d392bd6f39f1057c3a9bd0a53ac18cc8d9"}],"sha":"c27462fafd4db9af7b43260b2e2a3e1ff931815b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/c27462fafd4db9af7b43260b2e2a3e1ff931815b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/ce7f87d392bd6f39f1057c3a9bd0a53ac18cc8d9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:06:17Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:06:17Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"feat(architect): decide relevance from the record, not from a name\n\nA member saw a decision only if the decision''s text contained the member''s\ndisplay name. So a decision about the whole Room, naming nobody, reached nobody\nexcept the Conductor, and one member called Sam also received everything\naddressed to Samantha. Blockers had the same substring match on top of a string\nthat already began with the owner''s name.\n\nApplicability now comes from the record. A decision relates to a work item and\nthat item has an owner, so the brief carries an explicit member id, and a\ndecision that relates to no single item means the whole Room and reaches every\nmember. Blockers compare the name prefix instead of searching the line.\n\nDelegates also now receive what the user approved, and the findings as\nreferences. Approved decisions travel labelled as user approvals, because a\ndelegate must not read the owner''s recommendation as though the user had accepted\nit. Findings travel as the report paths written for task 6.2, never as the report\ntext, so a handoff is still not a transcript.\n\nVerification: 7 cases cover an unnamed decision reaching every member, a scoped\none reaching only its owner, a name inside a sentence not deciding relevance, a\nblocker reaching only the member that has it, the Conductor receiving the whole\nbrief, applicability taken from related work, and a decision about deleted work\nstaying global rather than vanishing. A dispatch case asserts approvals and\nfinding references travel while an open question and the report text do not.\nArchitect 355 tests, Orchestrator 1445, both typechecks clean.","tree":{"sha":"d4c67c827243f4d283d132124a7d2d3393bbd268","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/d4c67c827243f4d283d132124a7d2d3393bbd268"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/ce7f87d392bd6f39f1057c3a9bd0a53ac18cc8d9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/ce7f87d392bd6f39f1057c3a9bd0a53ac18cc8d9","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGNlN2Y4N2QzOTJiZDZmMzlmMTA1N2MzYTliZDBhNTNhYzE4Y2M4ZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/bf8654ad1a1dfee754096e3feb7fdca1c69ec979","sha":"bf8654ad1a1dfee754096e3feb7fdca1c69ec979","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/bf8654ad1a1dfee754096e3feb7fdca1c69ec979"}],"sha":"ce7f87d392bd6f39f1057c3a9bd0a53ac18cc8d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/ce7f87d392bd6f39f1057c3a9bd0a53ac18cc8d9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/bf8654ad1a1dfee754096e3feb7fdca1c69ec979/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:00:17Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:00:17Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"docs(architect): mark task 6.2 complete","tree":{"sha":"aaa81bc02eecaf9b47afaf267442cda6a6c9efb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/aaa81bc02eecaf9b47afaf267442cda6a6c9efb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/bf8654ad1a1dfee754096e3feb7fdca1c69ec979","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/bf8654ad1a1dfee754096e3feb7fdca1c69ec979","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKGJmODY1NGFkMWExZGZlZTc1NDA5NmUzZmViN2ZkY2ExYzY5ZWM5Nzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/99f0b81ae441609d16409f1c2e62c8e514da54c2","sha":"99f0b81ae441609d16409f1c2e62c8e514da54c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/99f0b81ae441609d16409f1c2e62c8e514da54c2"}],"sha":"bf8654ad1a1dfee754096e3feb7fdca1c69ec979","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/bf8654ad1a1dfee754096e3feb7fdca1c69ec979"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/99f0b81ae441609d16409f1c2e62c8e514da54c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:00:07Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:00:07Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"feat(architect): reference research reports instead of repeating them\n\nEvery wake embedded the last five research reports at up to 16 000 characters\neach, so a project with a few findings sent roughly 80 000 characters of history\nbefore the owner read a single instruction for the current objective. A milestone\nplan had no bound either, and every passing check added another command output,\nso the contract grew with the project rather than with the wake.\n\nA completed report is now saved beside the project and the contract carries a\nbounded summary plus a reference. The reference is relative to the project\nfolder, which is the owner session''s working directory and its only allowed cwd,\nso reading it needs no permission the owner does not already have and no new\ngrant. A report that could not be saved, or that predates this change, is\nreported as no longer on disk rather than pointed at as though it were there.\n\nA finished milestone''s plan travels as a summary: its title and status already\nsay it is done, and the detail stays on the record.\n\nThe contract also states the owner model and the model configuration revision,\nso a session that outlives a selection change knows which revision it is working\nagainst instead of assuming the one it was granted.\n\nVerification: 10 new cases cover the size bound on a record holding 40 reports\nand 20 milestones, the authority lines surviving that bound, summaries with\nreachable references, a missing report being reported as missing, the milestone\nplan and evidence-command caps, and the report writer skipping the reference when\nthe folder cannot be written. Architect 354 tests, both typechecks clean.","tree":{"sha":"8bd3ebd88a6e9508ce70af4bcfbf2abf60d95f75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/8bd3ebd88a6e9508ce70af4bcfbf2abf60d95f75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/99f0b81ae441609d16409f1c2e62c8e514da54c2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/99f0b81ae441609d16409f1c2e62c8e514da54c2","node_id":"C_kwDORLCb39oAKDk5ZjBiODFhZTQ0MTYwOWQxNjQwOWYxYzJlNjJjOGU1MTRkYTU0YzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sero-labs/sero/commit/707fa4a06d79a70daab10f57fe82cf01c919bc0e","sha":"707fa4a06d79a70daab10f57fe82cf01c919bc0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/707fa4a06d79a70daab10f57fe82cf01c919bc0e"}],"sha":"99f0b81ae441609d16409f1c2e62c8e514da54c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/99f0b81ae441609d16409f1c2e62c8e514da54c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/monobyte","id":128296,"login":"monobyte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODI5Ng==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monobyte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/commits/707fa4a06d79a70daab10f57fe82cf01c919bc0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T16:55:11Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T16:55:11Z","email":"danielrosscarter@gmail.com","name":"monobyte"},"message":"feat(architect): guide the owner by the work, not by a sequence\n\nThe contract told the owner to \"dispatch it as a Workflow or Room\" and to\n\"choose a Room, a Workflow or focused research according to the task\". Neither\nsays which fits what, so the choice was left to habit, and the milestone plan was\ndescribed without saying it has to be evaluable.\n\nThe build guidance now asks for an objective and acceptance criteria an evaluator\ncould check, says a Room is for investigation, solution planning and adversarial\nreview while a Workflow is for reaching an accepted objective through a\nstructured flow it plans itself, and refuses a worker whose only job is to\nrestate or administratively close work another step already finishes. Discovery\nadds when a question belongs in a Room rather than in one researcher''s hands.\n\nThe dispatch tool carries the same instruction, because that description is what\nthe owner reads while writing the call.\n\nNo new assertions were added. Task 6.1 asks for real planning behaviour to be\nassessed in 8.2, so this relies on the existing planner and dispatch suites:\nArchitect 344, Orchestrator 1438. The contract snapshots moved with the text,\nwhich is what they are for.","tree":{"sha":"f0ec3b2ecad9d7dd775f1380d123b9976c0d9524","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/trees/f0ec3b2ecad9d7dd775f1380d123b9976c0d9524"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sero-labs/sero/git/commits/707fa4a06d79a70daab10f57fe82cf01c919bc0e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.c