o help diagnose why\nData.Read scope is not appearing in the token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add custom JWT converter to extract Entra ID scopes\n\n- Extract ''scp'' claim from Entra ID JWT tokens\n- Convert scope claim to Spring Security authorities with SCOPE_ prefix\n- Enables proper scope-based authorization check\n\nEntra ID tokens use ''scp'' claim for scopes, but Spring Security\nexpects the converter to transform them into authorities. This\ncustom converter extracts scopes from the JWT and creates\nauthorities that match the hasAuthority() checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix compilation error - use Arrays.stream()\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update JWT issuer-uri to use sts.windows.net with tenant ID placeholder\n\n- Changed from login.microsoftonline.com v2.0 to sts.windows.net\n- Entra ID access tokens use sts.windows.net as issuer\n- Uses b033521b-5a18-4110-9d4e-9f28f461e099 placeholder for flexibility across environments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix remote ports and remove debugging logs\n\n- Update vite.config remote URLs to correct ports (metrics: 5178, analytics: 5179)\n- Remove temporary debugging console logs from App components\n- Clean up code after fixing port conflict issue\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve logout to properly clear session and redirect\n\n- Ensure clearSession endpoint is called successfully before clearing state\n- Add response status check for logout endpoint\n- Reload page to root (/) after logout to ensure clean state\n- Prevents showing last view after logout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix double slash in Entra ID OAuth URLs\n\n- Fix substring to remove both /v2.0 and trailing slash (5 chars instead of 4)\n- Applied to getCodeUrl, exchangeCodeForToken, and refreshToken methods\n- Prevents malformed URLs like https://...//oauth2/v2.0/authorize\n- Add login flow logging for debugging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix session authentication and YAML syntax error in BFF\n\n- Fixed duplicate ''server:'' key in application.yml causing YAML parse error\n- Merged server configuration into single block while preserving SameSite cookie config\n- Added SameSite=lax and secure=false to handle cross-site session cookies\n- This allows React app''s fetch requests to properly send session cookies to BFF\n- BFF should now recognize authenticated sessions for /v1/proxy/** requests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure fixed ports for MFE child apps and prevent auto-incrementing\n\n- react-metrics: Fixed port 5178 (was 5177) to match parent expectation\n- react-analytics: Fixed port 5179 (was 5178) to match parent expectation\n- Added strictPort: true to both apps'' server and preview configs\n- This prevents silent port auto-incrementing when ports are busy\n- Apps will now throw an error if the expected port is unavailable\n- Ensures parent app''s hardcoded remoteEntry.js URLs always load correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix BFF proxy routing and Data Backend RBAC\n\n    - BFF: Updated SecurityConfig to permitAll on /v1/proxy/** to allow manual session handling\n    - BFF: Fixed ProxyController to correctly preserve /v1 prefix in forwarded URLs\n    - BFF: Corrected Entra ID auth URL construction in AuthController\n    - Data: Enabled @EnableMethodSecurity and updated JwtAuthenticationConverter to extract roles\n    - Data: Added @PreAuthorize RBAC checks to DataController (metrics: alpha, analytics: beta)\n    - Data: Hardcoded tenant ID in application.yml to fix issuer validation\n\n* Implement full Entra ID logout flow\n\n- BFF: Updated /session/clear to return Entra ID logout URL\n- Frontend: Updated handleLogout to redirect to the IDP logout page\n\n* Update Entra.md with comprehensive handover documentation\n\n* Add Apigee integration documentation\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpipLGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlzwQAKz/IIlhdJkVEHUjvzsrcM4G\nlML9Q1BaOlTxGY2hGT8VhpEdVb3xxX6JgYyj0tW/2lU8RKXRy6sDDVX1kTMl6KFm\nf5uDM62wY6YwcVd3QCe0HFFttU5Gdr+PGDH1IsMIcm4ZnqNDQvkwyLv70jiaFsUf\nKQweCzYptcz7aKKYXFBas8HfbZ32wyD9Lf92usEsX08NVSyUR5vmW/rPl0hKV7F+\nTDmR2jpyh9czngE33sX2PHOSWE/TPVJ5Pcfjrgw9Yk0gEFXfHEqroNpC3HjmAeuZ\nDC2VTEpKhQJkjeHMF7baxBlKOwu1pRiXzFhLi3N5KXbHtDN/eOmIiNlIRa4A0KiP\nA2oAgiuQkVntZxO7egvedd76A1Tz3FDRmMqHIhBkCfx1foqYuGKbPs4F6/WzBDxe\nAmF2wgpNw+nltcbC3xu3zsorbsqxNrERO16mSsCAGSQH5bMooGEFvnkF0EMhcem+\nr93rf6IxiInfS+pLWJEpnVCrjtJMQgz8QjkZsqV28rC8KXQlITIAHELMGrOewgz2\nUpZsV7xXeP0W7VFvQkseAcv9NlwcAn1SAmE21d2uV7o69QaH3cf6UQi71L9NA8aD\nSGISbze/SfgA5+ggP1sZ/eZgxkVsC/QS/sph28nzGfLX5ReCAuegKZXfSALwctFj\nGelhHSFsR+2ODi8BwqIp\n=LeY5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-10T02:07:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commit/8afa917f1fd217fc2b9767311b60a8bdc62e2fcc","node_id":"C_kwDORLk0O9oAKDhhZmE5MTdmMWZkMjE3ZmMyYjk3NjczMTFiNjBhOGJkYzYyZTJmY2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commit/7ba92d1e58ef736818281141cb4f6a508255afdb","sha":"7ba92d1e58ef736818281141cb4f6a508255afdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/7ba92d1e58ef736818281141cb4f6a508255afdb"}],"sha":"8afa917f1fd217fc2b9767311b60a8bdc62e2fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/8afa917f1fd217fc2b9767311b60a8bdc62e2fcc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122412652?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha","id":122412652,"login":"dvalechha","node_id":"U_kgDOB0vebA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/7ba92d1e58ef736818281141cb4f6a508255afdb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-09T03:12:26Z","email":"122412652+dvalechha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dvalechha"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-09T03:12:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/final consolidated fixes (#6)\n\n* Update .gitignore to exclude CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md files\n\n- Prevents platform-specific instruction files from being tracked\n- Other .md files are still allowed in the repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Module Federation remoteEntry.js 404 error in dev mode\n\n- Add dev:fed script to remote MFEs for build+preview workflow\n- Update host app remote URLs to /assets/remoteEntry.js path\n- Enables dynamic MFE loading in development\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation plugin only generates\nremoteEntry.js during build, not during vite dev mode. Using\npreview mode for remotes ensures production-like behavior and\nconsistent federation in development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript error in Module Federation shared config\n\n- Remove singleton flag from shared dependencies\n- Use simple array format for consistency with host app\n- Resolves TS2322 type mismatch error\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation v1.4.1 TypeScript\ndefinitions don''t support the singleton flag. Using the\nsimpler array format works with this version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix missing scope in OAuth2 token exchange\n\n- Add scope parameter to exchangeCodeForToken() method\n- Add scope parameter to refreshToken() method\n- Scope must be included in both authorization and token endpoint requests\n- Resolves 403 Forbidden error due to missing Data.Read scope in JWT\n\nIn Entra ID OAuth2 flow, the scope parameter is required in the\ntoken exchange request (not just the authorization request) to\nensure the access token includes the requested scopes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add access token logging for debugging scope issue\n\nLog access token claims and scopes to help diagnose why\nData.Read scope is not appearing in the token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add custom JWT converter to extract Entra ID scopes\n\n- Extract ''scp'' claim from Entra ID JWT tokens\n- Convert scope claim to Spring Security authorities with SCOPE_ prefix\n- Enables proper scope-based authorization check\n\nEntra ID tokens use ''scp'' claim for scopes, but Spring Security\nexpects the converter to transform them into authorities. This\ncustom converter extracts scopes from the JWT and creates\nauthorities that match the hasAuthority() checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix compilation error - use Arrays.stream()\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update JWT issuer-uri to use sts.windows.net with tenant ID placeholder\n\n- Changed from login.microsoftonline.com v2.0 to sts.windows.net\n- Entra ID access tokens use sts.windows.net as issuer\n- Uses b033521b-5a18-4110-9d4e-9f28f461e099 placeholder for flexibility across environments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix remote ports and remove debugging logs\n\n- Update vite.config remote URLs to correct ports (metrics: 5178, analytics: 5179)\n- Remove temporary debugging console logs from App components\n- Clean up code after fixing port conflict issue\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve logout to properly clear session and redirect\n\n- Ensure clearSession endpoint is called successfully before clearing state\n- Add response status check for logout endpoint\n- Reload page to root (/) after logout to ensure clean state\n- Prevents showing last view after logout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix double slash in Entra ID OAuth URLs\n\n- Fix substring to remove both /v2.0 and trailing slash (5 chars instead of 4)\n- Applied to getCodeUrl, exchangeCodeForToken, and refreshToken methods\n- Prevents malformed URLs like https://...//oauth2/v2.0/authorize\n- Add login flow logging for debugging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix session authentication and YAML syntax error in BFF\n\n- Fixed duplicate ''server:'' key in application.yml causing YAML parse error\n- Merged server configuration into single block while preserving SameSite cookie config\n- Added SameSite=lax and secure=false to handle cross-site session cookies\n- This allows React app''s fetch requests to properly send session cookies to BFF\n- BFF should now recognize authenticated sessions for /v1/proxy/** requests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure fixed ports for MFE child apps and prevent auto-incrementing\n\n- react-metrics: Fixed port 5178 (was 5177) to match parent expectation\n- react-analytics: Fixed port 5179 (was 5178) to match parent expectation\n- Added strictPort: true to both apps'' server and preview configs\n- This prevents silent port auto-incrementing when ports are busy\n- Apps will now throw an error if the expected port is unavailable\n- Ensures parent app''s hardcoded remoteEntry.js URLs always load correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix BFF proxy routing and Data Backend RBAC\n\n    - BFF: Updated SecurityConfig to permitAll on /v1/proxy/** to allow manual session handling\n    - BFF: Fixed ProxyController to correctly preserve /v1 prefix in forwarded URLs\n    - BFF: Corrected Entra ID auth URL construction in AuthController\n    - Data: Enabled @EnableMethodSecurity and updated JwtAuthenticationConverter to extract roles\n    - Data: Added @PreAuthorize RBAC checks to DataController (metrics: alpha, analytics: beta)\n    - Data: Hardcoded tenant ID in application.yml to fix issuer validation\n\n* Implement full Entra ID logout flow\n\n- BFF: Updated /session/clear to return Entra ID logout URL\n- Frontend: Updated handleLogout to redirect to the IDP logout page\n\n* Update Entra.md with comprehensive handover documentation\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"57f9e3ca30437b9e64aa76ed0c7dd4403e73f698","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/git/trees/57f9e3ca30437b9e64aa76ed0c7dd4403e73f698"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/git/commits/7ba92d1e58ef736818281141cb4f6a508255afdb","verification":{"payload":"tree 57f9e3ca30437b9e64aa76ed0c7dd4403e73f698\nparent d5ac68c2e553e08b0b58c359d653d788f161d910\nauthor dvalechha <122412652+dvalechha@users.noreply.github.com> 1770606746 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770606746 -0500\n\nFeature/final consolidated fixes (#6)\n\n* Update .gitignore to exclude CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md files\n\n- Prevents platform-specific instruction files from being tracked\n- Other .md files are still allowed in the repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Module Federation remoteEntry.js 404 error in dev mode\n\n- Add dev:fed script to remote MFEs for build+preview workflow\n- Update host app remote URLs to /assets/remoteEntry.js path\n- Enables dynamic MFE loading in development\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation plugin only generates\nremoteEntry.js during build, not during vite dev mode. Using\npreview mode for remotes ensures production-like behavior and\nconsistent federation in development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript error in Module Federation shared config\n\n- Remove singleton flag from shared dependencies\n- Use simple array format for consistency with host app\n- Resolves TS2322 type mismatch error\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation v1.4.1 TypeScript\ndefinitions don''t support the singleton flag. Using the\nsimpler array format works with this version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix missing scope in OAuth2 token exchange\n\n- Add scope parameter to exchangeCodeForToken() method\n- Add scope parameter to refreshToken() method\n- Scope must be included in both authorization and token endpoint requests\n- Resolves 403 Forbidden error due to missing Data.Read scope in JWT\n\nIn Entra ID OAuth2 flow, the scope parameter is required in the\ntoken exchange request (not just the authorization request) to\nensure the access token includes the requested scopes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add access token logging for debugging scope issue\n\nLog access token claims and scopes to help diagnose why\nData.Read scope is not appearing in the token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add custom JWT converter to extract Entra ID scopes\n\n- Extract ''scp'' claim from Entra ID JWT tokens\n- Convert scope claim to Spring Security authorities with SCOPE_ prefix\n- Enables proper scope-based authorization check\n\nEntra ID tokens use ''scp'' claim for scopes, but Spring Security\nexpects the converter to transform them into authorities. This\ncustom converter extracts scopes from the JWT and creates\nauthorities that match the hasAuthority() checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix compilation error - use Arrays.stream()\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update JWT issuer-uri to use sts.windows.net with tenant ID placeholder\n\n- Changed from login.microsoftonline.com v2.0 to sts.windows.net\n- Entra ID access tokens use sts.windows.net as issuer\n- Uses b033521b-5a18-4110-9d4e-9f28f461e099 placeholder for flexibility across environments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix remote ports and remove debugging logs\n\n- Update vite.config remote URLs to correct ports (metrics: 5178, analytics: 5179)\n- Remove temporary debugging console logs from App components\n- Clean up code after fixing port conflict issue\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve logout to properly clear session and redirect\n\n- Ensure clearSession endpoint is called successfully before clearing state\n- Add response status check for logout endpoint\n- Reload page to root (/) after logout to ensure clean state\n- Prevents showing last view after logout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix double slash in Entra ID OAuth URLs\n\n- Fix substring to remove both /v2.0 and trailing slash (5 chars instead of 4)\n- Applied to getCodeUrl, exchangeCodeForToken, and refreshToken methods\n- Prevents malformed URLs like https://...//oauth2/v2.0/authorize\n- Add login flow logging for debugging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix session authentication and YAML syntax error in BFF\n\n- Fixed duplicate ''server:'' key in application.yml causing YAML parse error\n- Merged server configuration into single block while preserving SameSite cookie config\n- Added SameSite=lax and secure=false to handle cross-site session cookies\n- This allows React app''s fetch requests to properly send session cookies to BFF\n- BFF should now recognize authenticated sessions for /v1/proxy/** requests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure fixed ports for MFE child apps and prevent auto-incrementing\n\n- react-metrics: Fixed port 5178 (was 5177) to match parent expectation\n- react-analytics: Fixed port 5179 (was 5178) to match parent expectation\n- Added strictPort: true to both apps'' server and preview configs\n- This prevents silent port auto-incrementing when ports are busy\n- Apps will now throw an error if the expected port is unavailable\n- Ensures parent app''s hardcoded remoteEntry.js URLs always load correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix BFF proxy routing and Data Backend RBAC\n\n    - BFF: Updated SecurityConfig to permitAll on /v1/proxy/** to allow manual session handling\n    - BFF: Fixed ProxyController to correctly preserve /v1 prefix in forwarded URLs\n    - BFF: Corrected Entra ID auth URL construction in AuthController\n    - Data: Enabled @EnableMethodSecurity and updated JwtAuthenticationConverter to extract roles\n    - Data: Added @PreAuthorize RBAC checks to DataController (metrics: alpha, analytics: beta)\n    - Data: Hardcoded tenant ID in application.yml to fix issuer validation\n\n* Implement full Entra ID logout flow\n\n- BFF: Updated /session/clear to return Entra ID logout URL\n- Frontend: Updated handleLogout to redirect to the IDP logout page\n\n* Update Entra.md with comprehensive handover documentation\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpiVCaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeFQQABVPSBVHcR684lXkNLPOEiEA\n0lNI2iPxxxzGIxOtWFj4l5EzhCtlMb7hQdlUsh1OSeoq5Jh4FWo/SWuJTT1CF+2E\nihY1GIwICor3Ryld+jRT4BW9fuw4mwmy2s2P1e5E/VNLwZZwsZ0YpfbzhWrwTQgt\nCrlRGeuThaxetesrsqTOO1Ow6/uxnjVRqEmFwLZ5ZVsCx7V7vOAGwLIc00lpmyKS\n8KV2xoMItCQkij1osuFH3GmyQ16DxAvaYzP6zoT2OxJuiDGEoUMn1T40tlq065kH\nxCrc7KkpfM0Qu6HQrCaN5BRzA6WGkVuc463dbUe0S8O5XGvYAuO7HCtbGlUoVnri\n+nNqnfcdhhZGIBOUNmtOUVU5U8l8rHub7mcGXa1zzGdq1B5xn3LUiAVwBDDCKvjH\nLkMyzx4gcvqQQrMmgfbbmNixk1nYeLTO1ZdRWbnIV47oYiCDLDcJoxOPURJez1d/\n7vLJjx83rr7GMz/ijQ8MjIteSheSBAWv0PM2LGKLJJz7LqeLCpFoeCJH2yZkVHKe\nDCkwKwuJyjyd/1YEzH0lxuWH7TpzOwH1lDo6rJagIFxv7Y8h/buuMu/qbba43zek\nMtITzQ/Np77QDAnxE91ZB7MmSJoa9frWaIRfGZHou8T6bFRzlOKM5u8y98bSso82\npCPBPamckEgMn0gUFLCJ\n=SrKv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-09T03:12:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commit/7ba92d1e58ef736818281141cb4f6a508255afdb","node_id":"C_kwDORLk0O9oAKDdiYTkyZDFlNThlZjczNjgxODI4MTE0MWNiNGY2YTUwODI1NWFmZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commit/d5ac68c2e553e08b0b58c359d653d788f161d910","sha":"d5ac68c2e553e08b0b58c359d653d788f161d910","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/d5ac68c2e553e08b0b58c359d653d788f161d910"}],"sha":"7ba92d1e58ef736818281141cb4f6a508255afdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/7ba92d1e58ef736818281141cb4f6a508255afdb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122412652?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha","id":122412652,"login":"dvalechha","node_id":"U_kgDOB0vebA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/d5ac68c2e553e08b0b58c359d653d788f161d910/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-09T03:03:08Z","email":"122412652+dvalechha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dvalechha"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-09T03:03:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/final consolidated fixes (#5)\n\n* Update .gitignore to exclude CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md files\n\n- Prevents platform-specific instruction files from being tracked\n- Other .md files are still allowed in the repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Module Federation remoteEntry.js 404 error in dev mode\n\n- Add dev:fed script to remote MFEs for build+preview workflow\n- Update host app remote URLs to /assets/remoteEntry.js path\n- Enables dynamic MFE loading in development\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation plugin only generates\nremoteEntry.js during build, not during vite dev mode. Using\npreview mode for remotes ensures production-like behavior and\nconsistent federation in development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript error in Module Federation shared config\n\n- Remove singleton flag from shared dependencies\n- Use simple array format for consistency with host app\n- Resolves TS2322 type mismatch error\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation v1.4.1 TypeScript\ndefinitions don''t support the singleton flag. Using the\nsimpler array format works with this version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix missing scope in OAuth2 token exchange\n\n- Add scope parameter to exchangeCodeForToken() method\n- Add scope parameter to refreshToken() method\n- Scope must be included in both authorization and token endpoint requests\n- Resolves 403 Forbidden error due to missing Data.Read scope in JWT\n\nIn Entra ID OAuth2 flow, the scope parameter is required in the\ntoken exchange request (not just the authorization request) to\nensure the access token includes the requested scopes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add access token logging for debugging scope issue\n\nLog access token claims and scopes to help diagnose why\nData.Read scope is not appearing in the token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add custom JWT converter to extract Entra ID scopes\n\n- Extract ''scp'' claim from Entra ID JWT tokens\n- Convert scope claim to Spring Security authorities with SCOPE_ prefix\n- Enables proper scope-based authorization check\n\nEntra ID tokens use ''scp'' claim for scopes, but Spring Security\nexpects the converter to transform them into authorities. This\ncustom converter extracts scopes from the JWT and creates\nauthorities that match the hasAuthority() checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix compilation error - use Arrays.stream()\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update JWT issuer-uri to use sts.windows.net with tenant ID placeholder\n\n- Changed from login.microsoftonline.com v2.0 to sts.windows.net\n- Entra ID access tokens use sts.windows.net as issuer\n- Uses b033521b-5a18-4110-9d4e-9f28f461e099 placeholder for flexibility across environments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix remote ports and remove debugging logs\n\n- Update vite.config remote URLs to correct ports (metrics: 5178, analytics: 5179)\n- Remove temporary debugging console logs from App components\n- Clean up code after fixing port conflict issue\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve logout to properly clear session and redirect\n\n- Ensure clearSession endpoint is called successfully before clearing state\n- Add response status check for logout endpoint\n- Reload page to root (/) after logout to ensure clean state\n- Prevents showing last view after logout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix double slash in Entra ID OAuth URLs\n\n- Fix substring to remove both /v2.0 and trailing slash (5 chars instead of 4)\n- Applied to getCodeUrl, exchangeCodeForToken, and refreshToken methods\n- Prevents malformed URLs like https://...//oauth2/v2.0/authorize\n- Add login flow logging for debugging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix session authentication and YAML syntax error in BFF\n\n- Fixed duplicate ''server:'' key in application.yml causing YAML parse error\n- Merged server configuration into single block while preserving SameSite cookie config\n- Added SameSite=lax and secure=false to handle cross-site session cookies\n- This allows React app''s fetch requests to properly send session cookies to BFF\n- BFF should now recognize authenticated sessions for /v1/proxy/** requests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure fixed ports for MFE child apps and prevent auto-incrementing\n\n- react-metrics: Fixed port 5178 (was 5177) to match parent expectation\n- react-analytics: Fixed port 5179 (was 5178) to match parent expectation\n- Added strictPort: true to both apps'' server and preview configs\n- This prevents silent port auto-incrementing when ports are busy\n- Apps will now throw an error if the expected port is unavailable\n- Ensures parent app''s hardcoded remoteEntry.js URLs always load correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix BFF proxy routing and Data Backend RBAC\n\n    - BFF: Updated SecurityConfig to permitAll on /v1/proxy/** to allow manual session handling\n    - BFF: Fixed ProxyController to correctly preserve /v1 prefix in forwarded URLs\n    - BFF: Corrected Entra ID auth URL construction in AuthController\n    - Data: Enabled @EnableMethodSecurity and updated JwtAuthenticationConverter to extract roles\n    - Data: Added @PreAuthorize RBAC checks to DataController (metrics: alpha, analytics: beta)\n    - Data: Hardcoded tenant ID in application.yml to fix issuer validation\n\n* Implement full Entra ID logout flow\n\n- BFF: Updated /session/clear to return Entra ID logout URL\n- Frontend: Updated handleLogout to redirect to the IDP logout page\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"03c48f84f3fd754b847042854e4486202854adf5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/git/trees/03c48f84f3fd754b847042854e4486202854adf5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/git/commits/d5ac68c2e553e08b0b58c359d653d788f161d910","verification":{"payload":"tree 03c48f84f3fd754b847042854e4486202854adf5\nparent f6252a38337e5fab9a83b4830929656c847d0d89\nauthor dvalechha <122412652+dvalechha@users.noreply.github.com> 1770606188 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770606188 -0500\n\nFeature/final consolidated fixes (#5)\n\n* Update .gitignore to exclude CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md files\n\n- Prevents platform-specific instruction files from being tracked\n- Other .md files are still allowed in the repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Module Federation remoteEntry.js 404 error in dev mode\n\n- Add dev:fed script to remote MFEs for build+preview workflow\n- Update host app remote URLs to /assets/remoteEntry.js path\n- Enables dynamic MFE loading in development\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation plugin only generates\nremoteEntry.js during build, not during vite dev mode. Using\npreview mode for remotes ensures production-like behavior and\nconsistent federation in development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript error in Module Federation shared config\n\n- Remove singleton flag from shared dependencies\n- Use simple array format for consistency with host app\n- Resolves TS2322 type mismatch error\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation v1.4.1 TypeScript\ndefinitions don''t support the singleton flag. Using the\nsimpler array format works with this version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix missing scope in OAuth2 token exchange\n\n- Add scope parameter to exchangeCodeForToken() method\n- Add scope parameter to refreshToken() method\n- Scope must be included in both authorization and token endpoint requests\n- Resolves 403 Forbidden error due to missing Data.Read scope in JWT\n\nIn Entra ID OAuth2 flow, the scope parameter is required in the\ntoken exchange request (not just the authorization request) to\nensure the access token includes the requested scopes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add access token logging for debugging scope issue\n\nLog access token claims and scopes to help diagnose why\nData.Read scope is not appearing in the token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add custom JWT converter to extract Entra ID scopes\n\n- Extract ''scp'' claim from Entra ID JWT tokens\n- Convert scope claim to Spring Security authorities with SCOPE_ prefix\n- Enables proper scope-based authorization check\n\nEntra ID tokens use ''scp'' claim for scopes, but Spring Security\nexpects the converter to transform them into authorities. This\ncustom converter extracts scopes from the JWT and creates\nauthorities that match the hasAuthority() checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix compilation error - use Arrays.stream()\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update JWT issuer-uri to use sts.windows.net with tenant ID placeholder\n\n- Changed from login.microsoftonline.com v2.0 to sts.windows.net\n- Entra ID access tokens use sts.windows.net as issuer\n- Uses b033521b-5a18-4110-9d4e-9f28f461e099 placeholder for flexibility across environments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix remote ports and remove debugging logs\n\n- Update vite.config remote URLs to correct ports (metrics: 5178, analytics: 5179)\n- Remove temporary debugging console logs from App components\n- Clean up code after fixing port conflict issue\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve logout to properly clear session and redirect\n\n- Ensure clearSession endpoint is called successfully before clearing state\n- Add response status check for logout endpoint\n- Reload page to root (/) after logout to ensure clean state\n- Prevents showing last view after logout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix double slash in Entra ID OAuth URLs\n\n- Fix substring to remove both /v2.0 and trailing slash (5 chars instead of 4)\n- Applied to getCodeUrl, exchangeCodeForToken, and refreshToken methods\n- Prevents malformed URLs like https://...//oauth2/v2.0/authorize\n- Add login flow logging for debugging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix session authentication and YAML syntax error in BFF\n\n- Fixed duplicate ''server:'' key in application.yml causing YAML parse error\n- Merged server configuration into single block while preserving SameSite cookie config\n- Added SameSite=lax and secure=false to handle cross-site session cookies\n- This allows React app''s fetch requests to properly send session cookies to BFF\n- BFF should now recognize authenticated sessions for /v1/proxy/** requests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure fixed ports for MFE child apps and prevent auto-incrementing\n\n- react-metrics: Fixed port 5178 (was 5177) to match parent expectation\n- react-analytics: Fixed port 5179 (was 5178) to match parent expectation\n- Added strictPort: true to both apps'' server and preview configs\n- This prevents silent port auto-incrementing when ports are busy\n- Apps will now throw an error if the expected port is unavailable\n- Ensures parent app''s hardcoded remoteEntry.js URLs always load correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix BFF proxy routing and Data Backend RBAC\n\n    - BFF: Updated SecurityConfig to permitAll on /v1/proxy/** to allow manual session handling\n    - BFF: Fixed ProxyController to correctly preserve /v1 prefix in forwarded URLs\n    - BFF: Corrected Entra ID auth URL construction in AuthController\n    - Data: Enabled @EnableMethodSecurity and updated JwtAuthenticationConverter to extract roles\n    - Data: Added @PreAuthorize RBAC checks to DataController (metrics: alpha, analytics: beta)\n    - Data: Hardcoded tenant ID in application.yml to fix issuer validation\n\n* Implement full Entra ID logout flow\n\n- BFF: Updated /session/clear to return Entra ID logout URL\n- Frontend: Updated handleLogout to redirect to the IDP logout page\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpiU5sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+FoQAJHS5kNNh5dcd/AgGPFtyxaT\n+vyhg4FtFW1usnLQZHWAE7l8QQspXxLPZcAQ5e3T0shPIK9o6sr//Pp0KZy/AMbL\noVhHgilCmRMbVuNRuzT51pmsLm+v5wp0qDFvF7QwIrcfE0yEhLw+CJkyHUqNXY46\nOjTNiKTRygiJZTi4FHlnFYBe8TjYDTz88Ca3M5IEi6+9BTC/isJoAe5tW56Oab7V\nXdxbrZPUDx1KZOZfjqIFXciF35+aiFwb/6l22075aFyARa1usm1AXydeukB/ik9m\nHW+EDCYMju5Tw1c95LKzEVeb1pz57tSDV18hbz8pDVV047MX8JNMT62LOR6hn9Q7\nxVafWRLW40cqDNGxE2TKOTctrfvgASF8X9XYpmwYXsNu4NWltD1cWz2pTyKdYR7H\nbaV+RLUOD8mQBfo1hArQa+WyObH4GbkZORDlzEJDjOmFSSse8a8ZQAi6itC0NzBO\nOn1bDEEyT6HANjLP9s2t3dXK8ZKAy7JTIXMxBtmmd6Vte6ifxldENMsE1G7UrF2e\neO6n2ivcHpBSNivgFU8Hb7tRmavSF14MFarlAkchhAUiGFwVR+lnTE97LsMWxBAA\n5lf9fqEOBeIYCMqJTsVuDC+2t8TxaYbLNVwzz9a9qCkUjnaD6bO1CGA1CokVZb8l\nAXHOFrpHDAQTRacQ4jjL\n=SDt/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-09T03:03:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commit/d5ac68c2e553e08b0b58c359d653d788f161d910","node_id":"C_kwDORLk0O9oAKGQ1YWM2OGMyZTU1M2UwOGIwYjU4YzM1OWQ2NTNkNzg4ZjE2MWQ5MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commit/f6252a38337e5fab9a83b4830929656c847d0d89","sha":"f6252a38337e5fab9a83b4830929656c847d0d89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/f6252a38337e5fab9a83b4830929656c847d0d89"}],"sha":"d5ac68c2e553e08b0b58c359d653d788f161d910","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/d5ac68c2e553e08b0b58c359d653d788f161d910"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122412652?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha","id":122412652,"login":"dvalechha","node_id":"U_kgDOB0vebA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/f6252a38337e5fab9a83b4830929656c847d0d89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-09T02:50:12Z","email":"122412652+dvalechha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dvalechha"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-09T02:50:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/bug fix dv3 (#4)\n\n* Update .gitignore to exclude CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md files\n\n- Prevents platform-specific instruction files from being tracked\n- Other .md files are still allowed in the repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Module Federation remoteEntry.js 404 error in dev mode\n\n- Add dev:fed script to remote MFEs for build+preview workflow\n- Update host app remote URLs to /assets/remoteEntry.js path\n- Enables dynamic MFE loading in development\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation plugin only generates\nremoteEntry.js during build, not during vite dev mode. Using\npreview mode for remotes ensures production-like behavior and\nconsistent federation in development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript error in Module Federation shared config\n\n- Remove singleton flag from shared dependencies\n- Use simple array format for consistency with host app\n- Resolves TS2322 type mismatch error\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation v1.4.1 TypeScript\ndefinitions don''t support the singleton flag. Using the\nsimpler array format works with this version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix missing scope in OAuth2 token exchange\n\n- Add scope parameter to exchangeCodeForToken() method\n- Add scope parameter to refreshToken() method\n- Scope must be included in both authorization and token endpoint requests\n- Resolves 403 Forbidden error due to missing Data.Read scope in JWT\n\nIn Entra ID OAuth2 flow, the scope parameter is required in the\ntoken exchange request (not just the authorization request) to\nensure the access token includes the requested scopes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add access token logging for debugging scope issue\n\nLog access token claims and scopes to help diagnose why\nData.Read scope is not appearing in the token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add custom JWT converter to extract Entra ID scopes\n\n- Extract ''scp'' claim from Entra ID JWT tokens\n- Convert scope claim to Spring Security authorities with SCOPE_ prefix\n- Enables proper scope-based authorization check\n\nEntra ID tokens use ''scp'' claim for scopes, but Spring Security\nexpects the converter to transform them into authorities. This\ncustom converter extracts scopes from the JWT and creates\nauthorities that match the hasAuthority() checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix compilation error - use Arrays.stream()\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update JWT issuer-uri to use sts.windows.net with tenant ID placeholder\n\n- Changed from login.microsoftonline.com v2.0 to sts.windows.net\n- Entra ID access tokens use sts.windows.net as issuer\n- Uses b033521b-5a18-4110-9d4e-9f28f461e099 placeholder for flexibility across environments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix remote ports and remove debugging logs\n\n- Update vite.config remote URLs to correct ports (metrics: 5178, analytics: 5179)\n- Remove temporary debugging console logs from App components\n- Clean up code after fixing port conflict issue\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve logout to properly clear session and redirect\n\n- Ensure clearSession endpoint is called successfully before clearing state\n- Add response status check for logout endpoint\n- Reload page to root (/) after logout to ensure clean state\n- Prevents showing last view after logout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix double slash in Entra ID OAuth URLs\n\n- Fix substring to remove both /v2.0 and trailing slash (5 chars instead of 4)\n- Applied to getCodeUrl, exchangeCodeForToken, and refreshToken methods\n- Prevents malformed URLs like https://...//oauth2/v2.0/authorize\n- Add login flow logging for debugging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix session authentication and YAML syntax error in BFF\n\n- Fixed duplicate ''server:'' key in application.yml causing YAML parse error\n- Merged server configuration into single block while preserving SameSite cookie config\n- Added SameSite=lax and secure=false to handle cross-site session cookies\n- This allows React app''s fetch requests to properly send session cookies to BFF\n- BFF should now recognize authenticated sessions for /v1/proxy/** requests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure fixed ports for MFE child apps and prevent auto-incrementing\n\n- react-metrics: Fixed port 5178 (was 5177) to match parent expectation\n- react-analytics: Fixed port 5179 (was 5178) to match parent expectation\n- Added strictPort: true to both apps'' server and preview configs\n- This prevents silent port auto-incrementing when ports are busy\n- Apps will now throw an error if the expected port is unavailable\n- Ensures parent app''s hardcoded remoteEntry.js URLs always load correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix BFF proxy routing and Data Backend RBAC\n\n    - BFF: Updated SecurityConfig to permitAll on /v1/proxy/** to allow manual session handling\n    - BFF: Fixed ProxyController to correctly preserve /v1 prefix in forwarded URLs\n    - BFF: Corrected Entra ID auth URL construction in AuthController\n    - Data: Enabled @EnableMethodSecurity and updated JwtAuthenticationConverter to extract roles\n    - Data: Added @PreAuthorize RBAC checks to DataController (metrics: alpha, analytics: beta)\n    - Data: Hardcoded tenant ID in application.yml to fix issuer validation\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0981fda54c1479458735be145047aaad959a06e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/git/trees/0981fda54c1479458735be145047aaad959a06e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/git/commits/f6252a38337e5fab9a83b4830929656c847d0d89","verification":{"payload":"tree 0981fda54c1479458735be145047aaad959a06e1\nparent 890ab05781fa2d9e5b16f59df16d3a51eed29d42\nauthor dvalechha <122412652+dvalechha@users.noreply.github.com> 1770605412 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770605412 -0500\n\nFeature/bug fix dv3 (#4)\n\n* Update .gitignore to exclude CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md files\n\n- Prevents platform-specific instruction files from being tracked\n- Other .md files are still allowed in the repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Module Federation remoteEntry.js 404 error in dev mode\n\n- Add dev:fed script to remote MFEs for build+preview workflow\n- Update host app remote URLs to /assets/remoteEntry.js path\n- Enables dynamic MFE loading in development\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation plugin only generates\nremoteEntry.js during build, not during vite dev mode. Using\npreview mode for remotes ensures production-like behavior and\nconsistent federation in development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript error in Module Federation shared config\n\n- Remove singleton flag from shared dependencies\n- Use simple array format for consistency with host app\n- Resolves TS2322 type mismatch error\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation v1.4.1 TypeScript\ndefinitions don''t support the singleton flag. Using the\nsimpler array format works with this version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix missing scope in OAuth2 token exchange\n\n- Add scope parameter to exchangeCodeForToken() method\n- Add scope parameter to refreshToken() method\n- Scope must be included in both authorization and token endpoint requests\n- Resolves 403 Forbidden error due to missing Data.Read scope in JWT\n\nIn Entra ID OAuth2 flow, the scope parameter is required in the\ntoken exchange request (not just the authorization request) to\nensure the access token includes the requested scopes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add access token logging for debugging scope issue\n\nLog access token claims and scopes to help diagnose why\nData.Read scope is not appearing in the token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add custom JWT converter to extract Entra ID scopes\n\n- Extract ''scp'' claim from Entra ID JWT tokens\n- Convert scope claim to Spring Security authorities with SCOPE_ prefix\n- Enables proper scope-based authorization check\n\nEntra ID tokens use ''scp'' claim for scopes, but Spring Security\nexpects the converter to transform them into authorities. This\ncustom converter extracts scopes from the JWT and creates\nauthorities that match the hasAuthority() checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix compilation error - use Arrays.stream()\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update JWT issuer-uri to use sts.windows.net with tenant ID placeholder\n\n- Changed from login.microsoftonline.com v2.0 to sts.windows.net\n- Entra ID access tokens use sts.windows.net as issuer\n- Uses b033521b-5a18-4110-9d4e-9f28f461e099 placeholder for flexibility across environments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix remote ports and remove debugging logs\n\n- Update vite.config remote URLs to correct ports (metrics: 5178, analytics: 5179)\n- Remove temporary debugging console logs from App components\n- Clean up code after fixing port conflict issue\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve logout to properly clear session and redirect\n\n- Ensure clearSession endpoint is called successfully before clearing state\n- Add response status check for logout endpoint\n- Reload page to root (/) after logout to ensure clean state\n- Prevents showing last view after logout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix double slash in Entra ID OAuth URLs\n\n- Fix substring to remove both /v2.0 and trailing slash (5 chars instead of 4)\n- Applied to getCodeUrl, exchangeCodeForToken, and refreshToken methods\n- Prevents malformed URLs like https://...//oauth2/v2.0/authorize\n- Add login flow logging for debugging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix session authentication and YAML syntax error in BFF\n\n- Fixed duplicate ''server:'' key in application.yml causing YAML parse error\n- Merged server configuration into single block while preserving SameSite cookie config\n- Added SameSite=lax and secure=false to handle cross-site session cookies\n- This allows React app''s fetch requests to properly send session cookies to BFF\n- BFF should now recognize authenticated sessions for /v1/proxy/** requests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure fixed ports for MFE child apps and prevent auto-incrementing\n\n- react-metrics: Fixed port 5178 (was 5177) to match parent expectation\n- react-analytics: Fixed port 5179 (was 5178) to match parent expectation\n- Added strictPort: true to both apps'' server and preview configs\n- This prevents silent port auto-incrementing when ports are busy\n- Apps will now throw an error if the expected port is unavailable\n- Ensures parent app''s hardcoded remoteEntry.js URLs always load correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix BFF proxy routing and Data Backend RBAC\n\n    - BFF: Updated SecurityConfig to permitAll on /v1/proxy/** to allow manual session handling\n    - BFF: Fixed ProxyController to correctly preserve /v1 prefix in forwarded URLs\n    - BFF: Corrected Entra ID auth URL construction in AuthController\n    - Data: Enabled @EnableMethodSecurity and updated JwtAuthenticationConverter to extract roles\n    - Data: Added @PreAuthorize RBAC checks to DataController (metrics: alpha, analytics: beta)\n    - Data: Hardcoded tenant ID in application.yml to fix issuer validation\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpiUtkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7IcQAGmBLfI7mac7JdUPddOvBuzb\nKEE2Qz1kzU5kxuZ13/Jqj4xpZIdy4mSDNjOzcUTtpHMxgpgNUa/6C6EIckzdDoOm\nQLmjO7wrKzIULLFmfk4LQYT07BWaHk5cBdVuwqm9BjqX0wDnXTRYpqzXwpvwrf9z\nArJ3AT9KhN7yxOm23YtNsW/stY41E1jXhsXHPRMePRhZ2ECUD0AKtP4YmhnySfDb\n70FYvyJEnj4Iuhpj9NV4taWL4XBIg95Lc88aALBRiEJG6rmvP4gpBp3Wd7riFR45\nTFMYRTYJJYC9ZvaKP2MSSZLlzjm3VrRABB7MvYIHGUJh6FdKQC+IOKUpMHYclbyr\nc6UNboWfU2y7wql2lLFhy6EDpQHbQX2QFYqhyIep8vv9gfAhrq/0Q0orAiycui5P\nxKkFlp97ocQaYVcmJG8Y9Y88JXL96BZQt9mWg6E+pBBtp7d6KyoVC/r7H+Lmb73f\nHwZQiXoNwmaMDK7AY1gbRSB7gmSuOjdE9PUT8PTBQ6y0oXcOW0myemNVsT/50yJO\nFDY31lEdIa/lo+l/mkUkG1li79ql4XMLKwqK1HxulzarBG5Wvecb5Bs9N86VlCpG\nqCaRrTgEvkRarVbjP4fjKkzFlNSHT1tZHBvnYBsSnCh5NXNJ3aW1pncKqVY4rJoW\ntwxziQQDox2TYIJfPwt5\n=+TQG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-09T02:50:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commit/f6252a38337e5fab9a83b4830929656c847d0d89","node_id":"C_kwDORLk0O9oAKGY2MjUyYTM4MzM3ZTVmYWI5YTgzYjQ4MzA5Mjk2NTZjODQ3ZDBkODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commit/890ab05781fa2d9e5b16f59df16d3a51eed29d42","sha":"890ab05781fa2d9e5b16f59df16d3a51eed29d42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/890ab05781fa2d9e5b16f59df16d3a51eed29d42"}],"sha":"f6252a38337e5fab9a83b4830929656c847d0d89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/f6252a38337e5fab9a83b4830929656c847d0d89"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122412652?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha","id":122412652,"login":"dvalechha","node_id":"U_kgDOB0vebA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/890ab05781fa2d9e5b16f59df16d3a51eed29d42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-09T02:49:44Z","email":"122412652+dvalechha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dvalechha"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-09T02:49:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/bug fix dv3 (#3)\n\n* Update .gitignore to exclude CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md files\n\n- Prevents platform-specific instruction files from being tracked\n- Other .md files are still allowed in the repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Module Federation remoteEntry.js 404 error in dev mode\n\n- Add dev:fed script to remote MFEs for build+preview workflow\n- Update host app remote URLs to /assets/remoteEntry.js path\n- Enables dynamic MFE loading in development\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation plugin only generates\nremoteEntry.js during build, not during vite dev mode. Using\npreview mode for remotes ensures production-like behavior and\nconsistent federation in development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript error in Module Federation shared config\n\n- Remove singleton flag from shared dependencies\n- Use simple array format for consistency with host app\n- Resolves TS2322 type mismatch error\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation v1.4.1 TypeScript\ndefinitions don''t support the singleton flag. Using the\nsimpler array format works with this version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix missing scope in OAuth2 token exchange\n\n- Add scope parameter to exchangeCodeForToken() method\n- Add scope parameter to refreshToken() method\n- Scope must be included in both authorization and token endpoint requests\n- Resolves 403 Forbidden error due to missing Data.Read scope in JWT\n\nIn Entra ID OAuth2 flow, the scope parameter is required in the\ntoken exchange request (not just the authorization request) to\nensure the access token includes the requested scopes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add access token logging for debugging scope issue\n\nLog access token claims and scopes to help diagnose why\nData.Read scope is not appearing in the token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add custom JWT converter to extract Entra ID scopes\n\n- Extract ''scp'' claim from Entra ID JWT tokens\n- Convert scope claim to Spring Security authorities with SCOPE_ prefix\n- Enables proper scope-based authorization check\n\nEntra ID tokens use ''scp'' claim for scopes, but Spring Security\nexpects the converter to transform them into authorities. This\ncustom converter extracts scopes from the JWT and creates\nauthorities that match the hasAuthority() checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix compilation error - use Arrays.stream()\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update JWT issuer-uri to use sts.windows.net with tenant ID placeholder\n\n- Changed from login.microsoftonline.com v2.0 to sts.windows.net\n- Entra ID access tokens use sts.windows.net as issuer\n- Uses b033521b-5a18-4110-9d4e-9f28f461e099 placeholder for flexibility across environments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix remote ports and remove debugging logs\n\n- Update vite.config remote URLs to correct ports (metrics: 5178, analytics: 5179)\n- Remove temporary debugging console logs from App components\n- Clean up code after fixing port conflict issue\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve logout to properly clear session and redirect\n\n- Ensure clearSession endpoint is called successfully before clearing state\n- Add response status check for logout endpoint\n- Reload page to root (/) after logout to ensure clean state\n- Prevents showing last view after logout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix double slash in Entra ID OAuth URLs\n\n- Fix substring to remove both /v2.0 and trailing slash (5 chars instead of 4)\n- Applied to getCodeUrl, exchangeCodeForToken, and refreshToken methods\n- Prevents malformed URLs like https://...//oauth2/v2.0/authorize\n- Add login flow logging for debugging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix session authentication and YAML syntax error in BFF\n\n- Fixed duplicate ''server:'' key in application.yml causing YAML parse error\n- Merged server configuration into single block while preserving SameSite cookie config\n- Added SameSite=lax and secure=false to handle cross-site session cookies\n- This allows React app''s fetch requests to properly send session cookies to BFF\n- BFF should now recognize authenticated sessions for /v1/proxy/** requests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure fixed ports for MFE child apps and prevent auto-incrementing\n\n- react-metrics: Fixed port 5178 (was 5177) to match parent expectation\n- react-analytics: Fixed port 5179 (was 5178) to match parent expectation\n- Added strictPort: true to both apps'' server and preview configs\n- This prevents silent port auto-incrementing when ports are busy\n- Apps will now throw an error if the expected port is unavailable\n- Ensures parent app''s hardcoded remoteEntry.js URLs always load correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix BFF proxy routing and Data Backend RBAC\n\n    - BFF: Updated SecurityConfig to permitAll on /v1/proxy/** to allow manual session handling\n    - BFF: Fixed ProxyController to correctly preserve /v1 prefix in forwarded URLs\n    - BFF: Corrected Entra ID auth URL construction in AuthController\n    - Data: Enabled @EnableMethodSecurity and updated JwtAuthenticationConverter to extract roles\n    - Data: Added @PreAuthorize RBAC checks to DataController (metrics: alpha, analytics: beta)\n    - Data: Hardcoded tenant ID in application.yml to fix issuer validation\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0981fda54c1479458735be145047aaad959a06e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/git/trees/0981fda54c1479458735be145047aaad959a06e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/git/commits/890ab05781fa2d9e5b16f59df16d3a51eed29d42","verification":{"payload":"tree 0981fda54c1479458735be145047aaad959a06e1\nparent a639e45e45596ff585cba0a1e659b24e5c2e19bb\nauthor dvalechha <122412652+dvalechha@users.noreply.github.com> 1770605384 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770605384 -0500\n\nFeature/bug fix dv3 (#3)\n\n* Update .gitignore to exclude CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md files\n\n- Prevents platform-specific instruction files from being tracked\n- Other .md files are still allowed in the repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Module Federation remoteEntry.js 404 error in dev mode\n\n- Add dev:fed script to remote MFEs for build+preview workflow\n- Update host app remote URLs to /assets/remoteEntry.js path\n- Enables dynamic MFE loading in development\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation plugin only generates\nremoteEntry.js during build, not during vite dev mode. Using\npreview mode for remotes ensures production-like behavior and\nconsistent federation in development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript error in Module Federation shared config\n\n- Remove singleton flag from shared dependencies\n- Use simple array format for consistency with host app\n- Resolves TS2322 type mismatch error\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation v1.4.1 TypeScript\ndefinitions don''t support the singleton flag. Using the\nsimpler array format works with this version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix missing scope in OAuth2 token exchange\n\n- Add scope parameter to exchangeCodeForToken() method\n- Add scope parameter to refreshToken() method\n- Scope must be included in both authorization and token endpoint requests\n- Resolves 403 Forbidden error due to missing Data.Read scope in JWT\n\nIn Entra ID OAuth2 flow, the scope parameter is required in the\ntoken exchange request (not just the authorization request) to\nensure the access token includes the requested scopes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add access token logging for debugging scope issue\n\nLog access token claims and scopes to help diagnose why\nData.Read scope is not appearing in the token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add custom JWT converter to extract Entra ID scopes\n\n- Extract ''scp'' claim from Entra ID JWT tokens\n- Convert scope claim to Spring Security authorities with SCOPE_ prefix\n- Enables proper scope-based authorization check\n\nEntra ID tokens use ''scp'' claim for scopes, but Spring Security\nexpects the converter to transform them into authorities. This\ncustom converter extracts scopes from the JWT and creates\nauthorities that match the hasAuthority() checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix compilation error - use Arrays.stream()\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update JWT issuer-uri to use sts.windows.net with tenant ID placeholder\n\n- Changed from login.microsoftonline.com v2.0 to sts.windows.net\n- Entra ID access tokens use sts.windows.net as issuer\n- Uses b033521b-5a18-4110-9d4e-9f28f461e099 placeholder for flexibility across environments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix remote ports and remove debugging logs\n\n- Update vite.config remote URLs to correct ports (metrics: 5178, analytics: 5179)\n- Remove temporary debugging console logs from App components\n- Clean up code after fixing port conflict issue\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve logout to properly clear session and redirect\n\n- Ensure clearSession endpoint is called successfully before clearing state\n- Add response status check for logout endpoint\n- Reload page to root (/) after logout to ensure clean state\n- Prevents showing last view after logout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix double slash in Entra ID OAuth URLs\n\n- Fix substring to remove both /v2.0 and trailing slash (5 chars instead of 4)\n- Applied to getCodeUrl, exchangeCodeForToken, and refreshToken methods\n- Prevents malformed URLs like https://...//oauth2/v2.0/authorize\n- Add login flow logging for debugging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix session authentication and YAML syntax error in BFF\n\n- Fixed duplicate ''server:'' key in application.yml causing YAML parse error\n- Merged server configuration into single block while preserving SameSite cookie config\n- Added SameSite=lax and secure=false to handle cross-site session cookies\n- This allows React app''s fetch requests to properly send session cookies to BFF\n- BFF should now recognize authenticated sessions for /v1/proxy/** requests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure fixed ports for MFE child apps and prevent auto-incrementing\n\n- react-metrics: Fixed port 5178 (was 5177) to match parent expectation\n- react-analytics: Fixed port 5179 (was 5178) to match parent expectation\n- Added strictPort: true to both apps'' server and preview configs\n- This prevents silent port auto-incrementing when ports are busy\n- Apps will now throw an error if the expected port is unavailable\n- Ensures parent app''s hardcoded remoteEntry.js URLs always load correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix BFF proxy routing and Data Backend RBAC\n\n    - BFF: Updated SecurityConfig to permitAll on /v1/proxy/** to allow manual session handling\n    - BFF: Fixed ProxyController to correctly preserve /v1 prefix in forwarded URLs\n    - BFF: Corrected Entra ID auth URL construction in AuthController\n    - Data: Enabled @EnableMethodSecurity and updated JwtAuthenticationConverter to extract roles\n    - Data: Added @PreAuthorize RBAC checks to DataController (metrics: alpha, analytics: beta)\n    - Data: Hardcoded tenant ID in application.yml to fix issuer validation\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpiUtICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuU4QACsABjhXi9gneAUSKWz3xE2T\nfR2Kc5ckbF6o2JtEU3WFD3ZhaqNgGhLvqrRbmXId8PYXvukvAmJTUiNrCatejj3G\nerpN1GgIs9ix6Qpz7WnPMka5ffockNzIRmv8rEFNmd9cf7DT0lXkugdHSmbyEatJ\ndZF/9WMcYOa3mTSawS156LUo/OnmBZQjloMkDWxg7bLGSLT4JQcMs8HaIwCN6fyO\njQy408M1ple3LwrlvK9IfhQwmeu41vcm/tAl2lWxfBq3abwBJB9/o6dP6inW7icA\nBB65nk1r/qWeKvdJmLbo9PsDpUDXeHTNkfPP6KvpQnPH4ZMDNaoFc3VRka3uL1pX\nu9H+Ydq84qAu9AtvIRxNovOV86zjzC0GD3DQs5avphuj7BSDrbpWoOqCl/9gIsli\nXnFemY/Ro8b5rQrIFzqKihWXXIZyYNK7gdtm/ebHA+y/O+AfoI+dGLX5gioymQBC\n2Q5x0kIXOdu8dYP40n36pwtjrK3Ppg9MdE4zG0zybTbMeRxeQZ6f7iTeX+aaQIjU\nXrAQzR35+Kgr7krTwMfkklO1nU//Gh7rJEgbaXD5RRjEJ11W6+UfUWYIvqgIUqn1\nxv2354rS0S1jcGrXeYH4Xm4JWXX8O/6Pu3RXWaSi5GhVUBhbWSQ7QfEjSls7j9p3\nNvYd1nEdLKTMuUskkV8L\n=FaQR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-09T02:49:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commit/890ab05781fa2d9e5b16f59df16d3a51eed29d42","node_id":"C_kwDORLk0O9oAKDg5MGFiMDU3ODFmYTJkOWU1YjE2ZjU5ZGYxNmQzYTUxZWVkMjlkNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commit/a639e45e45596ff585cba0a1e659b24e5c2e19bb","sha":"a639e45e45596ff585cba0a1e659b24e5c2e19bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/a639e45e45596ff585cba0a1e659b24e5c2e19bb"}],"sha":"890ab05781fa2d9e5b16f59df16d3a51eed29d42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/890ab05781fa2d9e5b16f59df16d3a51eed29d42"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122412652?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha","id":122412652,"login":"dvalechha","node_id":"U_kgDOB0vebA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/a639e45e45596ff585cba0a1e659b24e5c2e19bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-09T02:48:36Z","email":"122412652+dvalechha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dvalechha"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-09T02:48:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Rebase dv (#2)\n\n* Update .gitignore to exclude CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md files\n\n- Prevents platform-specific instruction files from being tracked\n- Other .md files are still allowed in the repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Module Federation remoteEntry.js 404 error in dev mode\n\n- Add dev:fed script to remote MFEs for build+preview workflow\n- Update host app remote URLs to /assets/remoteEntry.js path\n- Enables dynamic MFE loading in development\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation plugin only generates\nremoteEntry.js during build, not during vite dev mode. Using\npreview mode for remotes ensures production-like behavior and\nconsistent federation in development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript error in Module Federation shared config\n\n- Remove singleton flag from shared dependencies\n- Use simple array format for consistency with host app\n- Resolves TS2322 type mismatch error\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation v1.4.1 TypeScript\ndefinitions don''t support the singleton flag. Using the\nsimpler array format works with this version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix missing scope in OAuth2 token exchange\n\n- Add scope parameter to exchangeCodeForToken() method\n- Add scope parameter to refreshToken() method\n- Scope must be included in both authorization and token endpoint requests\n- Resolves 403 Forbidden error due to missing Data.Read scope in JWT\n\nIn Entra ID OAuth2 flow, the scope parameter is required in the\ntoken exchange request (not just the authorization request) to\nensure the access token includes the requested scopes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add access token logging for debugging scope issue\n\nLog access token claims and scopes to help diagnose why\nData.Read scope is not appearing in the token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add custom JWT converter to extract Entra ID scopes\n\n- Extract ''scp'' claim from Entra ID JWT tokens\n- Convert scope claim to Spring Security authorities with SCOPE_ prefix\n- Enables proper scope-based authorization check\n\nEntra ID tokens use ''scp'' claim for scopes, but Spring Security\nexpects the converter to transform them into authorities. This\ncustom converter extracts scopes from the JWT and creates\nauthorities that match the hasAuthority() checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix compilation error - use Arrays.stream()\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update JWT issuer-uri to use sts.windows.net with tenant ID placeholder\n\n- Changed from login.microsoftonline.com v2.0 to sts.windows.net\n- Entra ID access tokens use sts.windows.net as issuer\n- Uses b033521b-5a18-4110-9d4e-9f28f461e099 placeholder for flexibility across environments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix remote ports and remove debugging logs\n\n- Update vite.config remote URLs to correct ports (metrics: 5178, analytics: 5179)\n- Remove temporary debugging console logs from App components\n- Clean up code after fixing port conflict issue\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve logout to properly clear session and redirect\n\n- Ensure clearSession endpoint is called successfully before clearing state\n- Add response status check for logout endpoint\n- Reload page to root (/) after logout to ensure clean state\n- Prevents showing last view after logout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix double slash in Entra ID OAuth URLs\n\n- Fix substring to remove both /v2.0 and trailing slash (5 chars instead of 4)\n- Applied to getCodeUrl, exchangeCodeForToken, and refreshToken methods\n- Prevents malformed URLs like https://...//oauth2/v2.0/authorize\n- Add login flow logging for debugging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix session authentication and YAML syntax error in BFF\n\n- Fixed duplicate ''server:'' key in application.yml causing YAML parse error\n- Merged server configuration into single block while preserving SameSite cookie config\n- Added SameSite=lax and secure=false to handle cross-site session cookies\n- This allows React app''s fetch requests to properly send session cookies to BFF\n- BFF should now recognize authenticated sessions for /v1/proxy/** requests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure fixed ports for MFE child apps and prevent auto-incrementing\n\n- react-metrics: Fixed port 5178 (was 5177) to match parent expectation\n- react-analytics: Fixed port 5179 (was 5178) to match parent expectation\n- Added strictPort: true to both apps'' server and preview configs\n- This prevents silent port auto-incrementing when ports are busy\n- Apps will now throw an error if the expected port is unavailable\n- Ensures parent app''s hardcoded remoteEntry.js URLs always load correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix BFF proxy routing and Data Backend RBAC\n\n    - BFF: Updated SecurityConfig to permitAll on /v1/proxy/** to allow manual session handling\n    - BFF: Fixed ProxyController to correctly preserve /v1 prefix in forwarded URLs\n    - BFF: Corrected Entra ID auth URL construction in AuthController\n    - Data: Enabled @EnableMethodSecurity and updated JwtAuthenticationConverter to extract roles\n    - Data: Added @PreAuthorize RBAC checks to DataController (metrics: alpha, analytics: beta)\n    - Data: Hardcoded tenant ID in application.yml to fix issuer validation\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0981fda54c1479458735be145047aaad959a06e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/git/trees/0981fda54c1479458735be145047aaad959a06e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/git/commits/a639e45e45596ff585cba0a1e659b24e5c2e19bb","verification":{"payload":"tree 0981fda54c1479458735be145047aaad959a06e1\nparent 595b332a4aeac6808efb3707d05b84ed47235b7d\nauthor dvalechha <122412652+dvalechha@users.noreply.github.com> 1770605316 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770605316 -0500\n\nRebase dv (#2)\n\n* Update .gitignore to exclude CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md files\n\n- Prevents platform-specific instruction files from being tracked\n- Other .md files are still allowed in the repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Module Federation remoteEntry.js 404 error in dev mode\n\n- Add dev:fed script to remote MFEs for build+preview workflow\n- Update host app remote URLs to /assets/remoteEntry.js path\n- Enables dynamic MFE loading in development\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation plugin only generates\nremoteEntry.js during build, not during vite dev mode. Using\npreview mode for remotes ensures production-like behavior and\nconsistent federation in development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript error in Module Federation shared config\n\n- Remove singleton flag from shared dependencies\n- Use simple array format for consistency with host app\n- Resolves TS2322 type mismatch error\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation v1.4.1 TypeScript\ndefinitions don''t support the singleton flag. Using the\nsimpler array format works with this version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix missing scope in OAuth2 token exchange\n\n- Add scope parameter to exchangeCodeForToken() method\n- Add scope parameter to refreshToken() method\n- Scope must be included in both authorization and token endpoint requests\n- Resolves 403 Forbidden error due to missing Data.Read scope in JWT\n\nIn Entra ID OAuth2 flow, the scope parameter is required in the\ntoken exchange request (not just the authorization request) to\nensure the access token includes the requested scopes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add access token logging for debugging scope issue\n\nLog access token claims and scopes to help diagnose why\nData.Read scope is not appearing in the token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add custom JWT converter to extract Entra ID scopes\n\n- Extract ''scp'' claim from Entra ID JWT tokens\n- Convert scope claim to Spring Security authorities with SCOPE_ prefix\n- Enables proper scope-based authorization check\n\nEntra ID tokens use ''scp'' claim for scopes, but Spring Security\nexpects the converter to transform them into authorities. This\ncustom converter extracts scopes from the JWT and creates\nauthorities that match the hasAuthority() checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix compilation error - use Arrays.stream()\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update JWT issuer-uri to use sts.windows.net with tenant ID placeholder\n\n- Changed from login.microsoftonline.com v2.0 to sts.windows.net\n- Entra ID access tokens use sts.windows.net as issuer\n- Uses b033521b-5a18-4110-9d4e-9f28f461e099 placeholder for flexibility across environments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix remote ports and remove debugging logs\n\n- Update vite.config remote URLs to correct ports (metrics: 5178, analytics: 5179)\n- Remove temporary debugging console logs from App components\n- Clean up code after fixing port conflict issue\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve logout to properly clear session and redirect\n\n- Ensure clearSession endpoint is called successfully before clearing state\n- Add response status check for logout endpoint\n- Reload page to root (/) after logout to ensure clean state\n- Prevents showing last view after logout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix double slash in Entra ID OAuth URLs\n\n- Fix substring to remove both /v2.0 and trailing slash (5 chars instead of 4)\n- Applied to getCodeUrl, exchangeCodeForToken, and refreshToken methods\n- Prevents malformed URLs like https://...//oauth2/v2.0/authorize\n- Add login flow logging for debugging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix session authentication and YAML syntax error in BFF\n\n- Fixed duplicate ''server:'' key in application.yml causing YAML parse error\n- Merged server configuration into single block while preserving SameSite cookie config\n- Added SameSite=lax and secure=false to handle cross-site session cookies\n- This allows React app''s fetch requests to properly send session cookies to BFF\n- BFF should now recognize authenticated sessions for /v1/proxy/** requests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure fixed ports for MFE child apps and prevent auto-incrementing\n\n- react-metrics: Fixed port 5178 (was 5177) to match parent expectation\n- react-analytics: Fixed port 5179 (was 5178) to match parent expectation\n- Added strictPort: true to both apps'' server and preview configs\n- This prevents silent port auto-incrementing when ports are busy\n- Apps will now throw an error if the expected port is unavailable\n- Ensures parent app''s hardcoded remoteEntry.js URLs always load correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix BFF proxy routing and Data Backend RBAC\n\n    - BFF: Updated SecurityConfig to permitAll on /v1/proxy/** to allow manual session handling\n    - BFF: Fixed ProxyController to correctly preserve /v1 prefix in forwarded URLs\n    - BFF: Corrected Entra ID auth URL construction in AuthController\n    - Data: Enabled @EnableMethodSecurity and updated JwtAuthenticationConverter to extract roles\n    - Data: Added @PreAuthorize RBAC checks to DataController (metrics: alpha, analytics: beta)\n    - Data: Hardcoded tenant ID in application.yml to fix issuer validation\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpiUsECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkawQADs1TwSW6Zx9tVp82anBBQ0i\nrdZ8547VZ0jn4xPuL18xuVjs2dlcpJgJu+3ABVQf5qMgakYuVJndjsx6g47ykiDK\np/COoirdfqyADBrLNwf/NfmmN0SvKSz7eIA2dOENydytR0j6NVkIA+wxeQbMJT1p\n9/gaujobZZ6DX7yDUjGl2W+sggYCNTkkfep0TGw3NXCME5n8VWmf5HxS3BM1x6ox\n0H+srvehvCl09X/CW/GLsFa2i1m73W2hb1nTAuaBBYNeRdaImdLvg5L2ykRcHkD4\nkcJ/zoMt4uqe18ica2ifWsLgmcaOAqLwfHGX50NUFfLd1vDZ2ed8FeMXFcDG1XQQ\na6yT5p1zF3M2NSMBOqvxItA8JLaDISSZKss0s1g6+/xSrDZsLCKvWHJ8LH3+dNSj\negu9R/ujbRxeI0j2UyuW/4U/S1UTw7NQQtoFmjUW73HDDOWdYrejUW9+JH03WtJN\nLr/XlHedG16T2Naw3duPWgZbKJVFkROp/CA/QN0xPM8HHSUNyaCZ3ISfmhjHGBDf\ndgVEUqmfQnqCWboVw3O12kDLZfVn6iKZ8NV805pmLJyglb7X1+FY9Nne0vqJx1/n\nRT0/91Uw89Yzr8wFfyrx3e2H4FDgtFVj5E0cFfKbDN3nx/vh7DZzK7FS0KUOqPur\nP20x6gdP4pHbXDzhq2PB\n=0c6z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-09T02:48:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commit/a639e45e45596ff585cba0a1e659b24e5c2e19bb","node_id":"C_kwDORLk0O9oAKGE2MzllNDVlNDU1OTZmZjU4NWNiYTBhMWU2NTliMjRlNWMyZTE5YmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commit/595b332a4aeac6808efb3707d05b84ed47235b7d","sha":"595b332a4aeac6808efb3707d05b84ed47235b7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/595b332a4aeac6808efb3707d05b84ed47235b7d"}],"sha":"a639e45e45596ff585cba0a1e659b24e5c2e19bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/a639e45e45596ff585cba0a1e659b24e5c2e19bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122412652?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dvalechha","id":122412652,"login":"dvalechha","node_id":"U_kgDOB0vebA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dvalechha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/commits/595b332a4aeac6808efb3707d05b84ed47235b7d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-09T02:43:48Z","email":"122412652+dvalechha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dvalechha"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-09T02:43:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/bug fix dv3 (#1)\n\n* Update .gitignore to exclude CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md files\n\n- Prevents platform-specific instruction files from being tracked\n- Other .md files are still allowed in the repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Module Federation remoteEntry.js 404 error in dev mode\n\n- Add dev:fed script to remote MFEs for build+preview workflow\n- Update host app remote URLs to /assets/remoteEntry.js path\n- Enables dynamic MFE loading in development\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation plugin only generates\nremoteEntry.js during build, not during vite dev mode. Using\npreview mode for remotes ensures production-like behavior and\nconsistent federation in development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript error in Module Federation shared config\n\n- Remove singleton flag from shared dependencies\n- Use simple array format for consistency with host app\n- Resolves TS2322 type mismatch error\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation v1.4.1 TypeScript\ndefinitions don''t support the singleton flag. Using the\nsimpler array format works with this version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix missing scope in OAuth2 token exchange\n\n- Add scope parameter to exchangeCodeForToken() method\n- Add scope parameter to refreshToken() method\n- Scope must be included in both authorization and token endpoint requests\n- Resolves 403 Forbidden error due to missing Data.Read scope in JWT\n\nIn Entra ID OAuth2 flow, the scope parameter is required in the\ntoken exchange request (not just the authorization request) to\nensure the access token includes the requested scopes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add access token logging for debugging scope issue\n\nLog access token claims and scopes to help diagnose why\nData.Read scope is not appearing in the token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add custom JWT converter to extract Entra ID scopes\n\n- Extract ''scp'' claim from Entra ID JWT tokens\n- Convert scope claim to Spring Security authorities with SCOPE_ prefix\n- Enables proper scope-based authorization check\n\nEntra ID tokens use ''scp'' claim for scopes, but Spring Security\nexpects the converter to transform them into authorities. This\ncustom converter extracts scopes from the JWT and creates\nauthorities that match the hasAuthority() checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix compilation error - use Arrays.stream()\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update JWT issuer-uri to use sts.windows.net with tenant ID placeholder\n\n- Changed from login.microsoftonline.com v2.0 to sts.windows.net\n- Entra ID access tokens use sts.windows.net as issuer\n- Uses b033521b-5a18-4110-9d4e-9f28f461e099 placeholder for flexibility across environments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix remote ports and remove debugging logs\n\n- Update vite.config remote URLs to correct ports (metrics: 5178, analytics: 5179)\n- Remove temporary debugging console logs from App components\n- Clean up code after fixing port conflict issue\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve logout to properly clear session and redirect\n\n- Ensure clearSession endpoint is called successfully before clearing state\n- Add response status check for logout endpoint\n- Reload page to root (/) after logout to ensure clean state\n- Prevents showing last view after logout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix double slash in Entra ID OAuth URLs\n\n- Fix substring to remove both /v2.0 and trailing slash (5 chars instead of 4)\n- Applied to getCodeUrl, exchangeCodeForToken, and refreshToken methods\n- Prevents malformed URLs like https://...//oauth2/v2.0/authorize\n- Add login flow logging for debugging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix session authentication and YAML syntax error in BFF\n\n- Fixed duplicate ''server:'' key in application.yml causing YAML parse error\n- Merged server configuration into single block while preserving SameSite cookie config\n- Added SameSite=lax and secure=false to handle cross-site session cookies\n- This allows React app''s fetch requests to properly send session cookies to BFF\n- BFF should now recognize authenticated sessions for /v1/proxy/** requests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure fixed ports for MFE child apps and prevent auto-incrementing\n\n- react-metrics: Fixed port 5178 (was 5177) to match parent expectation\n- react-analytics: Fixed port 5179 (was 5178) to match parent expectation\n- Added strictPort: true to both apps'' server and preview configs\n- This prevents silent port auto-incrementing when ports are busy\n- Apps will now throw an error if the expected port is unavailable\n- Ensures parent app''s hardcoded remoteEntry.js URLs always load correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix BFF proxy routing and Data Backend RBAC\n\n    - BFF: Updated SecurityConfig to permitAll on /v1/proxy/** to allow manual session handling\n    - BFF: Fixed ProxyController to correctly preserve /v1 prefix in forwarded URLs\n    - BFF: Corrected Entra ID auth URL construction in AuthController\n    - Data: Enabled @EnableMethodSecurity and updated JwtAuthenticationConverter to extract roles\n    - Data: Added @PreAuthorize RBAC checks to DataController (metrics: alpha, analytics: beta)\n    - Data: Hardcoded tenant ID in application.yml to fix issuer validation\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0981fda54c1479458735be145047aaad959a06e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/git/trees/0981fda54c1479458735be145047aaad959a06e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dvalechha/entra-workspace/git/commits/595b332a4aeac6808efb3707d05b84ed47235b7d","verification":{"payload":"tree 0981fda54c1479458735be145047aaad959a06e1\nparent 9cc1a0ed248e3359a7738b4a4e96143551a075d4\nauthor dvalechha <122412652+dvalechha@users.noreply.github.com> 1770605028 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770605028 -0500\n\nFeature/bug fix dv3 (#1)\n\n* Update .gitignore to exclude CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md files\n\n- Prevents platform-specific instruction files from being tracked\n- Other .md files are still allowed in the repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Module Federation remoteEntry.js 404 error in dev mode\n\n- Add dev:fed script to remote MFEs for build+preview workflow\n- Update host app remote URLs to /assets/remoteEntry.js path\n- Enables dynamic MFE loading in development\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation plugin only generates\nremoteEntry.js during build, not during vite dev mode. Using\npreview mode for remotes ensures production-like behavior and\nconsistent federation in development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript error in Module Federation shared config\n\n- Remove singleton flag from shared dependencies\n- Use simple array format for consistency with host app\n- Resolves TS2322 type mismatch error\n\nThe @originjs/vite-plugin-federation v1.4.1 TypeScript\ndefinitions don''t support the singleton flag. Using the\nsimpler array format works with this version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix missing scope in OAuth2 token exchange\n\n- Add scope parameter to exchangeCodeForToken() method\n- Add scope parameter to refreshToken() method\n- Scope must be included in both authorization and token endpoint requests\n- Resolves 403 Forbidden error due to missing Data.Read scope in JWT\n\nIn Entra ID OAuth2 flow, the scope parameter is required in the\ntoken exchange request (not just the authorization request) to\nensure the access token includes the requested scopes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add access token logging for debugging scope issue\n\nLog access token claims and scopes to help diagnose why\nData.Read scope is not appearing in the token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add custom JWT converter to extract Entra ID scopes\n\n- Extract ''scp'' claim from Entra ID JWT tokens\n- Convert scope claim to Spring Security authorities with SCOPE_ prefix\n- Enables proper scope-based authorization check\n\nEntra ID tokens use ''scp'' claim for scopes, but Spring Security\nexpects the converter to transform them into authorities. This\ncustom converter extracts scopes from the JWT and creates\nauthorities that match the hasAuthority() checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix compilation error - use Arrays.stream()\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update JWT issuer-uri to use sts.windows.net with tenant ID placeholder\n\n- Changed from login.microsoftonline.com v2.0 to sts.windows.net\n- Entra ID access tokens use sts.windows.net as issuer\n- Uses b033521b-5a18-4110-9d4e-9f28f461e099 placeholder for flexibility across environments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix remote ports and remove debugging logs\n\n- Update vite.config remote URLs to correct ports (metrics: 5178, analytics: 5179)\n- Remove temporary debugging console logs from App components\n- Clean up code after fixing port conflict issue\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Improve logout to properly clear session and redirect\n\n- Ensure clearSession endpoint is called successfully before clearing state\n- Add response status check for logout endpoint\n- Reload page to root (/) after logout to ensure clean state\n- Prevents showing last view after logout\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix double slash in Entra ID OAuth URLs\n\n- Fix substring to remove both /v2.0 and trailing slash (5 chars instead of 4)\n- Applied to getCodeUrl, exchangeCodeForToken, and refreshToken methods\n- Prevents malformed URLs like https://...//oauth2/v2.0/authorize\n- Add login flow logging for debugging\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix session authentication and YAML syntax error in BFF\n\n- Fixed duplicate ''server:'' key in application.yml causing YAML parse error\n- Merged server configuration into single block while preserving SameSite cookie config\n- Added SameSite=lax and secure=false to handle cross-site session cookies\n- This allows React app''s fetch requests to properly send session cookies to BFF\n- BFF should now recognize authenticated sessions for /v1/proxy/** requests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure fixed ports for MFE child apps and prevent auto-incrementing\n\n- react-metrics: Fixed port 5178 (was 5177) to match parent expectation\n- react-analytics: Fixed port 5179 (was 5178) to match parent expectation\n- Added strictPort: true to both apps'' server and preview configs\n- This prevents silent port auto-incrementing when ports are busy\n- Apps will now throw an error if the expected port is unavailable\n- Ensures parent app''s hardcoded remoteEntry.js URLs always load correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix BFF proxy routing and Data Backend RBAC\n\n    - BFF: Updated SecurityConfig to permitAll on /v1/proxy/** to allow manual session handling\n    - BFF: Fixed ProxyController to correctly preserve /v1 prefix in forwarded URLs\n    - BFF: Corrected Entra ID auth URL construction in Auth