pi.github.com/users/albertobaselga/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertobaselga/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertobaselga/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertobaselga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertobaselga/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertobaselga","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albertobaselga/prd-lifecycle/commits/ba213ea509b47e981e5b4f8f5538c683b8ab2890/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-08T23:35:54Z","email":"alberto.baselga@gmail.com","name":"Alberto Baselga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-08T23:35:54Z","email":"alberto.baselga@gmail.com","name":"Alberto Baselga"},"message":"Add Response Protocol to all 12 preambles for teammate→lead communication\n\nTeammates had no mechanism to respond to the Lead — they lacked the\nlead''s name, SendMessage examples, and team config discovery instructions.\nThis caused teammates to respond in plain text (invisible in Agent Teams).\n\nEach preamble now includes:\n- Response Protocol (CRITICAL) section with explicit SendMessage usage\n- Lead name discovery fallback via team config\n- Updated Communication Protocol reinforcing SendMessage-only responses\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"827f825825b0cb3da51e1fd910dee0a71245eb8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albertobaselga/prd-lifecycle/git/trees/827f825825b0cb3da51e1fd910dee0a71245eb8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albertobaselga/prd-lifecycle/git/commits/ba213ea509b47e981e5b4f8f5538c683b8ab2890","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5421854?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertobaselga/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"ht