/wizardsupreme","id":185259703,"login":"wizardsupreme","node_id":"U_kgDOCwrWtw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/a4775081cf977156ccd7c4eff88deed6a48ea472/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:13:13Z","email":"smn7818@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:17:09Z","email":"smn7818@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"message":"Block lists and mode gates watch both doors: _G and package.loaded\n\nEvery guard resolved names through lua.globals() only, while require reads\npackage.loaded first, so a blocked or gated stdlib table came back whole\nthrough require. tables_for() now resolves both, blocked bare names are\ndropped from the require caches, os mutators join the gated set, os.getenv\nanswers through env.allow, and both block lists apply once, after the gates.\nDocs corrected to say what a block list does and does not reach. 0.20.14.","tree":{"sha":"ec3ac0a36e4d3b64c62f4d4f6fae9f84e9189479","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/trees/ec3ac0a36e4d3b64c62f4d4f6fae9f84e9189479"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/commits/a4775081cf977156ccd7c4eff88deed6a48ea472","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185259703?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/events{/privacy}","followers_ur