content.com/u/92697?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon","id":92697,"login":"developerinlondon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNjk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/ef5036b38c567481446be866b3a45fbd4aa254f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T01:43:45Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T01:43:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(yaml): parse tagged nodes instead of failing (#281)\n\nyaml.parse and yaml.parse_all refused any document carrying a YAML tag, because the value went straight into serde_json::Value and a tagged node surfaced as an enum it cannot hold. Local and custom tags now parse as a one-key table keyed by the tag text (or are dropped under { tags = \"strip\" }), standard tags resolve to their scalar meaning, and yaml.encode round-trips a tag under { tags = \"wrap\" }. Untagged parsing and encoding are byte-identical to before: mapping keys keep the text the document wrote, duplicate keys keep last-wins, and the default encode path is unchanged. Releases assay-lua 0.20.9.\n\nCloses #281","tree":{"sha":"5e1d65220799b5413f3fae5e4357116a68dea2e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/trees/5e1d65220799b5413f3fae5e4357116a68dea2e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/commits/ef5036b38c567481446be866b3a45fbd4aa254f4","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e1d65220799b5413f3fae5e4357116a68dea2e0\nparent 0dd0167f86c086606083374d9456559664458b98\nauthor Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1789436625 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789436625 +0100\n\nfix(yaml): parse tagged nodes instead of failing (#281)\n\nyaml.parse and yaml.parse_all refused any document carrying a YAML tag, because the value went straight into serde_json::Value and a tagged node surfaced as an enum it cannot hold. Local and custom tags now parse as a one-key table keyed by the tag text (or are dropped under { tags = \"strip\" }), standard tags resolve to their scalar meaning, and yaml.encode round-trips a tag under { tags = \"wrap\" }. Untagged parsing and encoding are byte-identical to before: mapping keys keep the text the document wrote, duplicate keys keep last-wins, and the default encode path is unchanged. Releases assay-lua 0.20.9.\n\nCloses #281","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqKLRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhJ8QAKePGDISru8hoT82YX9ZrcUB\nrCWFVNU35IeSC3joOgPnd0bYw7nj1lahCrKz4ThL97KLu5Bi/RcC71RQuYBWPduf\n9CRhp+7TSe0dSRGwgfbjyFbBK0ahXQRefBC6VhPQYyhngLVOikvSVf0vv1J4G98M\njBS1ylC099KoJ2g9LHw5XYC2oXyW25sLu5iPkfQTjy6lsAkuPeupkoYOurnkhOTt\ntAlueqriSQVw1sLNFVTkCnU+IZu8sL3ZmjjOMTt1TpJ5NqskBBgKNbNOILsEvF2d\nVbYqniwQQ9cG/ed8CRg4YUdBhbXkjsgWdOxdYw50bjP5uaHGAzMue+3iiRPKHEWs\n2D7wFA2kxFjdBxGkGCHZl35A+I44mkfgxfV9qdLV2k6dTlbo4bjIk5Yd0OGjsTeR\nfaDpvt8HPqSc0cMluLkuPDUUQM09d7mQ118qBvv9vpQNP0Q3ZsR6HgMwhxIaBL9b\nbfreccqxlntELQIt7gzRxtJ3a+kkTzI/jNBMAVlc6DRbn6f6MKbqN/iqHDcxZ+WA\nZ0zZVisfFHIJelk9mabd+bEfFTMX5w4icw86h1dsjR3JAUOH3CldK8MEHXX6RdKN\nxreyVqjpt9XziaqHTQM0