users/developerinlondon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon","id":92697,"login":"developerinlondon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNjk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/0dd0167f86c086606083374d9456559664458b98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:51:47Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:51:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(email_verify): candidates() transliterates accented letters instead of dropping them (#280)\n\ncandidates() lowercased and then stripped every byte outside %a, so a name\nholding a Nordic or German letter (æ, ø, å, ä, ö, ü, and other accented\nLatin vowels) lost that letter entirely rather than guessing an ASCII\nspelling for it — the resulting top-ranked candidate, the only one the\npaid verification rung ever tries, was an address no mailbox could hold.\n\nThe primary guess now transliterates per the single-letter convention\n(æ→ae, ø→o, å→a, ä→a, ö→o, ü→u, é→e, and other common accented Latin\nletters). Names holding a letter with a common digraph alternate (ø, å,\nä, ö, ü) also get the digraph spelling (oe, aa, ae, oe, ue) appended as\nan extra candidate after the primary set.\n\nversion = \"0.20.8\"","tree":{"sha":"825610af09a84b9c8ed3a94de5fd10cfd6c8bbe1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/trees/825610af09a84b9c8ed3a94de5fd10cfd6c8bbe1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/commits/0dd0167f86c086606083374d9456559664458b98","verification":{"payload":"tree 825610af09a84b9c8ed3a94de5fd10cfd6c8bbe1\nparent 5697278284c78522705173475e718450bf9b419e\nauthor Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1789397507 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789397507 +0100\n\nfix(email_verify): candidates() transliterates accented letters instead of dropping them (#280)\n\ncandidates() lowercased and then stripped every byte outside %a, so a name\nholding a Nordic or German letter (æ, ø, å, ä, ö, ü, and other accented\nLatin vowels) lost that letter entirely rather than guessing an ASCII\nspelling for it — the resulting top-ranked candidate, the only one the\npaid verification rung ever tries, was an address no mailbox could hold.\n\nThe primary guess now transliterates per the single-letter convention\n(æ→ae, ø→o, å→a, ä→a, ö→o, ü→u, é→e, and other common accented Latin\nletters). Names holding a letter with a common digraph alternate (ø, å,\nä, ö, ü) also get the digraph spelling (oe, aa, ae, oe, ue) appended as\nan extra candidate after the primary set.\n\nversion = \"0.20.8\"","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqAoDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACGwQAIIOqihcjBr1U0x6i81KTsFH\n5S/ESDiJ9MUMjUEjOTfqd8RyJRcOxNVePU7TmzT5ZlY7YG2S7274T6orTNs455M4\nBlZOx79Cmn8cdgstZAIWyEV5ig+LAd5D2jJJV5RsFdz8pP6EisVK0qos0fqnLSoY\nH/Gfn+oygg2qg1Oj9TVmOw052S5zTNrpreOgAWqH304p/nQb/nZi66SgiJRvaNKG\nSlCvPK1CyHsxjnv4jzb6o9ZEaO+JMOSwb5gxI3yzAuXke2ui+v0y5clcTpo6kRr/\n99Ov3QuWSgzHRaNgRBkQ0UxtVuAQ16HH0tsjfjcfnCh/0dXe8o/C4t8FCNJXqwJn\n4GlolRVnCajSyIkVuTBb1AE1NllHWUkE8Zt7SWCnptD7mxlbCUHL42YdbVP6rFXh\n9h5W5bY/Q6TBk9KTJQ/M36ErAKYKeiNUQVkGSs0vKgcMsSnU/PaZ+6RduGdl387J\nN0W2pZ6VXMP1hOIXTnATfU5FPm1Gm7D9WIv/xrdya5uoockKBcesRWKF0/YnghSe\nh2ITI0RpsjffbO5qU0G5mVu2y9MxRO3ccXyFggmDf