er port so both protocols can bind it\n\nThe truncation test bound UDP on a kernel-chosen port and then assumed the\nsame number was free on TCP; the two are separate port spaces. The pair is now\nacquired as a unit: one socket stays bound while the other is attempted, and a\nfailed attempt discards the candidate and asks for a fresh one.\n\nCloses #14\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rd3ikB7kHqnRBnoW1mX8sh","tree":{"sha":"25e1785894e255f22983538243a56cdccce2ffa1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/trees/25e1785894e255f22983538243a56cdccce2ffa1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/commits/2386db4b7f486d1d273a6d74ab30107818796fa2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185259703?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wizardsupreme","id":185259703,"login":"wizardsupreme","node_id":"U_kgDOCwrWtw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wizardsupreme","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon/assay/commit/2386db4b7f486d1d273a6d74ab30107818796fa2","node_id":"C_kwDORLuRW9oAKDIzODZkYjRiN2Y0ODZkMWQyNzNhNmQ3NGFiMzAxMDc4MTg3OTZmYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon/assay/commit/ebf33f1795432459606bc815ae092f436ab9363a","sha":"ebf33f1795432459606bc815ae092f436ab9363a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/ebf33f1795432459606bc815ae092f436ab9363a"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon/assay/commit/aefbd8734d7016192b3d47a5031fd4a51f4792ae","sha":"aefbd8734d7016192b3d47a5031fd4a51f4792ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/aefbd8734d7016192b3d47a5031fd4a51f4792ae"}],"sha":"2386db4b7f486d1d273a6d74ab30107818796fa2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/2386db4b7f486d1d273a6d74ab30107818796fa2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92697?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon","id":92697,"login":"developerinlondon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNjk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/aefbd8734d7016192b3d47a5031fd4a51f4792ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T07:25:12Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T07:25:12Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"message":"docs(dns): state the invariant that actually makes bound_on_both correct\n\nThe comment claimed TCP is bound first because it is the half that cannot move,\nwhich is not true and not why the helper works. Both halves must share a port,\nso neither can move independently of the other; binding UDP first and retrying\nthe TCP half would be exactly as correct. The order carries no weight.\n\nTwo things do. The first socket stays bound while the second is attempted, so\nnothing can take the candidate port in between and the pair is acquired or\nabandoned as a unit. And a failed attempt is discarded whole, so each retry asks\nthe kernel for a fresh candidate rather than going back to a port already known\nto be contended.\n\nThat also names the original defect more accurately: it was the missing retry —\nan unwrap on the second bind — rather than the order the two binds happened in.\nThe subject of the previous commit inherits the same wrong framing; the code it\ndescribes is unchanged and correct.\n\nComment only. No behaviour change.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rd3ikB7kHqnRBnoW1mX8sh","tree":{"sha":"25e1785894e255f22983538243a56cdccce2ffa1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/trees/25e1785894e255f22983538243a56cdccce2ffa1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/commits/aefbd8734d7016192b3d47a5031fd4a51f4792ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 25e1785894e255f22983538243a56cdccce2ffa1\nparent 926a6b0d78ffada3295b973a78a4a5caff21f515\nauthor Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1788506712 +0000\ncommitter Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1788506712 +0000\n\ndocs(dns): state the invariant that actually makes bound_on_both correct\n\nThe comment claimed TCP is bound first because it is the half that cannot move,\nwhich is not true and not why the helper works. Both halves must share a port,\nso neither can move independently of the other; binding UDP first and retrying\nthe TCP half would be exactly as correct. The order carries no weight.\n\nTwo things do. The first socket stays bound while the second is attempted, so\nnothing can take the candidate port in between and the pair is acquired or\nabandoned as a unit. And a failed attempt is discarded whole, so each retry asks\nthe kernel for a fresh candidate rather than going back to a port already known\nto be contended.\n\nThat also names the original defect more accurately: it was the missing retry —\nan unwrap on the second bind — rather than the order the two binds happened in.\nThe subject of the previous commit inherits the same wrong framing; the code it\ndescribes is unchanged and correct.\n\nComment only. No behaviour change.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rd3ikB7kHqnRBnoW1mX8sh\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRV/FXDL+YfHsAYcfER+ZP89e7hTAUCappyWAAKCRAR+ZP89e7h\nTMt9AQCr9zBSydNae+/vqEweRZouMK9ECj/ZrAjmkfGM0EOcMQD/WgYP4fd23NMf\ndIYgyw3T3vNPqbDTzCKE8rILTS87cwg=\n=Z5Lg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T07:29:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92697?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon","id":92697,"login":"developerinlondon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNjk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon/assay/commit/aefbd8734d7016192b3d47a5031fd4a51f4792ae","node_id":"C_kwDORLuRW9oAKGFlZmJkODczNGQ3MDE2MTkyYjNkNDdhNTAzMWZkNGE1MWY0NzkyYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon/assay/commit/926a6b0d78ffada3295b973a78a4a5caff21f515","sha":"926a6b0d78ffada3295b973a78a4a5caff21f515","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/926a6b0d78ffada3295b973a78a4a5caff21f515"}],"sha":"aefbd8734d7016192b3d47a5031fd4a51f4792ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/aefbd8734d7016192b3d47a5031fd4a51f4792ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92697?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon","id":92697,"login":"developerinlondon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNjk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/926a6b0d78ffada3295b973a78a4a5caff21f515/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T07:14:26Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T07:14:26Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"message":"test(dns): take the nameserver port from the protocol that cannot move\n\na_truncated_answer_is_asked_again_over_tcp built its two-protocol nameserver in\nan order that assumes UDP and TCP share a port space. It bound UDP on :0, took\nthe port the kernel picked, and bound TCP on the same number. The spaces are\nindependent, so a port free on UDP is no evidence about TCP, and when anything\nalready held that TCP port the unwrap panicked and failed the build for a\nreason unrelated to whatever was under review. Rare enough to look like a real\nDNS regression when it hit.\n\nThe port now comes from TCP, which is the half that cannot move: the resolver\nretries a truncated answer at the address it already used, so both halves must\nshare one port and only one of them can choose it. UDP is bound to the port TCP\nwas given, and a number free on one but taken on the other costs another attempt\nrather than a failed test. The retry belongs to acquiring the port; there is\nnone around the assertion and no sleep anywhere.\n\nThe spawn bodies moved into serve_udp and serve_tcp so the UDP-only helper and\nthe both-protocol one share them rather than each carrying a copy.\n\nVerified by constructing the collision the old order assumed away — a port taken\non TCP and free on UDP — and confirming the old bind fails on it while the new\nallocator steps over it. The test then ran 30 times in a row without a failure.\n\nTest-only, so no version bump; release.yml keys on the crate version.\n\nCloses #14\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rd3ikB7kHqnRBnoW1mX8sh","tree":{"sha":"0debeb821663bb83cc6bf52df34f95b13476a07f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/trees/0debeb821663bb83cc6bf52df34f95b13476a07f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/commits/926a6b0d78ffada3295b973a78a4a5caff21f515","verification":{"payload":"tree 0debeb821663bb83cc6bf52df34f95b13476a07f\nparent ebf33f1795432459606bc815ae092f436ab9363a\nauthor Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1788506066 +0000\ncommitter Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1788506066 +0000\n\ntest(dns): take the nameserver port from the protocol that cannot move\n\na_truncated_answer_is_asked_again_over_tcp built its two-protocol nameserver in\nan order that assumes UDP and TCP share a port space. It bound UDP on :0, took\nthe port the kernel picked, and bound TCP on the same number. The spaces are\nindependent, so a port free on UDP is no evidence about TCP, and when anything\nalready held that TCP port the unwrap panicked and failed the build for a\nreason unrelated to whatever was under review. Rare enough to look like a real\nDNS regression when it hit.\n\nThe port now comes from TCP, which is the half that cannot move: the resolver\nretries a truncated answer at the address it already used, so both halves must\nshare one port and only one of them can choose it. UDP is bound to the port TCP\nwas given, and a number free on one but taken on the other costs another attempt\nrather than a failed test. The retry belongs to acquiring the port; there is\nnone around the assertion and no sleep anywhere.\n\nThe spawn bodies moved into serve_udp and serve_tcp so the UDP-only helper and\nthe both-protocol one share them rather than each carrying a copy.\n\nVerified by constructing the collision the old order assumed away — a port taken\non TCP and free on UDP — and confirming the old bind fails on it while the new\nallocator steps over it. The test then ran 30 times in a row without a failure.\n\nTest-only, so no version bump; release.yml keys on the crate version.\n\nCloses #14\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/sess