l":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon","id":92697,"login":"developerinlondon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNjk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/130af6c427eb65a6262da6fe95c02b25bac5a3ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:22:59Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:22:59Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"message":"feat(stdlib): set a Salesforge sequence''s rotation and its status\n\nThe sequencer seam needs both to stop holding the vendor''s host name itself,\nand 0.20.1 shipped neither. Taking a domain out of a rotation and pausing a\nsequence were the two calls a caller still had to make with its own HTTP client.\n\n`c:set_rotation(sequence_id, mailbox_ids)` replaces which mailboxes a sequence\nsends from; `c:set_sequence_status(sequence_id, status)` takes \"paused\" or\n\"active\". Both answer (true) or (nil, err) like the other writes, and\n`c:sequence(id)` already reads both back.\n\nThree refusals happen before a request rather than after a rejection: an empty\nrotation, because an empty Lua table encodes as a JSON object and a sequence\nwith no mailboxes cannot send; a blank sequence id, which would address the\nworkspace itself; and a status outside the two the vendor takes, so a typo is a\nconfig error the caller can read instead of a 400 it has to interpret.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rd3ikB7kHqnRBnoW1mX8sh","tree":{"sha":"bb4f86f20ab0595eaa06e50d4408e0ce7e5e87f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/trees/bb4f86f20ab0595eaa06e50d4408e0ce7e5e87f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/commits/130af6c427eb65a6262da6fe95c02b25bac5a3ad","verification":{"payload":"tree bb4f86f20ab0595eaa06e50d4408e0ce7e5e87f0\nparent 7fd61d16e7c8dce8bb09cedaf97e2894967867cf\nauthor Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1788502979 +0000\ncommitter Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1788502979 +0000\n\nfeat(stdlib): set a Salesforge sequence''s rotation and its status\n\nThe sequencer seam needs both to stop holding the vendor''s host name itself,\nand 0.20.1 shipped neither. Taking a domain out of a rotation and pausing a\nsequence were the two calls a caller still had to make with its own HTTP client.\n\n`c:set_rotation(sequence_id, mailbox_ids)` replaces which mailboxes a sequence\nsends from; `c:set_sequence_status(sequence_id, status)` takes \"paused\" or\n\"active\". Both answer (true) or (nil, err) like the other writes, and\n`c:sequence(id)` already reads both back.\n\nThree refusals happen before a request rather than after a rejection: an empty\nrotation, because an empty Lua table encodes as a JSON object and a sequence\nwith no mailboxes cannot send; a blank sequence id, which would address the\nworkspace itself; and a status outside the two the vendor takes, so a typo is a\nconfig error the caller can read instead of a 400 it has to interpret.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rd3ikB7kHqnRBnoW1mX8sh\n","reason":"valid","signature"