7cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/7fd61d16e7c8dce8bb09cedaf97e2894967867cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92697?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon","id":92697,"login":"developerinlondon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNjk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/aaeb266507bfa3166bdfebd39502443132ecbdce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:46:23Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:46:23Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"message":"feat(stdlib): report a truncated vendor listing instead of a short one\n\nReview of the three revenue modules found a list that could come back short in\nsilence. `p:mailboxes(domain_id)` filters client-side over Primeforge''s ten-row\nwindow because the tool accepts no filter, so a domain whose mailboxes fall\noutside that window answered zero rows and no error — indistinguishable from a\ndomain with nothing on it.\n\nEvery list call now answers a second value, `meta = {truncated, cap, seen}`.\n`truncated` means a cap stopped the walk rather than the vendor running out of\nrows: for Primeforge, that the vendor answered exactly its ten; for Clayinbox,\nSalesforge and Warmforge, that the page cap was reached. Warmforge''s `not_found`\nnow names the truncation too, so an address missing from a short window does not\nread as a mailbox the workspace lost.\n\nAlso from the review:\n\n  - The CHANGELOG claimed every method returns `(nil, err)`. The constructors\n    throw on a missing key or workspace, matching the rest of the stdlib, and\n    the text now says so.\n  - `SALESFORGE_EMAIL` and `SALESFORGE_PASSWORD` were read but named in no\n    quickref, so `assay context` never showed them.\n  - The MCP `Accept: application/json, text/event-stream` header was sent but\n    never asserted. It is now pinned on every mounted tool call, with both media\n    types in order.\n\n`parse_quickref` wants `signature -> return_hint | description` and silently\ndrops anything else, which swallowed two of the lines added here on the first\nattempt. A test now mirrors that rule across all three modules, so a quickref\nthat would never reach `assay context` fails the build instead of vanishing.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rd3ikB7kHqnRBnoW1mX8sh","tree":{"sha":"579aec393bdd4e83da497953fb528a88711e8e3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/trees/579aec393bdd4e83da497953fb528a88711e8e3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/commits/aaeb266507bfa3166bdfebd39502443132ecbdce","verification":{"payload":"tree 579aec393bdd4e83da497953fb528a88711e8e3f\nparent f55acdc1b619c825258540d36aef379d8c13b838\nauthor Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1788493583 +0000\ncommitter Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1788493583 +0000\n\nfeat(stdlib): report a truncated vendor listing instead of a short one\n\nReview of the three revenue modules found a list that could come back short in\nsilence. `p:mailboxes(domain_id)` filters client-side over Primeforge''s ten-row\nwindow because the tool accepts no filter, so a domain whose mailboxes fall\noutside that window answered zero rows and no error — indistinguishable from a\ndomain with nothing on it.\n\nEvery list call now answers a second value, `meta = {truncated, cap, seen}`.\n`truncated` means a cap stopped the walk rather than the vendor running out of\nrows: for Primeforge, that the vendor answered exactly its ten; for Clayinbox,\nSalesforge and Warmforge, that the page cap was reached. Warmforge''s `not_found`\nnow names the truncation too, so an address missing from a short window does not\nread as a mailbox the workspace lost.\n\nAlso from the review:\n\n  - The CHANGELOG claimed every method returns `(nil, err)`. The constructors\n    throw on a missing key or workspace, matching the rest of the stdlib, and\n    the text now says so.\n  - `SALESFORGE_EMAIL` and `SALESFORGE_PASSWORD` were read but named in no\n    quickref, so `assay context` never showed them.\n  - The MCP `Accept: application/json, text/event-stream` header was sent but\n    never asserted. It is now pinned on every mounted tool call, with both media\n    types in order.\n\n`parse_quickref` wants `signature -> return_hint | description` and silently\ndrops anything else, which swallowed two of the lines added here on the first\nattempt. A test now mirrors that rule across all three modules, so a quickref\nthat would never reach `assay context` fails the build instead of vanishing.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rd3ikB7kHqnRBnoW1mX8sh\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRV/FXDL+YfHsAYcfER+ZP89e7hTAUCapo/DwAKCRAR+ZP89e7h\nTB0iAP4/v83wtu2ea7CyQ58mSdD5sug/TQrReQqsBXMietBXGgD/eu4a2j1P6KsS\nTQGTa9UvcqI2uhTSCa0eAR4ieqYbdAE=\n=4kIS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T03:50:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.git