ists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon","id":92697,"login":"developerinlondon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNjk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/f55acdc1b619c825258540d36aef379d8c13b838/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:25:31Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:25:31Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"message":"feat(stdlib): assay.clayinbox, assay.forge, assay.salesforge for the revenue seams\n\nThe cold-email vendor stack existed twice and was reachable from neither an\nagent nor a second service: once in an ops script that reads OpenBao itself,\nand once in a TypeScript adapter inside one product. These three modules are\nthe one copy. Each takes its credentials from the caller — opts, or a\ndocumented environment variable — and reads no secret store, so the same code\nserves a script, a service and an agent that bakes it as a tool.\n\nEvery method answers (result) or (nil, err), where err carries code, status\nand message and prints as its message. `raw` on a mapped row is the vendor''s\nown record with credentials removed: both Clayinbox and Primeforge put a\nmailbox password on a list row.\n\nThe vendor behaviours pinned by the tests were each probed live on 2026-09-04\nand each has already cost someone a wrong answer:\n\n  - A Primeforge domain arrives as `sld` and `tld`, never as a whole name.\n  - primeforge_list_mailboxes takes only workspaceId and answers ten rows\n    whatever limit and offset say; offset 10 and offset 20 return the same ten\n    ids. The domain filter is therefore applied to what the vendor gives.\n  - A Warmforge health check the report omits is unknown, never invalid.\n  - Warm-up length is days done plus days left, not a constant.\n  - A placement row with no folder counts is a test nobody ran, not a zero.\n  - The Salesforge public key rides bare in Authorization; a Bearer prefix is\n    refused. Its internal API carries no reputationScore today, so an absent\n    heat is a reading nobody has yet.\n  - A workspace with no sequences answers with a JSON object where a list\n    belongs.\n  - Auth, rate limiting, the Growth-plan 402 and a Cloudflare block page under\n    an HTTP 200 all read as themselves rather than as an empty fleet.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rd3ikB7kHqnRBnoW1mX8sh","tree":{"sha":"9301e014106e8329b8085abd90095740158b41af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/trees/9301e014106e8329b8085abd90095740158b41af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/commits/f55acdc1b619c825258540d36aef379d8c13b838","verification":{"payload":"tree 9301e014106e8329b8085abd90095740158b41af\nparent 703590c5caa0fc264d06a3d87a2333d716836163\nauthor Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1788492331 +0000\ncommitter Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1788492331 +0000\n\nfeat(stdlib): assay.clayinbox, assay.forge, assay.salesforge for the revenue seams\n\nThe cold-email vendor stack existed twice and was reachable from neither an\nagent nor a second service: once in an ops script that reads OpenBao itself,\nand once in a TypeScript adapter inside one product. These three modules are\nthe one copy. Each takes its credentials from the caller — opts, or a\ndocumented environment variable — and reads no secret store, so the same code\nserves a script, a service and an agent that bakes it as a tool.\n\nEvery method answers (result) or (nil, err), where err carries code, status\nand message and prints as its message. `raw` on a mapped row is the vendor''s\nown record with credentials removed: both Clayinbox and Primeforge put a\nmailbox password on a list row.\n\nThe vendor behaviours pinned by the tests were each probed live on 2026-09-04\nand each has already cost someone a wrong answer:\n\n  - A Primeforge domain arrives as `sld` and `tld`, never as a whole name.\n  - primeforge_list_mailboxes takes only workspaceId and answers ten rows\n    whatever limit and offset say; offset 10 and offset 20 return the same ten\n    ids. The domain filter is therefore applied to what the vendor gives.\n  - A Warmforge health check the report omits is unknown, never invalid.\n  - Warm-up length is days done plus days left, not a constant.\n  - A placement row with no folder counts is a test nobody ran, not a zero.\n  - The Salesforge public key rides bare in Authorization; a Bearer prefix is\n    refused. Its internal API carries no reputationScore today, so an absent\n    heat is a reading nobody has yet.\n  - A workspace with no sequences answers with a JSON object where a list\n    belongs.\n  - Auth, rate limiting, the Growth-plan 402 and a Cloudflare block page under\n    an HTTP 200 all read as themselves rather than as an empty fleet.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rd3ikB7kHqnRBnoW1mX8sh\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRV/FXDL+YfHsAYcfER+ZP89e7hTAUCapo6KwAKCRAR+ZP89e7h\nTFNrAQCg7vDKMsVQEx6nBplfH7wLK8N921zvSftc4wFc4v8/awD9E7SI+HDnCKwT\ni3E32LIo6shg3hiWmE9syEuRLI3zNwQ=\n=9I/s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T03:50:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92697?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/events{/privacy}","followe