heaply and never inflates its evidence.","tree":{"sha":"d2e7982c700714bf43b5d7c037f32e57177a78ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/trees/d2e7982c700714bf43b5d7c037f32e57177a78ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/commits/f96b935dd52bee2619d98277a115a6eddf434cce","verification":{"payload":"tree d2e7982c700714bf43b5d7c037f32e57177a78ea\nparent ef8c1c907c81ad156a0635bee4ec13aa6dd95d39\nauthor Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1787798148 +0000\ncommitter Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1787798148 +0000\n\nassay.email_verify: the waterfall''s free rung (#33 tracks the SMTP half)\n\nSyntax that refuses what could never deliver, MX over DNS-over-HTTPS so\ntests mock one endpoint, and the pattern candidates an executive address\nusually takes. The vocabulary is deliberately capped at INVALID and\nUNKNOWN: the runtime has no raw TCP yet, so nothing here may claim what\nonly an SMTP conversation or a paid verifier can know — the free rung\nrejects cheaply and never inflates its evidence.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRV/FXDL+YfHsAYcfER+ZP89e7hTAUCao+ihAAKCRAR+ZP89e7h\nTEN9AP9JtIaEEiO5upY6TOose85hPppD3BfJBw4+9E31LOATsgEArZwwHeDGVjIJ\nzAK166xuyPrVPogGtTV50W2rkbXkag0=\n=4dsW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T02:39:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92697?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon","id":92697,"login":"developerinlondon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNjk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/orgs