,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/developerinlondon","id":92697,"login":"developerinlondon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNjk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developerinlondon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/252f330fa0a31de479a554c61dc1c21a4d864df6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T02:14:23Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T02:14:23Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"message":"Registry modules: everything the review found (#31)\n\nThe reviewer earned its keep: the CHANGELOG conflict resolution had\nclobbered six released sections — restored verbatim with the Unreleased\nblock on top. A private estate domain left the public test suite for a\ngeneric contact. An empty LEI no longer turns GLEIF''s collection endpoint\ninto a truthy garbage hit, and an empty find() needle errors instead of\nreturning the entire SEC ticker table. tickers() memoizes per client and\nshares one provenance table per fetch. Both modules use assay.url''s\nRFC 3986 encoder instead of hand-rolled locale-dependent gsubs, file\nunder a real ''registries'' category instead of squatting in Cloud & AWS,\nand appear in both llms.txt surfaces and the module counts. gleif''s\nheader now promises provenance per record, which is what it delivers.","tree":{"sha":"c31b7e7ef915a2608b5ebce747484003bf929a1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/trees/c31b7e7ef915a2608b5ebce747484003bf929a1c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/commits/252f330fa0a31de479a554c61dc1c21a4d864df6","verification":{"payload":"tree c31b7e7ef915a2608b5ebce747484003bf929a1c\nparent 73c89ab7a209777a29bbfa8cf533aec5755176bd\nauthor Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1787796863 +0000\ncommitter Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1787796863 +0000\n\nRegistry modules: everything the review found (#31)\n\nThe reviewer earned its keep: the CHANGELOG conflict resolution had\nclobbered six released sections — restored verbatim with the Unreleased\nblock on top. A private estate domain left the public test suite for a\ngeneric contact. An empty LEI no longer turns GLEIF''s collection endpoint\ninto a truthy garbage hit, and an empty find() needle errors instead of\nreturning the entire SEC ticker table. tickers() memoizes per client and\nshares one provenance table per fetch. Both modules use assay.url''s\nRFC 3986 encoder instead of hand-rolled locale-dependent gsubs, file\nunder a real ''registries'' category instead of squatting in Cloud & AWS,\nand appear in both llms.txt surfaces and the module counts. gleif''s\nheader now promises provenance per record, which is what it delivers.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRV/FXDL+YfHsAYcfER+ZP89e7hTAUCao+dfwAKCRAR+ZP89e7h\nTFzPAP91RnJI1m3ZGv3rwtDUECmeXyxw+Mb4xGDdFWblORA0XgD/VuWWU3zj6DgU\nS2WHYda1/EY0IJb41LxI9LZQVOFCdA8=\n=9+tI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T02:28:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92697?v=4","events_url":"https:/