om/users/developerinlondon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/commits/3977f552391917874589530d0d23094559e68e29/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T13:46:57Z","email":"developerinlondon@gmail.com","name":"Nayeem Syed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T13:46:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Sign-in fills the screen it is given (#276)\n\n* feat(dashboard): sign-in fills the screen it is given\n\nThe two-area composition fixed its sizes at the split breakpoint and never\ngrew again: a 40px headline and a 400px card marooned in the middle of a\n1920px window, the story and the form each reading as an isolated block.\nColumn widths, type sizes, card padding and control heights are clamped\nagainst the viewport, so the page scales as one composition.\n\nThe ground carries two accent blooms — behind the brand mark and under the\ncomposition — mixed from ASSAY_WHITELABEL_ACCENT, so a deployment re-colours\nthe whole page from the one variable it already sets. The headline''s second\nline takes the accent, the brand mark blooms at logo size, and the trust note\ngets a shield instead of the rule it shared with block quotes.\n\nASSAY_WHITELABEL_LOGIN_BRAND is new and optional: text after `|` takes the\naccent, so `Neutron|Core` renders `Core` in the brand colour. Unset renders\nNAME in one colour, which is what every deployment renders today, and a\ndeployment with no story configured keeps its centred single card.\n\nBoth fields carry placeholders, the submit is a gradient off the accent and\nsits a notch taller than the inputs, and the recovery page picks up the same\nplaceholders.\n\nCloses #275\n\n* fix(dashboard): 0.6.0, not 0.5.1 — the config struct gained a field\n\nWhitelabelConfig has public fields and no #[non_exhaustive], so adding\nlogin_brand breaks every struct-literal construction of it. For a 0.x crate\nthat is a minor bump, which is what the last field addition took too.\nassay-engine''s dependency moves with it.","tree":{"sha":"cf81f118bfe4603ecd26e8ee0ea199cdd890679d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/trees/cf81f118bfe4603ecd26e8ee0ea199cdd890679d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/commits/3977f552391917874589530d0d23094559e68e29","verification":{"payload":"tree cf81f118bfe4603ecd26e8ee0ea199cdd890679d\nparent 35b0202ec2f306febcbc09c5ab57e9192e5bd3b8\nauthor Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1787233617 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787233617 +0100\n\nSign-in fills the screen it is given (#276)\n\n* feat(dashboard): sign-in fills the screen it is given\n\nThe two-area composition fixed its sizes at the split breakpoint and never\ngrew again: a 40px headline and a 400px card marooned in the middle of a\n1920px window, the story and the form each reading as an isolated block.\nColumn widths, type sizes, card padding and control heights are clamped\nagainst the viewport, so the page scales as one composition.\n\nThe ground carries two accent blooms — behind the brand mark and under the\ncomposition — mixed from ASSAY_WHITELABEL_ACCENT, so a deployment re-colours\nthe whole page from the one variable it already sets. The headline''s second\nline takes the accent, the brand mark blooms at logo size, and the trust note\ngets a shield instead of the rule it shared with block quotes.\n\nASSAY_WHITELABEL_LOGIN_BRAND is new and optional: text after `|` takes the\naccent, so `Neutron|Core` renders `Core` in the brand colour. Unset renders\nNAME in one colour, which is what every deployment renders today, and a\ndeployment with no story configured keeps its centred single card.\n\nBoth fields carry placeholders, the submit is a gradient off the accent and\nsits a notch taller than the inputs, and the recovery page picks up the same\nplaceholders.\n\nCloses #275\n\n* fix(dashboard): 0.6.0, not 0.5.1 — the config struct gained a field\n\nWhitelabelConfig has public fields and no #[non_exhaustive], so adding\nlogin_brand breaks every struct-literal construction of it. For a 0.x crate\nthat is a minor bump, which is what the last field addition took too.\nassay-engine''s dependency moves with it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhwVRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2psQAECbEHVXBa9SUDGQ2HxtyZ66\nl7C8D0o8DX4VL6gqGlubTf1cc83nkCXjcrO2Jj1FlPTIMyH8NBQb7p7KX2C8Q/Km\nWoLkyLTSnLIYYYPIhsoGU12IlP5DqcWBKTlxt4NkdKCnyulAwOJqZA8+fCEocVpV\nrzZrkFqVM5Y19UM8l822mi01FEWTKXhocq9aYW+9K9CxvLSRXiYN+vRxt4U9PP+0\nsF57/wlzcM5d/WH9giRd0igLBGHqu12AfrWWXMFlBDaWhVVch4HSDg6du0C2jU0e\nFO7GBErv+xL7vCNWnXYyzQLGy7SPIvm1df+BpU/l8jnUwy0iWp1+sT/aXZtvD7AR\nQjDPsMCIcK/4oAvraml8PY7Ia0g2CCSxdw76xTNPl/XBwKNt9jm9R+Bt5mi7UhvY\nogjjvmWcGRCCg19vXAC1kozBfnlhXywVOET4dHDOmCHNNByq1xUn4ZlTYIELNdZU\nUg2QtC2DzU62u8S3yK+5hozHN7ZwZ8GY8BVAqFZOe1gJaIi/vvtFyP2JFjg+xceD\nPVb2VCOP3oS9+SuETUq3b1NSe15PcjRBUfj2T3IjOwLZ3pMmcGeAx3mic/Xd+p7T\nK8Z5RJui8X0+5Tn2KWXfudbmnNDFdG0EsryeZIHl3Xtz9oAMdquqOTZNmJsajgW8\nB+AHEkO5327k6+bJ6sG7\n=glTw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T13:46:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.co