ope and re-inject what the transactor\ndrops: _class on class-scoped reads, and any attribute the query already\npinned to a scalar. create_issue numbers an issue by atomically\nincrementing the project sequence, without which the issue is invisible\nin the UI. Requests ask for identity encoding because assay can decode\nneither snappy nor gzip.\n\nCloses #255","tree":{"sha":"275fc198f2fcd43e2d677d2dc1ab11ed41bda9d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/trees/275fc198f2fcd43e2d677d2dc1ab11ed41bda9d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developerinlondon/assay/git/commits/a0dd286e1b0f8de557f17eb6b2f83be7587a3ac6","verification":{"payload":"tree 275fc198f2fcd43e2d677d2dc1ab11ed41bda9d0\nparent 34a1399912c63b546f456d81a9af552539af205d\nauthor Nayeem Syed <developerinlondon@gmail.com> 1786629520 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786629520 +0100\n\nfeat(stdlib): add assay.huly module for the Huly transactor API (#256)\n\nHuly exposes no per-resource REST endpoints — every read is a\nclass-parameterised query and every write is a transaction document — so\nthe client is shaped around those two calls plus tracker helpers.\n\nReads unwrap the TotalArray envelope and re-inject what the transactor\ndrops: _class on class-scoped reads, and any attribute the query already\npinned to a scalar. create_issue numbers an issue by atomically\nincrementing the project sequence, without which the issue is invisible\nin the UI. Requests ask for identity encoding because assay can decode\nneither snappy nor gzip.\n\nCloses #255","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfc2QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqkcQAEIGrRehOfdYL5p8/XIRXgBq\nLxllHKRxJjKyY3EBdBK8DSx+77wV/qs7B3RYsBHch66dNa2CY/GW7R9IdJ9kQYea\n9lwTF1F1h3n26G8FDmQkbPu02z9uVfdEqm6X02iVQ9RpYjxSHryzhKw3Bblrv2GX\nk4nd4JUclwDDagJEVTazPR39HPtSwJei+M7Dx1c9ZhPLVgyNitXwr7hl0g9t3616\n2F4JL+U8tpZ6Ayh4ry7HX10Wf8fY3U2ePtJzBWr5bjeaqSNCGq44IsIJd4Zo3p8A\nmRPkTeCe523NjW2Niy/hNrGFbI5x8/dsiS