nts{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/6a9631fdc181dc9da72fb2f692e804255937c216/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:10:11Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:10:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(chat): bare topic words route deterministically; an executed answer is never turned into a plan preview (#573)\n\n* fix(chat): a bare topic word (\"Expenses\", \"balance\", \"tax\") routes to its read-only skill deterministically, never to a plan preview\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chat): a low classifier score never turns an already-executed answer into a plan preview\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chat): a write that already executed is never re-planned — no \"Proceed?\" that would book it twice\n\nrecord-expense and create-invoice are in DESTRUCTIVE_SKILLS but ship with\nconfirmBefore: false, so agent-brain Step 3c executes them inline and the POST\nlands. Step 4 then re-assessed the SAME text with afterExecution, where the\ndestructive-word rule (\\badd\\b, \\brecord\\b, \\bcreate\\b) matched the very word\nthat caused the write, returned ''complex'', and the brain threw the completed\nresult away for a \"Here''s my plan ... Proceed?\" preview. Confirming that plan\nre-runs the POST: \"add a $40 lunch\" booked the expense twice. A multi-intent\nmessage whose first intent had already executed did the same.\n\nassessComplexity now returns ''simple'' immediately when afterExecution is set\nand the skill writes (DESTRUCTIVE_SKILLS or confirmBefore), before the\nmulti-intent / destructive-word / conditional rules. Read-only skills may still\nbe planned after execution — that costs an extra call at worst, never a\nduplicate side effect. Pre-execution behaviour (no afterExecution) is\nunchanged, and pinned by paired assertions.\n\nTwo assertions in agent-planner-complexity.test.ts that pinned ''complex'' for a\ndestructive skill under afterExecution are deliberately changed: they pinned\nthe hazard. The read-only half of that rule is re-pinned on query-estimates,\nwhich is in none of the exempt sets.\n\nAlso from review, in bare-topic-routing.test.ts: the linearity case gets a\n39-char adversarial failing match, since the 50 kB string only ever proved the\nBARE_TOPIC_MAX_CHARS gate and never reached a regex; and the \"still reaches\nnormal routing\" cases now assert selectedSkill.name instead of\nconfidence !== 0.3, which almost any outcome satisfied.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3c6a9976406a86c61b528b4e9e317dbd123a96eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/3c6a9976406a86c61b528b4e9e317dbd123a96eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/6a9631fdc181dc9da72fb2f692e804255937c216","verification":{"payload":"tree 3c6a9976406a86c61b528b4e9e317dbd123a96eb\nparent 30b347eed1bcafaee2cb4babcaf67a6958e016d8\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1789348211 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789348211 -0700\n\nfix(chat): bare topic words route deterministically; an executed answer is never turned into a plan preview (#573)\n\n* fix(chat): a bare topic word (\"Expenses\", \"balance\", \"tax\") routes to its read-only skill deterministically, never to a plan preview\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chat): a low classifier score never turns an already-executed answer into a plan preview\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chat): a write that already executed is never re-planned — no \"Proceed?\" that would book it twice\n\nrecord-expense and create-invoice are in DESTRUCTIVE_SKILLS but ship with\nconfirmBefore: false, so agent-brain Step 3c executes them inline and the POST\nlands. Step 4 then re-assessed the SAME text with afterExecution, where the\ndestructive-word rule (\\badd\\b, \\brecord\\b, \\bcreate\\b) matched the very word\nthat caused the write, returned ''complex'', and the brain threw the completed\nresult away for a \"Here''s my plan ... Proceed?\" preview. Confirming that plan\nre-runs the POST: \"add a $40 lunch\" booked the expense twice. A multi-intent\nmessage whose first intent had already executed did the same.\n\nassessComplexity now returns ''simple'' immediately when afterExecution is set\nand the skill writes (DESTRUCTIVE_SKILLS or confirmBefore), before the\nmulti-intent / destructive-word / conditional rules. Read-only skills may still\nbe planned after execution — that costs an extra call at worst, never a\nduplicate side effect. Pre-execution behaviour (no afterExecution) is\nunchanged, and pinned by paired assertions.\n\nTwo assertions in agent-planner-complexity.test.ts that pinned ''complex'' for a\ndestructive skill under afterExecution are deliberately changed: they pinned\nthe hazard. The read-only half of that rule is re-pinned on query-estimates,\nwhich is in none of the exempt sets.\n\nAlso from review, in bare-topic-routing.test.ts: the linearity case gets a\n39-char adversarial failing match, since the 50 kB string only ever proved the\nBARE_TOPIC_MAX_CHARS gate and never reached a regex; and the \"still reaches\nnormal routing\" cases now assert selectedSkill.name instead of\nconfidence !== 0.3, which almost any outcome satisfied.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp0lzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfREQAFsJcVZDkzPjOaei9unOb11x\nqzg8xKFpJQZ2j4Dkqb846Pcfdu6abZSmVcX9fjobAVo3wMUMVHb5tfhie1HRCE6+\npVYj3i2HIvUWKiKOlxAlld1lg0HA7p6WCnOfNpDXKRUzQNk7qDj6YL+XlxHWo8iu\n9o1E1H2G/WggH61DLQsuV5PfOQBAP7nC8SkZLxbHHCKp08HX2r62lP8Ke1XvuoOq\ns8P6z/6nO/SbONCXfQExWnEQJnH1LyvaQiUOqQeHBlwUpWQKMFsGaBLYXcGqPMBl\n/5sPw2xKe4Q6ghnDK8s23PHnVHE+2n81Ruitk744JYikdRtPzR2hbQkZG21ucx0q\n2QeTZbu49isKkHLt1wBEFcN/h/oM0hL+5geCbuuJhF6PjvFPvhoO82BYAbSe9N1y\nZzarvfilpXjoic6TXX5CZvnwLaZvoYp3XirJRbVccorHnGyjGdcATRzoduzCEwNv\nyEFFxfPkslLo9QkH6cDQsYezoDhfCJu4XnfXpmUqziBRRMOgo8oZowKjUTU0BvNe\nGVnwiOuJWT7ViqUs7/f4Y8QTvUeq88Uzu8ijWSNF1lo89+ze0hu1N8RknbpDziDa\n1lwxkNKEue5otsD1r2GBcjmgqwLHP5EuTcGio0bAr6RO1jiv7RptldsUh50FdT9x\n2s/7ol8HxcFAwWe5c6n3\n=Ap2n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T01:10:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizat