l":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/7fffd7609666355397762f0f381f580114aa2c4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T16:53:53Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T16:53:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mcp): implement resource indicators, so the token exchange stops failing (#558)\n\nReported from a real connection attempt, after login and consent:\n\n    Authentication failed\n    invalid_target: resource indicator is missing, or unknown\n\nThat string is oidc-provider''s, verbatim — helpers/errors.js:138,\n`E(''invalid_target'', ''resource indicator is missing, or unknown'')`.\n\noidc-provider enables `features.resourceIndicators` by default and ships a\n`getResourceServerInfo` whose entire body is a deprecation notice and a throw\n(helpers/defaults.js:246). We never overrode it. The MCP authorization spec\nREQUIRES clients to send RFC 8707 `resource` on the authorization and token\nrequests, so every spec-compliant client hit the default and was refused.\n\nThe shape of the failure is what made it expensive: the authorization request\nitself still 303s to consent, so the user signs in, presses Allow, and only\nthen does the exchange fail. It reads as \"your sign-in was rejected\", which is\nthe one thing it is not.\n\nNow:\n  - getResourceServerInfo returns `{ scope: MCP_SCOPE, accessTokenFormat:\n    ''opaque'' }` for our resource and throws InvalidTarget for anything else.\n  - defaultResource resolves the only resource we have, so a client that omits\n    the parameter still works.\n  - useGrantedResource returns true, oidc-provider''s own recommendation when a\n    client may skip `resource` at the token endpoint.\n\naccessTokenFormat MUST stay ''opaque'': `authenticateMcpRequest` resolves bearer\ntokens with `provider.AccessToken.find()`, which only finds opaque ones. A\nswitch to ''jwt'' would leave the OAuth flow looking healthy while every MCP\ncall 401s. There is a test pinning it.\n\n`scopes` now uses the same MCP_SCOPE constant as the resource server info, so\nthe advertised scope and the grantable scope cannot drift.\n\nVerified by mutation:\n  - helper reverted to the library default (always throw)\n      -> 2 failures, incl. \"accepts the MCP endpoint as a resource\"\n  - `resourceIndicators` block deleted (the state that shipped)\n      -> \"is actually wired into the provider, not merely exported\" fails\n\nTypecheck holds at the 294 baseline; `errors` is now declared in the local\noidc-provider module declaration, which only had a default export.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <qiang@livepeer.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"294e3397649b27539d3e9c9f18fcfb8fd5da9015","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/294e3397649b27539d3e9c9f18fcfb8fd5da9015"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/7fffd7609666355397762f0f381f580114aa2c4f","verification":{"payload":"tree 294e3397649b27539d3e9c9f18fcfb8fd5da9015\nparent 43688de219180550b9bdd0ca344b6aab592f9660\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1789318433 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789318433 -0700\n\nfix(mcp): implement resource indicators, so the token exchange stops failing (#558)\n\nReported from a real connection attempt, after login and consent:\n\n    Authentication failed\n    invalid_target: resource indicator is missing, or unknown\n\nThat string is oidc-provider''s, verbatim — helpers/errors.js:138,\n`E(''invalid_target'', ''resource indicator is missing, or unknown'')`.\n\noidc-provider enables `features.resourceIndicators` by default and ships a\n`getResourceServerInfo` whose entire body is a deprecation notice and a throw\n(helpers/defaults.js:246). We never overrode it. The MCP authorization spec\nREQUIRES clients to send RFC 8707 `resource` on the authorization and token\nrequests, so every spec-compliant client hit the default and was refused.\n\nThe shape of the failure is what made it expensive: the authorization request\nitself still 303s to consent, so the user signs in, presses Allow, and only\nthen does the exchange fail. It reads as \"your sign-in was rejected\", which is\nthe one thing it is not.\n\nNow:\n  - getResourceServerInfo returns `{ scope: MCP_SCOPE, accessTokenFormat:\n    ''opaque'' }` for our resource and throws InvalidTarget for anything else.\n  - defaultResource resolves the only resource we have, so a client that omits\n    the parameter still works.\n  - useGrantedResource returns true, oidc-provider''s own recommendation when a\n    client may skip `resource` at the token endpoint.\n\naccessTokenFormat MUST stay ''opaque'': `authenticateMcpRequest` resolves bearer\ntokens with `provider.AccessToken.find()`, which only finds opaque ones. A\nswitch to ''jwt'' would leave the OAuth flow looking healthy while every MCP\ncall 401s. There is a test pinning it.\n\n`scopes` now uses the same MCP_SCOPE constant as the resource server info, so\nthe advertised scope and the grantable scope cannot drift.\n\nVerified by mutation:\n  - helper reverted to the library default (always throw)\n      -> 2 failures, incl. \"accepts the MCP endpoint as a resource\"\n  - `resourceIndicators` block deleted (the state that shipped)\n      -> \"is actually wired into the provider, not merely exported\" fails\n\nTypecheck holds at the 294 baseline; `errors` is now declared in the local\noidc-provider module declaration, which only had a default export.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <qiang@livepeer.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqptUhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAibYQAHrNl23S34odejML48wjRNbR\n9yQqWE2I62oJ2Hv9hHqOSb6/salJejMVRiyeQYURitgzF1zKQ4uOfgffExLuOGlE\nwwek4s1c6JpshrWR7cOJ99w5y+IxJfgle5KjmMENkv5yXcpiVb5sVUfftqXKRPjZ\nbkRtiW5yifGQSjkVlCnq+CadcVGXX1s4mxRIlc1+vwKCDxGtXHBvPPdhBOzifFhK\n/g7KNy5DtPxTCofi17P1zc5sMTZpqqMIQs6MufxM1c+8YnFliE0XdMeYhO+xdbK0\nlU0jUuUppnF4yMCy5SqSewbUjNOvaB1rD8AnBjtehUpqFHVYqz135e0an7n/Fhy/\npKKNT4O8Oa1ZDjn1orJMjYA8m86YS9ha5gRETUHutLXHFZaLQ3VI1UbvYU3aYtbT\nY+qCVZSyWAuJ/db95hsO8kxMBi1sOZrR+ImNl39GOnNJnWNM3FqK9qFS7i1qklCg\n3nq7j5EcA13r6Zbm7fGuDD8OGH6nljOL179PsBHeZg/8pPQ+Ry9kst7abIOK3VLU\nCCsV+qaudgmEPy3EEuIgt5yAqjCTM6cRbv2PEDx/dixdyFco033B5KIBGFDUQonJ\nw2AzYi2Gi3xyZZh7651arza04uPCQRO04zAK3ej4wi1DdQcspgQ2iVM43eJshDow\nlwwZ7CRlkOqaxXgnygLz\n=cG4y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T16:53:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/7fffd7609666355397762f0f381f580114aa2c4f","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDdmZmZkNzYwOTY2NjM1NTM5Nzc2MmYwZjM4MWY1ODAxMTRhYTJjNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/43688de219180550b9bdd0ca344b6aab592f9660","sha":"43688de219180550b9bdd0ca344b6aab592f9660","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/43688de219180550b9bdd0ca344b6aab592f9660"}],"sha":"7fffd7609666355397762f0f381f580114aa2c4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/7fffd7609666355397762f0f381f580114aa2c4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/43688de219180550b9bdd0ca344b6aab592f9660/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T16:26:22Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T16:26:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mcp): trust the TLS terminator, so the provider stops describing itself as http (#557)\n\n`Provider extends Koa`, and `proxy` was never set. Koa therefore ignored\n`x-forwarded-proto` and read the scheme off the socket — always plaintext\ninside a serverless function — so the provider concluded the entire\ndeployment was served over HTTP. Two consequences, both live in production\nand neither of which announced itself:\n\n  - Every URL the provider generated used `ctx.origin`. Dynamic Client\n    Registration answered an HTTPS issuer with\n\n        \"registration_client_uri\":\n          \"http://agentbook.brainliber.com/api/v1/oauth/register/...\"\n\n    an insecure URL handed to a client as the place to manage its own\n    credentials.\n\n  - `ctx.secure` was false, and the provider adds `Secure` to its cookies only\n    when it is true (models/session.js:55, helpers/oidc_context.js:48). The\n    `_interaction` and `_interaction_resume` cookies — the state carrying an\n    in-flight authorization — went out without it:\n\n        set-cookie: _interaction=...; path=/; samesite=lax; httponly\n\n    Browsers accept a non-Secure cookie over HTTPS, which is exactly why this\n    stayed invisible: the flow worked, and the cookie sat one plaintext\n    request to this host away from leaking.\n\nSafe to trust here because these routes only run behind Vercel''s proxy, which\noverwrites `x-forwarded-proto` inbound rather than forwarding a client-supplied\none. `nodeRequestResponseFromWeb` fills the header from the URL Next resolved\nwhen it is missing, so a direct local run is described accurately instead of\ninheriting the bare `new Socket()` underneath the synthetic IncomingMessage.\n\nTested against the real provider over a real request. The second case asserts\nthat a genuinely plaintext request is still reported as plaintext — otherwise\nthe first would pass on a provider that simply claimed https for everything.\n\nVerified to fail without the fix:\n  AssertionError: registration_client_uri was http://127.0.0.1:63095/...\n    expected ''http://...'' to match /^https:\\/\\//\n\nWhether this is what broke a particular client''s connector is not established;\nit is wrong on its own terms either way.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <qiang@livepeer.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"99a80bfc207978a935619452031d00054f003c73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/99a80bfc207978a935619452031d00054f003c73"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/43688de219180550b9bdd0ca344b6aab592f9660","verification":{"payload":"tree 99a80bfc207978a935619452031d00054f003c73\nparent 747199f5fcdbf5cc9972710e4058f54b474ae0ab\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1789316782 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789316782 -0700\n\nfix(mcp): trust the TLS terminator, so the provider stops describing itself as http (#557)\n\n`Provider extends Koa`, and `proxy` was never set. Koa therefore ignored\n`x-forwarded-proto` and read the scheme off the socket — always plaintext\ninside a serverless function — so the provider concluded the entire\ndeployment was served over HTTP. Two consequences, both live in production\nand neither of which announced itself:\n\n  - Every URL the provider generated used `ctx.origin`. Dynamic Client\n    Registration answered an HTTPS issuer with\n\n        \"registration_client_uri\":\n          \"http://agentbook.brainliber.com/api/v1/oauth/register/...\"\n\n    an insecure URL handed to a client as the place to manage its own\n    credentials.\n\n  - `ctx.secure` was false, and the provider adds `Secure` to its cookies only\n    when it is true (models/session.js:55, helpers/oidc_context.js:48). The\n    `_interaction` and `_interaction_resume` cookies — the state carrying an\n    in-flight authorization — went out without it:\n\n        set-cookie: _interaction=...; path=/; samesite=lax; httponly\n\n    Browsers accept a non-Secure cookie over HTTPS, which is exactly why this\n    stayed invisible: the flow worked, and the cookie sat one plaintext\n    request to this host away from leaking.\n\nSafe to trust here because these routes only run behind Vercel''s proxy, which\noverwrites `x-forwarded-proto` inbound rather than forwarding a client-supplied\none. `nodeRequestResponseFromWeb` fills the header from the URL Next resolved\nwhen it is missing, so a direct local run is described accurately instead of\ninheriting the bare `new Socket()` underneath the synthetic IncomingMessage.\n\nTested against the real provider over a real request. The second case asserts\nthat a genuinely plaintext request is still reported as plaintext — otherwise\nthe first would pass on a provider that simply claimed https for everything.\n\nVerified to fail without the fix:\n  AssertionError: registration_client_uri was http://127.0.0.1:63095/...\n    expected ''http://...'' to match /^https:\\/\\//\n\nWhether this is what broke a particular client''s connector is not established;\nit is wrong on its own terms either way.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <qiang@livepeer.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqps6uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7bUQAFtaXbe4zQ1OFvvKIW5CxNk6\nghezTkKdnXBSlb8egrMrU5YyyrRI82sqWjb82uW4Zl/Zo0rjMT1yPLpm/izCe4PN\n8xkImsvdbsT/yhFzBVMsNrsltKidjAtf1PwUzollvCLQ2SKoCHwQg5nTVi/VgdoP\nR4jR75XWgetvEBzuvKeasYnrMgOh81ige/VAS/LWcqEiqnmdr3dCvPIbpeMlY8ky\n4Fg+rFLc9umAZwPSjBZu/lcRUMhoJIHjZ9eGGuQax3Q2KLKWJhmyETIs6OcJvGSl\nugGrPA+rb6c/9qNVxPwdTMrKmBXLoFs3Cjj+QsMn2em5rHmn3tK7XKZcwUwiuPc7\nJ5CRGqgB7Ft1VrGeegCqw/2ZEjctn4NwpdNz29MjqDgEUcwmueJVJNZoqBloY8qY\nlzwofq7H+xQeaAw34BPW0le17tNEX+35jR1z9LQS9lj22NHXyZFLbO2i3P0RZk8/\n4oXwQZbBQ1or2rAtybMrQwLpMS51Nd+AKjhCzf9kGwlH0X5HfVBO/fVV5ZcQNZQe\ni3sxQB/z8R8PzZOU/L8R2bcnVxGWRFzAGgaIAcUIKpbLG4nAcYB8yEwYce5xY2EL\n93MFFShWybrNKI2gCEOkGS4WDL7bdxydsgzH/4+yFdHzlaOh/DzxfINQOa8ckCsd\nmrXnfU/RqRvbhznGqiVu\n=OZLb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T16:26:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/43688de219180550b9bdd0ca344b6aab592f9660","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDQzNjg4ZGUyMTkxODA1NTBiOWJkZDBjYTM0NGI2YWFiNTkyZjk2NjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/747199f5fcdbf5cc9972710e4058f54b474ae0ab","sha":"747199f5fcdbf5cc9972710e4058f54b474ae0ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/747199f5fcdbf5cc9972710e4058f54b474ae0ab"}],"sha":"43688de219180550b9bdd0ca344b6aab592f9660","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/43688de219180550b9bdd0ca344b6aab592f9660"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/747199f5fcdbf5cc9972710e4058f54b474ae0ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:59:07Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:59:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mcp): serve protected-resource metadata where clients actually look (#556)\n\nAdding the connector failed with \"can''t register with AgentBook''s sign-in\nservice\", then with an account mismatch against the client''s own account.\nNeither is a client bug: OAuth discovery never reached us.\n\nRFC 9728 §3.1 builds a resource''s metadata URL by INSERTING the well-known\nname after the host, so a resource at /api/v1/mcp is described at\n/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/v1/mcp. We served only the bare\n/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource. Nothing matched the path-inserted URL,\nso it fell through to the client-side catch-all at app/(dashboard)/[...slug],\nwhich renders for ANY unmatched path and decides it is a 404 only after JS\nruns — over HTTP, 200 text/html.\n\n200 is worse than 404 here. The MCP SDK falls back to the root metadata URL\nonly on a 4xx:\n\n    function shouldAttemptFallback(response, pathname) {\n      return !response || (response.status >= 400 && response.status < 500\n                           && pathname !== ''/'');\n    }\n\nSo the guess \"succeeded\", OAuthProtectedResourceMetadataSchema.parse(await\nresponse.json()) was handed a page of HTML, and discovery ended there. With no\nmetadata the client cannot learn the authorization server, cannot register,\nand falls back to a hand-entered client id or its own account linking — which\nis what the account mismatch was.\n\nTwo fixes:\n\n  - A route at .well-known/oauth-protected-resource/[...resource] serving the\n    metadata for /api/v1/mcp and 404ing everything else, deliberately, so a\n    client can fall back instead of parsing a page.\n  - resource_metadata=<url> added to the 401''s WWW-Authenticate header\n    (RFC 9728 §5.3, required by the MCP authorization spec). This removes the\n    guess entirely: the client is told where the metadata is.\n\nThe issuer, resource path and metadata URL now come from one place —\nthree copies were what let the header and the route disagree.\n\nVerified against a production build served locally:\n  /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/v1/nonsense\n    -> 404 application/json   (was 200 text/html)\n  /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/v1/mcp\n    -> reaches the handler (500 only because this box has no DATABASE_URL)\n  /.well-known/openid-configuration\n    -> still 200 text/html, confirming the catch-all was the cause and that\n       this route is what changed the outcome\n\nBoth new tests fail with their fix removed.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <qiang@livepeer.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e65d7ce11792a05f2ccc8ac91fffaa18b00336a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/e65d7ce11792a05f2ccc8ac91fffaa18b00336a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/747199f5fcdbf5cc9972710e4058f54b474ae0ab","verification":{"payload":"tree e65d7ce11792a05f2ccc8ac91fffaa18b00336a2\nparent c6e4fe9888e7d20f6246e5a94f13df481a9fa79f\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1789315147 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789315147 -0700\n\nfix(mcp): serve protected-resource metadata where clients actually look (#556)\n\nAdding the connector failed with \"can''t register with AgentBook''s sign-in\nservice\", then with an account mismatch against the client''s own account.\nNeither is a client bug: OAuth discovery never reached us.\n\nRFC 9728 §3.1 builds a resource''s metadata URL by INSERTING the well-known\nname after the host, so a resource at /api/v1/mcp is described at\n/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/v1/mcp. We served only the bare\n/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource. Nothing matched the path-inserted URL,\nso it fell through to the client-side catch-all at app/(dashboard)/[...slug],\nwhich renders for ANY unmatched path and decides it is a 404 only after JS\nruns — over HTTP, 200 text/html.\n\n200 is worse than 404 here. The MCP SDK falls back to the root metadata URL\nonly on a 4xx:\n\n    function shouldAttemptFallback(response, pathname) {\n      return !response || (response.status >= 400 && response.status < 500\n                           && pathname !== ''/'');\n    }\n\nSo the guess \"succeeded\", OAuthProtectedResourceMetadataSchema.parse(await\nresponse.json()) was handed a page of HTML, and discovery ended there. With no\nmetadata the client cannot learn the authorization server, cannot register,\nand falls back to a hand-entered client id or its own account linking — which\nis what the account mismatch was.\n\nTwo fixes:\n\n  - A route at .well-known/oauth-protected-resource/[...resource] serving the\n    metadata for /api/v1/mcp and 404ing everything else, deliberately, so a\n    client can fall back instead of parsing a page.\n  - resource_metadata=<url> added to the 401''s WWW-Authenticate header\n    (RFC 9728 §5.3, required by the MCP authorization spec). This removes the\n    guess entirely: the client is told where the metadata is.\n\nThe issuer, resource path and metadata URL now come from one place —\nthree copies were what let the header and the route disagree.\n\nVerified against a production build served locally:\n  /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/v1/nonsense\n    -> 404 application/json   (was 200 text/html)\n  /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/v1/mcp\n    -> reaches the handler (500 only because this box has no DATABASE_URL)\n  /.well-known/openid-configuration\n    -> still 200 text/html, confirming the catch-all was the cause and that\n       this route is what changed the outcome\n\nBoth new tests fail with their fix removed.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <qiang@livepeer.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpshLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+jsQAGygoASmyhEM+4IsRMERb6/k\nhIVy9QHxG0TMo0Gv5hn4T2bNyn/ggN98GKxcDoNwbntx51jhEzLB897AHlKmm8mY\nip++6F3NzSEmV5mjVZmwiIKYgI1ZpdUzW1b+GRZ3gOoce/C6vkAfNb434bSXbxrM\nMqxoEpKQfQt/62Ql5foQq12UxuoZ56d4YUwkGAo2kg/CKerVfqTt3bSr35ZpcfL0\nbPG70Mju0b1zdsGy8YN+w4iq/IwdqDGfnf3eDWnhHPPOFHKLsZVnj02IOgBDaPs1\nJVux8Fnv+fayUDdPfgrd4m4Bnl6RtaWYu4kzP1a5W652TnT9oZU/jUJZaGBVS1V3\nH/IkgPKyHsJ7F6gotz0X4d2/6pPMTGdNA1yYNXxeCWrwF3SVTxN2nR5WT2t+R0w6\nTD/4ZLGZeGycdifLzqRF5oIEQZVh80gCaRo6oVuO7OIH5Jd23GDe/qgy592dDeTt\nj8HTOKxtVNJH/1z1fMF1HMY9OzhS3kBDOQ/ad/Xcn5gAKkL0SFaqwjN6A9KLg1+a\n4HNApxQN0Nkzoal9iPVWjWHXc+Q8bEOS3NYP/WydxkrbERcDWmS8vxOpBpBzZJ9E\n/M5wk3u6/5x0NyHxP3+2okkYVNxwu8VxAXwX1ThdDgdFYBb3D92/+OgxJVPK+q7T\n5MMxXqIP3RPNaXGYT8HQ\n=RKaA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T15:59:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/747199f5fcdbf5cc9972710e4058f54b474ae0ab","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDc0NzE5OWY1ZmNkYmY1Y2M5OTcyNzEwZTQwNThmNTRiNDc0YWUwYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/c6e4fe9888e7d20f6246e5a94f13df481a9fa79f","sha":"c6e4fe9888e7d20f6246e5a94f13df481a9fa79f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/c6e4fe9888e7d20f6246e5a94f13df481a9fa79f"}],"sha":"747199f5fcdbf5cc9972710e4058f54b474ae0ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/747199f5fcdbf5cc9972710e4058f54b474ae0ab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/c6e4fe9888e7d20f6246e5a94f13df481a9fa79f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:12:00Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:12:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mcp): support the refresh_token grant, so clients can register at all (#555)\n\nConnecting Claude failed at the first request with \"can''t register with\nAgentBook''s sign-in service\". Not a Claude problem: the OAuth server was\nrefusing the registration.\n\noidc-provider only adds refresh_token to its enabled grant types when either\n`offline_access` is in `scopes` or `issueRefreshToken` is overridden\n(helpers/configuration.js:173). We had neither, so:\n\n  - Dynamic Client Registration returned 400 invalid_client_metadata,\n    \"grant_types can only contain ''implicit'' or ''authorization_code''\", to\n    every client that asked for refresh_token. Gemini CLI asks for exactly\n    [''authorization_code'',''refresh_token'']\n    (@google/gemini-cli-core/dist/src/mcp/oauth-provider.js:39) and Claude\n    reports the same failure, so the connector could not be added at all.\n  - A client that registered without it got one hour of access and no way to\n    renew, so the connector died hourly.\n  - The discovery document advertised refresh_token support the whole time.\n  - ttl.RefreshToken was dead configuration.\n\nThe default issueRefreshToken additionally requires `offline_access` in the\ngranted scopes, which an MCP client asking for `agentbook:full` never sends —\ndelegating to it would have re-created the same silence one layer down. So the\noverride issues whenever the client registered for the grant.\n\nReproduced against production before the fix:\n  POST /api/v1/oauth/register {\"grant_types\":[\"authorization_code\",\"refresh_token\"]}\n  -> 400 invalid_client_metadata\n  POST /api/v1/oauth/register {\"grant_types\":[\"authorization_code\"]}\n  -> 201\n\nWhy this shipped: oauth-provider.test.ts mocks `oidc-provider` wholesale and\nasserts the config object we pass in. The defect was never in our object — it\nwas in what the library does with it. The new suite constructs the real\nprovider and drives a real registration request through it, and fails without\nthe fix.\n\nAlso corrects the AGENTBOOK_MCP_JWKS comment and warning. Unset does not mean\n\"ephemeral per-instance keys\"; oidc-provider falls back to the keystore it\nships in the package, a fixed private key published on npm and identical in\nevery install. The failure mode is forgery, not flakiness.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <qiang@livepeer.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0d494f4f7f91a7ede01faa0378104eb63a21dc70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/0d494f4f7f91a7ede01faa0378104eb63a21dc70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/c6e4fe9888e7d20f6246e5a94f13df481a9fa79f","verification":{"payload":"tree 0d494f4f7f91a7ede01faa0378104eb63a21dc70\nparent c4972ac31b1e26c02e4a85d100fc751b8fd81721\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1789312320 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789312320 -0700\n\nfix(mcp): support the refresh_token grant, so clients can register at all (#555)\n\nConnecting Claude failed at the first request with \"can''t register with\nAgentBook''s sign-in service\". Not a Claude problem: the OAuth server was\nrefusing the registration.\n\noidc-provider only adds refresh_token to its enabled grant types when either\n`offline_access` is in `scopes` or `issueRefreshToken` is overridden\n(helpers/configuration.js:173). We had neither, so:\n\n  - Dynamic Client Registration returned 400 invalid_client_metadata,\n    \"grant_types can only contain ''implicit'' or ''authorization_code''\", to\n    every client that asked for refresh_token. Gemini CLI asks for exactly\n    [''authorization_code'',''refresh_token'']\n    (@google/gemini-cli-core/dist/src/mcp/oauth-provider.js:39) and Claude\n    reports the same failure, so the connector could not be added at all.\n  - A client that registered without it got one hour of access and no way to\n    renew, so the connector died hourly.\n  - The discovery document advertised refresh_token support the whole time.\n  - ttl.RefreshToken was dead configuration.\n\nThe default issueRefreshToken additionally requires `offline_access` in the\ngranted scopes, which an MCP client asking for `agentbook:full` never sends —\ndelegating to it would have re-created the same silence one layer down. So the\noverride issues whenever the client registered for the grant.\n\nReproduced against production before the fix:\n  POST /api/v1/oauth/register {\"grant_types\":[\"authorization_code\",\"refresh_token\"]}\n  -> 400 invalid_client_metadata\n  POST /api/v1/oauth/register {\"grant_types\":[\"authorization_code\"]}\n  -> 201\n\nWhy this shipped: oauth-provider.test.ts mocks `oidc-provider` wholesale and\nasserts the config object we pass in. The defect was never in our object — it\nwas in what the library does with it. The new suite constructs the real\nprovider and drives a real registration request through it, and fails without\nthe fix.\n\nAlso corrects the AGENTBOOK_MCP_JWKS comment and warning. Unset does not mean\n\"ephemeral per-instance keys\"; oidc-provider falls back to the keystore it\nships in the package, a fixed private key published on npm and identical in\nevery install. The failure mode is forgery, not flakiness.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <qiang@livepeer.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpr1ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYX0QAAfvcJhE2Juz6PU29tAyPyjN\nUxvxiGpluAfFQ6a8zssCD+qJn20u1wThTmBLm8i/w/+LQqK0A6el3vDwp0FqgOB/\noetYFkk2R4XyRQzQjmM8RCfsgCFMA67qF8XPeryrFgW8m8E91u+LmIFb/g+FCljG\n5I3fYNvRmau60BHQBQrG9sMSHU4cPZGZq0gGDBOYPyvS1eA2GaaiBBVB4Ytb44ef\nKaAFWicnjPlkUMVtfrXH8XoSMdT8NqSz8LJP7cIwp2n0BzYOIXwkj4nLKIjiErld\nMQrItsenCWTYvbzGtpTpdbuCh+P7zi2FWFnTEc2AFr5dRLXQiFbilRt7rsRtevyx\nPlW7AmnaXTA6P6ADHsT/Nm1+XNQ/c8ncLqfNuTcnFTbs8dOGtIwbUCSBtR64Fh4h\nz3amoGzKUlwvv2xaoQx8N7FzpPmE2pV8GdUoTsS0ZwMck4f+YCpaAI92bKmQKh7a\nPmBvoUSBHRxgOQpAiFXRsEtbIMf5G6wsnLl+pA0KgSXr2DljiEeqTSfJHAJHinkP\nc2DZBzcfmU8oUpvS2iKvw5gSs58jHLeORNvpCJ8upTT49AuV5kS7b1F0mVrL2oDN\nttxO+8UAAzmmAA/H9UUuKmGvHTsoLqeLU2DvnjiYTNzD8GeWumg+zTpLtl8gjIu4\n2UdHmle8zqrr8SH1H6s8\n=RRT+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T15:12:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/c6e4fe9888e7d20f6246e5a94f13df481a9fa79f","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGM2ZTRmZTk4ODhlN2QyMGY2MjQ2ZTVhOTRmMTNkZjQ4MWE5ZmE3OWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/c4972ac31b1e26c02e4a85d100fc751b8fd81721","sha":"c4972ac31b1e26c02e4a85d100fc751b8fd81721","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/c4972ac31b1e26c02e4a85d100fc751b8fd81721"}],"sha":"c6e4fe9888e7d20f6246e5a94f13df481a9fa79f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/c6e4fe9888e7d20f6246e5a94f13df481a9fa79f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/c4972ac31b1e26c02e4a85d100fc751b8fd81721/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T23:42:28Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T23:42:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(uptime): add a drill switch, so the alert path can be proven (#553)\n\nThe probe and the incident lookup are verified on the runner. Opening an\nincident and closing it again never has been — it only runs when production\nis actually down, which is the worst moment to discover a typo in it. My own\nrunbook says an untested alert path is the same as no alert path.\n\n`workflow_dispatch` now takes a `drill` boolean. It skips the request and\nasserts a failure: curl is already proven by every scheduled run, and what a\ndrill exists to exercise is everything after it. Skipping the request also\nskips 40 seconds of retries.\n\nA drill uses the REAL incident title, deliberately. The point is the round\ntrip — the next scheduled run finds that open incident and closes it exactly\nas it would a real one, which is the half that would otherwise stay\nuntested. A blockquote at the top of the body is what tells a reader it is\nnot an outage, and the drill closes itself within five minutes.\n\nVerified both branches locally: drill=true short-circuits in 8ms with\nstatus 503, drill=false still probes and gets 200; the banner appears for a\ndrill and is absent from a real incident, with no placeholder left behind.\n\nThe banner first rendered as a literal backslash-n — three layers of\nescaping between this file, the shell heredoc and the Python string, and I\nhad one too many. Caught by looking at the rendered output rather than the\ndiff.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d5f14140be613c758cad51c1c6ff8911c974ad2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/1d5f14140be613c758cad51c1c6ff8911c974ad2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/c4972ac31b1e26c02e4a85d100fc751b8fd81721","verification":{"payload":"tree 1d5f14140be613c758cad51c1c6ff8911c974ad2\nparent 028ce2a51de2a011dd2f366de3e69204af2af984\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788997348 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788997348 -0700\n\nci(uptime): add a drill switch, so the alert path can be proven (#553)\n\nThe probe and the incident lookup are verified on the runner. Opening an\nincident and closing it again never has been — it only runs when production\nis actually down, which is the worst moment to discover a typo in it. My own\nrunbook says an untested alert path is the same as no alert path.\n\n`workflow_dispatch` now takes a `drill` boolean. It skips the request and\nasserts a failure: curl is already proven by every scheduled run, and what a\ndrill exists to exercise is everything after it. Skipping the request also\nskips 40 seconds of retries.\n\nA drill uses the REAL incident title, deliberately. The point is the round\ntrip — the next scheduled run finds that open incident and closes it exactly\nas it would a real one, which is the half that would otherwise stay\nuntested. A blockquote at the top of the body is what tells a reader it is\nnot an outage, and the drill closes itself within five minutes.\n\nVerified both branches locally: drill=true short-circuits in 8ms with\nstatus 503, drill=false still probes and gets 200; the banner appears for a\ndrill and is absent from a real incident, with no placeholder left behind.\n\nThe banner first rendered as a literal backslash-n — three layers of\nescaping between this file, the shell heredoc and the Python string, and I\nhad one too many. Caught by looking at the rendered output rather than the\ndiff.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoe7kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3GwQAB7mt3lUzSYueclvVkc9aJ91\nmYU4lCLyt4P3mUknTW8suEly3gVw2Dvh8s0AsatROPDH+da2TsfDHuRTYbDfAUaQ\nVYx5cpcveMm7hwsUd5kc+hTzYx+zNJBKBc/V3mmGHTdersl++YiQW4V0NXzq5y+Q\n0hM4ciOsK+5/83Np9EqkMXOMP9472jJaPctmyFOlwjfqZhVRe3KjXJxmU62yXqRl\nXUJnAD+ct5VBL1cbDycmr3grFFFMivw0JHWWudOjmCJJ95i5pvLJBvsv0wcwMDht\nmHxLPhqJXj97InxfjCGsU1mCc/M4Fquqs8Aw3W65PQPKq6yBman5fW9SKgKJupkg\n7dPEg9q/Szkozr+UjE8rtov8+usBiUEMiBGoE7QzQGGlv4iIrMZDmujqkOWWTSZ3\naLHe+dc3fiq5+vpe8R0UkyiEF2SkKr6wLIHyvXzSzDvn+HKKz4+olz3dsnRdSPcX\nsqMZhdESDW/FUxwfOKC7MXYzr1l2TaWHOdt4FlOivvOiiXU+xuH1mF8dNOCrMml6\n0xxrcxQIK1KtCua/5nqnwSIDpb9aQbEUqouNPClKOuX2a0YwfuJNh/Riae+r+loT\n/vwpf231ZTbZ0M34GDIY7s9QNlWSDa3cuf2tROihcxue9UT9Rh+OQStyJ7sPw1qy\nGIxluKXb//T4bjmE790h\n=eHos\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T23:42:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/c4972ac31b1e26c02e4a85d100fc751b8fd81721","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGM0OTcyYWMzMWIxZTI2YzAyZTRhODVkMTAwZmM3NTFiOGZkODE3MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/028ce2a51de2a011dd2f366de3e69204af2af984","sha":"028ce2a51de2a011dd2f366de3e69204af2af984","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/028ce2a51de2a011dd2f366de3e69204af2af984"}],"sha":"c4972ac31b1e26c02e4a85d100fc751b8fd81721","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/c4972ac31b1e26c02e4a85d100fc751b8fd81721"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/028ce2a51de2a011dd2f366de3e69204af2af984/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T23:09:51Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T23:09:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): give the uptime monitor a repo to talk to (#552)\n\nThe first real run failed on `gh issue list`:\n\n  failed to run git: fatal: not a git repository\n\ngh infers the repository from a git remote, and this job deliberately has\nno checkout — cloning the repo every five minutes to curl one URL would be\nabsurd. `GH_REPO` tells gh which repository without one.\n\nWorth naming how this got through. I tested the lookup locally, and I ran\nit inside a checkout, so gh found a remote and the command worked. The\nrunner has no checkout, which is the one thing about its environment that\nmattered and the one thing my test did not reproduce. Verified this time by\nrunning the command from a directory that is not a git repository: exit 1\nwith the runner''s exact error before, exit 0 after.\n\nThe failure was also loud rather than silent, which is the one piece of\nluck: `set -euo pipefail` turned it into a red run instead of an empty\nNUMBER, which would have read as \"no open incident\" and opened a duplicate\nissue on every tick of a real outage.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b16f52d02a49b49a9e8dc90751d3eac513a9b0cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/b16f52d02a49b49a9e8dc90751d3eac513a9b0cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/028ce2a51de2a011dd2f366de3e69204af2af984","verification":{"payload":"tree b16f52d02a49b49a9e8dc90751d3eac513a9b0cc\nparent dd7fcd712f335df50278977654817b2f1b8f4939\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788995391 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788995391 -0700\n\nfix(ci): give the uptime monitor a repo to talk to (#552)\n\nThe first real run failed on `gh issue list`:\n\n  failed to run git: fatal: not a git repository\n\ngh infers the repository from a git remote, and this job deliberately has\nno checkout — cloning the repo every five minutes to curl one URL would be\nabsurd. `GH_REPO` tells gh which repository without one.\n\nWorth naming how this got through. I tested the lookup locally, and I ran\nit inside a checkout, so gh found a remote and the command worked. The\nrunner has no checkout, which is the one thing about its environment that\nmattered and the one thing my test did not reproduce. Verified this time by\nrunning the command from a directory that is not a git repository: exit 1\nwith the runner''s exact error before, exit 0 after.\n\nThe failure was also loud rather than silent, which is the one piece of\nluck: `set -euo pipefail` turned it into a red run instead of an empty\nNUMBER, which would have read as \"no open incident\" and opened a duplicate\nissue on every tick of a real outage.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoec/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgi8QADGwVGYGAj7nr4zQo1jGkc4U\nh4qycNKowBX9GKcpIM6bgYm3D5wa3yxlkWq3FSC4R7BVoiTBl/kUnkM2K6KX53gp\naj84Lg+ttOIoSUW3wKugfxYy60kPo6dWDzUV62k7qdPO//G1nnv5Ig7gLXdKLM93\n4fPjVSRbqCk5qvibR32a1WfpyPQ9I5BRHcLQtdskOztObId8m1k8u6UIJRYq8fNP\n4Dn7pFUfnT2W9nrYyQJIVMq80NulX6twjbgGiLLrbkk8CsFOvUVsyYejlaqeiL9f\nKIyNLjTKeoZBjcJlGu4WS1vMuk/tKfE3aAo1c1EanqomqzbHtjYqjqHFTOO4cRzU\nLnuZotTUm/Bd+pUe7fafhwAt/sbBACGlZu7EVqx1cypcxli17pZbF14IzUD1m1YG\nLFzC1oUjsy5BssVjzdACRvlVzMVJZIry3e29rz11nbEAo/wHjpdbU3Y+zGKfbtSH\nsm8R2e5ryQ7un5aWm7ETekQ4ApjxwxqV6ln+GlEtQMlz90UWnHGQqWgFGVMvAhsa\nXJfMfadWXnOOZnOJcgRelT5VmeFRU9GAlV/v3CcU5X5nyrsbzeEvKW38i7V+EhLJ\najbvQnCY0n00Rk/VnyFvjA3jLmoUPRoOMSaPvMEBkQob/ViBerDLKZ/ZQ9FHLDx6\nTUNusVCPRIgEX8cZ6uS0\n=J2gd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T23:09:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/028ce2a51de2a011dd2f366de3e69204af2af984","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDAyOGNlMmE1MWRlMmEwMTFkZDJmMzY2ZGUzZTY5MjA0YWYyYWY5ODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/dd7fcd712f335df50278977654817b2f1b8f4939","sha":"dd7fcd712f335df50278977654817b2f1b8f4939","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/dd7fcd712f335df50278977654817b2f1b8f4939"}],"sha":"028ce2a51de2a011dd2f366de3e69204af2af984","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/028ce2a51de2a011dd2f366de3e69204af2af984"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/dd7fcd712f335df50278977654817b2f1b8f4939/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T23:02:17Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T23:02:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: probe production from outside the deployment (#551)\n\nAgentBook checks its own dependencies at /api/health/deep and cannot check\nits own uptime — if the app is gone so is the checker, and that silence\nlooks exactly like everything being fine. This is the outside observer.\n\nIt is not a replacement for a hosted checker, and the header says so: a\nscheduled workflow drifts well past its five-minute floor under load, and\nGitHub disables scheduled workflows on a repo with no commits for 60 days.\nA monitor that switched itself off is worse than none, because you believe\nyou have one.\n\nAlerts on CHANGE, not on state. A GitHub issue is the incident record: down\nwith no open incident opens one, up with an open incident closes it with\nhow long it was down. Six hours down is two notifications rather than\nseventy-two. The job succeeds either way — the issue is the alert, and a red\nrun beside it would be a second notification for one event, so a red run\nhere means the workflow itself broke.\n\nThree attempts before declaring down: one timed-out request during a cold\nstart or a deploy is not an outage, and the same debounce the in-app cron\nuses.\n\nThree things the response body could otherwise have done, all tested with a\nserver returning 503 and a deliberately hostile payload:\n\n  - a line reading `TEMPLATE_END` would have closed the heredoc early, so\n    the body is substituted after the delimiter scan rather than inside it;\n  - the same string through GITHUB_OUTPUT would have broken the output\n    parser, so the body never goes through outputs — steps in one job share\n    a filesystem;\n  - a stray ``` would have escaped the fenced block, so those are replaced.\n\n`$(...)` and backticks in the payload stayed literal and created no files.\n\nThe incident lookup uses gh''s own --jq rather than piping to the jq binary.\njq is not installed everywhere, and the failure mode is the worst kind: an\nempty result reads exactly like \"no open incident\", so a down site would\nopen a duplicate issue every five minutes. Found because jq is missing on\nthe machine this was written on and the lookup silently returned nothing.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee7ff11ad1c9edf5ae8114632e82bc71369acabf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/ee7ff11ad1c9edf5ae8114632e82bc71369acabf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/dd7fcd712f335df50278977654817b2f1b8f4939","verification":{"payload":"tree ee7ff11ad1c9edf5ae8114632e82bc71369acabf\nparent 1007eaaf70ed3e1be7d397811f017c7e5c215d05\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788994937 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788994937 -0700\n\nci: probe production from outside the deployment (#551)\n\nAgentBook checks its own dependencies at /api/health/deep and cannot check\nits own uptime — if the app is gone so is the checker, and that silence\nlooks exactly like everything being fine. This is the outside observer.\n\nIt is not a replacement for a hosted checker, and the header says so: a\nscheduled workflow drifts well past its five-minute floor under load, and\nGitHub disables scheduled workflows on a repo with no commits for 60 days.\nA monitor that switched itself off is worse than none, because you believe\nyou have one.\n\nAlerts on CHANGE, not on state. A GitHub issue is the incident record: down\nwith no open incident opens one, up with an open incident closes it with\nhow long it was down. Six hours down is two notifications rather than\nseventy-two. The job succeeds either way — the issue is the alert, and a red\nrun beside it would be a second notification for one event, so a red run\nhere means the workflow itself broke.\n\nThree attempts before declaring down: one timed-out request during a cold\nstart or a deploy is not an outage, and the same debounce the in-app cron\nuses.\n\nThree things the response body could otherwise have done, all tested with a\nserver returning 503 and a deliberately hostile payload:\n\n  - a line reading `TEMPLATE_END` would have closed the heredoc early, so\n    the body is substituted after the delimiter scan rather than inside it;\n  - the same string through GITHUB_OUTPUT would have broken the output\n    parser, so the body never goes through outputs — steps in one job share\n    a filesystem;\n  - a stray ``` would have escaped the fenced block, so those are replaced.\n\n`$(...)` and backticks in the payload stayed literal and created no files.\n\nThe incident lookup uses gh''s own --jq rather than piping to the jq binary.\njq is not installed everywhere, and the failure mode is the worst kind: an\nempty result reads exactly like \"no open incident\", so a down site would\nopen a duplicate issue every five minutes. Found because jq is missing on\nthe machine this was written on and the lookup silently returned nothing.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoeV5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7n4QAK7x/Y2l5bdGKbS1WXqv4iqH\nzmaJ6W5fFlpzPR9qWbtjskHMqGOrtBFThvmbjzuf7gsNWHkbx+bGexO4sVbb3pp3\nmSEMvaZIYHkT35TdiiWgbdnXH52Ej8D/eonTp15zH9X/k8LtNGDOAFsGGijFSdmK\nIW4XZvLXIdFxjDwX4Gbpcxq8toDqT9gk9xV2NhwrfgFN1TIQucJ95lQ7GsCkI6UL\nmgS8Fr/MkfQOvH4tfM6eR9PD1u6jlVrm2Y8yCF4Q4HYbSwhl7vT1rIB44rPpktuQ\n7TaK1vN3oThxTtgniclA9MblFvUeOLzKumkEvvyppJLbVoSXJnGVezqoZPbDjqSl\nYrYoZYORa7V2cVvFKu69Tum3wOi6UwH14RRUc22K202LvOkdK6kwMZi3bg474WHS\nMfEySRgaA+j1Nwh8U4koqH6p9/DEHj6CPUD9zmPEpNvo+j7pOdCW1byva74TBeHV\nZP+1c4b86QQv08JK0oadHp4o/GYAFk6rF0Tv2RLImngINRUfvHt+2rKiIRZ47Rgp\nalY9GDaNpcP4PGm0+d1uIl3h4HTJ8Q1yk54Wwehi+dFjnn80Gaq2HP25G6ypYLIv\n6JWVliUaTmpkuFLQ512VP2NDIu1uXy0mAf6kZdiDuJHsbBfHtg74IF8tvD73E+jK\nb7F2Lq+CJa+ZVnD8Si06\n=clOQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T23:02:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/dd7fcd712f335df50278977654817b2f1b8f4939","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGRkN2ZjZDcxMmYzMzVkZjUwMjc4OTc3NjU0ODE3YjJmMWI4ZjQ5Mzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/1007eaaf70ed3e1be7d397811f017c7e5c215d05","sha":"1007eaaf70ed3e1be7d397811f017c7e5c215d05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/1007eaaf70ed3e1be7d397811f017c7e5c215d05"}],"sha":"dd7fcd712f335df50278977654817b2f1b8f4939","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/dd7fcd712f335df50278977654817b2f1b8f4939"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/1007eaaf70ed3e1be7d397811f017c7e5c215d05/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:08:33Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:08:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): close nine of the fifteen open CodeQL alerts (#545)\n\n* fix(security): close nine of the fifteen open CodeQL alerts\n\nTriage, not mass-suppression. Each of these is either a real defect, or a\nfalse positive whose underlying shape was worth removing anyway — and where\nthe alert is technically wrong, the thing it points at usually still is not\nright.\n\nSTACK TRACE TO THE CALLER — real, and the most serious of the nine.\nagentbook-route-host returned `error.message` and eight lines of\n`error.stack` in every plugin route''s 500 body. That is the class #492 went\nthrough 266 handlers to remove; this one survived because the raw text is\nassembled in the host wrapper, not at a throw site, so a sweep over route\nfiles never touched it. A module-load stack here names paths inside the\ndeployment, the bundler layout, and — for the Prisma failure this wrapper\nexists to diagnose — the host and database it could not reach. The\ndiagnosis goes to the log now, where the person debugging can read it and\nthe person probing cannot.\n\nREGEX INJECTION — real, though admin-gated. Skill registration validated\ntrigger patterns by compiling them, which proves only that they are\nsyntactically valid. `(a+)+$` is valid, and these patterns are STORED and\nthen run against every message a user sends: one registration is a\npermanent denial of service on the chat path, set off by ordinary traffic.\n`assessUserRegex` in @naap/utils refuses it, and the check that does the\nwork is empirical — three probe lengths, growth compared — because whether\na pattern backtracks is a property of the automaton and not of its source\ntext. The probes end in a character the pattern cannot match: a SUCCEEDING\nmatch returns on the first path tried and proves nothing.\n\nAlso fixed the route''s own doc comment, which claimed it was open when the\nsecret is unset. The code fails closed; the comment would have read as\npermission to leave it that way.\n\nIMG SRC x4 — flagged as DOM XSS, and on that charge wrong: `javascript:` in\nan img src does not execute, and an SVG loaded through <img> is\nscript-disabled. Dismissing on that reasoning would defend the wrong thing.\nAn arbitrary string in src still buys a request the page makes on the\nviewer''s behalf to a host of somebody else''s choosing. safeImageSrc refuses\nit. Consolidating also found a bug: the settings page''s own helper allowed\nhttp/https only, so a blob: preview of an avatar the user had just picked\nfrom disk was silently dropped.\n\nINCOMPLETE SANITIZATION x2 — the chat adapter''s tag strip now runs to a\nfixed point (bounded), because a single pass leaves `<<b>b>` as `<b>`. The\noutput is text and there is no XSS today; the point is that it stops being\nharmless the day somebody renders it as HTML. The per-diem alias regex now\nescapes every metacharacter rather than only the dot.\n\nNot touched, and reported rather than fixed: the gateway alerts\n(tainted-format-string, prototype-pollution), the unreferenced\nseed-storj-connector script, missing-rate-limiting, loop-bound-injection,\nand one stack-trace-exposure that re-emits a body this module itself built\nfrom literals.\n\n* fix(security): rebuild the image URL instead of echoing the input\n\nThe first version validated and returned the input unchanged. CodeQL did\nnot believe it — a checked value flowing out is the same value flowing out,\nso the function was transparent to taint tracking and all four alerts came\nback at their new line numbers.\n\nIt is also a fair complaint. \"We looked at it and it seemed fine\" is a\nweaker claim than \"we parsed it and emitted only the parts we understood\".\nEvery branch now returns a string assembled from parsed components, so\nanything not modelled cannot survive the round trip. The visible\nconsequence is normalisation, which the tests now pin.\n\n* docs(security): write down the CodeQL dismissals and their reasoning\n\nA dismissal with no reasoning attached is indistinguishable from someone\nclearing a red badge. The API caps a dismissal comment at 280 characters,\nwhich is not enough to argue a case, so the argument lives here where it\ncan be reviewed and disagreed with — including the two alerts deliberately\nleft open and why.\n\n* refactor(security): validate at the boundary so dismissals survive\n\nTwo shape changes, each defensible on its own and each also stopping an\nalert treadmill.\n\nsafeImageSrc is applied where a value ENTERS the component rather than at\nthe <img> that reads it — one check per value instead of one per render\nsite. The second effect: the <img src={...}> lines stay byte-identical, so\nthe dismissals attached to them survive. Wrapping at the render site moved\nthose lines and CodeQL raised the same four findings as new alerts on every\npush, which turns a dismissal into a treadmill.\n\nassessRegexSafety takes an already-compiled RegExp; the compile stays at the\nskills/register call site CodeQL already reports. The first version moved it\ninto @naap/utils, which relocated the alert rather than removing it — same\nfinding, now in a shared package, reported as new, and no longer covered by\nanything. Relocating an alert is not fixing one.\n\nThe split is the better API regardless: the caller owns the compile because\nit owns the user-facing ''that is not a valid regular expression'' message,\nand the helper owns the question the caller cannot answer.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"07a30227a466c5a8a2245fb5de339d76a915e0fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/07a30227a466c5a8a2245fb5de339d76a915e0fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/1007eaaf70ed3e1be7d397811f017c7e5c215d05","verification":{"payload":"tree 07a30227a466c5a8a2245fb5de339d76a915e0fd\nparent 636b07184f2b090d27fe63f97aa8ee50b42799ae\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788991713 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788991713 -0700\n\nfix(security): close nine of the fifteen open CodeQL alerts (#545)\n\n* fix(security): close nine of the fifteen open CodeQL alerts\n\nTriage, not mass-suppression. Each of these is either a real defect, or a\nfalse positive whose underlying shape was worth removing anyway — and where\nthe alert is technically wrong, the thing it points at usually still is not\nright.\n\nSTACK TRACE TO THE CALLER — real, and the most serious of the nine.\nagentbook-route-host returned `error.message` and eight lines of\n`error.stack` in every plugin route''s 500 body. That is the class #492 went\nthrough 266 handlers to remove; this one survived because the raw text is\nassembled in the host wrapper, not at a throw site, so a sweep over route\nfiles never touched it. A module-load stack here names paths inside the\ndeployment, the bundler layout, and — for the Prisma failure this wrapper\nexists to diagnose — the host and database it could not reach. The\ndiagnosis goes to the log now, where the person debugging can read it and\nthe person probing cannot.\n\nREGEX INJECTION — real, though admin-gated. Skill registration validated\ntrigger patterns by compiling them, which proves only that they are\nsyntactically valid. `(a+)+$` is valid, and these patterns are STORED and\nthen run against every message a user sends: one registration is a\npermanent denial of service on the chat path, set off by ordinary traffic.\n`assessUserRegex` in @naap/utils refuses it, and the check that does the\nwork is empirical — three probe lengths, growth compared — because whether\na pattern backtracks is a property of the automaton and not of its source\ntext. The probes end in a character the pattern cannot match: a SUCCEEDING\nmatch returns on the first path tried and proves nothing.\n\nAlso fixed the route''s own doc comment, which claimed it was open when the\nsecret is unset. The code fails closed; the comment would have read as\npermission to leave it that way.\n\nIMG SRC x4 — flagged as DOM XSS, and on that charge wrong: `javascript:` in\nan img src does not execute, and an SVG loaded through <img> is\nscript-disabled. Dismissing on that reasoning would defend the wrong thing.\nAn arbitrary string in src still buys a request the page makes on the\nviewer''s behalf to a host of somebody else''s choosing. safeImageSrc refuses\nit. Consolidating also found a bug: the settings page''s own helper allowed\nhttp/https only, so a blob: preview of an avatar the user had just picked\nfrom disk was silently dropped.\n\nINCOMPLETE SANITIZATION x2 — the chat adapter''s tag strip now runs to a\nfixed point (bounded), because a single pass leaves `<<b>b>` as `<b>`. The\noutput is text and there is no XSS today; the point is that it stops being\nharmless the day somebody renders it as HTML. The per-diem alias regex now\nescapes every metacharacter rather than only the dot.\n\nNot touched, and reported rather than fixed: the gateway alerts\n(tainted-format-string, prototype-pollution), the unreferenced\nseed-storj-connector script, missing-rate-limiting, loop-bound-injection,\nand one stack-trace-exposure that re-emits a body this module itself built\nfrom literals.\n\n* fix(security): rebuild the image URL instead of echoing the input\n\nThe first version validated and returned the input unchanged. CodeQL did\nnot believe it — a checked value flowing out is the same value flowing out,\nso the function was transparent to taint tracking and all four alerts came\nback at their new line numbers.\n\nIt is also a fair complaint. \"We looked at it and it seemed fine\" is a\nweaker claim than \"we parsed it and emitted only the parts we understood\".\nEvery branch now returns a string assembled from parsed components, so\nanything not modelled cannot survive the round trip. The visible\nconsequence is normalisation, which the tests now pin.\n\n* docs(security): write down the CodeQL dismissals and their reasoning\n\nA dismissal with no reasoning attached is indistinguishable from someone\nclearing a red badge. The API caps a dismissal comment at 280 characters,\nwhich is not enough to argue a case, so the argument lives here where it\ncan be reviewed and disagreed with — including the two alerts deliberately\nleft open and why.\n\n* refactor(security): validate at the boundary so dismissals survive\n\nTwo shape changes, each defensible on its own and each also stopping an\nalert treadmill.\n\nsafeImageSrc is applied where a value ENTERS the component rather than at\nthe <img> that reads it — one check per value instead of one per render\nsite. The second effect: the <img src={...}> lines stay byte-identical, so\nthe dismissals attached to them survive. Wrapping at the render site moved\nthose lines and CodeQL raised the same four findings as new alerts on every\npush, which turns a dismissal into a treadmill.\n\nassessRegexSafety takes an already-compiled RegExp; the compile stays at the\nskills/register call site CodeQL already reports. The first version moved it\ninto @naap/utils, which relocated the alert rather than removing it — same\nfinding, now in a shared package, reported as new, and no longer covered by\nanything. Relocating an alert is not fixing one.\n\nThe split is the better API regardless: the caller owns the compile because\nit owns the user-facing ''that is not a valid regular expression'' message,\nand the helper owns the question the caller cannot answer.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqodjhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABL4QAK6gjkiN21HFZpdWBhb6+sLm\nbA5e28HVBWw/BoOSq21f0AO0Ttfxty6XW8DwGf2axDMFjDRy5O30TkAJU6d+4ngQ\nKbUP3T20eeNfGHQE6VabzacIR/x4qonvZu8Iwa50uCNuvEDMGtxiZJkDm05iCkel\nPv896Pbvtb+C/cPFm7pNWf2oTzJWvZoUCDjAGCBbb0ZU27WlJgi+RHPBbxpxiXU8\n9TIXs7XhacaKGMmaeyZwxfz5bPIB9MNY5mmNVmhGvaApNgkMCSkq6DWp9i2MreXT\nuOTVuhpDDCZ+Io2W6blej+T+rnfJF8KHWKrC4M3NMxMn+KoyULg9YxJ1CXZ10kTZ\n4TJMTF6IDjBt2ysZPtVtS5Y/MBvSMw3ACMJQ2vZHslOLBdXiaPqpwZkcQoA+T56k\nniUCCAOrT1wsbqRl7wL+VDwAQNoTuQ/+aubinyGmQnSd9Mk6OtnsF8/6YH34+/ik\nN/1epR0C11P/6bd2Vd+xvNCKoEzAIADd4Ptl92vLGFxX/5scyeBRVy25mTx3Q8MC\nIWlW9dUq7T+XZ7FgNL73J+RmQH7dcMNc0lt0orLAd//iRVgwUUp0QzCkH3qAMaF/\nd22yF1A9ygZCnuEY+0mBJKsMHRH/CldpMcZI90IVYUh8Q8B+jw4GaVAjItyLLlhI\n8XslFGihY0aoADNmRkqX\n=pIyv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T22:08:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/1007eaaf70ed3e1be7d397811f017c7e5c215d05","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDEwMDdlYWFmNzBlZDNlMWJlN2QzOTc4MTFmMDE3YzdlNWMyMTVkMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/636b07184f2b090d27fe63f97aa8ee50b42799ae","sha":"636b07184f2b090d27fe63f97aa8ee50b42799ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/636b07184f2b090d27fe63f97aa8ee50b42799ae"}],"sha":"1007eaaf70ed3e1be7d397811f017c7e5c215d05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/1007eaaf70ed3e1be7d397811f017c7e5c215d05"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/636b07184f2b090d27fe63f97aa8ee50b42799ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:25:03Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:25:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(i18n): ship one locale to the browser, fetch the others on demand (#550)\n\nA browser needs one language and was being sent three. After the server-only\nnamespaces came out, that was most of what remained: 43 kB gzipped on every\npage route, dead weight for every user by definition, since nobody reads the\nproduct in two languages at once.\n\n`en` stays static. It is needed synchronously and unconditionally —\n`translationEnabled` starts false, so the first paint is English even for a\ntenant stored as fr-CA — and it is the last link in every lookup chain, which\nis what makes a pack that has not arrived render real English instead of\ndotted keys. fr-CA and zh-CN become one chunk each, behind loadLocalePack().\n\n  /marketplace  216 -> 173 kB      /settings   286 -> 243 kB\n  /plugins/[..] 209 -> 166 kB      /[...slug]  204 -> 161 kB\n\n-43 kB on all 35 page routes, none worse, shared-by-all unchanged at 103 kB.\nWith the previous change that is 251 -> 173 kB for /marketplace. /settings''\nexception goes 315 -> 270; what is left is ~20 kB of English UI strings, the\nfloor for rendering text without a round trip.\n\nWHY A DYNAMIC IMPORT IS NOT THE THING catalog.ts''s HEADER FORBIDS\n\nThat header rules out dynamic loading because of runtime `fs` and `fetch` of\nassets at COMPUTED paths — the reliable road to \"works locally, 500s in prod\".\nEvery specifier here is a literal, so webpack resolves it at build time and\nemits a chunk beside all the others: no filesystem, no URL to get wrong. It is\nclient-only, where chunk loading is already how the app works; the server and\nthe RSC paths keep importing the full static CATALOG.\n\nEach locale is ONE pack module rather than 25 dynamic imports, because webpack\nemits a chunk per import() and changing language should not be 25 requests.\n\nTIMING, HONESTLY\n\nA non-`en` pack is only wanted once /tenant-config has resolved and the flag is\non — already an await, already causing a swap from English to the tenant''s\nlanguage. This rides that boundary rather than adding one, but it does add a\nround trip inside it: the swap now happens after the config AND the chunk.\n\n`ready` therefore means both halves now, and that exposed a race the existing\nhook test caught: `configRead` and `translationEnabled` are set in one batch,\nso a readiness flag maintained by an effect went true for one render with\nEnglish still in force. Readiness is derived during render instead, which\ncannot lag the state it depends on.\n\nFAILURE IS ENGLISH\n\nA rejected chunk (offline, CDN blip, hashes rotated mid-session) and a tenant\nrow holding a tag this build no longer serves both degrade to the static `en`\npack, and both still report ready — leaving it false would mean \"translation is\nloading\" for the rest of that session. Six hook tests pin those branches, plus\none for the common case: an English tenant issues no request and downloads no\nchunk.\n\nGUARDS\n\n`--shell` now asserts two different things about a non-English pack: absent\nfrom the eager payload, and PRESENT somewhere. Absence alone would pass just as\nhappily if the packs had been dropped and every non-English user silently\nswitched to English. The eager set is read from app-build-manifest.json rather\nthan guessed from filenames, since which chunks are REACHED is the whole\nquestion; the guard fails, rather than passes, if it cannot read it.\n\nThe architecture invariant that the client catalog holds the same locales as\nthe full one is replaced, not dropped: static plus loadable must still cover\nevery locale the build claims to serve, or a locale could be offered in the\npicker with nothing behind it.\n\nAlso fixes a defect found while writing this: the loader''s `finally` read\n`packs` from a closure captured before the merge, booking every success as a\nfailure. Readiness happened not to care, which is what would have hidden it.\n\nNote the repo-wide typecheck ratchet reports 286 against a baseline of 280 on\nthis branch. That is main''s, not this change''s — verified by restoring main''s\nversion of every file touched here and re-counting, which gives 286 either way.\nThe i18n surface is clean at 0.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d8f506d2e41373217177c15916f2bd935b68f72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/8d8f506d2e41373217177c15916f2bd935b68f72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/636b07184f2b090d27fe63f97aa8ee50b42799ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d8f506d2e41373217177c15916f2bd935b68f72\nparent ceab79399c17c6a402afa09f6b0869e061d0003e\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788985503 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788985503 -0700\n\nperf(i18n): ship one locale to the browser, fetch the others on demand (#550)\n\nA browser needs one language and was being sent three. After the server-only\nnamespaces came out, that was most of what remained: 43 kB gzipped on every\npage route, dead weight for every user by definition, since nobody reads the\nproduct in two languages at once.\n\n`en` stays static. It is needed synchronously and unconditionally —\n`translationEnabled` starts false, so the first paint is English even for a\ntenant stored as fr-CA — and it is the last link in every lookup chain, which\nis what makes a pack that has not arrived render real English instead of\ndotted keys. fr-CA and zh-CN become one chunk each, behind loadLocalePack().\n\n  /marketplace  216 -> 173 kB      /settings   286 -> 243 kB\n  /plugins/[..] 209 -> 166 kB      /[...slug]  204 -> 161 kB\n\n-43 kB on all 35 page routes, none worse, shared-by-all unchanged at 103 kB.\nWith the previous change that is 251 -> 173 kB for /marketplace. /settings''\nexception goes 315 -> 270; what is left is ~20 kB of English UI strings, the\nfloor for rendering text without a round trip.\n\nWHY A DYNAMIC IMPORT IS NOT THE THING catalog.ts''s HEADER FORBIDS\n\nThat header rules out dynamic loading because of runtime `fs` and `fetch` of\nassets at COMPUTED paths — the reliable road to \"works locally, 500s in prod\".\nEvery specifier here is a literal, so webpack resolves it at build time and\nemits a chunk beside all the others: no filesystem, no URL to get wrong. It is\nclient-only, where chunk loading is already how the app works; the server and\nthe RSC paths keep importing the full static CATALOG.\n\nEach locale is ONE pack module rather than 25 dynamic imports, because webpack\nemits a chunk per import() and changing language should not be 25 requests.\n\nTIMING, HONESTLY\n\nA non-`en` pack is only wanted once /tenant-config has resolved and the flag is\non — already an await, already causing a swap from English to the tenant''s\nlanguage. This rides that boundary rather than adding one, but it does add a\nround trip inside it: the swap now happens after the config AND the chunk.\n\n`ready` therefore means both halves now, and that exposed a race the existing\nhook test caught: `configRead` and `translationEnabled` are set in one batch,\nso a readiness flag maintained by an effect went true for one render with\nEnglish still in force. Readiness is derived during render instead, which\ncannot lag the state it depends on.\n\nFAILURE IS ENGLISH\n\nA rejected chunk (offline, CDN blip, hashes rotated mid-session) and a tenant\nrow holding a tag this build no longer serves both degrade to the static `en`\npack, and both still report ready — leaving it false would mean \"translation is\nloading\" for the rest of that session. Six hook tests pin those branches, plus\none for the common case: an English tenant issues no request and downloads no\nchunk.\n\nGUARDS\n\n`--shell` now asserts two different things about a non-English pack: absent\nfrom the eager payload, and PRESENT somewhere. Absence alone would pass just as\nhappily if the packs had been dropped and every non-English user silently\nswitched to English. The eager set is read from app-build-manifest.json rather\nthan guessed from filenames, since which chunks are REACHED is the whole\nquestion; the guard fails, rather than passes, if it cannot read it.\n\nThe architecture invariant that the client catalog holds the same locales as\nthe full one is replaced, not dropped: static plus loadable must still cover\nevery locale the build claims to serve, or a locale could be offered in the\npicker with nothing behind it.\n\nAlso fixes a defect found while writing this: the loader''s `finally` read\n`packs` from a closure captured before the merge, booking every success as a\nfailure. Readiness happened not to care, which is what would have hidden it.\n\nNote the repo-wide typecheck ratchet reports 286 against a baseline of 280 on\nthis branch. That is main''s, not this change''s — verified by restoring main''s\nversion of every file touched here and re-counting, which gives 286 either way.\nThe i18n surface is clean at 0.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqocCfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaKAQAGMzEC/Dg/qK/BuUA5FEkc60\n2mwd+A2l2j6Urx7V1xywjqFDpMlPJnfKuwhAUIDkvu3eJVTdk9SGmenz7bBvftNL\nGqqOHYchgIcHIdFlQuV1Euetjhq05o5qnbr8GHY5hcuztqkJroS7Oh1sc26eny+y\nRrmaBM0QI7dJGDGKtzEQKueb/yvhBFC0G5ZBEre4HB1M9melR/F38WgaY9vLqWJL\n5bU63RFtdDMMTEn6YgPpYTNfw1agWgA2djWDboUTa+/l5MnWlBmw64l6SAwLxoVj\ncRjduxVMqtXziukoT2taleMbfA1DTqCmPr9HPGZe8T05Dc/88TxELTul/EBoISiu\nVmqe1zn/nvPsMdkYTPptw8CFObp0dqhrkavFVGnWBZfJZfX/IJnaRwPNo/DPgutK\nh+38gsBoiQvdzq9BUYWFRYbPuIOhsGFkd87H8Ps9kjfyRx6PnxfiL5U7smULKF7w\nHYvD65LSFU6+4YTh2zNzhVckgxJv8OZH93O25GIAXOIa6Qx3p6TTasw5rgJjSm0Z\ncTy/GAhWxm+FtsnMsSSorRZI2cNxDFXqoLXBuYdFIW+2ppZ9CpeqH+zCnhtrDBVZ\n9z8SYmx8R0Jdq/PW8f9N17vvOlpRxJ2CacQNOsExpi1ZZ22k4fhJsbEe1anBNYlD\neVV/1Tn0L7Uh9GW8Bg5I\n=GJJA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T20:25:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/636b07184f2b090d27fe63f97aa8ee50b42799ae","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDYzNmIwNzE4NGYyYjA5MGQyN2ZlNjNmOTdhYThlZTUwYjQyNzk5YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/ceab79399c17c6a402afa09f6b0869e061d0003e","sha":"ceab79399c17c6a402afa09f6b0869e061d0003e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ceab79399c17c6a402afa09f6b0869e061d0003e"}],"sha":"636b07184f2b090d27fe63f97aa8ee50b42799ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/636b07184f2b090d27fe63f97aa8ee50b42799ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ceab79399c17c6a402afa09f6b0869e061d0003e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:20:08Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:20:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): bound the CSV row parse and rebuild the auth error response (#549)\n\nThe last two CodeQL alerts I said needed examining rather than dismissing.\n\nLOOP BOUND INJECTION — parseCSVRow walked `line.length` on an uploaded CSV.\nThe parse is linear and advances monotonically, so a long line costs time\nproportional to its own length and nothing worse; the query overstates it.\nBut \"proportional to the input\" stops being reassuring when the input is an\nuploaded file — a single 4 MB line is a 4 MB string assembled one character\nat a time, and no bank export has produced one. Capped at 64 KB and 512\nfields, by constants, and truncating rather than throwing: a malformed row\nmust not fail an import of two thousand good ones.\n\nThe trailing push after the loop made the field cap off by one, which is the\nkind of nearly-bounded that leaves a limit untestable. Fixed, and the test\nasserts the exact ceiling.\n\nSTACK TRACE EXPOSURE — safeResolveAgentbookTenant re-emitted the body of a\nResponse it had itself thrown. That was safe: every throw site in the module\nbuilds the body from a string literal. CodeQL cannot see that, and it has a\npoint about the pattern rather than the instance — a future throw site\ninterpolating an exception into that body would start leaking with no\nvisible change at the re-wrap.\n\nThe rewrap is now its own exported function that rebuilds the response from\na known shape, which is also what makes the property testable: a body piped\nstraight through has nothing to assert on. Real auth messages still reach\nthe caller; anything else becomes ''unauthorized'' with the status preserved.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4233929bd52f13b4a87294db6e9d5db9f171e794","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/4233929bd52f13b4a87294db6e9d5db9f171e794"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/ceab79399c17c6a402afa09f6b0869e061d0003e","verification":{"payload":"tree 4233929bd52f13b4a87294db6e9d5db9f171e794\nparent ec55fb69349d15c52371225a661cb6627dac37fe\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788985208 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788985208 -0700\n\nfix(security): bound the CSV row parse and rebuild the auth error response (#549)\n\nThe last two CodeQL alerts I said needed examining rather than dismissing.\n\nLOOP BOUND INJECTION — parseCSVRow walked `line.length` on an uploaded CSV.\nThe parse is linear and advances monotonically, so a long line costs time\nproportional to its own length and nothing worse; the query overstates it.\nBut \"proportional to the input\" stops being reassuring when the input is an\nuploaded file — a single 4 MB line is a 4 MB string assembled one character\nat a time, and no bank export has produced one. Capped at 64 KB and 512\nfields, by constants, and truncating rather than throwing: a malformed row\nmust not fail an import of two thousand good ones.\n\nThe trailing push after the loop made the field cap off by one, which is the\nkind of nearly-bounded that leaves a limit untestable. Fixed, and the test\nasserts the exact ceiling.\n\nSTACK TRACE EXPOSURE — safeResolveAgentbookTenant re-emitted the body of a\nResponse it had itself thrown. That was safe: every throw site in the module\nbuilds the body from a string literal. CodeQL cannot see that, and it has a\npoint about the pattern rather than the instance — a future throw site\ninterpolating an exception into that body would start leaking with no\nvisible change at the re-wrap.\n\nThe rewrap is now its own exported function that rebuilds the response from\na known shape, which is also what makes the property testable: a body piped\nstraight through has nothing to assert on. Real auth messages still reach\nthe caller; anything else becomes ''unauthorized'' with the status preserved.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqob94CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYLIQAJz5lHXegzmjcGF737DUoyuW\n84IBBnfF73xOL96z3ot9POW57m23dvoH+kfIWyCc0kdqiqVNZWIwC2i6wtu0Xz/8\n0YcQ/IiM+G5PPQ+ZFWie/AMK654tOqRIsjdsLjQ2zbQO4YSCs0WkGxdYB7uBVDF+\n2H4XwU9I/3+5oqhhXCHwGL5phIrun+zwWClDtfrjbZZA6i9lBG/RwOJjep+XHBUe\n8qLWbXOFuZDYCuGpi8TURIBJbTYOb5xOAOcyVW0xODezPiM8WqD3exTiqW0Rlvwl\n3PIQ0XFceMWWbm3TQ8sb6joapOM6tAX46ND4VKjG9AYzfQi/oVY9efmbfT7jiaKh\nq06n1mFj6dVc2OO3x3094qUmgpRu/fhPOpG/QY3/9BuTc2SftiXjAAFo85ZRnc3n\nolxtfWOeBuSpRO16WJhxH7Lslyyb3S4iQiixhFfnq7u+9MTf9IOIr7Ju3hy/1J3Z\noPskE7BwfBvKc7prh65jV8ni67pZKt3ndxTcm1laMILQgSySrmMOOtOSmpmW/uye\nfpBI4IOzymqK65CCbawwL8AvU1HhOWxWz/pdnXubiMHtWy8bhUVtYR9zGQ93wbCS\nnMW6DJiaKRH2aX/reGZCvRaBX7VyUqDzGnKSCZnbv8i8X1g8a4rDDD2Pslr/Atcq\nw2OSv7kAuX5yfxOglKRH\n=WKWx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T20:20:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/ceab79399c17c6a402afa09f6b0869e061d0003e","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGNlYWI3OTM5OWMxN2M2YTQwMmFmYTA5ZjZiMDg2OWUwNjFkMDAwM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/ec55fb69349d15c52371225a661cb6627dac37fe","sha":"ec55fb69349d15c52371225a661cb6627dac37fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ec55fb69349d15c52371225a661cb6627dac37fe"}],"sha":"ceab79399c17c6a402afa09f6b0869e061d0003e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ceab79399c17c6a402afa09f6b0869e061d0003e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ec55fb69349d15c52371225a661cb6627dac37fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:08:50Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T20:08:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: delete the inherited NaaP service gateway (#547)\n\n`/api/v1/gw` was 25 live routes and `lib/gateway` 69 files implementing a\nthird-party service-connector proxy: register an upstream, publish it, and\nhave the platform forward authenticated requests to it. AgentBook publishes\nno connectors and no part of the product calls it. It came with the fork.\n\nIt was not free to keep. It carried three open CodeQL alerts nobody was\ngoing to fix, 50 of the repo''s pre-existing TypeScript errors, and a\n5-minute cron probing the upstreams of a connector table that is empty —\none of only two crons on the whole deployment running that often.\n\nAlso removed, all of it referring to code deleted here: four seed scripts,\ntwo tutorials, the ssh-bridge deploy action and the five example CD\nworkflows that used it (in .github/workflows/examples, so never executed).\n\nKept, deliberately:\n\n  `isPrivateHost` moved out of gateway/types.ts in #515 and stays — the\n  receipt fetcher, the dashboard connectivity test and the plugin backends\n  all still need it. Its comment explaining where it came from now says\n  that place no longer exists.\n\n  The ServiceConnector and ConnectorEndpoint Prisma models. Removing a model\n  from the schema means the next deploy''s `prisma db push --accept-data-loss`\n  DROPS the table, and I cannot see whether production holds rows. Dropping\n  them is a separate, deliberate step with a backup in front of it, not a\n  side effect of deleting some routes.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c2042c1ee2debb2509cccbdfb3219df46ac0e863","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/c2042c1ee2debb2509cccbdfb3219df46ac0e863"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/ec55fb69349d15c52371225a661cb6627dac37fe","verification":{"payload":"tree c2042c1ee2debb2509cccbdfb3219df46ac0e863\nparent 5fd07b8c4451225fa1a9d34d2478f98c9b1794a0\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788984530 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788984530 -0700\n\nchore: delete the inherited NaaP service gateway (#547)\n\n`/api/v1/gw` was 25 live routes and `lib/gateway` 69 files implementing a\nthird-party service-connector proxy: register an upstream, publish it, and\nhave the platform forward authenticated requests to it. AgentBook publishes\nno connectors and no part of the product calls it. It came with the fork.\n\nIt was not free to keep. It carried three open CodeQL alerts nobody was\ngoing to fix, 50 of the repo''s pre-existing TypeScript errors, and a\n5-minute cron probing the upstreams of a connector table that is empty —\none of only two crons on the whole deployment running that often.\n\nAlso removed, all of it referring to code deleted here: four seed scripts,\ntwo tutorials, the ssh-bridge deploy action and the five example CD\nworkflows that used it (in .github/workflows/examples, so never executed).\n\nKept, deliberately:\n\n  `isPrivateHost` moved out of gateway/types.ts in #515 and stays — the\n  receipt fetcher, the dashboard connectivity test and the plugin backends\n  all still need it. Its comment explaining where it came from now says\n  that place no longer exists.\n\n  The ServiceConnector and ConnectorEndpoint Prisma models. Removing a model\n  from the schema means the next deploy''s `prisma db push --accept-data-loss`\n  DROPS the table, and I cannot see whether production holds rows. Dropping\n  them is a separate, deliberate step with a backup in front of it, not a\n  side effect of deleting some routes.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqobzSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmV8QAHRe1v5kHV42dGyZc48CWrZy\n1jMMO8KvEzvgNonrnTJuzt0Q78W66cvJHgJ9qZHuxBkdNiWiUJY72eaPmzNEL3ht\nStmWjCeeq2vOju4G+mpdS3VMkFCYi2TICSYevDmitnm70ydzReOLzOF9UxckgWsK\n273upHbaswKl/9JfAI8r2lYgE8kRvuWYEX8RTt6kRuo/0JHbLXvC+h0lHPLKDE/+\nd4/1hSr39ubTiRWJ5+FQeSJE2HNSz9rlyl4NJs7KOVPVphpSAaIuUf1i3yyJz2eQ\n5NiymtijOvTPq/CzLyJQgWoU9zANlQmc+7+s0t7w5wC9ZBnUexBVukhRucYZ3elJ\nynBL9EheQq+QPsN8BmNaYOINlzHON8Gv1REMeLKr2CDZfb5aREDuW6AvFk1lrdZS\nEAHnTZPri7Sxy