b.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/5fd07b8c4451225fa1a9d34d2478f98c9b1794a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T19:58:14Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T19:58:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(tax): round per-form completeness percentage in chat messages (#544)\n\nfix(tax): round per-form completeness percentage in chat messages\n\nform.completeness is a 0-1 ratio (filled/total), but two message\nformatters (tax-filing-start and the tax-filing-status response\nshape) interpolated it directly with a \"%\" suffix and compared it\nagainst 100/50 as if already scaled — showing raw floats like\n\"0.13636363636363635% complete\" in prod and leaving the status icon\nstuck on red regardless of actual progress.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4da44daf3861ba671402211e48ee7a4967915517","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/4da44daf3861ba671402211e48ee7a4967915517"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/5fd07b8c4451225fa1a9d34d2478f98c9b1794a0","verification":{"payload":"tree 4da44daf3861ba671402211e48ee7a4967915517\nparent 0c5301041ca40f1b0841f1aae9142c01081084db\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788983894 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788983894 -0700\n\nfix(tax): round per-form completeness percentage in chat messages (#544)\n\nfix(tax): round per-form completeness percentage in chat messages\n\nform.completeness is a 0-1 ratio (filled/total), but two message\nformatters (tax-filing-start and the tax-filing-status response\nshape) interpolated it directly with a \"%\" suffix and compared it\nagainst 100/50 as if already scaled — showing raw floats like\n\"0.13636363636363635% complete\" in prod and leaving the status icon\nstuck on red regardless of actual progress.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqobpWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASKgQAC65D9fWRnrtgq3AUA3tO8fx\npZgqvIEPA3Pn+1doXAjecaK73YtaLO48lIniWtl+BPmvXtR9AzQacEvEfFpAn/Ym\nMXK54vtUIzfAqTyF7651YgmMUneJ6TFbfiehBk/vKlRMAZezXvVnJFeM+seroJG/\noKMxDEH8z3DlGfQUKOpm+32chsgZBQEzTO5xl3+qrnZqJEnDSDwvvunxivhlWhy0\nTvvOln18aJPc81RR3b6Uf+egVOa51auwQ3h61qCWkDmFRK7bIG+g8IsRPhDaK57Y\nTFcZkAOc+wQuqbN711cSK5cutOuW7qlmuDvbevUbktUSS7q0Qn4rcJ8iTMVmNmfo\nUEr2gAMIKIfH65u7IGEW+dGRi3B/xjHczhcsh9f575RVEM14KHEqORvLPr7G9CpA\nl25OVGLtFzfJsKACvGvlRHtorRrviy5UlvFb6cNRT1OOn+Pr5gnnzR1iCnjjXkMW\nOE5AbZIQ0RPQxhuIezlfXgZgAvfWcsMPGTArIDGZ85qrDrP7WTFX1qaDdDcRw26y\nuyOv2PKq97eYevyt3PiLzyUv0N79ltI2VqAzn6xNY+u4GM0N1LHTCqj3nSVEr+Zi\nehCZ0Oc6QDfb75PK5HE1KRZHPmjPuNrARqXhqNdmO3yolyIB8oCjIi4g5sNOCpmb\nSrduN88gnq9tT1OCa8o2\n=vI8C\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T19:58:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/5fd07b8c4451225fa1a9d34d2478f98c9b1794a0","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDVmZDA3YjhjNDQ1MTIyNWZhMWE5ZDM0ZDI0NzhmOThjOWIxNzk0YTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/0c5301041ca40f1b0841f1aae9142c01081084db","sha":"0c5301041ca40f1b0841f1aae9142c01081084db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/0c5301041ca40f1b0841f1aae9142c01081084db"}],"sha":"5fd07b8c4451225fa1a9d34d2478f98c9b1794a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/5fd07b8c4451225fa1a9d34d2478f98c9b1794a0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/0c5301041ca40f1b0841f1aae9142c01081084db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T19:57:53Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T19:57:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(i18n): stop shipping the server-only translation packs to the browser (#546)\n\n* perf(i18n): stop shipping the server-only translation packs to the browser\n\nThe catalog is one frozen object holding all three locale packs, and nothing\ntree-shakes it — a default-imported JSON module is one opaque value, and\nCATALOG[locale] plus readKey()''s dotted lookup are dynamic property access, so\nno bundler can prove any part unreachable. Measured directly: a bundle that\nimports createTranslator and CATALOG to resolve ONE key is 96.7 kB gzipped,\nagainst 728 bytes for the same bundle with an inline catalog. en/bot.json —\n25 kB of Telegram copy — is present in full for the sake of nav.expenses.\n\nIt reaches the browser through ShellProvider, which the root layout renders, so\nit is in the First Load JS of every page route. That is why eight keys written\nfor a Settings control pushed /marketplace over its budget, and why shortening\nthe copy to fit was addressing the wrong thing.\n\nFour namespaces are reached only from the server: bot (76.6 kB raw across three\nlocales, the webhook''s reply copy), skill, proactive and rate. They now live\nbehind ''@agentbook/i18n/catalog'' while client code imports\n''@agentbook/i18n/catalog-client'', which leaves them out.\n\n  /marketplace           250 -> 215 kB      /settings   320 -> 286 kB\n  /plugins/[pluginName]  242 -> 208 kB      /[...slug]  238 -> 203 kB\n\n-34 to -35 kB on all 35 page routes, no route worse, shared-by-all unchanged\nat 103 kB. /marketplace has 35 kB of headroom under the default again, and\n/settings'' exception drops 340 -> 315 rather than banking the saving as slack.\n\nWHAT THIS IS NOT\n\nNot a per-route split. Routes do not import the catalog — ShellProvider does,\nonce — so there is no route-level import to make selective; and the namespaces\nneeded at runtime are not statically knowable, because plugin frontends are UMD\nbundles injected by lib/plugins/umd-loader.ts, outside webpack entirely, which\nresolve keys through the shell''s injected t(). Which plugins mount is tenant\ndata. Namespaces no client code references at all are the decidable part, and\nthat is what this splits on.\n\nTHE TRAP, since it cost a day\n\nAnything DERIVED from CATALOG retains all of it. AVAILABLE_LOCALES was\nObject.keys(CATALOG), so the language switcher and the settings panel — which\nwanted nothing but a list of three language names — each pulled in 97 kB. The\nfirst attempt at this split cut 108 kB of raw JSON out and every route got\n3-4 kB BIGGER, because one such import was left behind and the build carried\nboth catalogs. So the locale list and readiness move to locale-meta.ts, which\nholds no packs, and the no-drift guarantee that motivated deriving them moves\nfrom DERIVED to ASSERTED: LOCALE_TAGS is declared and a test fails if it stops\nmatching Object.keys(CATALOG).\n\nGUARDS\n\nDropping a namespace the client does need is silent — useT() humanises the key,\nso core_ui.gst_help_unknown would render as \"Gst help unknown\". So the subset is\nnot a reviewed list: i18n-client-catalog.test.ts recomputes which namespaces\nclient source actually resolves keys from and fails if the client catalog omits\nany, and asserts every namespace is in exactly one of the two lists.\n\nbin/i18n-bundle-guard.sh gains --shell, which greps the built chunks for a\nmarker from each server-only namespace — the source-level check is what got\nfooled above. It runs in the build job, which Quality Gates aggregates, and\nfails rather than passes when the chunk directory is missing or incomplete.\nBoth guards were mutation-checked in both directions.\n\nThe full CATALOG export is unchanged, so createTranslator, the RSC paths and\nall five existing i18n architecture tests are untouched. Static imports\nthroughout: no runtime fs, no fetch, same behaviour in serverless.\n\nThe remaining lever is the locale axis — a browser needs one locale and ships\nthree, worth another ~42 kB measured — which needs lazy loading and is not\nattempted here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(i18n): leave the typecheck baseline where main has it\n\nMy earlier --update lowered it 280 -> 279 against the previous main, where this\nchange did remove one error. On current main the repo-wide count is 286 either\nway — verified by putting main''s version of every touched file back and\nre-counting — so this change now moves the number by zero and has no business\nrestating it.\n\nNot raised to 286 either. Those 7 errors arrived with other commits, and\nabsorbing them here would make this PR the thing that authorized them. Worth\nknowing separately: bin/i18n-typecheck-guard.sh is not referenced by any\nworkflow, so nothing has been enforcing this ratchet and main is 6 over it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cce903be48908de8082817aa645d3f3fc29fc409","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/cce903be48908de8082817aa645d3f3fc29fc409"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/0c5301041ca40f1b0841f1aae9142c01081084db","verification":{"payload":"tree cce903be48908de8082817aa645d3f3fc29fc409\nparent e8d225c83884a55f1197fcb1ca45df6df5ebd0e1\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788983873 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788983873 -0700\n\nperf(i18n): stop shipping the server-only translation packs to the browser (#546)\n\n* perf(i18n): stop shipping the server-only translation packs to the browser\n\nThe catalog is one frozen object holding all three locale packs, and nothing\ntree-shakes it — a default-imported JSON module is one opaque value, and\nCATALOG[locale] plus readKey()''s dotted lookup are dynamic property access, so\nno bundler can prove any part unreachable. Measured directly: a bundle that\nimports createTranslator and CATALOG to resolve ONE key is 96.7 kB gzipped,\nagainst 728 bytes for the same bundle with an inline catalog. en/bot.json —\n25 kB of Telegram copy — is present in full for the sake of nav.expenses.\n\nIt reaches the browser through ShellProvider, which the root layout renders, so\nit is in the First Load JS of every page route. That is why eight keys written\nfor a Settings control pushed /marketplace over its budget, and why shortening\nthe copy to fit was addressing the wrong thing.\n\nFour namespaces are reached only from the server: bot (76.6 kB raw across three\nlocales, the webhook''s reply copy), skill, proactive and rate. They now live\nbehind ''@agentbook/i18n/catalog'' while client code imports\n''@agentbook/i18n/catalog-client'', which leaves them out.\n\n  /marketplace           250 -> 215 kB      /settings   320 -> 286 kB\n  /plugins/[pluginName]  242 -> 208 kB      /[...slug]  238 -> 203 kB\n\n-34 to -35 kB on all 35 page routes, no route worse, shared-by-all unchanged\nat 103 kB. /marketplace has 35 kB of headroom under the default again, and\n/settings'' exception drops 340 -> 315 rather than banking the saving as slack.\n\nWHAT THIS IS NOT\n\nNot a per-route split. Routes do not import the catalog — ShellProvider does,\nonce — so there is no route-level import to make selective; and the namespaces\nneeded at runtime are not statically knowable, because plugin frontends are UMD\nbundles injected by lib/plugins/umd-loader.ts, outside webpack entirely, which\nresolve keys through the shell''s injected t(). Which plugins mount is tenant\ndata. Namespaces no client code references at all are the decidable part, and\nthat is what this splits on.\n\nTHE TRAP, since it cost a day\n\nAnything DERIVED from CATALOG retains all of it. AVAILABLE_LOCALES was\nObject.keys(CATALOG), so the language switcher and the settings panel — which\nwanted nothing but a list of three language names — each pulled in 97 kB. The\nfirst attempt at this split cut 108 kB of raw JSON out and every route got\n3-4 kB BIGGER, because one such import was left behind and the build carried\nboth catalogs. So the locale list and readiness move to locale-meta.ts, which\nholds no packs, and the no-drift guarantee that motivated deriving them moves\nfrom DERIVED to ASSERTED: LOCALE_TAGS is declared and a test fails if it stops\nmatching Object.keys(CATALOG).\n\nGUARDS\n\nDropping a namespace the client does need is silent — useT() humanises the key,\nso core_ui.gst_help_unknown would render as \"Gst help unknown\". So the subset is\nnot a reviewed list: i18n-client-catalog.test.ts recomputes which namespaces\nclient source actually resolves keys from and fails if the client catalog omits\nany, and asserts every namespace is in exactly one of the two lists.\n\nbin/i18n-bundle-guard.sh gains --shell, which greps the built chunks for a\nmarker from each server-only namespace — the source-level check is what got\nfooled above. It runs in the build job, which Quality Gates aggregates, and\nfails rather than passes when the chunk directory is missing or incomplete.\nBoth guards were mutation-checked in both directions.\n\nThe full CATALOG export is unchanged, so createTranslator, the RSC paths and\nall five existing i18n architecture tests are untouched. Static imports\nthroughout: no runtime fs, no fetch, same behaviour in serverless.\n\nThe remaining lever is the locale axis — a browser needs one locale and ships\nthree, worth another ~42 kB measured — which needs lazy loading and is not\nattempted here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(i18n): leave the typecheck baseline where main has it\n\nMy earlier --update lowered it 280 -> 279 against the previous main, where this\nchange did remove one error. On current main the repo-wide count is 286 either\nway — verified by putting main''s version of every touched file back and\nre-counting — so this change now moves the number by zero and has no business\nrestating it.\n\nNot raised to 286 either. Those 7 errors arrived with other commits, and\nabsorbing them here would make this PR the thing that authorized them. Worth\nknowing separately: bin/i18n-typecheck-guard.sh is not referenced by any\nworkflow, so nothing has been enforcing this ratchet and main is 6 over it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqobpBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArk4QAE9K7BC5TARh1ybUW0+llmpH\n218iHc7e+t+NJsJeO8bZRzTDTphY5AzyazJ4/E2wjXKCscmWwRDAARdBQSIuwW8P\nFu4b14aHouO9zgIHT0/S9W49mE9kzBc/JVbLfRv1tZN+VQ8UIGD72wV91a3kZSG2\nxoRMj5Zo3lhO54UtT/KhTqpo9/CILA5nkj2cfa7tkNQ82tA6lvrvkAh0bxj9wkAQ\nx9xFSpwGImKTCd2DlUK0jEpp3Pqp0GH8KT9ZJLqMJO90P5qbrv1I6VLPEGPVou6s\neN8wLZTXlOlZFy5xRZGLoupd+d6V4AijVvgCDLBYH8NdT3VzCZQEyhEDvjYk1n31\nNUwql2OVg3CRJUoNHBM/Jkjx2KbWWl6SNSkFb9ZUmm286xCj76J2z68r6FlMHerT\nOKOVY+GJ/g2RPhDJubPRsZsaCnkid3hXoyu31oW7LFuMNnwbo8+bknsOnCT/8Kyy\n5ArqGj5JvC51ErfSHYrrP3OG/diZAZYzydJyO2muxwyCItTmLsRHxOWw7h7OP1Mr\nXcixHlTUgCvl7GRwDwrQxUrRK1TnbzW+F6D4xlhNTePHpCgcdXlxCxJhPb5M7/op\n+YUP4x1/zY085VlCD2H2OSgjYOpUr4uDRn+DSAlLpfh4YBHYr1mBdk/3cpncQ5jv\nNibAWWdA36EjPWzD8lTu\n=WjF+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T19:57:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/0c5301041ca40f1b0841f1aae9142c01081084db","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDBjNTMwMTA0MWNhNDBmMWIwODQxZjFhYWU5MTQyYzAxMDgxMDg0ZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/e8d225c83884a55f1197fcb1ca45df6df5ebd0e1","sha":"e8d225c83884a55f1197fcb1ca45df6df5ebd0e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/e8d225c83884a55f1197fcb1ca45df6df5ebd0e1"}],"sha":"0c5301041ca40f1b0841f1aae9142c01081084db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/0c5301041ca40f1b0841f1aae9142c01081084db"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/e8d225c83884a55f1197fcb1ca45df6df5ebd0e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T19:09:44Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T19:09:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mileage): the CRA''s 4¢/km territories supplement was never modelled (#543)\n\nThe CRA publishes its automobile allowance rates for the ten provinces and\nallows an additional 4¢/km for travel in the Northwest Territories, Yukon and\nNunavut. Neither rate lookup took a region, so a territories-resident sole\ntrader was under-claimed 4¢ on every business kilometre — in the app, over\nchat, and again on every edit. Both rate files carried a comment saying so.\n\n`region?: string` is now a 4th optional positional on\n`MileageRateProvider.getRate`, implemented by the pack (blended model) and by\nthe shell''s `getMileageRate` (marginal-tier model — the copy that books the\nmoney). It is threaded at `resolveMileageDeduction`, the single chokepoint the\nPOST route, the PATCH service and the chat executor all come through.\n\nThree things the work turned up:\n\n  * `statutoryFactLines` calls the rate providers itself to build the LLM''s\n    grounding context, and `region` was already in scope there for sales tax\n    and self-employment tax — just never passed to mileage. Without that fix\n    chat quotes 73¢/km about a trip the app books at 77¢.\n\n  * `0.67 + 0.04` is 0.7100000000000001, and in the pack that figure reaches\n    the user inside `tierDescription`. Both files add the supplement in cents.\n\n  * ''NT'' is Canada''s Northwest Territories and also Australia''s Northern\n    Territory. The supplement is gated on the jurisdiction, never the code.\n\nSelf-review caught two more, fixed here: an explicit `jurisdictionOverride:\n''us''` stopped winning over a CA config, because reading tenant config\nunconditionally meant collapsing an `if (!override)` guard that had been\nhonouring every override value; and the supplement matched 2-letter codes\nonly, so config rows written before `normalizeRegionCode` — holding ''Yukon''\nrather than ''YT'' — kept under-claiming.\n\nTwo limits are documented in code rather than left to be discovered:\n`AbMileageEntry` has no region column, so the PATCH path re-derives from\ncurrent config and editing an old Yukon trip after moving re-prices it\nprovincially; and the CRA ties the supplement to travel IN the territories\nwhile we key on recorded residence.\n\nStill open, tracked separately: `ratePreview` in the expense plugin''s Mileage\npage hardcodes rates stale in all four jurisdictions and carries no\nsupplement, so the form shows 72¢ against 77¢ booked. Plugin frontends cannot\nimport the shell''s lib, so that needs a rate endpoint.\n\n78 tests across three files, all watched fail first and all verified to have\nexecuted in CI. Nine mutations confirmed red then restored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d364e9d66f88f85778e96db8699065a6ea91e4db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/d364e9d66f88f85778e96db8699065a6ea91e4db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/e8d225c83884a55f1197fcb1ca45df6df5ebd0e1","verification":{"payload":"tree d364e9d66f88f85778e96db8699065a6ea91e4db\nparent ec09316621e8edabbfbf0475115c928053ed34e6\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788980984 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788980984 -0700\n\nfix(mileage): the CRA''s 4¢/km territories supplement was never modelled (#543)\n\nThe CRA publishes its automobile allowance rates for the ten provinces and\nallows an additional 4¢/km for travel in the Northwest Territories, Yukon and\nNunavut. Neither rate lookup took a region, so a territories-resident sole\ntrader was under-claimed 4¢ on every business kilometre — in the app, over\nchat, and again on every edit. Both rate files carried a comment saying so.\n\n`region?: string` is now a 4th optional positional on\n`MileageRateProvider.getRate`, implemented by the pack (blended model) and by\nthe shell''s `getMileageRate` (marginal-tier model — the copy that books the\nmoney). It is threaded at `resolveMileageDeduction`, the single chokepoint the\nPOST route, the PATCH service and the chat executor all come through.\n\nThree things the work turned up:\n\n  * `statutoryFactLines` calls the rate providers itself to build the LLM''s\n    grounding context, and `region` was already in scope there for sales tax\n    and self-employment tax — just never passed to mileage. Without that fix\n    chat quotes 73¢/km about a trip the app books at 77¢.\n\n  * `0.67 + 0.04` is 0.7100000000000001, and in the pack that figure reaches\n    the user inside `tierDescription`. Both files add the supplement in cents.\n\n  * ''NT'' is Canada''s Northwest Territories and also Australia''s Northern\n    Territory. The supplement is gated on the jurisdiction, never the code.\n\nSelf-review caught two more, fixed here: an explicit `jurisdictionOverride:\n''us''` stopped winning over a CA config, because reading tenant config\nunconditionally meant collapsing an `if (!override)` guard that had been\nhonouring every override value; and the supplement matched 2-letter codes\nonly, so config rows written before `normalizeRegionCode` — holding ''Yukon''\nrather than ''YT'' — kept under-claiming.\n\nTwo limits are documented in code rather than left to be discovered:\n`AbMileageEntry` has no region column, so the PATCH path re-derives from\ncurrent config and editing an old Yukon trip after moving re-prices it\nprovincially; and the CRA ties the supplement to travel IN the territories\nwhile we key on recorded residence.\n\nStill open, tracked separately: `ratePreview` in the expense plugin''s Mileage\npage hardcodes rates stale in all four jurisdictions and carries no\nsupplement, so the form shows 72¢ against 77¢ booked. Plugin frontends cannot\nimport the shell''s lib, so that needs a rate endpoint.\n\n78 tests across three files, all watched fail first and all verified to have\nexecuted in CI. Nine mutations confirmed red then restored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoa74CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyvoQAEez+gDjM9r8D7LB0KBZLWA3\nlt5e38UTfsbE0bty/v+WExUjkEdFV9aObw5dtdLbIlcGs+g6VA5iW9ZhDDBGUIHW\nm91dkeFkWhEVpfvZCxOnqTjnR6J98MHGH/Hlq2+HK0uaOaMmkP4V7OZU3aY30OIM\nOWxHAr9j/Hf13D2n7wB4uoUMwv2qACShoXnvGIQ5ieoXO/fkU1ol7xcW09qs1miP\nDONBq89vYhl5D7jj4ZFx9kihuAYntIR0V5BeEubDWjvz8tBG+RV1P3D395MTBB1P\nj0nsbpoYNioEHSqQykxCTnTgLoNZNKJnXulSijZlYaBx2BAe9LCo1LYwuoggqC2H\nxAQpo/kV2htsMYtIBkKrsvJxQrfDLRWyG3jknCFL77S8lNzkMRAhgHmzAehbZUvj\nndFyZJ/zZYClPB0VBqnlzJnHIkbKlikbEhX+MfonqIgP0F6seqkIMg8p/WWCAEQG\nt7S+bJ+Emyja/K6yd/j+hdxnHMJJgiF1bdTqE2z+0xF/WUCaNjhOdip8Fza+i8Uc\n/ssKDerOWB5f3nvmAnaRAK3/jUkTggevhFcT+dLxZJuiXTGFDUtur++YliZb/KVs\nsaQpyfnrAL71Ybj2DlTamRep2blZNlaWt2+rJ1jsj+AzFwM8KJi4sFBi848QhzvZ\nujbdE1tfh9WmdOfDq+Ye\n=oorr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T19:09:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/e8d225c83884a55f1197fcb1ca45df6df5ebd0e1","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGU4ZDIyNWM4Mzg4NGE1NWYxMTk3ZmNiMWNhNDVkZjZkZjVlYmQwZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/ec09316621e8edabbfbf0475115c928053ed34e6","sha":"ec09316621e8edabbfbf0475115c928053ed34e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ec09316621e8edabbfbf0475115c928053ed34e6"}],"sha":"e8d225c83884a55f1197fcb1ca45df6df5ebd0e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/e8d225c83884a55f1197fcb1ca45df6df5ebd0e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ec09316621e8edabbfbf0475115c928053ed34e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:21:11Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:21:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ops): dependency health endpoint, recorded history, and alerts on change (#542)\n\nThere was no monitoring of AgentBook. The one cron named \"health\" probes\nthird-party service connectors from the old NaaP gateway, of which this\nproduct publishes none, and /api/health answers \"alive and can reach\nPostgres\" — which a monitor can already infer from a page loading.\n\nStarting with what this ISN''T, because calling it uptime monitoring would\nbe the whole mistake: a check that runs inside the deployment cannot tell\nyou the deployment is down. If the app is gone so is the checker, and the\nsilence looks exactly like everything being fine. Real uptime monitoring\nhas to come from outside.\n\nSo this builds the half that has to live in here, and documents the half\nthat cannot.\n\n/api/health/deep runs a probe per dependency: database connectivity, and\nseparately whether a real table can be read — a pooler answering SELECT 1\nmid-migration looks healthy to a liveness check while every real query\n500s. Plus LLM, blob storage, error tracking and cron auth.\n\nTwo kinds of answer, kept apart. \"Stripe is unreachable\" and \"no Stripe key\nis set\" are different facts: the first is an incident, the second is a\ndeployment nobody finished. Conflating them either pages someone about a\nfeature that was never enabled, or hides an outage behind a shrug. So\n`unconfigured` is a status of its own and never turns the endpoint red — it\nshows in the body, where a human reads it, not in the status code, where a\npager does.\n\nThe endpoint is public and unauthenticated on purpose: a monitor that needs\na credential is a monitor somebody turns off. That makes what it returns\nthe whole design. /api/health in this codebase once served substring(0, 40)\nof four Postgres connection strings — one character short of the password —\nso nothing here returns a URL, a host, a key or an error message. `detail`\nis a fixed phrase chosen from the probe module, never interpolated from an\nexception, and there is a test that fails every probe at once and asserts\nnone of it reaches the body.\n\nA 5-minute cron records the same probes so a dependency that was down for\nsix hours leaves a trace even though nobody was curling at the time. One\nrow per probe updated in place, not a time series: 1,440 rows a day that\nnobody reads is a retention problem, and what alerting needs is the current\nstate and how long it has held. Transitions go to AbEvent, which already\nhas retention.\n\nIt alerts on CHANGE, not on state — six hours down is two messages, not\nseventy-two — and needs two consecutive failures to enter one, because a\ntimed-out query on a cold start is not an outage and a channel that cries\nwolf gets muted. Recovery is not debounced: that would keep an incident\nopen after it is over.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2cd30940affeaadadeb91b0370c6ff005b72cdc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/2cd30940affeaadadeb91b0370c6ff005b72cdc9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/ec09316621e8edabbfbf0475115c928053ed34e6","verification":{"payload":"tree 2cd30940affeaadadeb91b0370c6ff005b72cdc9\nparent 7c79ab4506c415f11aa95e043e321f3119b22e63\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788978071 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788978071 -0700\n\nfeat(ops): dependency health endpoint, recorded history, and alerts on change (#542)\n\nThere was no monitoring of AgentBook. The one cron named \"health\" probes\nthird-party service connectors from the old NaaP gateway, of which this\nproduct publishes none, and /api/health answers \"alive and can reach\nPostgres\" — which a monitor can already infer from a page loading.\n\nStarting with what this ISN''T, because calling it uptime monitoring would\nbe the whole mistake: a check that runs inside the deployment cannot tell\nyou the deployment is down. If the app is gone so is the checker, and the\nsilence looks exactly like everything being fine. Real uptime monitoring\nhas to come from outside.\n\nSo this builds the half that has to live in here, and documents the half\nthat cannot.\n\n/api/health/deep runs a probe per dependency: database connectivity, and\nseparately whether a real table can be read — a pooler answering SELECT 1\nmid-migration looks healthy to a liveness check while every real query\n500s. Plus LLM, blob storage, error tracking and cron auth.\n\nTwo kinds of answer, kept apart. \"Stripe is unreachable\" and \"no Stripe key\nis set\" are different facts: the first is an incident, the second is a\ndeployment nobody finished. Conflating them either pages someone about a\nfeature that was never enabled, or hides an outage behind a shrug. So\n`unconfigured` is a status of its own and never turns the endpoint red — it\nshows in the body, where a human reads it, not in the status code, where a\npager does.\n\nThe endpoint is public and unauthenticated on purpose: a monitor that needs\na credential is a monitor somebody turns off. That makes what it returns\nthe whole design. /api/health in this codebase once served substring(0, 40)\nof four Postgres connection strings — one character short of the password —\nso nothing here returns a URL, a host, a key or an error message. `detail`\nis a fixed phrase chosen from the probe module, never interpolated from an\nexception, and there is a test that fails every probe at once and asserts\nnone of it reaches the body.\n\nA 5-minute cron records the same probes so a dependency that was down for\nsix hours leaves a trace even though nobody was curling at the time. One\nrow per probe updated in place, not a time series: 1,440 rows a day that\nnobody reads is a retention problem, and what alerting needs is the current\nstate and how long it has held. Transitions go to AbEvent, which already\nhas retention.\n\nIt alerts on CHANGE, not on state — six hours down is two messages, not\nseventy-two — and needs two consecutive failures to enter one, because a\ntimed-out query on a cold start is not an outage and a channel that cries\nwolf gets muted. Recovery is not debounced: that would keep an incident\nopen after it is over.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoaOXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWwIQABcZnY1o9XUaPgnson61+fWW\n2PxIYK/45DpwY7Rck/8TyKZOVGXxmyVHaqfSE+pjpIo8sXn6yz3Clq9QPYMpBUkP\nDB98Pm/mfpwfKjB+86SzQDUxrbmqEH5kSVw3KqrnZzdL6Dqk5IGiC+wKEbgwviuh\nNvUPw0Ovlzyv8TMYPCfSEH8wvL7BOJ24jtplX16qyuNoW3i4j/jOlMy+rhLpNdtk\n+giEIfK9GCHp9aoolv4VbuHdXjSeS6M4qdm5TTz3lV9DBVMCqG7/cIq2EBTwUeP/\nfoqdpypba737c7iM6plBBRQKRDQt9uzzdHblBJd7KeWKq94IDSTLcE3KFmupjNQ2\n9gkgv/FKiTiLqRnhZhU20FkpdCl8QeWON0ueseUuWFBv51XEiaUwj96rMmlvxjiK\nXKxmEKInFuxnaWRij6T5CiHZlKUmzDQkfMwMZnQzEMRt2vMC5fDSojuVIk1H0DJg\nvVotcyXNazli8qjbYmHhjpSlmNnqlada5N4VNX58dFwhCi/QyEFvMmFSmEeMvZJr\nzrwrNb5y7wek6qrk1/2rBiiMDalkAW8dCSAmLei/joaf+FqjSYeRlx1SZgnMasvz\naVmFdH1EX/3lOYg1BHzp1NUAGQ2fxCUXkPl87Fsek5OKo7F5tJaI6B3U2bS4UJIt\n8T7KBrNAdcnf016ayiXT\n=AKFQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T18:21:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/ec09316621e8edabbfbf0475115c928053ed34e6","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGVjMDkzMTY2MjFlOGVkYWJiZmJmMDQ3NTExNWM5MjgwNTNlZDM0ZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/7c79ab4506c415f11aa95e043e321f3119b22e63","sha":"7c79ab4506c415f11aa95e043e321f3119b22e63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/7c79ab4506c415f11aa95e043e321f3119b22e63"}],"sha":"ec09316621e8edabbfbf0475115c928053ed34e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ec09316621e8edabbfbf0475115c928053ed34e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/7c79ab4506c415f11aa95e043e321f3119b22e63/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:20:17Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:20:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(guides): Chinese share cards for the partner materials kit (#541)\n\n* feat(guides): Chinese share cards for the partner materials kit\n\nThe partner materials page was translated except for the thing a partner\nactually posts. It carried an honest note saying so — \"卡片图片本身目前是\n英文的\" — which beats pretending, and still left a Chinese partner with\nnothing to share.\n\nFive Chinese cards now live under /guides/cards/zh/, and each page links to\nthe other set.\n\nThe risk in a translated SVG is not the wording. A CJK glyph occupies a\nfull em square where a Latin one averages about 0.41em in this typeface, so\ncopy translated line-for-line runs off the 1200px canvas — nothing throws,\nthe headline is simply cut in half in every share. So the copy is written\nshort rather than translated literally, the headlines drop from 76px to\n64px, and the negative letter-spacing goes: it is tuned for Latin and\ncrushes CJK glyphs together.\n\nThe test measures geometry rather than words. The CJK half of that\nmeasurement is exact — n glyphs at f px is n × f px in any font — which is\nwhat makes the guard worth having. It is pointed only at the Chinese set:\nchecked against a rendered English card, the same estimator calls every\nEnglish sub-line an overflow when none of them is, and an approximation\nthat fails on known-good content is not a guard.\n\nThe cards also declare a CJK font stack. Nothing in the repo did — the app\nhas been relying on browser defaults for Chinese — and on a downloadable\nshare asset that means a different card per reader.\n\n* refactor(guides): drop the hand-written language cross-links\n\nGuidesChrome already renders a 中文 / English toggle on every guide page,\nresolved through guidesCounterpart. A second one written by hand on this\npage only is an inconsistency, and on the English side it is one more\nhardcoded user-facing string — which is how CI caught it, via the i18n\nratchet rather than review.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7077a4d55d382208782cbb035c580826e076f0ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/7077a4d55d382208782cbb035c580826e076f0ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/7c79ab4506c415f11aa95e043e321f3119b22e63","verification":{"payload":"tree 7077a4d55d382208782cbb035c580826e076f0ad\nparent 8e7b6b66eb11a402c1a59fe0a6afd83a94c93165\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788978017 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788978017 -0700\n\nfeat(guides): Chinese share cards for the partner materials kit (#541)\n\n* feat(guides): Chinese share cards for the partner materials kit\n\nThe partner materials page was translated except for the thing a partner\nactually posts. It carried an honest note saying so — \"卡片图片本身目前是\n英文的\" — which beats pretending, and still left a Chinese partner with\nnothing to share.\n\nFive Chinese cards now live under /guides/cards/zh/, and each page links to\nthe other set.\n\nThe risk in a translated SVG is not the wording. A CJK glyph occupies a\nfull em square where a Latin one averages about 0.41em in this typeface, so\ncopy translated line-for-line runs off the 1200px canvas — nothing throws,\nthe headline is simply cut in half in every share. So the copy is written\nshort rather than translated literally, the headlines drop from 76px to\n64px, and the negative letter-spacing goes: it is tuned for Latin and\ncrushes CJK glyphs together.\n\nThe test measures geometry rather than words. The CJK half of that\nmeasurement is exact — n glyphs at f px is n × f px in any font — which is\nwhat makes the guard worth having. It is pointed only at the Chinese set:\nchecked against a rendered English card, the same estimator calls every\nEnglish sub-line an overflow when none of them is, and an approximation\nthat fails on known-good content is not a guard.\n\nThe cards also declare a CJK font stack. Nothing in the repo did — the app\nhas been relying on browser defaults for Chinese — and on a downloadable\nshare asset that means a different card per reader.\n\n* refactor(guides): drop the hand-written language cross-links\n\nGuidesChrome already renders a 中文 / English toggle on every guide page,\nresolved through guidesCounterpart. A second one written by hand on this\npage only is an inconsistency, and on the English side it is one more\nhardcoded user-facing string — which is how CI caught it, via the i18n\nratchet rather than review.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoaNhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz0YQAKFeYxOIQtw5JSw13RocVpng\nt1jInJCUD6BChZj0MEYRtCgm4KL6eE8texCW1DjoW8k8Fyz1Gvajd7jPJy/cE9e/\n7tWH6mA+PGKXs1MhiUWyqR+w7bp6IHxV9yS4imjUw1TBiZvBiHwksIl0cshvZIK8\nnB1+fkEjfTI6I5FiN4cWXWgUcz/BmuvK9nQFiT6Z3C9CaqEXYv3z1rWE/Fdd3esj\nM1ij0Dhv9GY0xuS64ekmduLAiFmsW0zzvBwn7Pzy+QcuHEBOCY2CMej6dYnqr4sZ\nD0fT+9FP1zMK88oPf/uHmAches4k9BUcPv9C7UncPqghcCxPuG1bYG1U+4DyjlpV\nj00YPRGdFAYv4wERQc26gReBRWeyJ30KiCfbUHyvOR+6+6jVm+Za6Qxdh6DFWYEw\nnirY50NhJG7liFHKj28H4ZseyAdRkNR0ldFFpSZxDyVmlv6lEYlAkJkCZUjzqjyQ\n+50hXPxEOonuuq0/ux2bl9rapdDCw15c6nKvPkR9tpNG4WNBRKhO0diI05NnXuoH\n6eQ67BYGEL+NV0GMj121245MGatK7CCJWCrRANFHzMI8lGi7cmWA8lwOcpf7Jkek\nGPDk95dZdK/6X2vJMhwQF5y+oACHbpZNhK3aQOK2rBYYDg2jySav6n4wQQvXisPl\nEsDRHjeJSaJKccW8NKI+\n=I4/z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T18:20:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/7c79ab4506c415f11aa95e043e321f3119b22e63","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDdjNzlhYjQ1MDZjNDE1ZjExYWE5NWUwNDNlMzIxZjMxMTliMjJlNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/8e7b6b66eb11a402c1a59fe0a6afd83a94c93165","sha":"8e7b6b66eb11a402c1a59fe0a6afd83a94c93165","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/8e7b6b66eb11a402c1a59fe0a6afd83a94c93165"}],"sha":"7c79ab4506c415f11aa95e043e321f3119b22e63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/7c79ab4506c415f11aa95e043e321f3119b22e63"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/8e7b6b66eb11a402c1a59fe0a6afd83a94c93165/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:57:29Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:57:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(docs): give the Chinese documentation a landing page (#540)\n\nEvery page behind the docs landing was already translated. The landing\nitself was a hardcoded array of English strings inside app/docs/page.tsx,\nso there was nothing for /docs/zh to render — the route redirected a\nChinese reader straight past the front door into a quickstart, skipping the\nonly page that says what the documentation contains.\n\nThe copy moves into lib/docs/landing.ts, keyed by locale, and both landings\nrender from one component. A translated copy of the page would have been\nthe easier change and the one that drifts: the landing is the page most\nlikely to gain a section that its translation then silently lacks. Tests\nassert the two locales carry the same sections and links, in the same\norder, and that no user-visible field is still the English string.\n\nPaths in the copy are locale-bare and prefixed at render time, so a\ntranslated landing cannot link back into the English tree — asserted on the\nrendered DOM, because that is the failure this repo has actually shipped:\ngreen catalog guards beside a page the reader sees in English.\n\nThe bare-locale branch also gets its own metadata. It was falling through\nto the section-name fallback, which would have titled the page \"Zh\".\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"efd1687e23a32630e2036b6f45eb34781c4bc93e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/efd1687e23a32630e2036b6f45eb34781c4bc93e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/8e7b6b66eb11a402c1a59fe0a6afd83a94c93165","verification":{"payload":"tree efd1687e23a32630e2036b6f45eb34781c4bc93e\nparent 644e1ff7114bf330dcf9f6d34d9bda692b717c77\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788976649 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788976649 -0700\n\nfeat(docs): give the Chinese documentation a landing page (#540)\n\nEvery page behind the docs landing was already translated. The landing\nitself was a hardcoded array of English strings inside app/docs/page.tsx,\nso there was nothing for /docs/zh to render — the route redirected a\nChinese reader straight past the front door into a quickstart, skipping the\nonly page that says what the documentation contains.\n\nThe copy moves into lib/docs/landing.ts, keyed by locale, and both landings\nrender from one component. A translated copy of the page would have been\nthe easier change and the one that drifts: the landing is the page most\nlikely to gain a section that its translation then silently lacks. Tests\nassert the two locales carry the same sections and links, in the same\norder, and that no user-visible field is still the English string.\n\nPaths in the copy are locale-bare and prefixed at render time, so a\ntranslated landing cannot link back into the English tree — asserted on the\nrendered DOM, because that is the failure this repo has actually shipped:\ngreen catalog guards beside a page the reader sees in English.\n\nThe bare-locale branch also gets its own metadata. It was falling through\nto the section-name fallback, which would have titled the page \"Zh\".\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoZ4