ommit/644e1ff7114bf330dcf9f6d34d9bda692b717c77","sha":"644e1ff7114bf330dcf9f6d34d9bda692b717c77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/644e1ff7114bf330dcf9f6d34d9bda692b717c77"}],"sha":"8e7b6b66eb11a402c1a59fe0a6afd83a94c93165","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/8e7b6b66eb11a402c1a59fe0a6afd83a94c93165"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/644e1ff7114bf330dcf9f6d34d9bda692b717c77/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:50:46Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:50:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(whatsapp): read receipt photos and PDFs (#539)\n\nWhatsApp shipped text-only, and the route''s own header said why: receipt\ncapture was \"deliberately out of scope for this first pass\". The real\nobstacle was that the OCR pipeline lived inside the Telegram webhook route\nfile, so the only way for a second channel to scan a receipt was to write\nthe whole thing again.\n\nNothing in that pipeline was Telegram-specific — no reply formatting, no\nbot context, no translation calls. It moves to a shared module verbatim;\nTelegram imports it and behaves identically. The only edits are the\n`source` union gaining the WhatsApp values and log prefixes losing the word\n\"telegram\".\n\nThe new part is `ingestReceipt`, which composes the four steps — quota\ncheck, OCR, blob persistence, expense row — into one call. A second adapter\nwriting its own handler picks up three of the four and misses the first,\nand the first is `ocr_scans`: a metered, billed quota. A channel that\nscanned receipts without consulting it would be a free bypass of a paid\nfeature. That is the failure this shape prevents, and it is tested against\nthe real function rather than a mock, because every channel test mocks this\nmodule out.\n\nWhatsApp-side specifics:\n\n  - Meta hands over a media ID, not a URL. Resolving it takes two hops, and\n    the URL from the first is neither public nor long-lived, so the bytes\n    are pulled and handed on as a data: URI — a link would 401 or expire by\n    the time OCR or blob storage got to it.\n  - Size is refused from the metadata envelope, before the download.\n  - The link check runs BEFORE the scan. An unlinked number reaching a\n    shared business number must not be able to spend a tenant''s quota.\n  - A caption travels with the receipt; it is the user telling us what the\n    purchase was.\n  - \"I could see it but couldn''t make out the total\" is a distinct reply\n    from \"something went wrong\". The first sends the user back to their\n    camera, where the fix is; the second sends them to support.\n\nZero-amount OCR output is refused rather than booked: amount 0 with\nconfidence 0 is the model saying it could not read the receipt, and a\nzero-value expense is a silent wrong number in the ledger.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6f5dd6d9075375859b3132989bf04c0d000b36e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/6f5dd6d9075375859b3132989bf04c0d000b36e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/644e1ff7114bf330dcf9f6d34d9bda692b717c77","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f5dd6d9075375859b3132989bf04c0d000b36e7\nparent 873f17c6bc2b15534886a4e498a045a57218a80d\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788976246 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788976246 -0700\n\nfeat(whatsapp): read receipt photos and PDFs (#539)\n\nWhatsApp shipped text-only, and the route''s own header said why: receipt\ncapture was \"deliberately out of scope for this first pass\". The real\nobstacle was that the OCR pipeline lived inside the Telegram webhook route\nfile, so the only way for a second channel to scan a receipt was to write\nthe whole thing again.\n\nNothing in that pipeline was Telegram-specific — no reply formatting, no\nbot context, no translation calls. It moves to a shared module verbatim;\nTelegram imports it and behaves identically. The only edits are the\n`source` union gaining the WhatsApp values and log prefixes losing the word\n\"telegram\".\n\nThe new part is `ingestReceipt`, which composes the four steps — quota\ncheck, OCR, blob persistence, expense row — into one call. A second adapter\nwriting its own handler picks up three of the four and misses the first,\nand the first is `ocr_scans`: a metered, billed quota. A channel that\nscanned receipts without consulting it would be a free bypass of a paid\nfeature. That is the failure this shape prevents, and it is tested against\nthe real function rather than a mock, because every channel test mocks this\nmodule out.\n\nWhatsApp-side specifics:\n\n  - Meta hands over a media ID, not a URL. Resolving it takes two hops, and\n    the URL from the first is neither public nor long-lived, so the bytes\n    are pulled and handed on as a data: URI — a link would 401 or expire by\n    the time OCR or blob storage got to it.\n  - Size is refused from the metadata envelope, before the download.\n  - The link check runs BEFORE the scan. An unlinked number reaching a\n    shared business number must not be able to spend a tenant''s quota.\n  - A caption travels with the receipt; it is the user telling us what the\n    purchase was.\n  - \"I could see it but couldn''t make out the total\" is a distinct reply\n    from \"something went wrong\". The first sends the user back to their\n    camera, where the fix is; the second sends them to support.\n\nZero-amount OCR output is refused rather than booked: amount 0 with\nconfidence 0 is the model saying it could not read the receipt, and a\nzero-value expense is a silent wrong number in the ledger.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoZx2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5lUQABFFy/vS/eBJPGtw0/y78Hnf\nXZS1Q/YDatt/IHxkYCMHfmetBtmaPrFh3xFXiUPwYlsxpaa45b5EOPhqALnfvIEH\n0d9oLeswh2Q2HoJoqjLPZzNNi8aaUINDagwR/7+01RgDO8T2wUJcHWQjO5YF+O3H\nWrHBtyCE9TeVJ36AqltQska5E2haljEqfmsZTHzSoVOTZhlZkOixSe+XhBTs5x+F\n8N48UJqosz69GwTtiQ2aiSFFj1VHthxl6BEQ8AMEDOerSRu8g/CYNN9iJKJdJme3\n77wngosb1M5xToB40btrKOwtmMzTxq+VAwRqpamlp096PF1LQp4HOQ5cJBH+s3jA\ny81BNs5ymXzf79xzUH4/sIJw3h8BiBqhaBZ2JbPEM2fzH9fDj66gfp7IN71OowF7\nIn7uqvf2+4IWCkFJDPhxP6mibxmRLtrJbv7uKBaphLDQqo7SgZ51EwDUs34GxAeP\npqiNuAhXJsfwsgRDWk11wgjKr3h6riOeqAGMI51lHBwfaIINzru4Zp+upQJE+S8d\nf/kXeyGrdAp9DHZef2NZyBcS7cZG6jBC6j8P2hN4d5NaYzIOtfXY3qRhyfdFE6k2\nN7p78B13CXPA3jfKS0FG/JqzdBqsfATMLCuDR8Xva7qEfXEM2qq2MJBBlThrLdjB\ncmavjkrJ2P3s3ZE6bWYt\n=7aGH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T17:50:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/644e1ff7114bf330dcf9f6d34d9bda692b717c77","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDY0NGUxZmY3MTE0YmYzMzBkY2Y5ZjZkMzRkOWJkYTY5MmI3MTdjNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/873f17c6bc2b15534886a4e498a045a57218a80d","sha":"873f17c6bc2b15534886a4e498a045a57218a80d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/873f17c6bc2b15534886a4e498a045a57218a80d"}],"sha":"644e1ff7114bf330dcf9f6d34d9bda692b717c77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/644e1ff7114bf330dcf9f6d34d9bda692b717c77"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/873f17c6bc2b15534886a4e498a045a57218a80d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:42:57Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:42:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(chat): answer the question before introducing yourself (#538)\n\nThe advisor''s one-time introduction was prepended unconditionally on first\ncontact, so a user whose very first message was a real question — \"how much\ntax do I owe?\" — got four sentences of onboarding and had to scroll past\nthem to find their answer. On Telegram those four sentences are the whole\nvisible message. The scorecard recorded it as AU opening its first\nconsultative turn with the persona intro instead of the answer; AU was\nsimply the tenant that had not been introduced yet, so every region''s first\nsubstantive turn read that way.\n\nAnswer first, then say who you are. That is what a competent person does,\nand only a bare greeting inverts it, because then the greeting IS the turn.\n\n`isBareGreeting` is deliberately narrow: a salutation and nothing else, in\nany of the three shipped locales. \"hi, how much tax do I owe?\" is a\nquestion — answering the greeting and burying the question is the exact\nbehaviour this exists to prevent. Emoji and punctuation are stripped before\nmatching, because \"hey 👋\" is a greeting and the first version of this said\nit was not.\n\nThe trailing form drops the \"Hi —\" and the closing \"shall I log your first\nexpense?\": the user has already been greeted by the answer, and they\nalready have a next step — the thing they asked about. It keeps the AI\ndisclosure, which has to be said on first contact whatever else the turn\ncontained, and there is a test asserting it survives both orderings.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ead6c9062b1195bac6b62d982a9d226b7efe3136","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/ead6c9062b1195bac6b62d982a9d226b7efe3136"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/873f17c6bc2b15534886a4e498a045a57218a80d","verification":{"payload":"tree ead6c9062b1195bac6b62d982a9d226b7efe3136\nparent 5e8deb31f5fee2b81e80643c44e2c30f8153c6e7\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788975777 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788975777 -0700\n\nfix(chat): answer the question before introducing yourself (#538)\n\nThe advisor''s one-time introduction was prepended unconditionally on first\ncontact, so a user whose very first message was a real question — \"how much\ntax do I owe?\" — got four sentences of onboarding and had to scroll past\nthem to find their answer. On Telegram those four sentences are the whole\nvisible message. The scorecard recorded it as AU opening its first\nconsultative turn with the persona intro instead of the answer; AU was\nsimply the tenant that had not been introduced yet, so every region''s first\nsubstantive turn read that way.\n\nAnswer first, then say who you are. That is what a competent person does,\nand only a bare greeting inverts it, because then the greeting IS the turn.\n\n`isBareGreeting` is deliberately narrow: a salutation and nothing else, in\nany of the three shipped locales. \"hi, how much tax do I owe?\" is a\nquestion — answering the greeting and burying the question is the exact\nbehaviour this exists to prevent. Emoji and punctuation are stripped before\nmatching, because \"hey 👋\" is a greeting and the first version of this said\nit was not.\n\nThe trailing form drops the \"Hi —\" and the closing \"shall I log your first\nexpense?\": the user has already been greeted by the answer, and they\nalready have a next step — the thing they asked about. It keeps the AI\ndisclosure, which has to be said on first contact whatever else the turn\ncontained, and there is a test asserting it survives both orderings.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoZqhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm6IQAHbyPibX2GHM0AA138s/7iI7\n3JASbG2EwHTSLYnG0TQC4dCRqLL40eKAfxhPpA06zVw9jzNgF0etbyRkb+SGrdel\ngMIEXXToyBnw1HSM1xh6QEWcif8zoQX/auRauUvjGG0eRteWLWICyq3aYaHsYz6z\nMBpddATtGeIianegX1i0/n1fkaerl+y9CBJwuqomwTkTmR0McCIQWakO14D9hMu4\n56kpgSVLBQ3JGaJkklcRuSuw21NjYlmTGMg+etN6u984ee7UXujyp7mBI1P188Ao\nkCKFyCVDnXP8KQn4DolcyP/uGXNQlFmOr7GTyL7Kg4VYJfX6o+jtdGOoLllFppQN\nphNJpvY8mqDGpor3kAAcJ2+1y5EXIMwP3Avj7Dl7efvacHlsGrpSa1oqgc2NBxqv\naDB35k1t4orVUSq50LG4lw/7jO4A7S66wBEyz3UiKi1wrbNVe+JS0xo0pelthHvN\nqKU9vnqtYnPJ4x+ibMbRQFpQgD0ys4s1xfOBKVRgt2CHmaN8iItAqJhwWPyroJ7G\n1hSMeb31UcHL2BdH9MNa9rxS+mvA+MyjCyIzdifspJV5zkx39SwB/YSb4pNOGcAl\nT56q2Ld2VBIEWiybxNrqA8t6/+in8wYizkPeuTGm9P8Kw+uILAer2+2mBtaTjOrF\nxb76yjgRFTlE1o8W8tTZ\n=uWuB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T17:42:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/873f17c6bc2b15534886a4e498a045a57218a80d","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDg3M2YxN2M2YmMyYjE1NTM0ODg2YTRlNDk4YTA0NWE1NzIxOGE4MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/5e8deb31f5fee2b81e80643c44e2c30f8153c6e7","sha":"5e8deb31f5fee2b81e80643c44e2c30f8153c6e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/5e8deb31f5fee2b81e80643c44e2c30f8153c6e7"}],"sha":"873f17c6bc2b15534886a4e498a045a57218a80d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/873f17c6bc2b15534886a4e498a045a57218a80d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/5e8deb31f5fee2b81e80643c44e2c30f8153c6e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:42:19Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:42:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(chat): let the reviewer accept a rate the jurisdiction pack publishes (#536)\n\nThe consultation reviewer checks every rate in a draft against the\ngrounding facts and rejects the rest with \"Rates must come from the pack,\nnever from the model.\" Nothing ever put a pack rate into the grounding\nfacts. `buildGroundingFacts` supplies the tenant''s ledger and profile and\nnothing else, so the set of known numbers held the user''s own money and no\nstatutory figure at all.\n\nEvery percentage the model produced was therefore unverifiable. \"GST in\nAustralia is 10%\" — correct, from the pack we ship — was flagged, and the\nrepair brief told the model to delete it and say the rate \"depends on their\ncircumstances\". The reviewer built to stop invented figures was deleting\nthe true ones and handing the user a vaguer answer than the model had\nactually written. A published threshold was worse: \"A$75,000\" is\nmoney-shaped, so it was an ungrounded-amount, which BLOCKS — the GST\nregistration advice added in #532 could not be said out loud.\n\n`statutoryFactLines` reads the rates out of the packs and returns them as\nfact lines, given to the model as context AND to the reviewer as grounding.\nOne source, so what the model is told to quote and what the verifier\naccepts cannot drift.\n\nThe two sets stay separate. Money is grounded by the ledger plus published\nTHRESHOLDS; rates additionally by published rates. So a pack rate can never\nground a money claim — \"10%\" in the rate table must not make \"A$10.00 in\nyour account\" verifiable — and bracket boundaries are deliberately excluded\nfrom the pack lines, because a large round number admitted to the money set\nwould let a draft assert it about the user''s own income and pass.\n\nNothing is retyped: every figure is read back out of the pack that computes\nthe user''s actual bill. Writing this surfaced four lines that would have\nbeen quoted at users verbatim and were wrong or unreadable — \"UK federal\nincome tax\", \"45 cents per mile\" for the UK contradicting its own \"45p\" in\nthe same sentence, \"ON HST rate in ON\", and raw `medicare_levy` /\n`class_2` keys.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"88974a5c4a72771acbb8ece66e039ad801db64db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/88974a5c4a72771acbb8ece66e039ad801db64db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/5e8deb31f5fee2b81e80643c44e2c30f8153c6e7","verification":{"payload":"tree 88974a5c4a72771acbb8ece66e039ad801db64db\nparent 2e39ec3acd6e165c1f76d75432ff70bbbafb3ebe\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788975739 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788975739 -0700\n\nfix(chat): let the reviewer accept a rate the jurisdiction pack publishes (#536)\n\nThe consultation reviewer checks every rate in a draft against the\ngrounding facts and rejects the rest with \"Rates must come from the pack,\nnever from the model.\" Nothing ever put a pack rate into the grounding\nfacts. `buildGroundingFacts` supplies the tenant''s ledger and profile and\nnothing else, so the set of known numbers held the user''s own money and no\nstatutory figure at all.\n\nEvery percentage the model produced was therefore unverifiable. \"GST in\nAustralia is 10%\" — correct, from the pack we ship — was flagged, and the\nrepair brief told the model to delete it and say the rate \"depends on their\ncircumstances\". The reviewer built to stop invented figures was deleting\nthe true ones and handing the user a vaguer answer than the model had\nactually written. A published threshold was worse: \"A$75,000\" is\nmoney-shaped, so it was an ungrounded-amount, which BLOCKS — the GST\nregistration advice added in #532 could not be said out loud.\n\n`statutoryFactLines` reads the rates out of the packs and returns them as\nfact lines, given to the model as context AND to the reviewer as grounding.\nOne source, so what the model is told to quote and what the verifier\naccepts cannot drift.\n\nThe two sets stay separate. Money is grounded by the ledger plus published\nTHRESHOLDS; rates additionally by published rates. So a pack rate can never\nground a money claim — \"10%\" in the rate table must not make \"A$10.00 in\nyour account\" verifiable — and bracket boundaries are deliberately excluded\nfrom the pack lines, because a large round number admitted to the money set\nwould let a draft assert it about the user''s own income and pass.\n\nNothing is retyped: every figure is read back out of the pack that computes\nthe user''s actual bill. Writing this surfaced four lines that would have\nbeen quoted at users verbatim and were wrong or unreadable — \"UK federal\nincome tax\", \"45 cents per mile\" for the UK contradicting its own \"45p\" in\nthe same sentence, \"ON HST rate in ON\", and raw `medicare_levy` /\n`class_2` keys.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoZp7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAXAQAJ57gPgxDgUrJ1wGUIOq3Xux\nFbPLtODFMCBQ6yq7dXOQnVlQyah9fB2xM3XHVvlEzObmSB4+37ed/q/0QmyI02JC\nqFxJeR/CjYoIR/rtOKCz/NtWXyBZUIbwmZXD5MDDoyu2AT/2BePNd2tZnloQi+f4\nXIldz9RbXLXc6AtlzAM3dvkIO1KO8wqukaCusPGBDLk4rOazQOKcOyrCPzNfgotc\nUwlfZK/xRrGH2jstZ6At0keZL9BrNPxWJD7vfXmTwXnsA8zH0acdVnL+PoKAZxQK\nr4wtY2b+GQ0qhq783emIB94tzyUkLAOWy2Xi9jtr8PdeSlWnQEY7XoInjC9LMyIn\nc7+vBK0LoaJZPyChvlrsNA9IPpvyzqJ9i3NxVRc1zPj8MQwzAgeNLpmJ75BCrUJw\n0xXZckDOrkLPf1SYQDkkGcamsGa2XowruZTyO1u9mFzIU+EdmsTJBY2hzZmtSDdX\ncAgX4LCVsqcijB7P8Y+LGWkpIsNF2oFOnGNxACGY963FSq1xbJgpIzxMlG/WtUdz\np/zlSlh8FJCTAvi2UcTgzA9QT/P671z7baBd4VuzS/Tw7xzD6Ig0ciE8T4wyG2UD\nuaTnl6SCmAUXIxPVD5BAFihb2kZ5mHnGiFFH47jm3fSmnUw/ifFHfDnoxiOUzAnf\n4MELazexcDiR6XsDPP3e\n=vKF6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T17:42:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/5e8deb31f5fee2b81e80643c44e2c30f8153c6e7","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDVlOGRlYjMxZjVmZWUyYjgxZTgwNjQzYzQ0ZTJjMzBmODE1M2M2ZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/2e39ec3acd6e165c1f76d75432ff70bbbafb3ebe","sha":"2e39ec3acd6e165c1f76d75432ff70bbbafb3ebe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/2e39ec3acd6e165c1f76d75432ff70bbbafb3ebe"}],"sha":"5e8deb31f5fee2b81e80643c44e2c30f8153c6e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/5e8deb31f5fee2b81e80643c44e2c30f8153c6e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/2e39ec3acd6e165c1f76d75432ff70bbbafb3ebe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:30:54Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:30:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mileage): the rate tables were stale in all three regions, and nothing checked (#537)\n\nOn 9 September 2026 AgentBook was booking mileage at:\n\n  US  67c/mile  — the 2024 rate. The IRS allows 76c today.\n  CA  72c/66c   — the 2025 rates. The CRA moved to 73c/67c in January.\n  AU  88c/km    — FY2025-26. The ATO moved to 91c on 1 July.\n\nEvery suite was green, because every test asserted a table against a\nliteral copied out of the same table. One went further and accepted three\nanswers for a published figure that has exactly one:\n\n    expect([67, 65, 65.5]).toContain(r.ratePerUnitCents);\n\nThe US case was worse than stale. The rate existed in TWO places — the\njurisdictions pack said 70c, and the shell that actually books the\ndeduction said 67c — so the newer copy was the one nobody read. Deleted:\nthere is now one US table, in the pack, and the shell reads it.\n\nKeyed by effective DATE, not year. The IRS moved mid-year for 2026 (72.5c\nto 30 June, 76c from 1 July), which a year-keyed lookup cannot express, and\nrounding a half-year to whichever rate is \"mostly\" right misstates every\ntrip in the other half. `MileageRateProvider.getRate` takes an optional\n`asOf`, and `resolveMileageDeduction` already had the trip date to pass.\n\n72.5 is not a whole number of cents, so `AbMileageEntry.ratePerUnitCents`\nbecomes Float. Rounding the snapshot would make it disagree with the amount\nbooked, and rounding up over-claims. The deduction itself stays whole cents.\n\nEvery `?? 0.88`-style fallback now points at the table''s own latest entry\nrather than a frozen literal, so \"the most recent rate we publish\" cannot\nquietly come to mean a superseded one.\n\nThe durable part is mileage-rate-staleness.test.ts. A rate table cannot be\nverified against itself, so it checks the one thing a test can know without\nan authority to call: whether the table still claims to cover today. It\ngoes red when the calendar passes the newest entry, naming the\ndetermination to go and read. Run against the code as shipped, it fails in\nall three jurisdictions.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"265af1d4e667c4be2e1ef24fbf4a4a778508a5af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/265af1d4e667c4be2e1ef24fbf4a4a778508a5af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/2e39ec3acd6e165c1f76d75432ff70bbbafb3ebe","verification":{"payload":"tree 265af1d4e667c4be2e1ef24fbf4a4a778508a5af\nparent c0347d671940a3149f467417f193e5be4f50338f\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788975054 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788975054 -0700\n\nfix(mileage): the rate tables were stale in all three regions, and nothing checked (#537)\n\nOn 9 September 2026 AgentBook was booking mileage at:\n\n  US  67c/mile  — the 2024 rate. The IRS allows 76c today.\n  CA  72c/66c   — the 2025 rates. The CRA moved to 73c/67c in January.\n  AU  88c/km    — FY2025-26. The ATO moved to 91c on 1 July.\n\nEvery suite was green, because every test asserted a table against a\nliteral copied out of the same table. One went further and accepted three\nanswers for a published figure that has exactly one:\n\n    expect([67, 65, 65.5]).toContain(r.ratePerUnitCents);\n\nThe US case was worse than stale. The rate existed in TWO places — the\njurisdictions pack said 70c, and the shell that actually books the\ndeduction said 67c — so the newer copy was the one nobody read. Deleted:\nthere is now one US table, in the pack, and the shell reads it.\n\nKeyed by effective DATE, not year. The IRS moved mid-year for 2026 (72.5c\nto 30 June, 76c from 1 July), which a year-keyed lookup cannot express, and\nrounding a half-year to whichever rate is \"mostly\" right misstates every\ntrip in the other half. `MileageRateProvider.getRate` takes an optional\n`asOf`, and `resolveMileageDeduction` already had the trip date to pass.\n\n72.5 is not a whole number of cents, so `AbMileageEntry.ratePerUnitCents`\nbecomes Float. Rounding the snapshot would make it disagree with the amount\nbooked, and rounding up over-claims. The deduction itself stays whole cents.\n\nEvery `?? 0.88`-style fallback now points at the table''s own latest entry\nrather than a frozen literal, so \"the most recent rate we publish\" cannot\nquietly come to mean a superseded one.\n\nThe durable part is mileage-rate-staleness.test.ts. A rate table cannot be\nverified against itself, so it checks the one thing a test can know without\nan authority to call: whether the table still claims to cover today. It\ngoes red when the calendar passes the newest entry, naming the\ndetermination to go and read. Run against the code as shipped, it fails in\nall three jurisdictions.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoZfOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk9MQADNl5e1Q6syhdcY6Y3rzJzKH\nINXaCdXE9TPD7kbGNyLGqlKfuuYZaZNqkZrflgUV/Yxb3L0qeve/6unJX7/vpKEv\nE/7lVzbHVMtGjpkDKymkwPre1dXL7UGX+qWCKhqiHpzLkAno/oB7oysaCEY8Nf43\nWMEBbwqUVqHY8B/xB+X8Ngr5OwQYHTK+p0jYHpFBiQnpA5N4Akmpit2P31BTWyya\nSLHh5Wvj561Urw4Lgv4RmLGK9r/f+T6n+WpXdW1Uu3wyra84MooaTlCg9AOhuZTr\nmA8bO2q8tK2Z90COpd/CIhCOKnxs3DJEV+75bnNc2FDG/zCWH2+ExSfAMw3WubJF\nD2aJeN/F9l++Tl6S6/eFu2/pk8EEzyNsWZrjorQ3Mb+3RFidjaWu3k5Ku8LbQSzd\ncWYwMikzI523Y3758ag6RkFC1wuJTJs5OGXNS4QXjDSm4iNtjtEkl5OU4qUExn8A\nb03vF9jZt2ltQVsA6QI2BEfUrnK8cWb7nmN8kJ2GwJ/g+nkk3uODkV+BeWvI1HM0\n9Xga47ApvYkJRjqRywvPOtNITKBqOxRyYJGSCnLSu3LwCzFM3ZLI0388B1nd3xw6\nWMqrhBjg8nJUhl77f8ONUlGDtrb4osZpNvlB3GrHtRmzo5d4FDM2zrHaokJOORbR\nsgMoqmPJ+yqdtkseMyoy\n=yNyt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T17:30:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/2e39ec3acd6e165c1f76d75432ff70bbbafb3ebe","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDJlMzllYzNhY2Q2ZTE2NWMxZjc2ZDc1NDMyZmY3MGJiYmFmYjNlYmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/c0347d671940a3149f467417f193e5be4f50338f","sha":"c0347d671940a3149f467417f193e5be4f50338f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/c0347d671940a3149f467417f193e5be4f50338f"}],"sha":"2e39ec3acd6e165c1f76d75432ff70bbbafb3ebe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/2e39ec3acd6e165c1f76d75432ff70bbbafb3ebe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/c0347d671940a3149f467417f193e5be4f50338f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:24:32Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:24:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(perdiem): say why per-diem doesn''t exist outside the US, instead of promising it (#535)\n\nThe launch scorecard carried \"AU: no per-diem\" as a missing rate table. It\nis the opposite of a missing table.\n\nA per-diem is a SUBSTANTIATION SHORTCUT — deduct a daily meal amount\nwithout keeping receipts — so whether one exists for you is a question\nabout who your revenue authority excuses from record-keeping, not about\nwhich tables we have shipped. The ATO''s reasonable travel amounts remove\nthe evidence requirement only for an EMPLOYEE who received a bona fide\ntravel allowance. A sole trader does not pay themselves an allowance, so\nthe exception never reaches them: actual costs, with tax invoices, plus a\ntravel diary past six consecutive nights.\n\nBuilding an AU table would therefore not have closed a gap. It would have\ninvited a sole trader to claim meals without the receipts the ATO requires\nand handed them an audit problem the product created. The same holds for\nCA (simplified meal method is for transport employees and moving/medical\ntravel; the self-employed deduct 50% of actual) and the UK (benchmark\nscale rates reimburse employees).\n\nSo the fix is the explanation. `perDiemAvailability` in the jurisdictions\npack owns it, the route and the chat executor both call it, and it replaces\n\"(Coming in a future release.)\" — which promised a feature that cannot\nexist and told the user nothing they could act on.\n\nAlso closes a hole in the old gate: it listed ''ca'' | ''au'' | ''uk''\nexplicitly, so a tenant on any other jurisdiction fell through and was\nbooked US GSA rates for a deduction their authority does not recognise.\nUnknown now refuses.\n\nThe e2e that was meant to cover this declared its own `expectedBody` and\nasserted `expectedBody.code === ''unsupported_jurisdiction''` — a literal\ncompared with itself, which passes whatever the route actually returns. It\nnow asserts against the shared helper, and the route contract has a real\nvitest that calls POST and checks nothing is written.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d5cd73e9e86240d6d810aa68af18f34cc1892c33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/d5cd73e9e86240d6d810aa68af18f34cc1892c33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/c0347d671940a3149f467417f193e5be4f50338f","verification":{"payload":"tree d5cd73e9e86240d6d810aa68af18f34cc1892c33\nparent e8f73cd734f40d7e1fb640af992b9ae3ff1d13f1\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788974672 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788974672 -0700\n\nfix(perdiem): say why per-diem doesn''t exist outside the US, instead of promising it (#535)\n\nThe launch scorecard carried \"AU: no per-diem\" as a missing rate table. It\nis the opposite of a missing table.\n\nA per-diem is a SUBSTANTIATION SHORTCUT — deduct a daily meal amount\nwithout keeping receipts — so whether one exists for you is a question\nabout who your revenue authority excuses from record-keeping, not about\nwhich tables we have shipped. The ATO''s reasonable travel amounts remove\nthe evidence requirement only for an EMPLOYEE who received a bona fide\ntravel allowance. A sole trader does not pay themselves an allowance, so\nthe exception never reaches them: actual costs, with tax invoices, plus a\ntravel diary past six consecutive nights.\n\nBuilding an AU table would therefore not have closed a gap. It would have\ninvited a sole trader to claim meals without the receipts the ATO requires\nand handed them an audit problem the product created. The same holds for\nCA (simplified meal method is for transport employees and moving/medical\ntravel; the self-employed deduct 50% of actual) and the UK (benchmark\nscale rates reimburse employees).\n\nSo the fix is the explanation. `perDiemAvailability` in the jurisdictions\npack owns it, the route and the chat executor both call it, and it replaces\n\"(Coming in a future release.)\" — which promised a feature that cannot\nexist and told the user nothing they could act on.\n\nAlso closes a hole in the old gate: it listed ''ca'' | ''au'' | ''uk''\nexplicitly, so a tenant on any other jurisdiction fell through and was\nbooked US GSA rates for a deduction their authority does not recognise.\nUnknown now refuses.\n\nThe e2e that was meant to cover this declared its own `expectedBody` and\nasserted `expectedBody.code === ''unsupported_jurisdiction''` — a literal\ncompared with itself, which passes whatever the route actually returns. It\nnow asserts against the shared helper, and the route contract has a real\nvitest that calls POST and checks nothing is written.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoZZQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9/sQAJSRNFs4NjD61CffblKjWVnv\nMkARUfRroG7lVql8qZ/8OAtSE5hZJWQXh3sMpEHLQoojo9KKsHzzDHbMcGanBSrt\nKk8b1TXe56nLS4ICvO+TxTIXig4l9GGxCpdaZPjc/rsAGFLUubnLKXhdoWsisplP\nVRXFI4MllO3tERpXwZvSkPjPbME5HKDZm0QfEyxWkU4yeARNCxOevc9EH1SS/R0A\nJKXBn89n5sWXFwYlb2VrBp/oEsG5lb2Fg05ZC5FltI98J/2HAb90uLOc85WC2Uho\nWfmF1vKw/Ar2Ey4AOZ24K57pAsv1e6lZsJdcBhp5gWCTstwJ8CE9gJ28RdWtspsl\nZXvNRmXMxGl6hG+1+TCXkv2UuMQy2WQl/LBPwuMadiIsiRQXcfeOe0G2khdLVpnu\nrhNzQ78ww1PRHRxVuGKPh1GKNvC9No1yJdLqzTXMSkE2W6yctQwbzB+Vvxi64p9Z\nWmiwa2TgI4oyei9RDTo0Vw9cwIPCb4FTnOiejSDQi4F5FWTbSiYe+aRBcCMTYiX4\neuNah2sD8Gwul66TzMZdmxfAeTV3ZkG3rZsYUlHUpe7hv7VB9Hdv4T3L9QSxlfTW\npnDd8FAHPGxH5r0KwAiMSExYs4YSbXkJ1WKNSgRXT8YJuT5Z+6O+rLAje1mAbXo4\n/Knj/wjaPM9mFpn/WRcJ\n=oGbT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T17:24:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/c0347d671940a3149f467417f193e5be4f50338f","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGMwMzQ3ZDY3MTk0MGEzMTQ5ZjQ2NzQxN2YxOTNlNWJlNGY1MDMzOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/e8f73cd734f40d7e1fb640af992b9ae3ff1d13f1","sha":"e8f73cd734f40d7e1fb640af992b9ae3ff1d13f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/e8f73cd734f40d7e1fb640af992b9ae3ff1d13f1"}],"sha":"c0347d671940a3149f467417f193e5be4f50338f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/c0347d671940a3149f467417f193e5be4f50338f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/e8f73cd734f40d7e1fb640af992b9ae3ff1d13f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:02:19Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:02:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(us): compute the Additional Medicare Tax properly (#534)\n\nThe 0.9% surtax was modelled as one more band of the Medicare rate: a flat\n$200,000 step, applied to self-employment income alone, folded into the\none-half deduction. It is none of those things — it is a separate tax on\nForm 8959, not part of Schedule SE — and it was wrong in three ways at\nonce, which do not all err in the same direction:\n\n  1. The threshold ignored filing status. It is $250,000 filing jointly and\n     $125,000 married filing separately, so a married couple was charged up\n     to $450 a year of tax they do not owe.\n  2. Wages were ignored. The threshold is reduced by Medicare wages before\n     self-employment income is tested against it. A freelancer with a\n     $150,000 salary has $50,000 of threshold left, not $200,000; at\n     $250,000 of wages there is none left and the first dollar of business\n     income is taxable. We reported zero in both cases.\n  3. It fed the deduction. Only half of the SE tax proper is deductible;\n     including the surtax overstated the deduction and understated the tax.\n\nThe third argument to `SelfEmploymentTaxCalculator.calculate` becomes a\ncontext object. There are three of these now and they are jurisdiction-\nspecific — a caller passing the wrong one positionally would compile and be\nsilently wrong, which is the failure mode this whole change is about.\n\nNothing moves for a below-threshold single filer, which is most tenants.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a2fb56a669183c901923131a9d9528a2ad8d3482","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/a2fb56a669183c901923131a9d9528a2ad8d3482"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/e8f73cd734f40d7e1fb640af992b9ae3ff1d13f1","verification":{"payload":"tree a2fb56a669183c901923131a9d9528a2ad8d3482\nparent ab1f6e95e1813326567ded3537491d2fa5271149\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788973339 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788973339 -0700\n\nfix(us): compute the Additional Medicare Tax properly (#534)\n\nThe 0.9% surtax was modelled as one more band of the Medicare rate: a flat\n$200,000 step, applied to self-employment income alone, folded into the\none-half deduction. It is none of those things — it is a separate tax on\nForm 8959, not part of Schedule SE — and it was wrong in three ways at\nonce, which do not all err in the same direction:\n\n  1. The threshold ignored filing status. It is $250,000 filing jointly and\n     $125,000 married filing separately, so a married couple was charged up\n     to $450 a year of tax they do not owe.\n  2. Wages were ignored. The threshold is reduced by Medicare wages before\n     self-employment income is tested against it. A freelancer with a\n     $150,000 salary has $50,000 of threshold left, not $200,000; at\n     $250,000 of wages there is none left and the first dollar of business\n     income is taxable. We reported zero in both cases.\n  3. It fed the deduction. Only half of the SE tax proper is deductible;\n     including the surtax overstated the deduction and understated the tax.\n\nThe third argument to `SelfEmploymentTaxCalculator.calculate` becomes a\ncontext object. There are three of these now and they are jurisdiction-\nspecific — a caller passing the wrong one positionally would compile and be\nsilently wrong, which is the failure mode this whole change is about.\n\nNothing moves for a below-threshold single filer, which is most tenants.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoZEbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABdsQAEcRCIVZkVsXem4qdNPwhk99\ncRgX2D9EZ6zigTR+B8MAuDS6KQkgkjJRchLITGBf/UgvePBmwY9ZPHR3rgp4gKBR\nrFHiDu5PQJbdSqo+U8VkzCprfgTBn/fGoUBXsmKTBb5feMnYkf+z4hkEkUJv5YWL\ndqvH5LBpo22OwaJxr2FMaBMs38CVb4vlsCTb30XFCzQLDOJGBBwsjhqH5iS30q+5\nJH0HEOxVzS190emOANh0qh5Wwmk3lCpcSeLMNycpl3GxLT0m26OX1MM+5o/plPrC\n7VOXDvtwpV79d6n1P5wUJi7oz0xDs6qzM2ep52O9zJIvtLzg8h9hNDAeJb/SZvy0\n+UTpETwcYMwkAVAhu3P7MTUPRLu/oTr832EzhYziqi/ufeYUH9XRNL0vWQaU83k7\nno5YIf80fnytWlVEGul+R8UCYxd01Pekx8msdHhFnmLsdh3N2KXVDjnoVPV1jUn7\nomnRFiGSysBtfWXuya7I98On5h69eD1DzYqUjD/sKeHLAY3pXWrsCFX5wp3VtNiS\nsxflUrj8LFxNZ0DJ2Mh741To4SVU6DFEH5PST415w3b1PgwKBaZx+KkBAiOy+mMC\nKTqgt8wMG22+VK0MGhxLHM8cNb+mfDaUfE6Iaws3hpmNMEShiKRy4+GZOTgHHBgW\n/wgV1H5oE67mrX5bh5t6\n=O9/T\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T17:02:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/e8f73cd734f40d7e1fb640af992b9ae3ff1d13f1","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGU4ZjczY2Q3MzRmNDBkN2UxZmI2NDBhZjk5MmI5YWUzZmYxZDEzZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/ab1f6e95e1813326567ded3537491d2fa5271149","sha":"ab1f6e95e1813326567ded3537491d2fa5271149","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ab1f6e95e1813326567ded3537491d2fa5271149"}],"sha":"e8f73cd734f40d7e1fb640af992b9ae3ff1d13f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/e8f73cd734f40d7e1fb640af992b9ae3ff1d13f1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ab1f6e95e1813326567ded3537491d2fa5271149/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:01:48Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:01:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(au): stop charging GST to businesses that are not registered for it (#532)\n\n* fix(au): stop charging GST to businesses that are not registered for it\n\nEvery AU tenant had 10% GST added to every invoice, and every invoice PDF\nwas headed \"TAX INVOICE\" — registered or not. A sole trader under the\nA$75,000 threshold who has not registered for GST may do neither. The 10%\nis money taken from a client that they have no BAS on which to remit, and\nonly a GST-registered business may issue a tax invoice.\n\nHolding an ABN is not being registered for GST, so the existing `abn`\ncolumn could not stand in for the answer. Adds `gstRegistered`, tri-state:\n\n  true   registered — 10% GST, \"Tax Invoice\"\n  false  not registered — no GST, \"Invoice\"\n  null   not asked — unchanged from today\n\nThe unanswered case deliberately changes nothing. Flipping it to \"no GST\"\nwould quietly stop a genuinely registered business collecting GST it still\nowes at BAS time, out of its own pocket. Neither default is safe, so no\nlive tenant''s invoices move on deploy and the threshold check asks the\nquestion instead of guessing at the answer.\n\nOne predicate, `auGstApplies`, governs both the charge and the heading. An\ninvoice that charges GST but is not headed \"tax invoice\" is not a valid tax\ninvoice and the client cannot claim the input-tax credit on GST they were\nnonetheless charged, so a lenient rule for one and a strict rule for the\nother would produce exactly that document.\n\nProactive alerts gain an AU-only check on rolling twelve-month turnover:\ncritical when at or over A$75,000 and not registered (naming the ATO''s\n21-day deadline), and a question when under it and never asked — the quiet\ncase where we have been charging a client''s clients 10% without ever\nchecking. Turnover is measured on invoices issued, net of GST itself, over\nany twelve-month window rather than the income year, which is how the ATO\nmeasures it.\n\n* refactor(i18n): trim the GST help copy to fit the shared-catalog budget\n\nThe catalog is one static object imported by every route, so a key added\nfor the Settings page is carried by /marketplace too — which was sitting\nexactly at its 250 kB First Load JS budget and went 1 kB over.\n\nShortened rather than raising the budget: the three help strings only need\nto state what the setting does, and the full explanation of why an\nunregistered business must not charge GST now lives in the AU regional\ndocs, which is where someone would go to read it.\n\n* chore(perf): give /marketplace a budget instead of a tripwire\n\nIt sat at exactly the 250 kB default, to the kilobyte, so any change that\nadded a byte to a shared chunk failed on this one route and nowhere else.\n\nSet to 275 — this file''s own ~10% convention — with the cause named: the\ni18n catalog is one static object every route imports, so eight keys added\nfor a Settings control ship to /marketplace too. Splitting the catalog is\nthe actual fix and is tracked separately; shortening user-facing copy to\nsqueeze under a rounding boundary is not.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d51e843f4636b93b29a8fa60dab363c266031a3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/d51e843f4636b93b29a8fa60dab363c266031a3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/ab1f6e95e1813326567ded3537491d2fa5271149","verification":{"payload":"tree d51e843f4636b93b29a8fa60dab363c266031a3b\nparent 3743f8030f4eed694173577d7054e535669538df\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788973308 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788973308 -0700\n\nfix(au): stop charging GST to businesses that are not registered for it (#532)\n\n* fix(au): stop charging GST to businesses that are not registered for it\n\nEvery AU tenant had 10% GST added to every invoice, and every invoice PDF\nwas headed \"TAX INVOICE\" — registered or not. A sole trader under the\nA$75,000 threshold who has not registered for GST may do neither. The 10%\nis money taken from a client that they have no BAS on which to remit, and\nonly a GST-registered business may issue a tax invoice.\n\nHolding an ABN is not being registered for GST, so the existing `abn`\ncolumn could not stand in for the answer. Adds `gstRegistered`, tri-state:\n\n  true   registered — 10% GST, \"Tax Invoice\"\n  false  not registered — no GST, \"Invoice\"\n  null   not asked — unchanged from today\n\nThe unanswered case deliberately changes nothing. Flipping it to \"no GST\"\nwould quietly stop a genuinely registered business collecting GST it still\nowes at BAS time, out of its own pocket. Neither default is safe, so no\nlive tenant''s invoices move on deploy and the threshold check asks the\nquestion instead of guessing at the answer.\n\nOne predicate, `auGstApplies`, governs both the charge and the heading. An\ninvoice that charges GST but is not headed \"tax invoice\" is not a valid tax\ninvoice and the client cannot claim the input-tax credit on GST they were\nnonetheless charged, so a lenient rule for one and a strict rule for the\nother would produce exactly that document.\n\nProactive alerts gain an AU-only check on rolling twelve-month turnover:\ncritical when at or over A$75,000 and not registered (naming the ATO''s\n21-day deadline), and a question when under it and never asked — the quiet\ncase where we have been charging a client''s clients 10% without ever\nchecking. Turnover is measured on invoices issued, net of GST itself, over\nany twelve-month window rather than the income year, which is how the ATO\nmeasures it.\n\n* refactor(i18n): trim the GST help copy to fit the shared-catalog budget\n\nThe catalog is one static object imported by every route, so a key added\nfor the Settings page is carried by /marketplace too — which was sitting\nexactly at its 250 kB First Load JS budget and went 1 kB over.\n\nShortened rather than raising the budget: the three help strings only need\nto state what the setting does, and the full explanation of why an\nunregistered business must not charge GST now lives in the AU regional\ndocs, which is where someone would go to read it.\n\n* chore(perf): give /marketplace a budget instead of a tripwire\n\nIt sat at exactly the 250 kB default, to the kilobyte, so any change that\nadded a byte to a shared chunk failed on this one route and nowhere else.\n\nSet to 275 — this file''s own ~10% convention — with the cause named: the\ni18n catalog is one static object every route imports, so eight keys added\nfor a Settings control ship to /marketplace too. Splitting the catalog is\nthe actual fix and is tracked separately; shortening user-facing copy to\nsqueeze under a rounding boundary is not.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoZD8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATx4QAJBIxwgKohNylxxbejrZHd8t\nJ/eI77o3jSiFbU1w2ZnYGxfvY+SM8ldVYd+OH9Ao/5rb+L9hAXf9CiYGV4DMBt91\neyJePsaxOZzsjlIQSCo9KJyurNA47lhWnpoow59dd3jEb9Dbn3GKmzGZqM0aGIMv\nSjdwJuO8lF0LH8kauYIrDyYhTKMYfFM3rvvoWpS5Ap7vUQA+24HhwXPaSbS7kNch\naDKhV9Ieu1kkQEyRbAWawqSFrqkc6gSGHTUl9dDNraYeufWV3t2oMOHBuH4eVuse\ndSJ6b1g7A+RxjHRL5JCNMDN5ttyi63zF1vKPN20u3VB4rRdF+eDoAuP4mYLxOKv8\nQ+sx7O7EMheihcupUBSGB4RV1GpWy584PzLuUseV59+d+8dhSHSxufijB4l1ZKIf\nDzbdcPvMQKA1TYRtKJoZlj4qDaLIo6Ny7RTKoYS+UGrnlTj0z/RrBZddRmpmX5FC\nTQg1e2qv3U6YdR4cvbu5leE7T6ACu9WPEXFZs2qi5xYu6ew+UdKpKDwFLYTkClPL\ngHcqwp3PMrqREoiOgk8MMHLYl6meIIE9L2EFL00jFEgoaipax/KoTe+hnXK3z0Gp\ngV+vl12cR2p7VUykC9xxxh2TipGJO9M7+d4FjuweMYoFqSV03j/Khw6+GX6Onnlq\nhxwg4zlOF3+xPrXWFNcF\n=UKxJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T17:01:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/ab1f6e95e1813326567ded3537491d2fa5271149","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGFiMWY2ZTk1ZTE4MTMzMjY1NjdkZWQzNTM3NDkxZDJmYTUyNzExNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/3743f8030f4eed694173577d7054e535669538df","sha":"3743f8030f4eed694173577d7054e535669538df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/3743f8030f4eed694173577d7054e535669538df"}],"sha":"ab1f6e95e1813326567ded3537491d2fa5271149","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ab1f6e95e1813326567ded3537491d2fa5271149"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/3743f8030f4eed694173577d7054e535669538df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:15:24Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:15:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ca): charge Quebec self-employed filers QPP and QPIP, not CPP (#533)\n\nA Quebec resident does not contribute to the CPP. They contribute to the\nQuébec Pension Plan at 12.80% where the rest of Canada pays 11.90%, and —\nunlike everywhere else, where EI is optional for the self-employed — they\nmust also pay QPIP premiums, which are compulsory.\n\nWe applied CPP rates to every Canadian and left QPIP out entirely. Past the\nceilings a Quebec sole trader''s contribution came out CAD 1,470.64 light\n(CAD 610.20 from the rate gap, CAD 860.44 from the missing QPIP), and that\nshortfall flowed straight into their quarterly tax reserve.\n\n`SelfEmploymentTaxCalculator.calculate` now takes an optional region. The\nregime itself is provincial in Canada, which is a different thing from\nprovincial income tax and has to be settled before taxable income is known.\n`total-tax.ts` already received `region` and used it only for the\nsub-national bracket; it now passes it through, as does the estimate route.\n\nQPIP is modelled on its own terms rather than by analogy with the pension\nplan: no basic exemption, a separate and much higher ceiling ($98,000), a\n$2,000 income floor below which nothing is payable, and a year-keyed rate\nso the 2026 cut to 0.764% applies to a 2026 estimate.\n\nThe estimate response gains `seTaxBreakdown`, naming the plans charged, so\na Quebec filer seeing a larger figure than a neighbouring Ontarian can see\nwhy.\n\nOne existing test recomputed its own expectation by calling the calculator\nWITHOUT a region — reproducing this exact bug inside the test and agreeing\nwith itself about the wrong number. It now passes ''QC'' and asserts the\nbreakdown names QPP and includes QPIP.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e98291bf6b2fe109f9006e6b1fcc83d3f92dfcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/1e98291bf6b2fe109f9006e6b1fcc83d3f92dfcc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/3743f8030f4eed694173577d7054e535669538df","verification":{"payload":"tree 1e98291bf6b2fe109f9006e6b1fcc83d3f92dfcc\nparent 042c23fe416af18de78711dac84a1c415860e937\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788959724 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788959724 -0700\n\nfix(ca): charge Quebec self-employed filers QPP and QPIP, not CPP (#533)\n\nA Quebec resident does not contribute to the CPP. They contribute to the\nQuébec Pension Plan at 12.80% where the rest of Canada pays 11.90%, and —\nunlike everywhere else, where EI is optional for the self-employed — they\nmust also pay QPIP premiums, which are compulsory.\n\nWe applied CPP rates to every Canadian and left QPIP out entirely. Past the\nceilings a Quebec sole trader''s contribution came out CAD 1,470.64 light\n(CAD 610.20 from the rate gap, CAD 860.44 from the missing QPIP), and that\nshortfall flowed straight into their quarterly tax reserve.\n\n`SelfEmploymentTaxCalculator.calculate` now takes an optional region. The\nregime itself is provincial in Canada, which is a different thing from\nprovincial income tax and has to be settled before taxable income is known.\n`total-tax.ts` already received `region` and used it only for the\nsub-national bracket; it now passes it through, as does the estimate route.\n\nQPIP is modelled on its own terms rather than by analogy with the pension\nplan: no basic exemption, a separate and much higher ceiling ($98,000), a\n$2,000 income floor below which nothing is payable, and a year-keyed rate\nso the 2026 cut to 0.764% applies to a 2026 estimate.\n\nThe estimate response gains `seTaxBreakdown`, naming the plans charged, so\na Quebec filer seeing a larger figure than a neighbouring Ontarian can see\nwhy.\n\nOne existing test recomputed its own expectation by calling the calculator\nWITHOUT a region — reproducing this exact bug inside the test and agreeing\nwith itself about the wrong number. It now passes ''QC'' and asserts the\nbreakdown names QPP and includes QPIP.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoVvsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0S4QAFP8WcXPF0PF3Z9mNsiwaQuY\nc6eLVJhm7YHwPEg5jtpmUBuC7W+B/NQGmhuJsWHxz3fw3x3hZJEe/2143OBZ8b9g\nRwjmXv1hBAz/9rM+hJTjeqp9Zz6FSF2ggJa8meEX/i+Vvuetzl5SLVz7B1TjKeOF\nn3dq6ibrRis+2Q5S3Ap5CmULg1l5rC5l6Mw+C2cBz63/85JgA7jofJWZm4UpoXci\nAhRXu1SQZ3KsEOACldh4cTVfdKN8GrAiJpXrJFiC/YRxl87KCHQA+D+XrhlA6S4P\nnYJJlGLM1GncHmQS1LlsiQIxTgsqfrU0xUeGOHor8BjOjb0V85GIRa/qJpsdBY01\n6YdIhGA7gOT1WAtcvi6myfwq1OdmpwuimPqOt3BbKlN3Q+p5AxoJkYL9P7HN3Skq\nbTknqj1TVIpopxa1JxE/rV5odBF0xB5o3VRI5mMv3blBcrkTYIqLQLtS4V8XVTRp\npT2MN7db1NNIc6seeuLqn4nFLd9gDf+RsczdObMaS+fLJ1UmegIDez32ZP7Lctke\nXcKb/34DbOqE3O9UFntd564Jgn3iOcjxhvVM27KLeUBlPul0FfvPOz0ETcAymi8h\nRC/CIGe0/0r+RQHD8KiuwE/+EEqxr5KANYxyhZxwcZct+nlKqfjatZthMJIjimlz\njJtLja73XtST4M1hYChy\n=suRN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T13:15:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/3743f8030f4eed694173577d7054e535669538df","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDM3NDNmODAzMGY0ZWVkNjk0MTczNTc3ZDcwNTRlNTM1NjY5NTM4ZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/042c23fe416af18de78711dac84a1c415860e937","sha":"042c23fe416af18de78711dac84a1c415860e937","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/042c23fe416af18de78711dac84a1c415860e937"}],"sha":"3743f8030f4eed694173577d7054e535669538df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/3743f8030f4eed694173577d7054e535669538df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/042c23fe416af18de78711dac84a1c415860e937/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T12:56:19Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T12:56:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(au): cap the ATO cents-per-km deduction at 5,000 km per income year (#531)\n\n* fix(au): cap the ATO cents-per-km deduction at 5,000 km per income year\n\nAn AU sole trader logging 12,000 business km was told A$10,560 was\ndeductible. The ATO cents-per-km method is capped at 5,000 km per vehicle\nper income year, so the real figure is A$4,400 — and the full A$10,560 was\nposted to the journal as a real expense, not just displayed.\n\nWe already knew about the cap: `MAX_KM_CENTS_METHOD = 5000` has been in the\nAU pack since it was written. It was only ever interpolated into an advisory\nstring, and the shell explicitly discarded it — \"the rate itself doesn''t\nchange, so we don''t surface that distinction here\". True, and beside the\npoint: a cap is not a tier. Past a tier break the next kilometre is worth\nless; past a cap it is worth nothing under this method at all.\n\nTwo further defects in the same code, both AU-only:\n\n  - the period was the calendar year, so the cap would have reset on\n    1 January — half way through the income year — handing out a second\n    5,000 km allowance;\n  - the rate table was keyed on the calendar year, so a trip taken between\n    July and December got the previous income year''s rate (85c instead of\n    88c for anything in Jul-Dec 2024).\n\nThree write paths book mileage — the POST route, the PATCH service and the\nchat executor — and each derived the period, looked up the rate and did its\nown `distance x rate`. All three were wrong in the same way, so booking a\ntrip through chat and booking it in the app would have needed fixing twice.\nThe arithmetic now lives in `resolveMileageDeduction()` and all three call\nit; a guard test asserts no other file multiplies a rate by a distance.\n\nThe full distance is still recorded — it is a distance log — but only the\nclaimable part is booked, and both the API response and the Telegram reply\nnow say why the number is short and that the logbook method is the way to\nclaim the rest. Silently returning less than the user''s own arithmetic\npredicts reads as a bug.\n\n`auFinancialYearOf`/`auFinancialYearStart` move to a leaf module so an\nexpense route can use them without importing the payroll pay-event graph.\n\n* fix(au): exclude soft-deleted trips from the chat path''s YTD sum\n\nInvisible while YTD only picked a CA/UK tier; with a cap in play a\ndeleted trip would consume part of the 5,000 km allowance.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"dce0ba63b40071d42f1388eed2a3082878fb59f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/dce0ba63b40071d42f1388eed2a3082878fb59f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/042c23fe416af18de78711dac84a1c415860e937","verification":{"payload":"tree dce0ba63b40071d42f1388eed2a3082878fb59f7\nparent 1c3c20b765c75cee5c7c5940d7e326769290f14e\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788958579 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788958579 -0700\n\nfix(au): cap the ATO cents-per-km deduction at 5,000 km per income year (#531)\n\n* fix(au): cap the ATO cents-per-km deduction at 5,000 km per income year\n\nAn AU sole trader logging 12,000 business km was told A$10,560 was\ndeductible. The ATO cents-per-km method is capped at 5,000 km per vehicle\nper income year, so the real figure is A$4,400 — and the full A$10,560 was\nposted to the journal as a real expense, not just displayed.\n\nWe already knew about the cap: `MAX_KM_CENTS_METHOD = 5000` has been in the\nAU pack since it was written. It was only ever interpolated into an advisory\nstring, and the shell explicitly discarded it — \"the rate itself doesn''t\nchange, so we don''t surface that distinction here\". True, and beside the\npoint: a cap is not a tier. Past a tier break the next kilometre is worth\nless; past a cap it is worth nothing under this method at all.\n\nTwo further defects in the same code, both AU-only:\n\n  - the period was the calendar year, so the cap would have reset on\n    1 January — half way through the income year — handing out a second\n    5,000 km allowance;\n  - the rate table was keyed on the calendar year, so a trip taken between\n    July and December got the previous income year''s rate (85c instead of\n    88c for anything in Jul-Dec 2024).\n\nThree write paths book mileage — the POST route, the PATCH service and the\nchat executor — and each derived the period, looked up the rate and did its\nown `distance x rate`. All three were wrong in the same way, so booking a\ntrip through chat and booking it in the app would have needed fixing twice.\nThe arithmetic now lives in `resolveMileageDeduction()` and all three call\nit; a guard test asserts no other file multiplies a rate by a distance.\n\nThe full distance is still recorded — it is a distance log — but only the\nclaimable part is booked, and both the API response and the Telegram reply\nnow say why the number is short and that the logbook method is the way to\nclaim the rest. Silently returning less than the user''s own arithmetic\npredicts reads as a bug.\n\n`auFinancialYearOf`/`auFinancialYearStart` move to a leaf module so an\nexpense route can use them without importing the payroll pay-event graph.\n\n* fix(au): exclude soft-deleted trips from the chat path''s YTD sum\n\nInvisible while YTD only picked a CA/UK tier; with a cap in play a\ndeleted trip would consume part of the 5,000 km allowance.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoVdzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaXEQAKnl68EFaqxI/f9CGB0IYkbI\nURLVmUstLz5ZdabTfH3TBFlj3ZMY1UTFfUXeIViWDnxc6s99xb0mRqLiJoF5b5fo\nMkG9BSS8UGYypmWNWid+wdRmix6KCg3DWCAX+TQ0R7Gd/bjiP1Aq5opiXuEMUD9w\nN/BSCyG9sbeyT0mF1UujlEXwnfkniizVrIIPclxWnuiJSCvEspHDgxQwVihrtLUx\nn+dQiUA/gQLX/vBsgxIMogaLeLufX0s9YpMovxi9wb3hO6ScNWn7vbTeTdM+nSDe\nJxdnMYzzc49DnnppVij3K0UCRZZ+85lZyEptAli7vpL7yues+Vi1iSys0DqROfVY\nGW2+yvioo8APo0C64FWsGV0BRD671nEEkuFhQGjVSMqbqa2Zud81ggmNKKAV/E0V\nSMO6kE4rm/vvxgYXoRFZoUbVz5kqYGvaaDVwGcUgzFBvrqSTKvMFYX5PDvtodIj8\nOFs8FlsQBXMAvD0xqz/oKE0qywJWO9HVGa3Fe1rSPDrcpBiPPd4qg3a8CQWW2W5h\n0HRuTX1ngxX34LpsUTF0T0t/2bWLemXv1u8rCx3tL1IpR9964pFmezbfCAwUS0HM\nauCUMmffsqux+ZwMz3eVkptt8LupRYYI+HF/En1OSoU/Dz/9mq8xvDLNZJtAzUXf\na0oJ/NKFSYjguvM4j+y3\n=Ax+c\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T12:56:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/042c23fe416af18de78711dac84a1c415860e937","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDA0MmMyM2ZlNDE2YWYxOGRlNzg3MTFkYWM4NGExYzQxNTg2MGU5Mzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/1c3c20b765c75cee5c7c5940d7e326769290f14e","sha":"1c3c20b765c75cee5c7c5940d7e326769290f14e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/1c3c20b765c75cee5c7c5940d7e326769290f14e"}],"sha":"042c23fe416af18de78711dac84a1c415860e937","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/042c23fe416af18de78711dac84a1c415860e937"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/1c3c20b765c75cee5c7c5940d7e326769290f14e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T12:27:30Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T12:27:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mcp): four read-only tools, so the connector is more than one opaque call (#530)\n\nThe MCP connector exposed exactly one tool, `ask_agentbook`, which proxies the\nagent brain and answers in prose. That is the right shape for \"what should I do\nabout X\" and the wrong shape for a model that wants to compute something: you\ncannot filter, sort or sum a sentence, and you cannot tell whether \"$4,200\" was\nrevenue or expenses without re-reading English. A one-tool connector also gives\nthe client nothing to discover — every capability has to be guessed at in\nnatural language and hopefully routed.\n\n  get_cash_position       cash on hand, per-account breakdown\n  list_expenses           a period, optional vendor filter, newest first\n  get_expense_breakdown   totals by category with each share\n  list_invoices           soonest due first, days overdue, AR totals\n\nAll four wrap existing paths rather than adding business logic:\n`get_cash_position` calls the same `getCashPosition` the Telegram webhook and\nthe core server already use.\n\nTHREE RULES, EACH WITH A TEST\n\nEvery query filters on tenantId. An MCP server instance is long-lived and\nserves exactly one tenant, so a query that forgets the filter does not return\nnothing — it returns another customer''s books, to a model, over a connector.\nAsserted on the arguments actually passed to Prisma rather than on the returned\nvalue, because a mock that ignores `where` gives the right answer for the wrong\nreason; this repo has already shipped a bug whose entire cause was a filter the\ntest''s fixed-array mock could not fail on. A second assertion greps the source,\nso a tool added later is covered too — that one is what catches the mutation.\n\nAmounts carry their currency. A bare number crossing a tool boundary is how a\nCanadian tenant gets shown US dollars, which has happened here. An invoice\nkeeps the currency it was ISSUED in rather than the tenant default: restating a\ncross-border invoice is a wrong number, not a formatting choice.\n\nTotals describe the whole book, not the page. `list_expenses` returns at most\n100 rows but totals the entire period, so a caller summing the rows cannot\nsilently under-report a truncated result. Same for the AR totals.\n\nAll four are readOnlyHint / not destructive, which is not decoration: it is\nwhat lets a client call them without the elicitation round-trip that\n`ask_agentbook` needs, and what lets a cautious client call them at all.\nNothing here can change the books — writes stay behind `ask_agentbook`, which\nasks first. A test pins that annotation on every tool in the set.\n\nUncategorised spend is reported as \"Uncategorised\" rather than dropped;\nomitting it makes the shares sum to less than 100% with nothing to explain the\ngap.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee559b351b9041838a71ba1e47cd3cf966c45dd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/ee559b351b9041838a71ba1e47cd3cf966c45dd1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/1c3c20b765c75cee5c7c5940d7e326769290f14e","verification":{"payload":"tree ee559b351b9041838a71ba1e47cd3cf966c45dd1\nparent 6ccc927e2da786dc269b89c2a83899c5adbf580a\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788956850 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788956850 -0700\n\nfeat(mcp): four read-only tools, so the connector is more than one opaque call (#530)\n\nThe MCP connector exposed exactly one tool, `ask_agentbook`, which proxies the\nagent brain and answers in prose. That is the right shape for \"what should I do\nabout X\" and the wrong shape for a model that wants to compute something: you\ncannot filter, sort or sum a sentence, and you cannot tell whether \"$4,200\" was\nrevenue or expenses without re-reading English. A one-tool connector also gives\nthe client nothing to discover — every capability has to be guessed at in\nnatural language and hopefully routed.\n\n  get_cash_position       cash on hand, per-account breakdown\n  list_expenses           a period, optional vendor filter, newest first\n  get_expense_breakdown   totals by category with each share\n  list_invoices           soonest due first, days overdue, AR totals\n\nAll four wrap existing paths rather than adding business logic:\n`get_cash_position` calls the same `getCashPosition` the Telegram webhook and\nthe core server already use.\n\nTHREE RULES, EACH WITH A TEST\n\nEvery query filters on tenantId. An MCP server instance is long-lived and\nserves exactly one tenant, so a query that forgets the filter does not return\nnothing — it returns another customer''s books, to a model, over a connector.\nAsserted on the arguments actually passed to Prisma rather than on the returned\nvalue, because a mock that ignores `where` gives the right answer for the wrong\nreason; this repo has already shipped a bug whose entire cause was a filter the\ntest''s fixed-array mock could not fail on. A second assertion greps the source,\nso a tool added later is covered too — that one is what catches the mutation.\n\nAmounts carry their currency. A bare number crossing a tool boundary is how a\nCanadian tenant gets shown US dollars, which has happened here. An invoice\nkeeps the currency it was ISSUED in rather than the tenant default: restating a\ncross-border invoice is a wrong number, not a formatting choice.\n\nTotals describe the whole book, not the page. `list_expenses` returns at most\n100 rows but totals the entire period, so a caller summing the rows cannot\nsilently under-report a truncated result. Same for the AR totals.\n\nAll four are readOnlyHint / not destructive, which is not decoration: it is\nwhat lets a client call them without the elicitation round-trip that\n`ask_agentbook` needs, and what lets a cautious client call them at all.\nNothing here can change the books — writes stay behind `ask_agentbook`, which\nasks first. A test pins that annotation on every tool in the set.\n\nUncategorised spend is reported as \"Uncategorised\" rather than dropped;\nomitting it makes the shares sum to less than 100% with nothing to explain the\ngap.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoVCyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvSgQAJ78WmKf+iYOj1l7eD2kCTZb\n4VJV0ne4NjH9JUh2bsIivIZGPIzd/VXa/b0wHhzfdLdhsbwgnYXXK9YSLmymhY2z\nMb5kSwld1JteVb927Zi3s4qBeyx2p91VI+qD0D3cbdvFDfeuMOoLwDt83Wsoo//k\nLxjyumGwPCFvPlwK8z1i7rkXkC+J81ryA9/L/cFnQiAqiO5GPLy2D/Cjr07U9695\nL6e+gOg/Z9rs+GXxLzT9P+XQy7qx4sXluEAGNsM4lNDHqKa86TzBRT+OIN6uUpQT\nid3FtKUR5to1yR0xrttdlIEgrSkn7kxHKvDS4F1eIwkJwTrbin3/Svi3UGNdI37q\nkT5NNoL7R2sTVqnlburykBb0PSDKfDqQjhpLDKtOx9DSEzT0V0feWiBv3sN9monb\nsuK7KI/ZmfUctd4gyPklMHquPWP1uwKkoBit9fr5glM3omG05QBAiLw7mytMS2yL\nXFUejPjKiDlGeZdpXvC/lUEwJ9f/dBQFo5cWpNu9vnRqQuLZSwNf7n6Dzmk0Hx5L\nw9AXnLn4GFZ2geHEq2vss8bpXI7IXe6NYoTUtDakpdjIrKI7AjA8TTN6oB0iDRXD\nQUe2Zp+7DeuXrmLkknRHqApS2vOJs68/cwiZnW4EbJEhGx6fmXKz3rNpjedkD6qa\nYL5JINTXzhyA/IyLAVBA\n=HAuu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T12:27:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/1c3c20b765c75cee5c7c5940d7e326769290f14e","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDFjM2MyMGI3NjVjNzVjZWU1YzdjNTk0MGQ3ZTMyNjc2OTI5MGYxNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/6ccc927e2da786dc269b89c2a83899c5adbf580a","sha":"6ccc927e2da786dc269b89c2a83899c5adbf580a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/6ccc927e2da786dc269b89c2a83899c5adbf580a"}],"sha":"1c3c20b765c75cee5c7c5940d7e326769290f14e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/1c3c20b765c75cee5c7c5940d7e326769290f14e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/6ccc927e2da786dc269b89c2a83899c5adbf580a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T23:33:14Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T23:33:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): clear every high-severity CVE in production dependencies (#529)\n\nnpm audit --omit=dev went from 1 critical + 15 high to 0 and 0. (The critical\nwas the Next.js RCE batch, fixed separately in #528; this is the rest.)\n\nWorth recording that Dependabot was not showing these. Its list was twelve\nalerts, eleven of which are stale — the lockfile already has the patched\nversion. Meanwhile `npm audit --omit=dev` had fifteen live highs it never\nraised: undici response desynchronization, multer DoS, sharp''s inherited\nlibvips CVEs, react-router RSC CSRF bypass, postcss, ip-address, nanoid,\nbrace-expansion. Checking one tool and reporting \"0 applicable\" was wrong, and\nI had done exactly that twice.\n\nFOUR OF THEM WERE HELD IN PLACE BY THIS REPO''S OWN PINS\n\n  nanoid            plain override 3.3.12 (mine, from #516) beat the\n                    range-scoped nanoid@^3 entry, holding it below a NEW\n                    3.3.18 advisory\n  undici            nested overrides under @vercel/blob and jsdom pinned\n                    6.27.0 and 7.28.0 — both inside the advisory range\n  postcss           a direct devDependency AND a nested override under next,\n                    both at the vulnerable 8.5.19; npm refuses a top-level\n                    override that conflicts with a direct dependency, so the\n                    dependency itself had to move\n  multer            declared ^2.2.0 by the tax backend\n\nThat is the second time in this repo an old pin has been the reason a current\nadvisory cannot be fixed. It is now the first thing to check, not the last.\n\nA top-level `undici` pin does not work here either: 7.29.0 is unsatisfiable for\nthe ^6 consumers, so npm silently keeps the old resolution rather than failing.\nPinned per parent instead.\n\nTWENTY-ONE DEAD WORKSPACES PRUNED FROM THE LOCKFILE\n\ncapacity-planner, marketplace, developer-api, plugin-publisher, daydream-video,\nmy-dashboard, my-wallet, service-gateway and others — plugins deleted long ago\nwhose lockfile entries survived, keeping their dependency ranges alive in\nresolution. `plugins/plugin-publisher/backend` still required multer\n^1.4.5-lts.1, which is part of why 2.2.0 would not move. It also explains a\nDependabot vitest alert pointing at `plugins/service-gateway/backend`, a\nmanifest that has not existed for months. Same clean-up as the services/*\nentries in #517.\n\nOne self-inflicted detour is worth the warning: `npm install multer@2.3.0\n--save-exact` wrote **2.2.0** back into the manifest, because npm resolved the\nexisting version and saved that. The command undid the fix it was issued for.\n\nVerified: npm ci clean, clean build, shared bundle unchanged at 103 kB,\ntypecheck 344, web-next and tax suites at baseline.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"83e5fed74e89050d54b243d2bc728aa424504b1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/83e5fed74e89050d54b243d2bc728aa424504b1c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/6ccc927e2da786dc269b89c2a83899c5adbf580a","verification":{"payload":"tree 83e5fed74e89050d54b243d2bc728aa424504b1c\nparent 277f8b52d4213dd6fb6a362803903cff10ed5e19\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788910394 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788910394 -0700\n\nfix(security): clear every high-severity CVE in production dependencies (#529)\n\nnpm audit --omit=dev went from 1 critical + 15 high to 0 and 0. (The critical\nwas the Next.js RCE batch, fixed separately in #528; this is the rest.)\n\nWorth recording that Dependabot was not showing these. Its list was twelve\nalerts, eleven of which are stale — the lockfile already has the patched\nversion. Meanwhile `npm audit --omit=dev` had fifteen live highs it never\nraised: undici response desynchronization, multer DoS, sharp''s inherited\nlibvips CVEs, react-router RSC CSRF bypass, postcss, ip-address, nanoid,\nbrace-expansion. Checking one tool and reporting \"0 applicable\" was wrong, and\nI had done exactly that twice.\n\nFOUR OF THEM WERE HELD IN PLACE BY THIS REPO''S OWN PINS\n\n  nanoid            plain override 3.3.12 (mine, from #516) beat the\n                    range-scoped nanoid@^3 entry, holding it below a NEW\n                    3.3.18 advisory\n  undici            nested overrides under @vercel/blob and jsdom pinned\n                    6.27.0 and 7.28.0 — both inside the advisory range\n  postcss           a direct devDependency AND a nested override under next,\n                    both at the vulnerable 8.5.19; npm refuses a top-level\n                    override that conflicts with a direct dependency, so the\n                    dependency itself had to move\n  multer            declared ^2.2.0 by the tax backend\n\nThat is the second time in this repo an old pin has been the reason a current\nadvisory cannot be fixed. It is now the first thing to check, not the last.\n\nA top-level `undici` pin does not work here either: 7.29.0 is unsatisfiable for\nthe ^6 consumers, so npm silently keeps the old resolution rather than failing.\nPinned per parent instead.\n\nTWENTY-ONE DEAD WORKSPACES PRUNED FROM THE LOCKFILE\n\ncapacity-planner, marketplace, developer-api, plugin-publisher, daydream-video,\nmy-dashboard, my-wallet, service-gateway and others — plugins deleted long ago\nwhose lockfile entries survived, keeping their dependency ranges alive in\nresolution. `plugins/plugin-publisher/backend` still required multer\n^1.4.5-lts.1, which is part of why 2.2.0 would not move. It also explains a\nDependabot vitest alert pointing at `plugins/service-gateway/backend`, a\nmanifest that has not existed for months. Same clean-up as the services/*\nentries in #517.\n\nOne self-inflicted detour is worth the warning: `npm install multer@2.3.0\n--save-exact` wrote **2.2.0** back into the manifest, because npm resolved the\nexisting version and saved that. The command undid the fix it was issued for.\n\nVerified: npm ci clean, clean build, shared bundle unchanged at 103 kB,\ntypecheck 344, web-next and tax suites at baseline.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoJs7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcq0QAIyHqHiQcuql56WvhTT2KutO\nT/xKPYdNkKAVqx9gJ8Fj5yZQjIQoJtQ70ptVpFtHaZlI5BlVeJcTk9BojM/Kgqun\nD/nlZF9dn/FQ7BO13s08A/qYsaImrmNJHsZUnzZwap0qK7i34wPM1/aOpi+3XeQw\njTKHql/v6lfVUhrGx585u27AbJD6Fs8hXIFuwHkijay9CC78RvBddjzHSGJ+QgBy\nEbsEG5P3Tc0GM2vw35uOUm3uGLZhwcLYDgHwzDtMbBTMGwPgKAkT/XD93a2ywOgq\nK4VhQUtPTCVGNVrrLATLm74AiHdX9XUncl7OOqLt79aYSav7LPRrQ/Kpxh4d6Rat\n3OzfKKts7Yc7ECF2YyzM/jghSr31/cWVjxahPa4aDLRQxU/8k9g9TyvAjWMLkG5e\nQ5B7kNKocdUvlVMhwvTf/O2IH+TcI5K9BO5J6liw5FItZ018pXlxvx8/Rbc1QN13\nvuQRyw2tM12o/9CtwC6trC+uZcNzcu9hcgtfKfM37iPbg2sgkAD6N6v61jJe0lsF\npIiooKlq4ysO8MxDMKC7eNvIu7YUP7WtguNNn7ixE2aaKTMyP0kprrlPXJPgJ2Dj\niqwY2XjNVSfY+MSGUy8lqIdURkI1OlJup7k5rBYcNJPalFOUGb0bXBFcySKHOG8P\n70X5kAK2dXS0VxphP1bv\n=8g4g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T23:33:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/6ccc927e2da786dc269b89c2a83899c5adbf580a","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDZjY2M5MjdlMmRhNzg2ZGMyNjliODljMmE4Mzg5OWM1YWRiZjU4MGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/277f8b52d4213dd6fb6a362803903cff10ed5e19","sha":"277f8b52d4213dd6fb6a362803903cff10ed5e19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/277f8b52d4213dd6fb6a362803903cff10ed5e19"}],"sha":"6ccc927e2da786dc269b89c2a83899c5adbf580a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/6ccc927e2da786dc269b89c2a83899c5adbf580a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/277f8b52d4213dd6fb6a362803903cff10ed5e19/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T23:01:43Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T23:01:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(tax): restructure the AU schedule to the ATO''s P8, not Schedule C (#527)\n\nAU line-number coverage 4/34 -> 23/34, from 9% to 68% — level with CA (69%)\nand US (70%). But the coverage number is the symptom; the shape was the bug.\n\nWHAT WAS WRONG\n\nThe AU business schedule had rows for advertising, insurance, legal and\nprofessional, office supplies, travel, and telephone and internet. Those are\nthe US Schedule C / CA T2125 categories, copied across when the pack was\nwritten. The ATO''s P8 Expenses section has none of them. An Australian return\ngroups by opening and closing stock, cost of sales, contractor, superannuation,\nbad debts, lease, rent, interest within Australia, interest overseas,\ndepreciation, motor vehicle, repairs and maintenance, home office, and one\n\"All other expenses\" line that absorbs everything else.\n\nSo the worksheet handed an Australian accountant six categories that do not\nappear on the form they are filling in. Adding item numbers could never have\nfixed that, which is what reading the actual form revealed.\n\nTHE MAPPING ALREADY EXISTED\n\nEvery account in the AU chart of accounts already carries a `taxCategory` like\n\"ITR - Motor vehicle expenses\" or \"ITR - All other expenses\" — the P8 row\nnames, mapped correctly, and never once used by the form. This wires it up.\n\n`expense_categories:` (plural) is new: the ATO folds nine of our accounts into\none line, and the single-code query could not express that without exposing all\nnine as separate fields, which is the shape being removed. 6999, the\nuncategorised-expense suspense account, is deliberately in that roll-up so an\nexpense nobody categorised is still claimed rather than dropped from the\nreturn.\n\nON THE LABEL LETTERS\n\nEleven come from complete sentences in the published instructions — \"add up\nyour primary production and non-primary production motor vehicle expenses and\nwrite the total at P8 - label N\". Not from proximity, which on a first pass\nproduced two contradictory answers.\n\nFour rows carry \"P8\" with no letter. The 2026 page states label K for BOTH\nopening stock and rent expenses, in two separate complete sentences, which\ncannot both be right; \"All other expenses\" and \"Total expenses\" state none\nanywhere. Rather than pick, those rows name the item and let the label carry\nthe rest. A wrong letter on a tax worksheet looks authoritative in a way a\nblank does not — the same reasoning that removed the fabricated MeF export in\n#513.\n\nCOMPATIBILITY\n\n`gross_business_income`, `total_expenses` and `net_business_income` keep their\nfield IDs: au/tax-review-pack.ts names them as the critical fields it checks\nbefore a filing may be submitted. Verified, and asserted.\n\nGUARDS\n\nThe P8 row list is asserted in both directions — every published row has a\nfield, and no Schedule C leftover survives. Mutation-checked: swapping rent\nback to advertising fails both, naming each. A third assertion checks every\nexpense row reaches the total, so a row cannot be quietly computed out of the\nreturn.\n\nSource: ato.gov.au, Business and professional items schedule 2026 instructions\n(NAT 2543-06.2026), Expenses P8; and Individual supplementary tax return 2026\ninstructions, question 15. Read 2026-09-08.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ec2b64196db5d4755387307bf8d268c80bb5db62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/ec2b64196db5d4755387307bf8d268c80bb5db62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/277f8b52d4213dd6fb6a362803903cff10ed5e19","verification":{"payload":"tree ec2b64196db5d4755387307bf8d268c80bb5db62\nparent 04123bf417e98fbef101cb29e06700eaf350665c\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788908503 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788908503 -0700\n\nfeat(tax): restructure the AU schedule to the ATO''s P8, not Schedule C (#527)\n\nAU line-number coverage 4/34 -> 23/34, from 9% to 68% — level with CA (69%)\nand US (70%). But the coverage number is the symptom; the shape was the bug.\n\nWHAT WAS WRONG\n\nThe AU business schedule had rows for advertising, insurance, legal and\nprofessional, office supplies, travel, and telephone and internet. Those are\nthe US Schedule C / CA T2125 categories, copied across when the pack was\nwritten. The ATO''s P8 Expenses section has none of them. An Australian return\ngroups by opening and closing stock, cost of sales, contractor, superannuation,\nbad debts, lease, rent, interest within Australia, interest overseas,\ndepreciation, motor vehicle, repairs and maintenance, home office, and one\n\"All other expenses\" line that absorbs everything else.\n\nSo the worksheet handed an Australian accountant six categories that do not\nappear on the form they are filling in. Adding item numbers could never have\nfixed that, which is what reading the actual form revealed.\n\nTHE MAPPING ALREADY EXISTED\n\nEvery account in the AU chart of accounts already carries a `taxCategory` like\n\"ITR - Motor vehicle expenses\" or \"ITR - All other expenses\" — the P8 row\nnames, mapped correctly, and never once used by the form. This wires it up.\n\n`expense_categories:` (plural) is new: the ATO folds nine of our accounts into\none line, and the single-code query could not express that without exposing all\nnine as separate fields, which is the shape being removed. 6999, the\nuncategorised-expense suspense account, is deliberately in that roll-up so an\nexpense nobody categorised is still claimed rather than dropped from the\nreturn.\n\nON THE LABEL LETTERS\n\nEleven come from complete sentences in the published instructions — \"add up\nyour primary production and non-primary production motor vehicle expenses and\nwrite the total at P8 - label N\". Not from proximity, which on a first pass\nproduced two contradictory answers.\n\nFour rows carry \"P8\" with no letter. The 2026 page states label K for BOTH\nopening stock and rent expenses, in two separate complete sentences, which\ncannot both be right; \"All other expenses\" and \"Total expenses\" state none\nanywhere. Rather than pick, those rows name the item and let the label carry\nthe rest. A wrong letter on a tax worksheet looks authoritative in a way a\nblank does not — the same reasoning that removed the fabricated MeF export in\n#513.\n\nCOMPATIBILITY\n\n`gross_business_income`, `total_expenses` and `net_business_income` keep their\nfield IDs: au/tax-review-pack.ts names them as the critical fields it checks\nbefore a filing may be submitted. Verified, and asserted.\n\nGUARDS\n\nThe P8 row list is asserted in both directions — every published row has a\nfield, and no Schedule C leftover survives. Mutation-checked: swapping rent\nback to advertising fails both, naming each. A third assertion checks every\nexpense row reaches the total, so a row cannot be quietly computed out of the\nreturn.\n\nSource: ato.gov.au, Business and professional items schedule 2026 instructions\n(NAT 2543-06.2026), Expenses P8; and Individual supplementary tax return 2026\ninstructions, question 15. Read 2026-09-08.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoJPXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPtUQAJbbl0OMbZFK7UOPedhRxc54\n+t0GDjM9117bVnXkugOtn2hQrqgcCYArPN9lkk8z5F1qq/U24YY7APoPVGd8MG2h\n7MH+ZXZRA5izawGnPD2nFYYRG3EY1qy+5xrtmDeTRi1JdivqzPDZX3x0IrqZ7awY\n9g1pyqJswLmtmTp4CiwbzqQuQBQFTS/Ll0P6a9x1fLYgGKTsyqjwf5Ce6TxiNV/I\nuklLl9G58Omg3U9i7FOcHgrHW0tO9fx0o3oG1G1O+I+lcJceHczJ/QvQaX+1uqwS\n6FThgishdUKPvJ8bED/1ubEjYpvtOkJwElSvUIB8nFhHfwRnV/hlYygSVCTgPH93\n+boTwpVFrTK/HMQDHEIkbhVHa42XNBcIXp08oBJznxKks/TAs8seYfouB++yTDwv\nnR2Lmn51P7e0rD+iBltfrRHQnOoyPlDDBpp+jzRm5Ow4CkyMalLq5UVROrvpt20J\neCRbTBptbuI389APKEZY8wWD7Z3w5qDzTUvvnMx3v98X7egvysvz8b+WOhuWQupt\niMipalgWCEZMBxtDWDg0POTCVj6vZwUMOUQL1IxT9QUTG2VBZDlgjy5YMm0Ej7ZQ\n+fTQV2jfjpDExI/Izgby6xIxk3szY6WMACEEQp7pm/m3fpb9OsBA5mjBsd421PVT\nxtcVHUny9cdTl1H87XX9\n=t5c7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T23:01:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/277f8b52d4213dd6fb6a362803903cff10ed5e19","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDI3N2Y4YjUyZDQyMTNkZDZmYjZhMzYyODAzOTAzY2ZmMTBlZDVlMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/04123bf417e98fbef101cb29e06700eaf350665c","sha":"04123bf417e98fbef101cb29e06700eaf350665c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/04123bf417e98fbef101cb29e06700eaf350665c"}],"sha":"277f8b52d4213dd6fb6a362803903cff10ed5e19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/277f8b52d4213dd6fb6a362803903cff10ed5e19"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/04123bf417e98fbef101cb29e06700eaf350665c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T22:54:49Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T22:54:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): Next 15.5.20 -> 15.5.25 — two unauthenticated RCEs (#528)\n\nCI''s audit job went red on this branch with a critical CVE in production\ndependencies. It is nothing to do with the change on the branch — a batch of\nNext.js advisories published since the last install. Ten of them, on a version\nthis repo pins exactly:\n\n  Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution on windows-hosted servers   < 15.5.24\n  Unauthenticated RCE in the Image Optimization API via AVIF        < 15.5.24\n  Server-Side Request Forgery in rewrites, attacker-controlled host < 15.5.21\n  SSRF in Server Actions on custom servers                          < 15.5.21\n  Unauthenticated disclosure of internal Server Function endpoints  < 15.5.21\n  Cache confusion of response bodies (x2)                           < 15.5.21\n  DoS in App Router Server Actions / Image Optimization via SVG     < 15.5.21\n  Unbounded Server Action payload in the Edge runtime               < 15.5.21\n\n15.5.20 -> 15.5.25, a patch bump inside the same minor. Critical count 1 -> 0.\n\nThe pin exists in two places — the root package.json and apps/web-next — and\nbumping only one left 15.5.20 resolved in the lockfile alongside 15.5.25.\nChecked rather than assumed.\n\nNot done: the audit also suggested \"@sentry/nextjs@10.26.0\" as a fix, which\nwould be a DOWNGRADE from the ^10.66.0 this repo already has. Its high-severity\nflags come through transitive glob/brace-expansion, which the override block\nalready pins. Taking npm''s fixAvailable at face value there would have moved\nthe package backwards by forty minor versions.\n\nVerified: clean build, shared bundle unchanged at 103 kB, typecheck 344,\nsuite at baseline.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d755e48ec59c76999fa2a4e8e361f17fca785aca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/d755e48ec59c76999fa2a4e8e361f17fca785aca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/04123bf417e98fbef101cb29e06700eaf350665c","verification":{"payload":"tree d755e48ec59c76999fa2a4e8e361f17fca785aca\nparent aa4afa7539b872554ba524f3cdc7778947b35b4a\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788908089 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788908089 -0700\n\nfix(security): Next 15.5.20 -> 15.5.25 — two unauthenticated RCEs (#528)\n\nCI''s audit job went red on this branch with a critical CVE in production\ndependencies. It is nothing to do with the change on the branch — a batch of\nNext.js advisories published since the last install. Ten of them, on a version\nthis repo pins exactly:\n\n  Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution on windows-hosted servers   < 15.5.24\n  Unauthenticated RCE in the Image Optimization API via AVIF        < 15.5.24\n  Server-Side Request Forgery in rewrites, attacker-controlled host < 15.5.21\n  SSRF in Server Actions on custom servers                          < 15.5.21\n  Unauthenticated disclosure of internal Server Function endpoints  < 15.5.21\n  Cache confusion of response bodies (x2)                           < 15.5.21\n  DoS in App Router Server Actions / Image Optimization via SVG     < 15.5.21\n  Unbounded Server Action payload in the Edge runtime               < 15.5.21\n\n15.5.20 -> 15.5.25, a patch bump inside the same minor. Critical count 1 -> 0.\n\nThe pin exists in two places — the root package.json and apps/web-next — and\nbumping only one left 15.5.20 resolved in the lockfile alongside 15.5.25.\nChecked rather than assumed.\n\nNot done: the audit also suggested \"@sentry/nextjs@10.26.0\" as a fix, which\nwould be a DOWNGRADE from the ^10.66.0 this repo already has. Its high-severity\nflags come through transitive glob/brace-expansion, which the override block\nalready pins. Taking npm''s fixAvailable at face value there would have moved\nthe package backwards by forty minor versions.\n\nVerified: clean build, shared bundle unchanged at 103 kB, typecheck 344,\nsuite at baseline.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoJI5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeGEQAJpLyqytT1PlqwwzMj/808a/\n2YsPrAN/YXR+n/l7rzBaoqrRNXPWDRlgz4THzHS4NRYxog9xGZtUNdRG9BLrOo08\n1dUwT9dTTHVuaUerpxMc7x46Lg59/gvmIhXIU42UMEiyJoLXVVdZFsDxvLlZeMk0\