cdc7778947b35b4a"}],"sha":"04123bf417e98fbef101cb29e06700eaf350665c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/04123bf417e98fbef101cb29e06700eaf350665c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/aa4afa7539b872554ba524f3cdc7778947b35b4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T21:04:45Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T21:04:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(e2e): the telegram phase asserted English against a French tenant (#526)\n\n* feat(tax): map the AU lines the ATO actually publishes — and say why the rest cannot be\n\nAuthorised to fetch the ATO forms, so I did. Two mappings are now sourced\nverbatim from \"15 Net income or loss from business 2026\":\n\n  \"Transfer your net income or loss from a non-primary production business\n   you showed at P8 Business income and expenses - label Z ... to question\n   15 - label C in your supplementary tax return.\"\n\nA sole trader is non-primary production, so net business income is P8 Z and\nlands at item 15 C. AU line-number coverage 2/23 -> 4/23, floor raised.\n\nIT STOPS AT 4, AND THAT IS THE FINDING\n\nI expected to add ~20 item numbers. Reading the actual schedule shows the\npremise was wrong. The expense rows in the AU template — advertising,\ninsurance, legal and professional, office supplies, travel, telephone and\ninternet — are the US Schedule C / CA T2125 shape. The ATO''s P8 Expenses\nsection has entirely different rows: opening and closing stock, purchases,\ncost of sales, foreign resident withholding, contractor/sub-contractor/\ncommission, superannuation, bad debts, lease, rent, interest within Australia,\ninterest overseas, depreciation, motor vehicle, repairs and maintenance, all\nother expenses, home office, total expenses.\n\nNot one of our six has a counterpart. On an Australian return they all roll\ninto \"All other expenses\". Giving them item letters would invent a\ncorrespondence that does not exist — the same class of mistake as the\nfabricated MeF export removed in #513, which is exactly what I was asked to\navoid repeating.\n\nI also stopped short of the individual expense letters I could have guessed at.\nScraping the instructions page returned label K for both Opening stock and Rent\nexpenses, which cannot both be right: label H recurs throughout as the\nreconciliation-adjustment reference and contaminates a text scan. Two letters\nquoted in a complete sentence are worth more than twenty inferred from\nproximity.\n\nClosing AU properly means restructuring these rows to match P8. That changes\nwhat the engine computes, so it wants its own design and an Australian\naccountant''s eye — not a labelling pass.\n\nSource: ato.gov.au, Business and professional items schedule 2026 instructions\n(NAT 2543-06.2026) and Individual supplementary tax return 2026 instructions,\nread 2026-09-08.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(e2e): the telegram phase asserted English against a French tenant\n\nLast night''s remaining failure was not a bug. The reply was\n\n    \"Quel Acme vouliez-vous dire — to Acme for ou Acme Corp?\"\n\nwhich is the disambiguation prompt working, in the right language, against two\nsimilarly-named client records on that tenant. (\"to Acme for\" is a junk client\nrow left by an earlier bad parse, not untranslated copy.) The test asserted\n/invoice|created|draft/i and failed a correctly-localized product.\n\nThe capture tenant is fr-CA and chat localization is deliberately ungated — the\nfeature flag covers the web shell only, by decision. So any assertion on reply\nTEXT in this phase has to accept both languages, and two did not.\n\nSecond one in the same file after the balance assertion, and the same shape:\nan expectation written when the product only spoke English, left behind when\nit stopped.\n\nAlso confirms #524 deployed and works — the joiner is now \"ou\", not \"or\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1aef035aec83b60d27ffdb6386573545fc7794a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/1aef035aec83b60d27ffdb6386573545fc7794a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/aa4afa7539b872554ba524f3cdc7778947b35b4a","verification":{"payload":"tree 1aef035aec83b60d27ffdb6386573545fc7794a1\nparent ec2878bc658d8c0dfe6676068ca09868c04f64f0\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788901485 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788901485 -0700\n\ntest(e2e): the telegram phase asserted English against a French tenant (#526)\n\n* feat(tax): map the AU lines the ATO actually publishes — and say why the rest cannot be\n\nAuthorised to fetch the ATO forms, so I did. Two mappings are now sourced\nverbatim from \"15 Net income or loss from business 2026\":\n\n  \"Transfer your net income or loss from a non-primary production business\n   you showed at P8 Business income and expenses - label Z ... to question\n   15 - label C in your supplementary tax return.\"\n\nA sole trader is non-primary production, so net business income is P8 Z and\nlands at item 15 C. AU line-number coverage 2/23 -> 4/23, floor raised.\n\nIT STOPS AT 4, AND THAT IS THE FINDING\n\nI expected to add ~20 item numbers. Reading the actual schedule shows the\npremise was wrong. The expense rows in the AU template — advertising,\ninsurance, legal and professional, office supplies, travel, telephone and\ninternet — are the US Schedule C / CA T2125 shape. The ATO''s P8 Expenses\nsection has entirely different rows: opening and closing stock, purchases,\ncost of sales, foreign resident withholding, contractor/sub-contractor/\ncommission, superannuation, bad debts, lease, rent, interest within Australia,\ninterest overseas, depreciation, motor vehicle, repairs and maintenance, all\nother expenses, home office, total expenses.\n\nNot one of our six has a counterpart. On an Australian return they all roll\ninto \"All other expenses\". Giving them item letters would invent a\ncorrespondence that does not exist — the same class of mistake as the\nfabricated MeF export removed in #513, which is exactly what I was asked to\navoid repeating.\n\nI also stopped short of the individual expense letters I could have guessed at.\nScraping the instructions page returned label K for both Opening stock and Rent\nexpenses, which cannot both be right: label H recurs throughout as the\nreconciliation-adjustment reference and contaminates a text scan. Two letters\nquoted in a complete sentence are worth more than twenty inferred from\nproximity.\n\nClosing AU properly means restructuring these rows to match P8. That changes\nwhat the engine computes, so it wants its own design and an Australian\naccountant''s eye — not a labelling pass.\n\nSource: ato.gov.au, Business and professional items schedule 2026 instructions\n(NAT 2543-06.2026) and Individual supplementary tax return 2026 instructions,\nread 2026-09-08.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(e2e): the telegram phase asserted English against a French tenant\n\nLast night''s remaining failure was not a bug. The reply was\n\n    \"Quel Acme vouliez-vous dire — to Acme for ou Acme Corp?\"\n\nwhich is the disambiguation prompt working, in the right language, against two\nsimilarly-named client records on that tenant. (\"to Acme for\" is a junk client\nrow left by an earlier bad parse, not untranslated copy.) The test asserted\n/invoice|created|draft/i and failed a correctly-localized product.\n\nThe capture tenant is fr-CA and chat localization is deliberately ungated — the\nfeature flag covers the web shell only, by decision. So any assertion on reply\nTEXT in this phase has to accept both languages, and two did not.\n\nSecond one in the same file after the balance assertion, and the same shape:\nan expectation written when the product only spoke English, left behind when\nit stopped.\n\nAlso confirms #524 deployed and works — the joiner is now \"ou\", not \"or\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoHhtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAo3UQAJYAs+hg+MFcK8M5dbMDFDln\nQKX2ENYyKXuz8AVJJQ6tBhH0QxpJ4D/BrAZg+XObBIhrcRkWZS2FMm8iCxZmTh4Q\n+JpWZLdZhHKvxdqhJsTj6z28Hz+j/fwIUr7OkDx9WFMfQBj6PX7H5hysKLyRvIXx\nfq5GPqNC+amL3lCtoo+7Nti7naae6VhEoHfMdnKFlRI/DWcjWSSKB8/hpxddeyQk\nq16kijny0eCK07XwWGK/fW7wWUY5vdaHeTf03S4pMlVtim6H6lwrus3gUcUsq3di\nRHKYnBhD1ohJQmZjf4v1+9vmlZiEKwUpT7J29uq74zHx+HLMmpFPQMTODivw38uH\nQenqo0wvPUDh9f47KLwp7BDCsuggbhGlpID6g2s+wg0Mx4w7Wu0KBY5weQ7Xvh5s\n73nHuYejqJSo4++7SefsKZ9c+9ozHiORRSjmVdUFOjrSn2mp5rV33UfxvfFnIDjn\nkNKOPjoUBTlIhErbPXqzr/TZX+t3KTSka6OytKtRFh2wZuu/RjNtpaPfxQ/StHIL\nPoa9WhVauwJeg9ufra9hstESZ88uxX43pedJOJfrr3ulynA7SzXixqwE4q54w/FR\nnwqvIPelNuIHyAJ8ec4JcXNsiTiynT1LR8675dVOvD1oMgU/auydHHwXlU7/qvHF\n06zw9fepmHbneNHjnOVe\n=GwWs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T21:04:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/aa4afa7539b872554ba524f3cdc7778947b35b4a","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGFhNGFmYTc1MzliODcyNTU0YmE1MjRmM2NkYzc3Nzg5NDdiMzViNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/ec2878bc658d8c0dfe6676068ca09868c04f64f0","sha":"ec2878bc658d8c0dfe6676068ca09868c04f64f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ec2878bc658d8c0dfe6676068ca09868c04f64f0"}],"sha":"aa4afa7539b872554ba524f3cdc7778947b35b4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/aa4afa7539b872554ba524f3cdc7778947b35b4a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ec2878bc658d8c0dfe6676068ca09868c04f64f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T20:39:55Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T20:39:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(tax): map the AU lines the ATO actually publishes — and say why the rest cannot be (#525)\n\nAuthorised to fetch the ATO forms, so I did. Two mappings are now sourced\nverbatim from \"15 Net income or loss from business 2026\":\n\n  \"Transfer your net income or loss from a non-primary production business\n   you showed at P8 Business income and expenses - label Z ... to question\n   15 - label C in your supplementary tax return.\"\n\nA sole trader is non-primary production, so net business income is P8 Z and\nlands at item 15 C. AU line-number coverage 2/23 -> 4/23, floor raised.\n\nIT STOPS AT 4, AND THAT IS THE FINDING\n\nI expected to add ~20 item numbers. Reading the actual schedule shows the\npremise was wrong. The expense rows in the AU template — advertising,\ninsurance, legal and professional, office supplies, travel, telephone and\ninternet — are the US Schedule C / CA T2125 shape. The ATO''s P8 Expenses\nsection has entirely different rows: opening and closing stock, purchases,\ncost of sales, foreign resident withholding, contractor/sub-contractor/\ncommission, superannuation, bad debts, lease, rent, interest within Australia,\ninterest overseas, depreciation, motor vehicle, repairs and maintenance, all\nother expenses, home office, total expenses.\n\nNot one of our six has a counterpart. On an Australian return they all roll\ninto \"All other expenses\". Giving them item letters would invent a\ncorrespondence that does not exist — the same class of mistake as the\nfabricated MeF export removed in #513, which is exactly what I was asked to\navoid repeating.\n\nI also stopped short of the individual expense letters I could have guessed at.\nScraping the instructions page returned label K for both Opening stock and Rent\nexpenses, which cannot both be right: label H recurs throughout as the\nreconciliation-adjustment reference and contaminates a text scan. Two letters\nquoted in a complete sentence are worth more than twenty inferred from\nproximity.\n\nClosing AU properly means restructuring these rows to match P8. That changes\nwhat the engine computes, so it wants its own design and an Australian\naccountant''s eye — not a labelling pass.\n\nSource: ato.gov.au, Business and professional items schedule 2026 instructions\n(NAT 2543-06.2026) and Individual supplementary tax return 2026 instructions,\nread 2026-09-08.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9fd89c5baf88fa27ea3f159cca67bc603dbe7d36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/9fd89c5baf88fa27ea3f159cca67bc603dbe7d36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/ec2878bc658d8c0dfe6676068ca09868c04f64f0","verification":{"payload":"tree 9fd89c5baf88fa27ea3f159cca67bc603dbe7d36\nparent f1ba1ba36508c3a2bd401821fa4a4cdc786bbf9c\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788899995 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788899995 -0700\n\nfeat(tax): map the AU lines the ATO actually publishes — and say why the rest cannot be (#525)\n\nAuthorised to fetch the ATO forms, so I did. Two mappings are now sourced\nverbatim from \"15 Net income or loss from business 2026\":\n\n  \"Transfer your net income or loss from a non-primary production business\n   you showed at P8 Business income and expenses - label Z ... to question\n   15 - label C in your supplementary tax return.\"\n\nA sole trader is non-primary production, so net business income is P8 Z and\nlands at item 15 C. AU line-number coverage 2/23 -> 4/23, floor raised.\n\nIT STOPS AT 4, AND THAT IS THE FINDING\n\nI expected to add ~20 item numbers. Reading the actual schedule shows the\npremise was wrong. The expense rows in the AU template — advertising,\ninsurance, legal and professional, office supplies, travel, telephone and\ninternet — are the US Schedule C / CA T2125 shape. The ATO''s P8 Expenses\nsection has entirely different rows: opening and closing stock, purchases,\ncost of sales, foreign resident withholding, contractor/sub-contractor/\ncommission, superannuation, bad debts, lease, rent, interest within Australia,\ninterest overseas, depreciation, motor vehicle, repairs and maintenance, all\nother expenses, home office, total expenses.\n\nNot one of our six has a counterpart. On an Australian return they all roll\ninto \"All other expenses\". Giving them item letters would invent a\ncorrespondence that does not exist — the same class of mistake as the\nfabricated MeF export removed in #513, which is exactly what I was asked to\navoid repeating.\n\nI also stopped short of the individual expense letters I could have guessed at.\nScraping the instructions page returned label K for both Opening stock and Rent\nexpenses, which cannot both be right: label H recurs throughout as the\nreconciliation-adjustment reference and contaminates a text scan. Two letters\nquoted in a complete sentence are worth more than twenty inferred from\nproximity.\n\nClosing AU properly means restructuring these rows to match P8. That changes\nwhat the engine computes, so it wants its own design and an Australian\naccountant''s eye — not a labelling pass.\n\nSource: ato.gov.au, Business and professional items schedule 2026 instructions\n(NAT 2543-06.2026) and Individual supplementary tax return 2026 instructions,\nread 2026-09-08.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoHKbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5uUQAHHZ18BWKqzC2VaZ7NyisLR0\nV7XnckHzs/qoFu4GxHYRSEqOPh1YaPoktpTY/PZBy+3JVonxzDJvuikAvtcAPj8D\nRaY+Ll0pWjJ/hA3pmaoNrIOjbqQ5xYGUVOnBEzkC2zkEWwhHIAkiF0X1YJGp7hh7\nHbQ9nJ/Eo6+Bj7dIx1VOiigT9QMWDKpvWc9Ty0NTd8buRytqjYOAl+vQrxpb/0wi\nMUgkI1KJNnFWkBPWoYJpaSzsr4PKb/EZGN1I6NPsXMxS7rkj8d4wo5D2HrFQz8xf\nodhJZNbQHc0AzgsFukc1jytqO5QCeJiOFnjgl3rO3P3BvVneT5/XDExItEHnfr5s\njUbYznCKv/ESJ5IMx5EPtYjACgGpDGNp7z3NdzcB1c+Hi8kiiaulLSBOlebUERwF\n7Uab//PrcDc2pk8rSWNvmIdDvpTofW5ua0IyG3/Vgsndk9gvLe/+SE4j1P6clWLB\nlCJs04ZKIfn9VkSr0DR/t7ffzOEcriou8IP/kbwaoJUWLnnD6BUwAwgu7zptGN2Y\npYtTnXEBWFDR2yj41SE6mXyVVZcFD4jW85kD5WwLQyxhlhtkvei7ZqmEtCqOMTRO\nSX1biyn5uQDfPBMcKd5RVCpQob3jD0UCekQBGCEIbmXO6Q15EO6PhUACHPMSLwua\nm6SrmCbc4GvelUwPxw51\n=bZS2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T20:39:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/ec2878bc658d8c0dfe6676068ca09868c04f64f0","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGVjMjg3OGJjNjU4ZDhjMGRmZTY2NzYwNjhjYTA5ODY4YzA0ZjY0ZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/f1ba1ba36508c3a2bd401821fa4a4cdc786bbf9c","sha":"f1ba1ba36508c3a2bd401821fa4a4cdc786bbf9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/f1ba1ba36508c3a2bd401821fa4a4cdc786bbf9c"}],"sha":"ec2878bc658d8c0dfe6676068ca09868c04f64f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/ec2878bc658d8c0dfe6676068ca09868c04f64f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/f1ba1ba36508c3a2bd401821fa4a4cdc786bbf9c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T19:56:14Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T19:56:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(i18n): the half-French reply, plus a config doctor (#524)\n\n* fix(i18n): the disambiguation reply was half French\n\nFound in last night''s e2e log, on production:\n\n    \"Quel Acme vouliez-vous dire — to Acme for or Acme Corp?\"\n\nThe sentence comes from the catalog. The \" or \" joining the candidates did\nnot — `.join('' or '')` at three call sites — nor did the ` (and 2 more)`\noverflow suffix, built as a template literal. Both are handed to the translated\ntemplate as parameters, so the catalog invariants see a fully translated string\nand the reply still reads half English.\n\nP1-6''s extractor could not have found these: it reads JSX text and attributes,\nand these are neither. They are the residual class — English assembled in\nTypeScript and interpolated into a translated sentence — which is why the guard\nadded here is written against the call sites rather than the catalog.\n\nTwo keys in `bot`, both padded (` ou `, not `ou`), with an assertion on the\npadding: dropping the spaces renders \"AcmeouAcme Corp\" and nothing else in the\nsuite would notice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(ops): a config doctor for the four settings that fail silently\n\nFour settings gate the launch score and none lives in the repo: two\nActions/Vercel secrets that must hold the SAME value in two places, a Sentry\nDSN, and a database row. Every one fails in a way that looks like something\nelse — a CRON_SECRET mismatch looks like a broken cron, an unset\nE2E_RESET_TOKEN looks like a flaky test, an unset SENTRY_DSN looks like \"no\nerrors happened\", and the i18n flag off looks like \"translation is unfinished\".\n\n`bin/config-doctor.sh` checks each from the outside. It needs no secrets and\nreports what it can; supplying CRON_SECRET or DATABASE_URL lets it prove the\ntwo-copies-in-sync cases, which is the whole difficulty.\n\nTwo detections are worth recording because the obvious ones do not work.\n\nAn unauthenticated 401 on a cron route proves only that the DEPLOYMENT has a\nsecret — not that Actions holds the same one. That is exactly why the nightly\ncan be red while a spot check looks healthy, so the matching check is a real\nauthenticated request and it is reported as SKIP, never PASS, when the value is\nnot supplied.\n\nFor Sentry, probing the `/monitoring` tunnel route is useless here: this app\nserves a 200 HTML shell for unmatched paths, verified against a nonsense URL\nthat also returns 200. What does discriminate is the deployed client bundle —\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN is inlined at BUILD time, so the SDK is either in the\nchunks or it is not. Currently it is not.\n\nSKIP is printed separately from PASS and the footer says unchecked is not\npassing, because a doctor that reports green on what it did not look at is the\nsame failure as the config it exists to find.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(e2e): the nightly balance assertion was stale, not a product bug\n\n`query-finance includes seeded balance` asserted a literal $5,000 and had been\nred for weeks, reading like a broken skill. It is not. The capture chat maps to\na seeded persona tenant, and `reset-e2e-user` reseeds the E2E USER rather than\nthat one, so the balance drifts as the nightly books expenses against it. Last\nnight the reply was \"You have CA$207,081.10 on hand\" — the product working.\n\nA figure that drifts cannot be asserted, so it now asserts what must hold: a\nformatted amount, in the tenant''s own currency, non-zero, and not a question\nback. That last one is the #487 regression — every region used to answer this\nquestion with a question — and is the part actually worth guarding.\n\nWorth separating from the config work: this one looked like a secret problem\nand was not. `reset-e2e-user` returns 200 in the nightly log, so\nE2E_RESET_TOKEN is set correctly and is NOT one of the outstanding config\nitems, contrary to what the scorecard has said since rev 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b87e9ca0f1dcb76952d630280bae9058b6feea14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/b87e9ca0f1dcb76952d630280bae9058b6feea14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/f1ba1ba36508c3a2bd401821fa4a4cdc786bbf9c","verification":{"payload":"tree b87e9ca0f1dcb76952d630280bae9058b6feea14\nparent e10eb36b69b154eb88958ab619d0ba1dfcd6b012\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788897374 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788897374 -0700\n\nfix(i18n): the half-French reply, plus a config doctor (#524)\n\n* fix(i18n): the disambiguation reply was half French\n\nFound in last night''s e2e log, on production:\n\n    \"Quel Acme vouliez-vous dire — to Acme for or Acme Corp?\"\n\nThe sentence comes from the catalog. The \" or \" joining the candidates did\nnot — `.join('' or '')` at three call sites — nor did the ` (and 2 more)`\noverflow suffix, built as a template literal. Both are handed to the translated\ntemplate as parameters, so the catalog invariants see a fully translated string\nand the reply still reads half English.\n\nP1-6''s extractor could not have found these: it reads JSX text and attributes,\nand these are neither. They are the residual class — English assembled in\nTypeScript and interpolated into a translated sentence — which is why the guard\nadded here is written against the call sites rather than the catalog.\n\nTwo keys in `bot`, both padded (` ou `, not `ou`), with an assertion on the\npadding: dropping the spaces renders \"AcmeouAcme Corp\" and nothing else in the\nsuite would notice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(ops): a config doctor for the four settings that fail silently\n\nFour settings gate the launch score and none lives in the repo: two\nActions/Vercel secrets that must hold the SAME value in two places, a Sentry\nDSN, and a database row. Every one fails in a way that looks like something\nelse — a CRON_SECRET mismatch looks like a broken cron, an unset\nE2E_RESET_TOKEN looks like a flaky test, an unset SENTRY_DSN looks like \"no\nerrors happened\", and the i18n flag off looks like \"translation is unfinished\".\n\n`bin/config-doctor.sh` checks each from the outside. It needs no secrets and\nreports what it can; supplying CRON_SECRET or DATABASE_URL lets it prove the\ntwo-copies-in-sync cases, which is the whole difficulty.\n\nTwo detections are worth recording because the obvious ones do not work.\n\nAn unauthenticated 401 on a cron route proves only that the DEPLOYMENT has a\nsecret — not that Actions holds the same one. That is exactly why the nightly\ncan be red while a spot check looks healthy, so the matching check is a real\nauthenticated request and it is reported as SKIP, never PASS, when the value is\nnot supplied.\n\nFor Sentry, probing the `/monitoring` tunnel route is useless here: this app\nserves a 200 HTML shell for unmatched paths, verified against a nonsense URL\nthat also returns 200. What does discriminate is the deployed client bundle —\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN is inlined at BUILD time, so the SDK is either in the\nchunks or it is not. Currently it is not.\n\nSKIP is printed separately from PASS and the footer says unchecked is not\npassing, because a doctor that reports green on what it did not look at is the\nsame failure as the config it exists to find.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(e2e): the nightly balance assertion was stale, not a product bug\n\n`query-finance includes seeded balance` asserted a literal $5,000 and had been\nred for weeks, reading like a broken skill. It is not. The capture chat maps to\na seeded persona tenant, and `reset-e2e-user` reseeds the E2E USER rather than\nthat one, so the balance drifts as the nightly books expenses against it. Last\nnight the reply was \"You have CA$207,081.10 on hand\" — the product working.\n\nA figure that drifts cannot be asserted, so it now asserts what must hold: a\nformatted amount, in the tenant''s own currency, non-zero, and not a question\nback. That last one is the #487 regression — every region used to answer this\nquestion with a question — and is the part actually worth guarding.\n\nWorth separating from the config work: this one looked like a secret problem\nand was not. `reset-e2e-user` returns 200 in the nightly log, so\nE2E_RESET_TOKEN is set correctly and is NOT one of the outstanding config\nitems, contrary to what the scorecard has said since rev 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoGheCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsxIQACNYiY+QWFvPHzU53EErDoc1\niPrg8eII4d0AFXDHiR/JE8tv6lPlvGV4TYtcITA5JCaKe9pc817uLuSWbX6mUbil\nNrYBXxmOslNMmtTUsixAodYs+dpKSGsDtC0AEluwAABnvo3bipvM6Le1GvIRSYTn\nq6tg3oiK2BOgnc9BSGGekhG+Bvj6pqRMhnJxxm7huC/+fD0VtpwjqFSQYo4gkEwP\n4uM4yS+1G+WnDC0oOuyetsP7XCVzgdice86n8KZrWG0GG467L/lcLCZ/bbNX82oO\ndFOrC89pDxT+HWip2aPyptLUoq7mZfAKMtT+0pjVwEPWAlz/xf4HZf+AjMdkXfPs\n7uPXc9CX/bXE5XRGk9642Xu8CedOrt8Kfg7XRx8jjfjOem3CDotFvXje4lDts2nK\nSD+Kn1jUG1uJgBw/KFytS2tEhzH92xbI05XzPH3cZZmQXbRzQN21cSJ8wVOJhwY1\nqlrGWNZf6fSjkhM7u7Y6x3+KNLi78Q0fdt3ccu772qHNTBwDzD5wytmxh6ddXi8j\ndUbawGoVt4YRMBNONLvBGl/sQNER7I1qPc4Cv4EJo1EHXSOyhixzI+z3Finy65Jr\n6/q1FXxDws0GOuK3zGMa5/qlnB6W6G4o6+SvmumsSuevdpR5HqWXY6ZgZ2CpiGI9\n+j5vK4/ERfu+Wpf5yHAD\n=dsPB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T19:56:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/f1ba1ba36508c3a2bd401821fa4a4cdc786bbf9c","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGYxYmExYmEzNjUwOGMzYTJiZDQwMTgyMWZhNGE0Y2RjNzg2YmJmOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/e10eb36b69b154eb88958ab619d0ba1dfcd6b012","sha":"e10eb36b69b154eb88958ab619d0ba1dfcd6b012","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/e10eb36b69b154eb88958ab619d0ba1dfcd6b012"}],"sha":"f1ba1ba36508c3a2bd401821fa4a4cdc786bbf9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/f1ba1ba36508c3a2bd401821fa4a4cdc786bbf9c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/e10eb36b69b154eb88958ab619d0ba1dfcd6b012/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T19:18:24Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T19:18:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(i18n): localize the plugin frontends (P1-6, tranche 3 — final) (#523)\n\n41 strings across 21 plugin frontend files, 38 new keys in each locale, placed\nin each plugin''s own namespace: tax_ui, invoice_ui, student_ui, startup_ui,\ncommunity_ui, expenses_ui, core_ui.\n\nP1-6 IS NOW DONE. Repo-wide, hardcoded user-facing literals went 570 -> 357\nacross the three tranches, and every surface a fr-CA or zh-CN user reaches is\ntranslated. The locale flag `agentbook.i18n.locales.enabled` can be turned on.\n\nSEVEN LITERALS REMAIN, ON PURPOSE\n\nTelegram, WhatsApp, Webhook, AgentBook, the \"Starbucks\" search placeholder and\nC-corp. Giving them keys is a regression twice over: the value is identical in\nevery locale, so the key buys nothing, and the unwired-key guard flags any\nliteral whose exact English value exists as a key — so every plain mention of\n\"Telegram\" anywhere in the repo would start failing a measure that must be\nzero. That is not hypothetical; it is what happened in tranche 2 and had to be\nundone. A test now asserts these values have NO catalog key, and fails with the\nreason if someone adds one.\n\nTWO THINGS THE CODEMOD COULD NOT KNOW\n\nRoommatesPanel binds the translator as `const { t: tr } = useI18n()`, so the\ngenerated `t(...)` calls did not compile. Only the type-checker found it —\nwhich is why this pass runs tsc per plugin rather than trusting the codemod.\n\n`startup_ui.documents` collided with \"Documents\" in the PWA docs page. The word\nis generic and two unrelated surfaces use it, so a plugin-scoped namespace was\nthe wrong home: moved to `common.documents` and both call sites wired.\n\nRATCHETS\n\n  unwired-keys  plugins 0, shell 0, server 39 -> 40\n  literals      361 -> 357\n\nThe one new server-component entry is \"Amount Due\" on the public invoice page,\nwhich is server-rendered and cannot call the client translator. The key has to\nexist for the tax Quarterly page, so the collision is unavoidable wherever the\nkey lives.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7118fd21cca039406347b6c2cb6085b7f7ef653d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/7118fd21cca039406347b6c2cb6085b7f7ef653d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/e10eb36b69b154eb88958ab619d0ba1dfcd6b012","verification":{"payload":"tree 7118fd21cca039406347b6c2cb6085b7f7ef653d\nparent d06ea7004a3b4a1d5a4bd99f998811831f4f5616\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788895104 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788895104 -0700\n\nfeat(i18n): localize the plugin frontends (P1-6, tranche 3 — final) (#523)\n\n41 strings across 21 plugin frontend files, 38 new keys in each locale, placed\nin each plugin''s own namespace: tax_ui, invoice_ui, student_ui, startup_ui,\ncommunity_ui, expenses_ui, core_ui.\n\nP1-6 IS NOW DONE. Repo-wide, hardcoded user-facing literals went 570 -> 357\nacross the three tranches, and every surface a fr-CA or zh-CN user reaches is\ntranslated. The locale flag `agentbook.i18n.locales.enabled` can be turned on.\n\nSEVEN LITERALS REMAIN, ON PURPOSE\n\nTelegram, WhatsApp, Webhook, AgentBook, the \"Starbucks\" search placeholder and\nC-corp. Giving them keys is a regression twice over: the value is identical in\nevery locale, so the key buys nothing, and the unwired-key guard flags any\nliteral whose exact English value exists as a key — so every plain mention of\n\"Telegram\" anywhere in the repo would start failing a measure that must be\nzero. That is not hypothetical; it is what happened in tranche 2 and had to be\nundone. A test now asserts these values have NO catalog key, and fails with the\nreason if someone adds one.\n\nTWO THINGS THE CODEMOD COULD NOT KNOW\n\nRoommatesPanel binds the translator as `const { t: tr } = useI18n()`, so the\ngenerated `t(...)` calls did not compile. Only the type-checker found it —\nwhich is why this pass runs tsc per plugin rather than trusting the codemod.\n\n`startup_ui.documents` collided with \"Documents\" in the PWA docs page. The word\nis generic and two unrelated surfaces use it, so a plugin-scoped namespace was\nthe wrong home: moved to `common.documents` and both call sites wired.\n\nRATCHETS\n\n  unwired-keys  plugins 0, shell 0, server 39 -> 40\n  literals      361 -> 357\n\nThe one new server-component entry is \"Amount Due\" on the public invoice page,\nwhich is server-rendered and cannot call the client translator. The key has to\nexist for the tax Quarterly page, so the collision is unavoidable wherever the\nkey lives.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoF+ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9RkQAIIP8Ausk6Nb1UUqYZkD0a88\n8XfGPYIAOj5OKB8zzbi/SuECPpwxHzmnXnKlKU84nNPsmjVM+D979esS8WuImdCj\nOe0Chzcv06ttfHxUPQdTYvdMyHoK62sM9qVMj4Zzc4GEMh3EngZnNA81G0ogw25h\nnvrvOCDSPTmyO0WfBqqW1KY1gj0VcuCrl6AAx/PFv9ofceXLNJvWAS7650hJmOSp\nTfTo9noTaFNuRmnfDlhTxpp4UgO3fmo23fVr1zhxzjY+ggI1hZ1hC63u4gjYlOQO\nlHGHjvJUzxy9xMDuEqY/mn2cV1rzm6ntdObHB8WwsBGci133P1G0esHXGwgEykvL\nGqvKw7BqtbUQBYLBCThecPehDxCGM9Jp0nbWGgJIaosARfa0TFEnnQ3RS8v//+TN\nvA9l5X6CcRujoObI5uCad2KnOwEKTJCNoFVs3a/3Ih64kNjf/og9pESl3KawWLow\nTWk+lhSeVFU9SeQMOCN+HJJidTVacg12Kpquh6ITWuwtmctgxeP923Xw+UOjMd1g\nPQnYmOKiS6xBEFv3gJghaKoeC7x79eFE5wIW0tJGxpIde/b/diDgyekhAQBt3EdJ\n9FMM0OJHgL7SfLvGG1fWK9wViXJzFYOJinU8ypUCBjrkUBPb5dt7iy9Fw3Iz9TFS\nrQaWIPEFWeKjcqH6wSTu\n=sVP/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T19:18:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/e10eb36b69b154eb88958ab619d0ba1dfcd6b012","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGUxMGViMzZiNjliMTU0ZWI4ODk1OGFiNjE5ZDBiYTFkZmNkNmIwMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/d06ea7004a3b4a1d5a4bd99f998811831f4f5616","sha":"d06ea7004a3b4a1d5a4bd99f998811831f4f5616","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/d06ea7004a3b4a1d5a4bd99f998811831f4f5616"}],"sha":"e10eb36b69b154eb88958ab619d0ba1dfcd6b012","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/e10eb36b69b154eb88958ab619d0ba1dfcd6b012"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/d06ea7004a3b4a1d5a4bd99f998811831f4f5616/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T18:05:15Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T18:05:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(i18n): localize the shell for fr-CA and zh-CN (P1-6, tranches 1+2) (#522)\n\n* i18n(settings): localize the settings surfaces (P1-6, tranche 1 of 3)\n\n83 hardcoded English strings across the settings page and the AgentBook\nsettings panel, replaced with catalog keys and translated into fr-CA and\nzh-CN. 76 new keys in core_ui; 5 strings reused keys that already existed.\n\nWHY THIS IS THE BLOCKER, NOT A POLISH ITEM\n\nThe fr-CA/zh-CN locale flag (`agentbook.i18n.locales.enabled`) is off, and its\nown comment says why: flipping it while any surface is half-translated ships\nmixed French and English. Measuring that surface found 290 user-visible strings\nbypassing the translator, 284 of them in files that ALREADY call `t()` — so\nthose pages would render half in each language. Settings is the largest single\npiece at 83 and the surface a Canadian user configuring their business spends\nthe most time in.\n\nFOUR COMPONENTS HAD NO TRANSLATOR AT ALL\n\nProfilePreview, ShareCard, QrCard and ParentShareTab render user-visible text\nand never called useT(). Rather than guess at scope, the literals were replaced\nfirst and the compiler asked: it named exactly those four with \"Cannot find\nname ''t''\".\n\nTHE GUARD, AND WHY IT IS NOT ANOTHER CATALOG TEST\n\ni18n-catalog.test.ts already proves the catalog is internally consistent — same\nkeys everywhere, matching variables, nothing untranslated. All of that passed\nduring the last rollout while the running page was still visibly English,\nbecause a consistent catalog says nothing about whether the COMPONENT asks for\na key or hardcodes the sentence.\n\nSo the new test asserts both halves: the literals really left each file, and\nevery key the files now use resolves through the REAL translator to a real\ntranslation in all three locales. The second half matters because `t()` never\nthrows on a missing key — useT''s fallback humanises `core_ui.accounting_basis`\ninto \"Accounting basis\", which reads as correct English and hides the miss.\n\nIt also guards the guard: `not.toContain` passes just as happily on an empty\nfile, so the test checks the files still hold their text and their t() calls.\n\nMutation-checked both ways: restoring one English literal fails it, and copying\nan English value into fr-CA fails it.\n\nTelegram, WhatsApp, \"webhook\" and \"Logo\" are in IDENTICAL_ALLOWED — a Chinese\nuser configuring a Telegram bot looks for the word \"Telegram\", and translating\na brand is a bug rather than a courtesy.\n\nRemaining for tranches 2 and 3: 201 strings, mostly teams, sales-rep, payroll\nand admin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(i18n): localize the rest of the shell (P1-6, tranche 2)\n\n156 more hardcoded strings across 37 shell files — teams, sales-rep, payroll,\nnotifications, admin, PWA, marketplace — plus 132 new core_ui keys in all three\nlocales. The shell is now down to 4 untranslated strings, two of which are the\nWordmark''s brand name and stay that way.\n\nTHREE THINGS THE FIRST PASS GOT WRONG, ALL CAUGHT BEFORE MERGE\n\n1. The codemod ate a leading space. `>([^<>{}\\n]...)<` captures the whitespace\n   between a tag and its text, and the replacement discarded it, so\n   `<strong>Configure:</strong> Member can modify...` became\n   `<strong>{t(...)}</strong>{t(...)}` — rendering \"Configurer :Member can\n   modify\". JSX preserves a space that is not adjacent to a newline, so this\n   was a real visual regression at 28 sites, four of them from tranche 1.\n   Repaired by diffing against origin/main and restoring the exact leading and\n   trailing whitespace each site had.\n\n2. The extractor misses text followed by `{'' ''}` rather than `<`. Two sentences\n   in member-access-modal sat between converted ones, leaving one paragraph\n   half-translated — precisely the state this work exists to remove. The\n   measured 290 was therefore a floor, not a total.\n\n3. The codemod translated `aria-label=\"AgentBook\"` in Wordmark. A locale must\n   not be able to rename the product. Reverted, the key deleted, and asserted.\n\nTHE NEW GUARD, AND WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT COVER\n\ni18n-shell-wiring.test.ts scrapes every `t(''ns.key'')` from every file that\nimports useT — 56 files, 573 keys — and resolves each through the real\ntranslator in all three locales. That catches a typo or a key nobody added,\nwhich `t()` hides completely: useT''s fallback humanises\n`core_ui.accounting_basis` into \"Accounting basis\", correct-looking English.\n\nIt does NOT catch a key missing from one locale: the lookup chain\nfr-CA -> fr -> en returns the English string, so the check sees a value and\npasses. Verified by deleting one — this file stayed green and\ni18n-catalog.test.ts''s key-parity assertion failed instead. The two are\ncomplementary and the header says so, because assuming otherwise leaves a hole.\n\nScoped to useT importers after a false positive: components/docs uses a\ndifferent `t` from @/lib/i18n with its own catalog and a (key, locale)\nsignature, and the first version reported its keys as missing.\n\nmember-access-modal.test.tsx now renders inside a real English translator\nrather than bare. Without a provider its assertions were matching useT''s\nhumanised fallback, which is close enough to English to pass while proving\nnothing about the catalog.\n\nTen more words joined IDENTICAL_ALLOWED: Deel, Finch, Google Gemini and GitHub\nare names; Pro, Info, Urgent, Version, Visible and Test are spelled the same in\nFrench.\n\nRemaining: 49 strings in the plugin frontends, for tranche 3. The flag stays\noff until those land.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(i18n): satisfy the unwired-key guard, and drop the brand-name keys\n\nCI''s `unwired-keys` guard caught three things the tranche got wrong. It exists\nto find literals whose translation ALREADY sits in the catalog unused — \"all of\nthe cost, none of the benefit\", as its header puts it — and it was right on\nevery count.\n\nBRAND NAMES SHOULD NEVER HAVE HAD KEYS\n\nTelegram, WhatsApp, webhook, Deel, Finch, Google Gemini and GitHub were given\ncore_ui keys whose value is identical in all three locales. That buys nothing,\nand it actively hurts: every occurrence of the word anywhere in the repo then\nregisters as an unwired key, which is how four plugin files started failing a\nguard that must be zero. The keys are deleted, the call sites reverted to\nliterals, and the reason is recorded where the IDENTICAL_ALLOWED entries used\nto be so nobody re-adds them.\n\nEIGHT SHELL SITES THE CODEMOD COULD NOT SEE\n\n\"Sign Out\", \"Core\", \"Create Team\", \"Danger Zone\", \"Delete Team\" and \"Transfer\nOwnership\" already had keys but were still literals in six places — the JSX-text\nregex misses text split across lines or wrapped in a child tag. Same root cause\nas the two sentences found in member-access-modal. Now wired; shell is 0.\n\nPlugins 0, shell 0.\n\nTHE SERVER-COMPONENT RATCHET, RAISED DELIBERATELY: 27 -> 39\n\nThe remaining twelve are server components, which cannot call useT — that is\nwhy this measure is a ratchet and not a hard zero. Nine are the plan names\n\"Pro\" and \"Business\" in the /guides marketing pages, including /guides/zh,\nwhich correctly keeps the English plan name in its pricing table: those routes\nare localized by separate fr/zh route trees, so wiring them to the app catalog\nwould be wrong. Two are \"Page Not Found\" in not-found.tsx and one is alt text\nin a server-rendered OG image.\n\nAll four colliding keys were checked and each IS used by a real client\ncomponent, so none is dead weight — the collision is only that the same English\nword appears in a differently-localized surface.\n\nbin/i18n-string-ratchet.sh: 570 -> 361 literals, locked in.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d6319c034dbf43353afa4829047157dde3d8c115","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/d6319c034dbf43353afa4829047157dde3d8c115"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/d06ea7004a3b4a1d5a4bd99f998811831f4f5616","verification":{"payload":"tree d6319c034dbf43353afa4829047157dde3d8c115\nparent 5b17f5cb13be37317e1c0ccc8b541e836afa13fa\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788890715 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788890715 -0700\n\nfeat(i18n): localize the shell for fr-CA and zh-CN (P1-6, tranches 1+2) (#522)\n\n* i18n(settings): localize the settings surfaces (P1-6, tranche 1 of 3)\n\n83 hardcoded English strings across the settings page and the AgentBook\nsettings panel, replaced with catalog keys and translated into fr-CA and\nzh-CN. 76 new keys in core_ui; 5 strings reused keys that already existed.\n\nWHY THIS IS THE BLOCKER, NOT A POLISH ITEM\n\nThe fr-CA/zh-CN locale flag (`agentbook.i18n.locales.enabled`) is off, and its\nown comment says why: flipping it while any surface is half-translated ships\nmixed French and English. Measuring that surface found 290 user-visible strings\nbypassing the translator, 284 of them in files that ALREADY call `t()` — so\nthose pages would render half in each language. Settings is the largest single\npiece at 83 and the surface a Canadian user configuring their business spends\nthe most time in.\n\nFOUR COMPONENTS HAD NO TRANSLATOR AT ALL\n\nProfilePreview, ShareCard, QrCard and ParentShareTab render user-visible text\nand never called useT(). Rather than guess at scope, the literals were replaced\nfirst and the compiler asked: it named exactly those four with \"Cannot find\nname ''t''\".\n\nTHE GUARD, AND WHY IT IS NOT ANOTHER CATALOG TEST\n\ni18n-catalog.test.ts already proves the catalog is internally consistent — same\nkeys everywhere, matching variables, nothing untranslated. All of that passed\nduring the last rollout while the running page was still visibly English,\nbecause a consistent catalog says nothing about whether the COMPONENT asks for\na key or hardcodes the sentence.\n\nSo the new test asserts both halves: the literals really left each file, and\nevery key the files now use resolves through the REAL translator to a real\ntranslation in all three locales. The second half matters because `t()` never\nthrows on a missing key — useT''s fallback humanises `core_ui.accounting_basis`\ninto \"Accounting basis\", which reads as correct English and hides the miss.\n\nIt also guards the guard: `not.toContain` passes just as happily on an empty\nfile, so the test checks the files still hold their text and their t() calls.\n\nMutation-checked both ways: restoring one English literal fails it, and copying\nan English value into fr-CA fails it.\n\nTelegram, WhatsApp, \"webhook\" and \"Logo\" are in IDENTICAL_ALLOWED — a Chinese\nuser configuring a Telegram bot looks for the word \"Telegram\", and translating\na brand is a bug rather than a courtesy.\n\nRemaining for tranches 2 and 3: 201 strings, mostly teams, sales-rep, payroll\nand admin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(i18n): localize the rest of the shell (P1-6, tranche 2)\n\n156 more hardcoded strings across 37 shell files — teams, sales-rep, payroll,\nnotifications, admin, PWA, marketplace — plus 132 new core_ui keys in all three\nlocales. The shell is now down to 4 untranslated strings, two of which are the\nWordmark''s brand name and stay that way.\n\nTHREE THINGS THE FIRST PASS GOT WRONG, ALL CAUGHT BEFORE MERGE\n\n1. The codemod ate a leading space. `>([^<>{}\\n]...)<` captures the whitespace\n   between a tag and its text, and the replacement discarded it, so\n   `<strong>Configure:</strong> Member can modify...` became\n   `<strong>{t(...)}</strong>{t(...)}` — rendering \"Configurer :Member can\n   modify\". JSX preserves a space that is not adjacent to a newline, so this\n   was a real visual regression at 28 sites, four of them from tranche 1.\n   Repaired by diffing against origin/main and restoring the exact leading and\n   trailing whitespace each site had.\n\n2. The extractor misses text followed by `{'' ''}` rather than `<`. Two sentences\n   in member-access-modal sat between converted ones, leaving one paragraph\n   half-translated — precisely the state this work exists to remove. The\n   measured 290 was therefore a floor, not a total.\n\n3. The codemod translated `aria-label=\"AgentBook\"` in Wordmark. A locale must\n   not be able to rename the product. Reverted, the key deleted, and asserted.\n\nTHE NEW GUARD, AND WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT COVER\n\ni18n-shell-wiring.test.ts scrapes every `t(''ns.key'')` from every file that\nimports useT — 56 files, 573 keys — and resolves each through the real\ntranslator in all three locales. That catches a typo or a key nobody added,\nwhich `t()` hides completely: useT''s fallback humanises\n`core_ui.accounting_basis` into \"Accounting basis\", correct-looking English.\n\nIt does NOT catch a key missing from one locale: the lookup chain\nfr-CA -> fr -> en returns the English string, so the check sees a value and\npasses. Verified by deleting one — this file stayed green and\ni18n-catalog.test.ts''s key-parity assertion failed instead. The two are\ncomplementary and the header says so, because assuming otherwise leaves a hole.\n\nScoped to useT importers after a false positive: components/docs uses a\ndifferent `t` from @/lib/i18n with its own catalog and a (key, locale)\nsignature, and the first version reported its keys as missing.\n\nmember-access-modal.test.tsx now renders inside a real English translator\nrather than bare. Without a provider its assertions were matching useT''s\nhumanised fallback, which is close enough to English to pass while proving\nnothing about the catalog.\n\nTen more words joined IDENTICAL_ALLOWED: Deel, Finch, Google Gemini and GitHub\nare names; Pro, Info, Urgent, Version, Visible and Test are spelled the same in\nFrench.\n\nRemaining: 49 strings in the plugin frontends, for tranche 3. The flag stays\noff until those land.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(i18n): satisfy the unwired-key guard, and drop the brand-name keys\n\nCI''s `unwired-keys` guard caught three things the tranche got wrong. It exists\nto find literals whose translation ALREADY sits in the catalog unused — \"all of\nthe cost, none of the benefit\", as its header puts it — and it was right on\nevery count.\n\nBRAND NAMES SHOULD NEVER HAVE HAD KEYS\n\nTelegram, WhatsApp, webhook, Deel, Finch, Google Gemini and GitHub were given\ncore_ui keys whose value is identical in all three locales. That buys nothing,\nand it actively hurts: every occurrence of the word anywhere in the repo then\nregisters as an unwired key, which is how four plugin files started failing a\nguard that must be zero. The keys are deleted, the call sites reverted to\nliterals, and the reason is recorded where the IDENTICAL_ALLOWED entries used\nto be so nobody re-adds them.\n\nEIGHT SHELL SITES THE CODEMOD COULD NOT SEE\n\n\"Sign Out\", \"Core\", \"Create Team\", \"Danger Zone\", \"Delete Team\" and \"Transfer\nOwnership\" already had keys but were still literals in six places — the JSX-text\nregex misses text split across lines or wrapped in a child tag. Same root cause\nas the two sentences found in member-access-modal. Now wired; shell is 0.\n\nPlugins 0, shell 0.\n\nTHE SERVER-COMPONENT RATCHET, RAISED DELIBERATELY: 27 -> 39\n\nThe remaining twelve are server components, which cannot call useT — that is\nwhy this measure is a ratchet and not a hard zero. Nine are the plan names\n\"Pro\" and \"Business\" in the /guides marketing pages, including /guides/zh,\nwhich correctly keeps the English plan name in its pricing table: those routes\nare localized by separate fr/zh route trees, so wiring them to the app catalog\nwould be wrong. Two are \"Page Not Found\" in not-found.tsx and one is alt text\nin a server-rendered OG image.\n\nAll four colliding keys were checked and each IS used by a real client\ncomponent, so none is dead weight — the collision is only that the same English\nword appears in a differently-localized surface.\n\nbin/i18n-string-ratchet.sh: 570 -> 361 literals, locked in.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoE5bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPq0QAE2eTchM+zxfPuDvu7+v4oWb\nP1KFCJHO9BSJJb7fY7/os+lEVLB8q+cVW6pYCLPPwAcxfy4MhyD5SLYc0zcknqa7\nxyMllOA10tL9B+tnagjpcRGvMlgS2U/39Fumu+WreroZ/SDMPSysgVb9Hzm96w6V\n4r10fQbCNBhaNiIouGYZ4d0VR3afIc0fJk617NbHjy+Hcz+ktLTD89MYDS5TiJS3\nCigl9D+6/5DRVYcWCuJ6rI2PB3LQmT3tMPFAkMYZagGS7ZrdrXhI5B3ZKwGIty85\nzILv7sDd7DTXbOOw8wUpcvrjFeaRCDEkHeCJx/RH9WYL/LL3thqVEjXaxOJwy0La\nXd0X7/6AuD1fVcJbJytCEIwtcVD/nEih+8IiYTpFkBcZZtEBhN9FMgstsHR2+vFu\nid10o/88PyffzpVJ3TwJ2CLT3U8+PrBEEzGJCDKUBAID44nybv12ajQ874YXeFJn\njiVMz25ZwgcwdJh175o/qftraMV6aQZeuaYlupU8zZ2lHQhXfdbeREgSDqVLGmjW\nYI0cMFbX6hhC9HPnwVobacyPOZIinQ7q6Gn2KqWWHlVxSQpWwq9F9IoPVga4HmRG\n+G4ssdn86oHiZvw0MlTPRbSA1AKN3W41hVry9c6PGO5k+14LCuvA+EnroDL12bvT\nPuF+KpWBpg4aGwQCWfDm\n=0Ns1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T18:05:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/d06ea7004a3b4a1d5a4bd99f998811831f4f5616","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGQwNmVhNzAwNGEzYjRhMWQ1YTRiZDk5Zjk5ODgxMTgzMWY0ZjU2MTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/5b17f5cb13be37317e1c0ccc8b541e836afa13fa","sha":"5b17f5cb13be37317e1c0ccc8b541e836afa13fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/5b17f5cb13be37317e1c0ccc8b541e836afa13fa"}],"sha":"d06ea7004a3b4a1d5a4bd99f998811831f4f5616","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/d06ea7004a3b4a1d5a4bd99f998811831f4f5616"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/5b17f5cb13be37317e1c0ccc8b541e836afa13fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T17:20:42Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T17:20:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): bound 25 backtracking regexes — one burned 27s of CPU on 16kB (#521)\n\n* fix(security): bound 25 backtracking regexes — one burned 27s of CPU on 16kB\n\nAll 25 `js/polynomial-redos` alerts. I had previously assessed these as\nunreachable and I was measuring the wrong code path.\n\nWHAT I GOT WRONG\n\nThe earlier triage timed a hostile message through skill ROUTING — all 85\nbuilt-in skills dispatch a 60k-char message in under 9ms, which is true and\nirrelevant. Eighteen of these patterns live in `localBrainFallback` and\n`localEngagementFallback`, the tables that run when the LLM call fails or\nreturns empty. Different path, reached from `catch`, with the raw user text.\n\nMeasured on the shipped patterns, failing match, 4x input scaling:\n\n    how.*file.*tax        419ms -> 27,028ms    ratio 64.5   (two gaps: cubic)\n    [.!]+$                 25ms ->    397ms    ratio 15.9\n    can.*deduct             6ms ->    100ms    ratio 15.9\n    ...and six more at ~16x\n\n27 seconds of CPU for a 16 kB message, on the path that only runs when the LLM\nis already down. That is the worst possible moment to add a synchronous stall,\nand a handful of concurrent messages would hold the process indefinitely.\n\nTHE FIX\n\nEvery unbounded gap between two literals becomes a bounded quantifier —\n`register.*business` -> `register.{0,30}business`, `(.+?)\\s+\\$` ->\n`(.{1,80}?)\\s+\\$`, `[.!]+$` -> `[.!]{1,10}$`, and so on across the intent\ntables, the vendor/invoice/timer extractors, the money scraper, the vendor\nalias parser, the planner''s `if.+then` and the corrections category matcher.\nSame shape, bounded work.\n\nBounds are wider than real usage: 204 combinations of the twelve changed intent\npatterns against seventeen realistic messages produce zero behaviour\ndifferences, and the four extractors still return the same captures.\n\nTHE TEST, AND WHY IT IS SHAPED THIS WAY\n\nTiming a match proves nothing — a pattern returns at the first success however\nbad its backtracking is. Every input ends with a character the pattern cannot\nconsume, and the test asserts the input does NOT match before timing it, so a\nfuture edit cannot quietly turn these into fast successful matches.\n\nIt compares n against 4n rather than checking a millisecond threshold: linear\nis ~4x, quadratic ~16x, and 9 sits clear of both, so it does not flake on a\nloaded runner. Mutation-checked by restoring the shipped patterns — nine cases\nfail with ratios of 15.9 to 64.5.\n\nIt also asserts the source files no longer contain the unbounded forms, since\nthe timing cases run their own copies and would otherwise keep passing while\n`.*` came back.\n\nNOTED, NOT FIXED: `localBrainFallback` (agent-brain.ts) and\n`localEngagementFallback` (server.ts) are near-duplicate tables of 11 and 12\nrules. Both were patched here. Unifying them is a behaviour-risk refactor that\ndoes not belong in a security fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): bound the whitespace runs too — CodeQL found what my test missed\n\nThe first pass bounded the `.` gaps and built its hostile inputs from repeated\nletters. CodeQL still flagged five patterns, and it was right: the remaining\nambiguity was the `\\s+` sitting next to a lazy `.` group. Because `.` matches a\nspace as well, a run of spaces can be divided between the two quantifiers many\nways — and an input of repeated letters never exercises that split, so the test\nwas green on a pattern that was still quadratic.\n\n`\\s+` -> `\\s{1,20}` and `\\s*` -> `\\s{0,20}` in the invoice, estimate/quote,\ntimer, vendor-alias and rename patterns. The number of divisions becomes a\nconstant.\n\nBehaviour verified against the originals rather than assumed: identical\ncaptures on seven real commands, including that `SQ *COFFEE` is rejected by\nboth, since `*` is outside the vendor character class and the bound should not\nbe blamed for a rejection it did not cause.\n\nThe new timing cases use space runs, so this vector cannot reopen unnoticed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a965ffa1cb72b674ca9479fef037fce60e93a175","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/a965ffa1cb72b674ca9479fef037fce60e93a175"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/5b17f5cb13be37317e1c0ccc8b541e836afa13fa","verification":{"payload":"tree a965ffa1cb72b674ca9479fef037fce60e93a175\nparent c7f0f50e2691162d2ab9952b1e9c0a4da94a9453\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788888042 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788888042 -0700\n\nfix(security): bound 25 backtracking regexes — one burned 27s of CPU on 16kB (#521)\n\n* fix(security): bound 25 backtracking regexes — one burned 27s of CPU on 16kB\n\nAll 25 `js/polynomial-redos` alerts. I had previously assessed these as\nunreachable and I was measuring the wrong code path.\n\nWHAT I GOT WRONG\n\nThe earlier triage timed a hostile message through skill ROUTING — all 85\nbuilt-in skills dispatch a 60k-char message in under 9ms, which is true and\nirrelevant. Eighteen of these patterns live in `localBrainFallback` and\n`localEngagementFallback`, the tables that run when the LLM call fails or\nreturns empty. Different path, reached from `catch`, with the raw user text.\n\nMeasured on the shipped patterns, failing match, 4x input scaling:\n\n    how.*file.*tax        419ms -> 27,028ms    ratio 64.5   (two gaps: cubic)\n    [.!]+$                 25ms ->    397ms    ratio 15.9\n    can.*deduct             6ms ->    100ms    ratio 15.9\n    ...and six more at ~16x\n\n27 seconds of CPU for a 16 kB message, on the path that only runs when the LLM\nis already down. That is the worst possible moment to add a synchronous stall,\nand a handful of concurrent messages would hold the process indefinitely.\n\nTHE FIX\n\nEvery unbounded gap between two literals becomes a bounded quantifier —\n`register.*business` -> `register.{0,30}business`, `(.+?)\\s+\\$` ->\n`(.{1,80}?)\\s+\\$`, `[.!]+$` -> `[.!]{1,10}$`, and so on across the intent\ntables, the vendor/invoice/timer extractors, the money scraper, the vendor\nalias parser, the planner''s `if.+then` and the corrections category matcher.\nSame shape, bounded work.\n\nBounds are wider than real usage: 204 combinations of the twelve changed intent\npatterns against seventeen realistic messages produce zero behaviour\ndifferences, and the four extractors still return the same captures.\n\nTHE TEST, AND WHY IT IS SHAPED THIS WAY\n\nTiming a match proves nothing — a pattern returns at the first success however\nbad its backtracking is. Every input ends with a character the pattern cannot\nconsume, and the test asserts the input does NOT match before timing it, so a\nfuture edit cannot quietly turn these into fast successful matches.\n\nIt compares n against 4n rather than checking a millisecond threshold: linear\nis ~4x, quadratic ~16x, and 9 sits clear of both, so it does not flake on a\nloaded runner. Mutation-checked by restoring the shipped patterns — nine cases\nfail with ratios of 15.9 to 64.5.\n\nIt also asserts the source files no longer contain the unbounded forms, since\nthe timing cases run their own copies and would otherwise keep passing while\n`.*` came back.\n\nNOTED, NOT FIXED: `localBrainFallback` (agent-brain.ts) and\n`localEngagementFallback` (server.ts) are near-duplicate tables of 11 and 12\nrules. Both were patched here. Unifying them is a behaviour-risk refactor that\ndoes not belong in a security fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): bound the whitespace runs too — CodeQL found what my test missed\n\nThe first pass bounded the `.` gaps and built its hostile inputs from repeated\nletters. CodeQL still flagged five patterns, and it was right: the remaining\nambiguity was the `\\s+` sitting next to a lazy `.` group. Because `.` matches a\nspace as well, a run of spaces can be divided between the two quantifiers many\nways — and an input of repeated letters never exercises that split, so the test\nwas green on a pattern that was still quadratic.\n\n`\\s+` -> `\\s{1,20}` and `\\s*` -> `\\s{0,20}` in the invoice, estimate/quote,\ntimer, vendor-alias and rename patterns. The number of divisions becomes a\nconstant.\n\nBehaviour verified against the originals rather than assumed: identical\ncaptures on seven real commands, including that `SQ *COFFEE` is rejected by\nboth, since `*` is outside the vendor character class and the bound should not\nbe blamed for a rejection it did not cause.\n\nThe new timing cases use space runs, so this vector cannot reopen unnoticed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoEPqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4hMQAD1OIVhuDkBBdIb9SNTN4OFt\nRtsYtn7CnByBSGFpACXpNDVVezZOM7nksJLqrhMkFOrpxY5mb8F01dkJFk/MnaHn\nKyCOXIMwUiRGdKoV2gE092wphyBLgZdTRD0zAEO7pQH0sjxxPTqR9XjXHVTn1n2R\nev4Ypttme/97etou5GexQ4cQjDiOvE9ahqmVvKVPFm6aiTENaJwlVZvSF5jnXKgo\nJUoOmYB3SWvlplsGlVGQDdLaF9PPj8Ru/eA2Akm/rliHqCmwaz4e2kDemwTPQlH+\nHwlg0dbFyO7Y21pHPVr35ETkergvj0IFng2IX18oFdqLcERot20HZZZ677yVcDOH\nEB7jXKl/SvSigLNc56Rg/SH431x06Blpia4it05t4Cf/mM1j+kPDVrP/SkchRYYQ\nLcJW+am8mZHg1CMvYezEecG6Sr5cid0TdXm3HxcI1su3nQ3Bmc+kNl14IrGOGbkW\n3DkUGDmKEo/94DnKALQRSZYeVZdAMb8snlMEQkruwaT6tAxzPr7sZ4Dw1OxWZFO9\n9Bituh6LQoWxnAyLMtVhe7Hp9IKC/OluJtBGaZEUgRJC5+4FOq9+lo6k6jyCgCbk\npLL2doMl+jClEj1D8floDvhMl3p/h2DhtEQY8Ml4LcpVQEHaPSsXTfNnoE2tKFXM\n3/GjCzkZ59PyUMq2SWgR\n=ozJ1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T17:20:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/5b17f5cb13be37317e1c0ccc8b541e836afa13fa","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKDViMTdmNWNiMTNiZTM3MzE3ZTFjMGNjYzhiNTQxZTgzNmFmYTEzZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/c7f0f50e2691162d2ab9952b1e9c0a4da94a9453","sha":"c7f0f50e2691162d2ab9952b1e9c0a4da94a9453","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/c7f0f50e2691162d2ab9952b1e9c0a4da94a9453"}],"sha":"5b17f5cb13be37317e1c0ccc8b541e836afa13fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/5b17f5cb13be37317e1c0ccc8b541e836afa13fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/c7f0f50e2691162d2ab9952b1e9c0a4da94a9453/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:50:05Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:50:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(dev): unbreak `npm run dev`, which #517 left starting deleted services (#520)\n\n`npm run dev` and `npm start` both run bin/start.sh, and start_core() did:\n\n    start_base_service &   # cd \"$ROOT_DIR/services/base-svc\"\n    start_plugin_server &  # cd \"$ROOT_DIR/services/plugin-server\"\n    ...\n    [ $_core_fail -gt 0 ] && exit 1\n\nBoth directories were deleted in #517, so the script exited 1 before starting\na single plugin backend or the Next.js shell. Local dev has been broken on main\nsince that merge. My grep when preparing #517 was truncated at 25 hits and I\ntook it for the whole list.\n\nRemoved from bin/start.sh: the two start functions, their entries in\nstart_core/stop_services/status/validate, the generated BASE_SVC_URL and\nPLUGIN_SERVER_URL, the base-svc .env creation and DATABASE_URL cross-check, the\nport variables, and five summary banners advertising endpoints that no longer\nanswer. `bash -n` clean.\n\nOthers in the same state:\n\n  ecosystem.config.cjs        deleted — its `apps` array held base-svc and\n                              plugin-server and nothing else\n  bin/health-monitor.sh       watched plugin-server AND the plugin backends;\n                              kept the half that still exists\n  bin/regression-guard.sh     required services/base-svc/package.json, so the\n                              guard would have failed on a clean checkout\n  bin/health-check.sh         stale comment\n\nscripts/quality-gates/check.ts ran `prisma validate` in services/base-svc — a\nper-service schema from the old multi-database layout. Pointed at\npackages/database, where the one schema lives. It also now passes placeholder\nURLs, because `prisma validate` resolves env() at parse time and fails P1012\nwhen DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED is unset: the gate was reporting the shell''s\nenvironment rather than schema validity, and before that was reporting a\nmissing directory. It actually validates now.\n\nVerified: every touched script passes `bash -n`; bin/lifecycle-smoke.sh and\nbin/regression-guard.sh (7/7) pass; `prisma validate` reports the schema valid.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"db5e9ceae506bd5659f5946b382273b1b38252ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/db5e9ceae506bd5659f5946b382273b1b38252ff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/c7f0f50e2691162d2ab9952b1e9c0a4da94a9453","verification":{"payload":"tree db5e9ceae506bd5659f5946b382273b1b38252ff\nparent f6058c1ad54da8661da690d7d43e1ba2cd281745\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788886205 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788886205 -0700\n\nfix(dev): unbreak `npm run dev`, which #517 left starting deleted services (#520)\n\n`npm run dev` and `npm start` both run bin/start.sh, and start_core() did:\n\n    start_base_service &   # cd \"$ROOT_DIR/services/base-svc\"\n    start_plugin_server &  # cd \"$ROOT_DIR/services/plugin-server\"\n    ...\n    [ $_core_fail -gt 0 ] && exit 1\n\nBoth directories were deleted in #517, so the script exited 1 before starting\na single plugin backend or the Next.js shell. Local dev has been broken on main\nsince that merge. My grep when preparing #517 was truncated at 25 hits and I\ntook it for the whole list.\n\nRemoved from bin/start.sh: the two start functions, their entries in\nstart_core/stop_services/status/validate, the generated BASE_SVC_URL and\nPLUGIN_SERVER_URL, the base-svc .env creation and DATABASE_URL cross-check, the\nport variables, and five summary banners advertising endpoints that no longer\nanswer. `bash -n` clean.\n\nOthers in the same state:\n\n  ecosystem.config.cjs        deleted — its `apps` array held base-svc and\n                              plugin-server and nothing else\n  bin/health-monitor.sh       watched plugin-server AND the plugin backends;\n                              kept the half that still exists\n  bin/regression-guard.sh     required services/base-svc/package.json, so the\n                              guard would have failed on a clean checkout\n  bin/health-check.sh         stale comment\n\nscripts/quality-gates/check.ts ran `prisma validate` in services/base-svc — a\nper-service schema from the old multi-database layout. Pointed at\npackages/database, where the one schema lives. It also now passes placeholder\nURLs, because `prisma validate` resolves env() at parse time and fails P1012\nwhen DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED is unset: the gate was reporting the shell''s\nenvironment rather than schema validity, and before that was reporting a\nmissing directory. It actually validates now.\n\nVerified: every touched script passes `bash -n`; bin/lifecycle-smoke.sh and\nbin/regression-guard.sh (7/7) pass; `prisma validate` reports the schema valid.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoDy9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADHEQADSq9q37+wOHzGeiIbnOW55K\nSRxQTVYrgPScO4wLZLXAgJE59ONn13TSjgg0TRXsMefTnGTF/BfiHbOfJ1rz8Vom\nZbgTS72tommfUhiTV6RVBupf6elDtVv1NOVVNpk/iF8gKZ+F7Zs/4XY8/JZS6BHY\nTGwocfpVJ4xdsLVOafuGLu3cAYtip0hRpHXz1qiTm8S9ajgAuZVXv4Xov+IoTBBA\nW7/xakU5VEFaYQBuKmLgL4ZjBYm0N3TJdOfd6TeCBbUVrmZCj2JApz+clCz+88Wn\nmBGE6cnV8Um3QwXHP4vhxLRwqF0f6xlSx+8zg6gtyM853+8c2wb6PCb8bk+yx6ue\nRA1K0HIl/XUK68PeNSKu97iBJtsScM0nRxqFbktV73LoEtL6tdnjxOSxQ0BcEcYK\nhfC8QqmjMpLirLkmR2ZLlgR+cUJ+twOET4qo+DaFNdCGjZx6R8HZoVSIeIAci/bG\n9YTKO1gSixcRtx+iS0r4T0MGfwnZ0EST057ryXj4AJgxtvfR2uDlSJBBb3QRxs0A\nJ/ZI9QXTq6QA15tkDFpkmhKI09xFVm2o4nFO5n9a4PscC4sptNfBzD7KAi1uo7TA\npLZnb3ZK/acbZNHUMvw6LT3de4phIKBzu8cF/Li+PizrmMEZQmr7YK8jzcFVBGrH\nJdSJNPu/2qTNAXirnv28\n=lTly\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T16:50:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/c7f0f50e2691162d2ab9952b1e9c0a4da94a9453","node_id":"C_kwDORLz5u9oAKGM3ZjBmNTBlMjY5MTE2MmQyYWI5OTUyYjFlOWMwYTRkYTk0YTk0NTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan/a3p/commit/f6058c1ad54da8661da690d7d43e1ba2cd281745","sha":"f6058c1ad54da8661da690d7d43e1ba2cd281745","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/f6058c1ad54da8661da690d7d43e1ba2cd281745"}],"sha":"c7f0f50e2691162d2ab9952b1e9c0a4da94a9453","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/c7f0f50e2691162d2ab9952b1e9c0a4da94a9453"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1487500?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qianghan","id":1487500,"login":"qianghan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODc1MDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qianghan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/commits/f6058c1ad54da8661da690d7d43e1ba2cd281745/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:39:04Z","email":"qiang.han@gmail.com","name":"qianghan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:39:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: delete the workflow web apps orphaned by #517 (#519)\n\n`apps/workflows/` held capacity-planner-web, community-web, developer-web and\nmarketplace-web — the frontends for the four `services/workflows/*` backends\ndeleted in #517. With their backends gone they had nothing to talk to, and\nthey were already unreferenced before that: the only matches for\n`@naap/capacity-planner-web` and its three siblings anywhere in the repo are\nthe `name` fields in their own package.json files. No import, no CI job, no\nscript, no path filter.\n\nAlso removes `bin/db-migrate.sh`, which #517 should have taken with\n`db-reset.sh` and `db-seed.sh`. It is the third of the same trio: a banner\ndeclaring itself DEPRECATED, `exit 1` on line 18, and forty lines of\nunreachable code below resolving paths under `services/workflows/`.\n\nStale `apps/workflows/*` entries pruned from package-lock.json, and the\nworkspace glob removed. `npm ci` clean before and after.\n\nVerified: clean build, shared bundle unchanged at 103 kB, web-next typecheck\n344, suite at baseline, lifecycle-smoke passes.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"368427f43ce2addb5cf8d0414452d864270b542a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/trees/368427f43ce2addb5cf8d0414452d864270b542a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qianghan/a3p/git/commits/f6058c1ad54da8661da690d7d43e1ba2cd281745","verification":{"payload":"tree 368427f43ce2addb5cf8d0414452d864270b542a\nparent 119427cdc22e7733b871e909d98b8e4cd3645ed9\nauthor qianghan <qiang.han@gmail.com> 1788885544 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788885544 -0700\n\nchore: delete the workflow web apps orphaned by #517 (#519)\n\n`apps/workflows/` held capacity-planner-web, community-web, developer-web and\nmarketplace-web — the frontends for the four `services/workflows/*` backends\ndeleted in #517. With their backends gone they had nothing to talk to, and\nthey were already unreferenced before that: the only matches for\n`@naap/capacity-planner-web` and its three siblings anywhere in the repo are\nthe `name` fields in their own package.json files. No import, no CI job, no\nscript, no path filter.\n\nAlso removes `bin/db-migrate.sh`, which #517 should have taken with\n`db-reset.sh` and `db-seed.sh`. It is the third of the same trio: a banner\ndeclaring itself DEPRECATED, `exit 1` on line 18, and forty lines of\nunreachable code below resolving paths under `services/workflows/`.\n\nStale `apps/workflows/*` entries pruned from package-lock.json, and the\nworkspace glob removed. `npm ci` clean before and after.\n\nVerified: clean build, shared bundle unchanged at 103 kB, web-next typecheck\n344, suite at baseline, lifecycle-smoke passes.\n\nCo-authored-by: seanhanca <103605970+seanhanca@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoDooCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9c0QAF+Rla8bbQuzVti4kCamryA/\neBqJpFF5lYL5wHv